-- QuestLocFlavor (generado 2026-10-17): objetivos completos, con dialogos, solo para narrar.
_G.QuestLocFlavor = _G.QuestLocFlavor or {}
QuestLocFlavor[25] = {
[12500]={"Habla con Alla en el lado noreste de Musgovilla.","'¿Es cierto que Dai estuvo a punto de ser devorado por ratas? Eso es realmente asombroso, ${PLAYER}. Buen trabajo salvándolo, supongo. Aun así, ahora tiene una historia realmente emocionante para contar. ¿Se quedó con el queso, o tuvo que devolverlo a los proveedores?\
\
'He estado pensándolo mientras estabas fuera, y creo que quizá no nos desafiaremos más durante un tiempo. ¡Durante un tiempo dije! No digo nunca, así que no creas que nos estás deteniendo si se nos ocurre uno realmente bueno.\
\
'Adiós por ahora, ${PLAYER}.'","Bevan, guardia del pueblo de Musgovilla, ha oído que los niños de la aldea se están planteando desafíos y pruebas cada vez más peligrosos, y espera que puedas hacer algo al respecto.","'¡Ratas! ¡Hay ratas por todas partes! ¡Me seguían hasta que logré despistarlas!'","'No sé dónde está Dai, pero tiene que estar en algún lugar de Musgovilla.'","Dai debe estar en algún lugar de Musgovilla, y con los bolsillos llenos de queso es probable que esté en serios problemas con la población de roedores del pueblo.","Dado el problema reciente de roedores en Musgovilla, Dai podría estar en serios problemas.","'Los niños no dieron ninguna razón para querer queso. ¿Acaso alguien necesita una razón?'","Quizá la niña Alla te diga qué planean los niños.","Musgovilla tiene varios proveedores, pero uno de ellos suele estar afuera de su almacén en el lado oeste de la plaza del pueblo.","El Último Desafío","Encuentra a Dai en Musgovilla y habla con él.","Alla está junto al pajar en el lado noreste de Musgovilla.","'Varios niños merodeaban afuera del almacén de provisiones hace unos minutos, y podría ser que alguno de los proveedores haya escuchado parte de su conversación. Necesitamos llegar al fondo de esto antes de que alguien salga herido, ${PLAYER}.'","'¿Un grupo de niños? Sí, los vi. Esperaban conseguir la mayor cantidad de queso posible, lo cual me resultó un tanto extraño. No les di tanto como pedían, pero pensé que un pequeño bloque del almacén para cada uno estaría bien.\
\
'Esos chicos han pasado por mucho, con la incursión Uruk en Musgovilla, y he visto pocos problemas que no puedan aliviarse con queso.'","'He oído rumores de que los niños de Musgovilla se están planteando desafíos y pruebas cada vez más peligrosos entre ellos, ¡y me preocupa que esto se salga de control, si no lo ha hecho ya! Ninguno de los guardias del pueblo logrará averiguar nada... sabes cómo son los niños... pero quizá alguien de fuera pueda descubrir algo.\
\
'Varios niños merodeaban afuera del almacén de provisiones hace unos minutos, y podría ser que alguno de los proveedores haya escuchado parte de su conversación. Necesitamos llegar al fondo de esto antes de que alguien salga herido, ${PLAYER}.'","Habla con uno de los proveedores en el lado oeste de la plaza del pueblo de Musgovilla.","'¿Qué haces aquí, ${PLAYER}? Pensé que ya te habrías marchado de Musgovilla. Será mejor que te pongas en camino, creo. ¡Hasta luego!'\
\
Te mantienes firme y le preguntas a Alla por qué los niños de Musgovilla necesitaban tanto queso del almacén. Sus ojos se abren de par en par y una expresión de pánico cruza su rostro.\
\
'¿No estamos en problemas, verdad? Es solo que por fin logramos darle la vuelta a la situación con el bravucón del pueblo, ¡y tú nos ayudaste a hacerlo! Si estamos en problemas, creo que tú también deberías estarlo... ¡es lo justo!\
\
'Verás, hay un chico llamado Dai, y siempre nos desafía con estas pruebas, y si no las completamos quedamos como cobardes. Siempre me pide que corra muy rápido hasta ciertos lugares, vea un objeto que él dejó allí, y luego regrese al pueblo, y si no describo el objeto correcto sabrá que no lo hice.'\
\
Le señalas a la niña que ella no completó ninguno de los desafíos, ya que obtuvo la información de ti, pero que aparentemente Dai sí fue a cada uno de esos lugares primero para dejar los objetos.\
\
'Siento que eso solo significa que soy muy lista, ${PLAYER}, ¿no te parece? Pero como completamos esos dos últimos desafíos... no discutas conmigo, sigue contando... entonces Dai tiene que llenar sus bolsillos de queso y caminar por Musgovilla.'\
\
Le preguntas a la niña si ha considerado que quizá ella sea en realidad la bravucóna del pueblo, y ella inclina la cabeza hacia un lado, pensándolo.\
\
'Mmm. No, no lo creo. Pero lo pensaré.'"},
[12501]={"'Hola. Quizá puedas ayudarme. Estamos en un aprieto aquí. Esta es la última granja en las Quebradas del Norte; todos los demás propietarios han sido expulsados por los orcos.\
\
No me avergüenza decir que los orcos que se han instalado en la zona son más de lo que puedo manejar solo. He hecho amistad con algunos Montaraces y los he estado abasteciendo durante muchos años. Ya es hora de que me devuelvan el favor.\
\
Ahora, no sé qué hace con ello, pero llevo sus provisiones a un Montaraz que acampa cerca de esas viejas ruinas al noroeste de mi granja. Ost Lagoros es como lo llaman, creo. El hombre se llama Orthonn.'","'No puedo ayudar a Gatson... Se le advirtió que debía abandonar las Quebradas del Norte, y eso es lo que debe hacer.'","'¿Gatson? ¿No huyó al sur como se le indicó? Sí, nos ha ayudado con provisiones en muchas ocasiones, pero siempre se le ha pagado en monedas o bienes.\
\
Cuando supimos que un gran ejército de orcos se reunía en el norte, preparándose para marchar sobre Eriador, enviamos mensajes a todos los granjeros de las Quebradas del Norte, advirtiéndoles que huyeran al sur. Mi gente no tiene suficientes números para defender a estos granjeros del ejército orco.\
\
La granja de Gatson está en el camino del ejército de Angmar. Regresa con él, si quieres, y exhórtalo a él y a sus trabajadores a marcharse de inmediato. Su granja no es defendible.'","'Los que aún estamos aquí seremos fieles al maestro Gatson pase lo que pase, aunque los orcos sean nuestro final.'","La última granja","Los orcos han entrado en las Quebradas del Norte desde el norte. Los granjeros de la región huyeron al sur, excepto el viejo Gatson, que está decidido a defender su tierra contra los orcos.","Gatson te espera en su granja al este de Ost Lagoros.\
\
Orthonn admitió que Gatson les había abastecido a menudo, pero te dijo que los Montaraces no tenían suficientes números para defender las granjas de las Quebradas del Norte. Te pidió que regresaras con Gatson y exhortaras al granjero y a sus trabajadores a huir de inmediato.","Orthonn puede encontrarse en las ruinas de Ost Lagoros, al noroeste de la granja de Gatson junto al río.\
\
El granjero Gatson te dijo que ha estado ayudando a los Montaraces con provisiones durante muchos años y ahora espera que le ayuden a proteger su granja. Te ha enviado a hablar con el Montaraz al que entrega la comida, un hombre llamado Orthonn.","'¡Por favor, ve con Orthonn a esas viejas ruinas y consigue ayuda para defender mi granja de los orcos!'","'¿Orthonn no ayudará? ¡Pero no puedo irme! ¡Esos orcos vendrán y lo quemarán todo! Mi familia ha tenido esta granja desde tiempos inmemoriales, y no seré yo quien la deje caer en la ruina.\
\
Los jornaleros que no han huido... Gilmar y esos otros tontos se quedarán conmigo hasta el final si me quedo. ¿Qué puedo hacer?'"},
[12502]={"Habla con Ravaedron frente a la Cabaña del Helechal","'Aquí es: la Cabaña del Helechal, hogar de mis amigos Maddoc y Glenys, y de su hijo Bran. Los Astaciervo fueron muy amables conmigo mientras me aventuraba por estas tierras, y los echaré de menos cuando me marche.\
\
'Agradezco que estés aquí, ${PLAYER}. Decir adiós siempre es difícil, y me gustaría que mis amigos supieran que contarán con aventureros como tú para cuidar de ellos cuando yo no esté.'","'Aquí es: la Cabaña del Helechal, hogar de mis amigos los Astaciervo.'","'Si me acompañas a la cabaña de los Astaciervo y me ayudas a despedirme, me harías un favor, pues lo he estado posponiendo. Viven en una agradable cabaña al sureste, más allá de la antigua aldea de Glynafon.'","Has llegado a la Cabaña del Helechal, hogar de los Astaciervo","Ravaedron se encuentra en el camino que va hacia el sur desde el Bosque de los Trolls hasta el Ángulo.","'Muy bien, ${PLAYER:mi nuevo amigo[m]|mi nueva amiga[f]}. ¡Eres muy ${PLAYER:diestro[m]|diestra[f]} enfrentándote a este tipo de amenazas! No me extraña que Elladan y Elrohir confíen tanto en ti. ¿Te enviaron ellos a una misión como la mía? Me mandaron aquí en busca de oscuros sirvientes del Enemigo, jinetes de negro que burlaron las defensas de Imladris. Ah... tal vez no debería hablar más de ellos. Elrohir fue muy claro en que era un asunto secreto.'\
\
Ravaedron hace el gesto de cerrar sus labios con llave y colgarla de una cadena invisible en su cuello.\
\
'Digamos simplemente que no hallé rastro de nuestra presa, y dejémoslo ahí. Aun así, mi búsqueda no fue en vano, pues encontré algo que ahora me es muy querido. Entablé amistad con una familia de leñadores, los Astaciervo. Viven no muy lejos de aquí, y valoro mucho su amistad; la última amistad que hallaré en la Tierra Media, pues mis pasos me llevan ahora hacia los Puertos Grises y navegaré hacia el Oeste, dando fin a este capítulo de mi vida.'\
\
Ravaedron ríe de repente.\
\
'¡Aunque quizá los Astaciervo no sean la última amistad que haga aquí, ${PLAYER}, pues no contaba con conocerte! Pero si me acompañas a su cabaña y me ayudas a despedirme, te lo agradecería muchísimo... pues lo he estado posponiendo. Viven en una agradable cabaña al sureste, más allá de la antigua aldea de Glynafon.'","Ravaedron se encuentra frente a la Cabaña del Helechal, el hogar de sus amigos, al sureste de la antigua aldea de Glynafon.","Habla con Ravaedron en el camino que viene del Bosque de los Trolls","Derrota a enemigos amenazantes en el Ángulo del Mitheithel (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has derrotado a enemigos en el Ángulo para Ravaedron (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","En el camino que lleva hacia el sur desde el Bosque de los Trolls hasta el Ángulo del Mitheithel, encontraste a un elfo que solicitaba tu ayuda.","'¡Salvaguardemos las tierras salvajes para la buena gente que habita en esta región! Quizá después me ayudes con la tarea que tanto he retrasado.'","La Cabaña del Helechal, el hogar de los amigos de Ravaedron, se encuentra al sureste, más allá de la aldea de Glynafon en el Ángulo del Mitheithel.","La última amistad","Enemigos peligrosos acechan los bosques rocosos del Ángulo, y Ravaedron desea que lo ayudes a combatirlos.","'Mae govannen, ${PLAYERNAME:forastero[m]|forastera[f]}. Has llegado al Ángulo del Mitheithel, pero vas hacia el sur en lugar de hacia el norte. ¡Qué curioso! He descubierto que quienes viajan por estas tierras suelen hacerlo de paso hacia algún otro lugar, como es mi caso. No permaneceré mucho tiempo aquí en el Ángulo.'\
\
El elfo sonríe brevemente.\
\
'¡Pero qué modales los míos! Permíteme que me presente de inmediato: me llamo Ravaedron, y llegué al Ángulo hace algún tiempo por un encargo de los hijos de Elrond. ¡Ah! ¿Te conocen? Entonces seamos amigos también, pues compartimos el mismo propósito: ¡salvaguardar las tierras salvajes para la buena gente que vive en ellas! No te supondrá una gran molestia ayudarme con esto, ¿verdad? Hay algo que debo hacer, pero lo he estado posponiendo. Enfrentémonos primero a los peligros que se presentan aquí en el Mitheithel, y después tal vez vuelvas a ayudarme.'","Busca la Cabaña del Helechal, el hogar de los amigos de Ravaedron, más allá de la aldea de Glynafon al sureste"},
[12503]={"'Do you not see, ${PLAYER}? More likely than not, this is to be the last stand of the Rohirrim. The Hornburg is our best hope in surviving this night.\
\
'The enemy sends all of his might to meet us at this very place. If he wants a fight, he will have it.\
\
'Join us, friend. We will make the White Hand rue the day they set foot on this land!'","Ask Gamling for news","Éomer wishes to speak with you.\
\
You should speak with Éomer.","Habla con Éomer","'¿Si?'","Gamling the Old can be found at Helm's Dike in the southern Westfold.\
\
You should ask Gamling for news of the Westfold.","Éomer is at Helm's Dike in the south-eastern Westfold.\
\
You should speak with Éomer.","Learn of the events that changed Théoden's course","'The Fords have fallen already, stranger. It is lucky that Théoden King turned his course when he did, for even Erkenbrand and his company could not withstand the might of the enemy.\
\
'We hold this gate for Erkenbrand, and wait now for his return. We have heard naught of him since the second battle at the Fords, in which the lords of the Westfold were scattered.\
\
'Have you had news of him? Our hope lies in Erkenbrand's strength. He is the master of this keep!'","Éomer wishes to relay the counsel of Gandalf, and the news they received upon the road.\
\
You should speak with Éomer.","You regretfully tell Gamling that you have had no news at all of Erkenbrand","You cannot help but wonder why the king turned south to the keep of Helm's Deep, rather than ride down his enemy upon the plains of the Westfold.","'It is not my wish to make dire predictions for the fate of my people. I will tell you of the events upon the road, when Gandalf parted from our company and bade us come here.'","You ask the king why he and his company turned away from the Fords. Would it not be better to block the forces of Isengard from pouring through the gap?\
\
'It is a just question, ${PLAYER}, but things have taken a dire turn. Such is the news we received when Gandalf rode off. It is his counsel I follow, and you would be wise to do the same.\
\
'I had hoped to ride to the Fords to aid Erkenbrand, but Gamling here has more current news.'","You ask Éomer why the Rohirrim do not attempt to ride the enemy down on the plain, since the riders have such a great advantage on horseback.\
\
'It is true that we are far stronger than any foe on foot, but....'\
\
Éomer trails off.","The Last Great Stronghold","Éomer is reluctant to speak his thoughts"},
[12504]={"'No sé dónde podrías encontrar el oro que Hjortur robó, aunque la historia del fracaso de Halmur dice que Hjortur está dentro de los muros de Gabilazan. Quizás allí encuentres alguna pista sobre el lingote robado.'","'Derrotaste a Hjortur, ¿pero no revisaste su cofre? ¡Regresa al lugar donde lo derrotaste de inmediato y recupera el lingote robado del cofre que custodiaba!'","Lleva el cofre enano antiguo a Larus Fragmentoagudo","El Último Lingote","El lingote robado podría estar dentro del cofre de Hjortur, dentro de los muros de Gabilazan.\
\
Has derrotado a Hjortur Duramano y ahora deberías revisar el cofre que custodiaba para encontrar el lingote robado.","Revisa el cofre de Hjortur para encontrar el lingote robado","Halmur Modelapiedra está en la tumba de su ancestro, en la colina a la izquierda al acercarte a la fortaleza enana en el paso de Gabilazan desde el norte.\
\
Halmur Modelapiedra está esperando que regreses con el lingote de oro enano robado que recuperaste del descendiente del ladrón que lo robó hace mucho tiempo.","El segundo cofre está dentro de la tumba de Halmur Modelapiedra, en el paso de Gabilazan. Larus Fragmentoagudo se encuentra en un campamento al norte del Risco Alto.\
\
Después de ayudar a Halmur Modelapiedra a recuperar el lingote robado y cumplir el juramento de su familia, te ha permitido llevar el cofre a Larus Fragmentoagudo.","El lingote robado podría encontrarse dentro de los muros de Gabilazan.\
\
Halmur Modelapiedra te sugirió buscar el lingote robado allí.","Lingote de oro enano robado reunido","Reúne el lingote de oro enano robado","'¡Ja! Vienes de parte de uno de esos necios Modelapiedra, ¿verdad? Has oído la historia de su \\qjuramento\\q sobre ese cofre, ¿no? Pues déjame contarte una historia.\
\
'El primer Hjortur Duramano robó el oro no para su propio tesoro, sino para hacer quedar como un tonto a Halmur Modelapiedra. Al enterarse del juramento de Halmur, Hjortur hizo uno propio: él y sus hijos conservarían el lingote para siempre y harían que los Modelapiedra quedaran como tontos para siempre.\
\
'Yo también vengo de una larga línea... una larga línea de Hjortur Duramano. ¡Y cumpliré con el juramento! Solo tendrás el lingote si puedes tomar el cofre sobre mi cadáver. Y no creo que eso sea muy probable...'","'Mis ojos deben engañarme, tú ${RACE}, embaucador. No puedes tener el lingote robado que me ha mantenido a mí y a los míos encadenados a este lugar durante tantos años.\
\
'Y sin embargo... ¡es él! ¿Puede ser? ¿Se ha cumplido al fin mi deber?'","'Ya veo... ¿así que fuiste enviado por un enano de las Montañas Azules? Quizás sean los largos años en soledad, pero te creo. Ahora, déjame contarte una historia.\
\
'Hace mucho tiempo, el primer Halmur Modelapiedra, hijo de Vithurr, fue encargado de custodiar los tesoros aquí. Montó guardia día y noche, incluso en días de celebración. Pero bajó la guardia una sola vez, y un enano vil, Hjortur Duramano, se coló y robó un único lingote de oro enano. Habiendo fallado en su deber, Halmur juró que él y sus hijos vigilarían el oro restante hasta que ese lingote fuera devuelto. Yo soy solo uno en una larga línea de Halmur que han mantenido ese juramento.\
\
'Si devuelves el lingote robado, el juramento se cumplirá. Entonces el cofre será tuyo para devolverlo al enano que te envió. No puedo decirte, sin embargo, dónde encontrar a Hjortur, aunque las leyendas del fracaso de Halmur dicen que Hjortur está en algún lugar dentro de Gabilazan. Quizás allí puedas encontrar el oro.'","'¡Bien, bien! Espero que el cofre no haya sido muy difícil de encontrar. Heikki Vigilaoro estará complacido con esto. ¡Sus registros no dirán nada malo de mí!\
\
'Ahora, sé que ya has hecho mucho, pero quizás podría pedirte un pequeño favor más.'","Halmur Modelapiedra, descendiente del Halmur original, hijo de Vithurr, ha sido encargado de custodiar el cofre que buscas hasta que todo su contenido sea devuelto.","'El cofre es tuyo, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Mi juramento ha sido cumplido. Ahora soy libre. ¡Libre para ir donde quiera!'","'No has recuperado el lingote robado, ${RACE} sin fe. Mantengo mi vigilancia.'","'¿Has encontrado ya el otro cofre?'","Encuentra a Hjortur Duramano","Cofre enano antiguo reunido","Lleva el lingote de oro enano robado a Halmur Modelapiedra"},
[12505]={"Henneth Annûn can be found in north-central North Ithilien.\
\
Mablung has asked you to patrol around the borders of Henneth Annûn for possible threats to the refuge.","As the last remaining refuge of the Rangers of Ithilien, the secrecy of Henneth Annûn has never been more critical to the continued presence of the Rangers in North Ithilien.","'Our enemies have come closer to Henneth Annûn each day, and unless we act to keep them from it, we shall be discovered before long.\
\
'There are many ways for our foes to approach Henneth Annûn, but thankfully, very few through which they could enter. I would have you scout the far reaches of Ithilien surrounding Henneth Annûn for any sign of our foes.\
\
'Their whereabouts in Ithilien are mostly known to us, but they move deeper into the woods with each passing hour and we cannot chance them drawing too close, especially after Rhadrog's encounter with that troll...\
\
'With our other refuges fallen, any task that draws us into Ithilien risks leading our foes back to the refuge. Go swiftly, and take care that you are not followed.\
\
'I shall await a report upon your return.'","Talk to Mablung","Patrol the lands around Henneth Annûn for threats (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Mablung can be found in Henneth Annûn.\
\
You have scouted the lands surrounding Henneth Annûn and should now report back to Mablung.","A Ranger stumbles out of the bush!","Arrows of Ranger make protrude from the flesh of this fallen Orc...","Only the calls of nearby birds break the silence at the Forbidden Pool...","The Enemy's forces may have recently passed through this location, but none remain...","'I am relieved that our foes have not encroached any more closely, but I do not trust that we are free of them. They will come again, and we must be ready for them.\
\
'Dornach means well, but I shall speak to him about using more caution while scouting. Even the slightest rustle can expose our position, and to be exposed means to be slain.\
\
'Thank you, ${PLAYER}.'","The lowlands to the west of Henneth Annûn are still, but your foes have passed through recently...","The Last Refuge","The roadway south of Henneth Annûn is clear of foes..."},
[12506]={"'¡Fue un buen combate, ${PLAYER}! ¡Un ejercicio así no se presenta todos los días!'","'Greetings, ${PLAYER}. A glorious battle awaits us!\
\
'Are you and your allies ready? My father has given me the Key-stone, so I am prepared. Let us go now into the Mountains to defeat Skorgrím and his Dourhands!'","'Speak to Gimli when your allies are ready, and he will lead you to the dwarf-keep.'","The Last Refuge -- Redux","'I have a dangerous task for you and your companions. The Dwarf Glóin has come into possession of a special key which will allow access to a passage that leads into the fortress of Skorgrím Dourhand.\
\
'Glóin has bidden me send him a group of warriors who -- led by his son Gimli, who knows the secret ways of that place -- will put an end to Skorgrím's treachery once and for all.\
\
'Seek out Gimli in one of the guest rooms on the southern slope of the Vale of Imladris when you have gathered your companions and are prepared to embark.'","Speak to Gimli","Handarod has asked you to gather some allies and seek out the Dwarf Gimli. Gimli will accompany you to the dwarf-keep where the Nazgûl and Skorgrím may be hiding. Gimli is staying in one of the guest rooms along the road that winds up the southern slope of the Vale of Imladris.","Glóin is at his camp in the Misty Mountains, north of Rivendell.\
\
The Nazgûl left the dwarf-keep, commanding Skorgrím to slay you. Fortunately, you were able to defeat Skorgrím, but a fell spirit emerged from his corpse and cursed the Longbeards before vanishing. You should tell Glóin all that has transpired.","'You bring tidings both joyous and dark, ${PLAYER}. The Dourhands are done! They will never hope to threaten the Longbeards again.\
\
'While the news of the spirit that was driven from Skorgrím is unsettling, it is not as disturbing as the news of the Nazgûl's escape. What is worse, you tell me that he spoke of bringing Men to Helegrod. What he seeks in that old dwarf-hall is a mystery to me.\
\
'Unfortunately, there is more that must be done if Rivendell is to be secured. Know, though, that I will give you whatever help I can.'","Habla con Glóin","'You have done the Longbeards a great service, my friend! The line of Durin is at your service!'","'Our battke with the Dourhands was glorious!'","Handarod told you of the trials of the dwarves at Glóin's camp in the Misty Mountains and of the plans to finally assault the ancient dwarf-hold of Gabilazan"},
[12508]={"Teodoro Tojo está en la Posada Abandonada.\
\
Has encontrado el tesoro que Teodoro Tojo no pudo encontrar, pero solo era un pergamino con un mensaje críptico. Deberías llevárselo con la triste noticia de que no había ningún tesoro.","Teodoro Tojo está en la Posada Abandonada.\
\
Bingo quiere que sepas si Teodoro Tojo, autoproclamado maestro buscador de tesoros, le enseñaría la profesión.","'¿Teodoro es un maestro buscador de tesoros? Eso suena muy emocionante, y sería un capítulo muy interesante en el relato de mis aventuras.\
\
'${PLAYER}, ¡he tenido una gran idea! ¿Le preguntarías a Teodoro si me entrenaría para ser un buscador de tesoros? Por lo que he visto mi manuscrito trata mayormente sobre pasar tiempo en tabernas, ¡y convertirme en un cazatesoros nos transportará a las tierras salvajes!\
\
'Será una lectura más interesante, ¡eso seguro! ¿Podrías pedírselo, por favor?'","'¿Qué? ¿Dices que has resuelto el acertijo y resuelto el tesoro? ¡No me lo creo!'\
\
Le dices a Teodoro que, aunque va a decepcionarle, no había un tesoro como tal, y que la caja fuerte contenía solo un pergamino con un crítico mensaje en él.\
\
'¿Decepcionarme? ¡No estoy para nada decepcionado? ¿Ves lo que esto significa? Alguien encontró el tesoro antes, ¡y lo reemplazó con este mensaje! ¡Alguien que ha vencido al maestro buscador de tesoros en su propio juego! ¡Se acabó la jubilación, ${PLAYER}! ¡Tengo un tesoro que encontrar!'","Teodoro te entrega un pequeño pergamino con un acertijo en él.","'Sí, soy el gran Teodoro Tojo, maestro buscador de tesoros y vagabundo de las tierras salvajes. Si hay tesoro que encontrar en lugares ocultos de este mundo, ya he estado allí y los he encontrado. Mis hazañas son extensas y bien documentadas, y mis virtudes igual de bien conocidas. Soy tan prominente en este campo que solo me queda una cosa que hacer: jubilarme.'","Encuentra la caja fuerte oculta que Teodoro no puedo encontrar, en algún lugar de las Tierras Solitarias","'Teodoro dice ser un maestro buscador de tesoros a todo el mundo que se pare a escucharle. Tristemente, parece que soy yo en este momento.\
\
'Cualquiera puede proclamar ser un gran buscador de tesoros. De hecho, ¡cualquiera puede hacer la parte de la búsqueda! ¡Es encontrarlo lo que diferencia a aquellos que han conseguido logros reales de los impostores!'","'¿Puedo ver el acertijo?'\
\
Le muestra a Bingo el acertijo y cierra los ojos, absorto en sus pensamientos.\
\
'¡Este es uno difícil, ${PLAYER}! Quizá debas estudiar el acertijo algo más para ver si describe algo más específico.'","Habla con Teodoro Tojo en la Posada Abandonada","'El acertijo parece describir algunas cosas que podrían ser significativas. Suena como si hubiera una cascada cerca, y la última línea me hace pensar en árboles caídos.\
\
'Envuelto en la sombra del alba' suena como si se describiera una dirección o una hora del día. ¿Dónde hay sombra por la mañana pero no por la tarde?\
\
'No me parece muy difícil, ¡pero me deleita que Teodoro se haya quedado bloqueado con este acertijo!'","'¿Has encontrado el tesoro que Teodoro no puedo encontrar? ¡Increíble! ¡Quizá debería pedirte que me des algunas lecciones sobre buscar tesoros, ${PLAYER}!'","'El pergamino que te di es aparentemente una pista a un tesoro que se encuentra en las Tierras Solitarias, uno que nunca encontré. Si entre los dos podéis resolver este acertijo y encontráis el tesoro, quizá sea capaz de enseñaros algo después de todo. ¡Buena suerte, y adiós!'","Teodoro recibe el mensaje críptico de tus manos y lo examina sin poder ocultar su emoción","Teodoro te ha dado un pergamino con un acertijo escrito en él, aparentemente una pista sobre la localización de un tesoro en las Tierras Solitarias. El pergamino dice:\
\
Un torrente bajo la sombra de la mañana fluía,\
mientras desde lo alto lo observaba el vigía.\
La ardilla roja trepó desafiante aquel umbral,\
pero el Tiempo todo lo abate, pues nada es inmortal.'","Bingo ha venido a las Tierras Solitarias en busca de aventuras, y la gente de la Posada Abandonada seguro que se las proporcionan.","Habla con Bingo en la Posada Abandonada","Teodoro Tojo y Haley Pradodulce han atraído la atención de Bingo en la Posada Abandonada, y quiere saber más sobre ellos.","'¡Esta es una clientela muy silenciosa, muy diferente de la del Poney Pisador! Milo era un tipo amigable, y espero que no se haya molestado por nuestra apresurada partida, pero es importante no disfrutar demasiado tiempo de las comodidades o el viaje se verá comprometido!\
\
'Dije que este era un lugar oscuro y sombrío, pero mira esos dos de la esquina. Parecen individuos coloridos, y no parecen encajar con el resto de la parroquia. Veamos qué los tiene tan alterados, ¿de acuerdo?'","El último tesoro","'¡Hola! ¿Puedo ayudarte? A menos que... sí, debes haber oído mi nombre y deseas saber más sobre mis hazañas, ¿no es así? ¡Siempre es un placer hablar con admiradores! Justo estaba hablándole a Haley aquí presente sobre mis grandes hallazgos, y estaba embelesada mientras escuchaba, ¡como seguro te hubiera pasado a ti!'\
\
Un rápido vistazo a Haley Pradodulce prueba que seguramente ese no era el caso.\
\
'Sí, soy el gran Teodoro Tojo, maestro buscador de tesoros y vagabundo de las tierras salvajes. Si hay tesoro que encontrar en lugares ocultos de este mundo, ya he estado allí y los he encontrado. Mis hazañas son extensas y bien documentadas, y mis virtudes igual de bien conocidas. Soy tan prominente en este campo que solo me queda una cosa que hacer: jubilarme.'","Habla con Haley Pradodulce en la Posada Abandonada","'Tu amigo hobbit debería mejor pedirle a Teodoro que lo entrene para convertirse en un Fanfarrón, Pomposo y Cargante, en mi opinión.'","'¿Qué dices? ¿Tu amigo hobbit quiere convertirse en un buscador de tesoros? Me encantaría enseñarle, ¡pero por degracia no es algo que pueda enseñarse tan fácilmente! Si no tiene disposición natural para estas aventuras, se resistirá a cualquier tipo de entrenamiento que pueda brindarle. Además, estoy a punto de jubilarme, y pretendo pasar el tiempo disfrutando con Haley aquí presente las historias de mi interesante y ajetreada vida. ¡Así que apreciaría que se permitiera hacer eso!'\
\
Teodoro piensa durante un momento, y entona una disculpa.\
\
'No pretendía ser tan brusco. Ten, un acertijo. Aparentemente es una pista a un tesoro que se encuentra en las Tierras Solitarias, uno que nunca encontré. Si entre los dos podéis resolver este acertijo y encontráis el tesoro, quizá sea capaz de enseñaros algo después de todo. ¡Buena suerte, y adiós!'","La caja fuerte está vacía salvo por un solo pergamino que contiene frases crípticas","'¿Le preguntarías a Teodoro si me entrenaría para ser un cazatesoros? Por lo que he visto mi manuscrito trata mayormente sobre pasar tiempo en tabernas, ¡y convertirme en un cazatesoros nos transportará a las tierras salvajes!\
\
'Será una lectura más interesante, ¡eso seguro! ¿Podrías pedírselo, por favor?'","Bingo está en la Posada Abandonada, en las Tierras Solitarias.","'Has vencido a Teodoro en su propio juego, ${PLAYER}! ¡No puedo agradecértelo lo suficiente! Quizá ahora dejará de comerme la oreja sobre la maestría que cree tener como buscador de tesoros.'","Lleva el mensaje críptico a Teodoro Tojo en la Posada Abandonada","'Dices que no había tesoro en esa caja fuerte, ${PLAYER}, pero creo que no tienes razón en ese punto. Creo que le has dado a Teodoro el mejor tesoro de todos: ¡una razón para seguir! Ahora está emocionado con su profesión de nuevo, y no tiene que pasar los días reviviendo las aventuras de su juventud.... ¡puede vivir nuevas aventuras! Quizás su destino se entrelace con el nuestro durante un tiempo. ¡Después de todo, hay un tesoro ahí fuera!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>La semana que viene 'Un profundo valle' (Nivel recomendado: 28)</rgb>","'Dije que este era un lugar oscuro y sombrío, pero mira esos dos de la esquina. Parecen individuos coloridos, y no parecen encajar con el resto de la parroquia. Veamos qué los tiene tan alterados, ¿de acuerdo?'","'Alguien encontró el tesoro antes, ¡y lo reemplazó con este mensaje! ¡Alguien que ha vencido al maestro buscador de tesoros en su propio juego! ¡Se acabó la jubilación, ${PLAYER}! ¡Tengo un tesoro que encontrar!'","Bingo Boffin está en la Posada Abandonada."},
[12509]={"The Last Vestiges","Defeated enemies at the Gostannon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'It seems that I was hasty in my judgement, ${PLAYER}. It will take more than a single assault to drive the Orcs out for good.'","Talk to Rongal atop Amon Angened","'The road to the Gostannon lies to the north of here, ${PLAYER}. The Enemy encamped there is not strong...I believe you could destroy them all in one assault.'","The road to the Gostannon lies to the north of Amon Angeled, leading eastwards.\
\
Rongal has asked you to utterly destroy the Enemy at the Gostannon.","'${PLAYER}, if you are journeying again to the Gostannon, you may be able to effect a greater victory against the Enemy than merely frightening them as Dannaswen would have you do.\
\
'I suggest you enter the camp and wipe the last vestiges of the Enemy from the Gostannon. Our passage would then be assured for the duration of this expedition.\
\
'Return to me when you have completed your task.'","The Elves of the Golden Host are concerned with the continuing presence of Orcs in the Mirk-eaves and in procuring supplies for the Malledhrim in the east.","Rongal is at the Elf-waypost atop Amon Angened, south of the Gostannon.\
\
While the Enemy encamped at the Gostannon is greatly weakened, they are still stronger than Rongal surmised. You should return to Rongal with the tidings.","Defeat enemies at the Gostannon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12511]={"Brombard Colazorro está en la Casa de los Mathoms en Cavada Grande, al oeste de Alforzaburgo.\
\
Adelard Tuk te ha pedido que vayas a la Casa de los Mathoms en Cavada Grande y le pidas al guardián Colazorro el cohete que envió allí.","Los últimos fuegos artificiales","'Buenos días. ¿Así que Adelard quiere recuperar el cohete que envió aquí?\
\
'Bueno, sí lo tengo. De hecho, no he tenido la oportunidad de hacer nada con él todavía. Un momento, por favor...\
\
'¡Ah, aquí lo tienes! Ten cuidado... aunque es bastante viejo, apostaría a que, como fue hecho por Gandalf el Gris, ¡sigue siendo potente!'","El escenario de Methel está en el lado sur de la carretera que sale de Delagua hacia el oeste.\
\
Adelard Tuk te ha pedido que lances el cohete desde el escenario de Methel en Delagua, con la esperanza de que la vista de este último cohete apacigüe al fantasma del Viejo Tuk.","'No creo que Adelard haya enviado nada más a la Casa de los Mathoms recientemente, aparte de este cohete. En todo caso, nada de importancia.\
\
'Si busca otro objeto, ¡hágamelo saber!'","Subes al escenario de Methel","Al ordenar su biblioteca, Adelard Tuk se topó con un cohete de la última fiesta del Solsticio de verano del Viejo Tuk. Lo envió a la Casa de los Mathoms en Cavada Grande, pero cree que eso podría haber molestado al fantasma del Viejo Tuk.","'¡Maravilloso, has recuperado el cohete de la Casa de los Mathoms! Ahora, por favor, ve al escenario de Methel en Delagua y lánzalo.\
\
'Apuesto a que al ver eso, el fantasma del Viejo Tuk se calmará... ¡Y dejará mi biblioteca en paz!'","'Oh, puedo notar por el olor de tu ropa que has lanzado el cohete. ¡Fantástico!\
\
'Esto seguramente apaciguará al fantasma del Viejo Tuk. Voy a ir a comprobarlo a la biblioteca ahora mismo. Tengo un buen presentimiento, estoy seguro de que ha apaciguado a su fantasma.'","Has lanzado el último de los cohetes.","'¡El fantasma sigue en mi biblioteca! ¿Cuándo me dejará en paz? Verá, todo esto empezó cuando estaba ordenando un poco por allí, enviando un par de cosas a la Casa de los Mathoms, y cosas así...\
\
'Di con un viejo cohete de la última fiesta del Solsticio de verano del Viejo Tuk. Gandalf el Gris y él eran grandes amigos, y Gandalf siempre traía los fuegos artificiales más espléndidos. ¿Quizá molesté al fantasma del Viejo Tuk al enviar ese cohete a la Casa de los Mathoms? ¡Puede que quiera verlo lanzado!\
\
'Si pudiéramos recuperar el cohete y lanzarlo, eso podría apaciguar a su fantasma. ¿Podrías hablar con el guardián Brombard Colazorro en Cavada Grande para recuperarlo? La Casa de los Mathoms está en una colina, al noroeste del centro de Cavada Grande. Una vez que tengas los petardos, ¿podrías lanzarlos desde el escenario de Methel en Delagua?'","Lanza el cohete","'Necesitas viajar a Cavada Grande, a la Casa de los Mathoms, para recuperar el cohete que envié allí. ¡Creo que eso es lo que ha molestado al fantasma del Viejo Tuk!\
\
'Si puedes conseguir ese cohete y lanzarlo desde el escenario de Methel en Delagua, eso podría apaciguar al fantasma.'","Encuentra el escenario de Methel en Delagua","Adelard Tuk se encuentra en los Grandes Smials de Alforzaburgo.\
\
Debes volver con Adelard Tuk y hacerle saber que has hecho lo que te pidió."},
[12512]={"Aragorn está en uno de los cuartos de invitados de la Casa de Elrond en Rivendel.\
\
Calenglad te ha dado el Silithar para que se lo lleves a Aragorn. Su luz será usada para reforjar la espada que fue quebrada.","Has recuperado el último de los Silithair, diamantes brillantes fabricados por los elfos de la casa de Feänor en los días antiguos. Debe ser utilizado para reforjar la hoja que fue quebrada.","'Me apena verte marchar, ${PLAYER}, ¡pero debes hacerlo! ¡Aragorn espera el Silithar!'","Lleva el Silithar a Aragorn en Rivendel","'Reclamando el último de los Silithair, has conseguido lo que Aragorn te envió a hacer aquí, ${PLAYER}, y por el camino nos has ayudado en gran medida a todos los que vivimos en las orillas del lago Nenuial. Me apena verte marchar.\
\
'¡Pero debes hacerlo, para que Narsil sea reforjada! ¡Vuelve a Rivendel lo antes posible, lejos hacia el este, y entrega el Silithar a Aragorn! ¡Ha llegado la hora por fin de que la hoja que se quebró sea reforjada!'","El último de los Silithair","'Vuelves de la espesura, ${PLAYER}, ¡y mi corazón se regocija al verte! ¡A menos que mis ojos me engañan, has superado los desafíos de Gwindeth y vuelves portando el último de los Silithair!'","'El hijo de Arathorn ha aprendido mucho desde que me encontré con él hace muchos años. Se convertirá en un gran líder, si las batallas que vengan no le arrebatan la vida antes.\
\
'Entrégale el Silithar, pues pertenece a su linaje, y ha pasado mi prueba.'","'Necesitamos el Silithar, ${PLAYER}. Sin su luz, la espada que forjemos con los fragmentos de Narsil nunca será de tanta valía como su predecesora.'"},
[12513]={"'Quiero arreglar las cosas. Veamos si los montaraces nos ayudan una vez más.'","Ravaedron se encuentra fuera de la Cabaña del Helechal.","'He tenido otra idea, ${PLAYER}, y necesito tu ayuda.'","Habla con Maddoc Astaciervo dentro de la Cabaña del Helechal","'Los Astaciervo te han invitado a entrar para ver dónde colocarán el cuadro, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}. Y ahora me despido.'","La amistad duradera","Entra en la Cabaña del Helechal y mira dónde se expondrá el cuadro","El segundo cuadro de Ravaedron cuelga con orgullo en la Cabaña del Helechal","'Te doy las gracias una vez más, , por ayudarme a aprender lo que podría haber descubierto hace mucho tiempo: al igual que la felicidad es parte del mundo, también lo es la tristeza. Intentar evitarla puede retrasar el dolor, pero no lo destruye. Las lágrimas no deberían ser motivo de vergüenza.\
\
'Viajaré a los Puertos Grises con mi propia tristeza, y la llevaré a través del Mar. Pero también llevaré mis recuerdos de los tiempos felices. No sopesaré unos con otros, sino que cargaré con ambos. Y en los años venideros, tal vez Maddoc, Glenys y el joven Bran contemplen este segundo cuadro, y habrá días en los que deseen llorar, y días en los que les haga sonreír. Puede que haya sido de las últimas amistades que he forjado en esta Tierra Media, ${PLAYER}, pero será duradera. ¡Y también lo será la mía contigo!'\
\
Ravaedron ríe, un sonido más alegre y satisfecho del que le habías oído hasta ahora al elfo.\
\
'Los Astaciervo te han invitado a entrar para ver dónde colocarán el cuadro, ${PLAYER:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}. Y ahora me despido.'","Habla con Ravaedron y ayuda al apenado artista a intentar arreglar las cosas","Habla con Ravaedron fuera de la Cabaña del Helechal","'Siempre creí que los elfos debían ser más sabios que los demás, , ¡pero entonces mi mujer y yo conocimos a Ravaedron! Le tenemos mucho aprecio y valoramos el tiempo que hemos pasado con él, ¡pero te digo de verdad que a veces podía ser más exasperante de lo que era nuestro Bran de bebé!\
\
'Supongo que la gente es complicada, y en eso al menos los elfos son iguales que el resto de nosotros. Gracias por ayudarnos a los tres, ${PLAYER}. Siempre serás ${PLAYER:bienvenido[m]|bienvenida[f]} en la Cabaña del Helechal.'","Maddoc Astaciervo te ha invitado a entrar para ver dónde se expondrá el nuevo cuadro de Ravaedron.","Maddoc Astaciervo desea hablar contigo dentro de su cabaña.","Ravaedron ha tenido otra idea, y una vez más necesita tu ayuda.","Decidido a arreglar las cosas, Ravaedron necesita tu ayuda una vez más."},
[12514]={"'Greetings traveller, do you have a moment? I am in dire need of help.\
\
'My dear husband, Tirneldir, set out to tend to his traps along the shore, but has not yet returned. I am worried something has happened to him with all these Corsairs about as he is never too careful when he should be.\
\
'It may all be for nothing... and mayhap he stopped at \\qThe Brew and Bounty\\q and lost track of the day... but please go and check for me, you can find the tavern if you take the northern lift down and go up the stairs behind it. Send him back home when you find him. You can mark him by his brown hair and azure tunic he wears.'","Lindil needs your help finding her missing spouse.","The Late Fisherman","You do not see Tirneldir within \\qThe Brew and Bounty\\q in Lond Cirion. The guard sitting at the table may know where he went.","Search for Lindil's spouse in \\qThe Brew and Bounty\\q near the docks","You don't see Tirneldir. The guard nearby may have information","Lindil has asked you to check \\qThe Brew and Bounty\\q for her spouse, Tirneldir, in lower Lond Cirion near the northern lift.","'Eh? What can I do for you, adventurer?'\
\
You tell them that you are looking for Tirneldir.\
\
'Ah, Tirneldir, you say? Afford me a moment to gather my thoughts.'"},
[12515]={"The Lay of the Dry Land","Mizâdi is ready to meet with her allies and plan her strategy for Idagâl.\
\
You should speak to Mizâdi at her camp near the border of An Shêru to begin the meeting.","Complete 'Instance: The Lay of the Dry Land'","Talk to Mizâdi","'Welcome, friend. We come to this arid place for one reason: to make a stand against Ordâkh. We know that Bârshud has come this way, likely to regroup with his Ordâkhai masters. Their stronghold must be here, and I aim to find a way to take it from them.\
\
'Our group is small for now, only my most trusted allies. The rest of my army will follow when we are ready. Now, we must discuss what the scouts have found in Idagâl, and prepare our strategy.'\
\
You ask about the newcomer in the left tent. She appears to be a scholar from Zajâna. Mizâdi stifles a sigh.\
\
'Ah, yes. Meet Sorkamâl, my new diplomat. Numûru has convinced me we need one after that... misunderstanding in Zajâna. I am sure she will prove herself a valuable member of our cause.\
\
'Now, let us gather the others.'","Mizâdi Shâra-ingari has come to Idagâl with a small force, seeking to confront her rival, Bârshud, and to find a way to push the Ordâkhai from their stronghold in Mûr Ghala.","Mizâdi is ready to put her plan into motion.\
\
You should speak to Mizâdi at her camp near the border of An Shêru to begin the meeting.","'Are you ready to hear the report of our scouts?'","'There is much to consider, and much to do. The path forward will not be easy. I hope I can count on you to walk it with me, friend.'"},
[12516]={"'The Wargs of the Ashenslades follow a pack-leader by the name of Morglok, who drives them to harry our forces. If Morglok were to be defeated, the Ashenslades may become safe enough for our scouts to explore further.\
\
'I charge you with hunting down this Morglok and bringing his reign of the pack to an end. He will likely be found among the pack at Naur-hoit, to the south of here.\
\
'When you have defeated Morglok, return to me with your tale.'","Morglok is at Naur-hoit, south of Mithechad.\
\
Perindúr has asked you to seek out and defeat the Warg-packleader Morglok.","Talk to Perindúr at Mithechad","The Wargs of Naur-hoit are led by a great pack-leader called Morglok. The Elves of the Golden Host believe that his defeat may be the key to driving forth the Wargs from the ruins.","'Seek out Morglok and bring his reign as leader of the pack to an end. He will likely be found among the Wargs at Naur-hoit, to the south of here.'","The Leader of the Pack","Defeated Morglok the Warg-packleader","Perindúr is at Mithechad, north of Naur-hoit.\
\
You should return at once to Perindúr and let him know that Morglok has been defeated.","Defeat Morglok the Warg-packleader","'By defeating Morglok, you have made our mission in the Ashenslades easier.\
\
'While there may be call to thin the numbers of the Wargs patrolling the area, you have struck a great blow to the forces of Dol Guldur here in the Ashenslades.'"},
[12517]={"Maelgun Garrarroja ha jurado responder con la muerte a cualquiera que toque un desafío en el cuerno que dejó al oeste de la puerta de las Ruinas de la Guardia del Sur.","Habla con el Maestro Buencorazón al sureste de las Ruinas de la Guardia del Sur","'El líder de los asaltantes del Camino Verde es un hombre llamado Maelgun Garrarroja, y es un tipo muy malo. Está tan seguro de su liderazgo que ha dejado un cuerno sobre una mampostería al oeste de la entrada a las Ruinas de la Guardia del Sur, ¡y afirma que permitirá que cualquiera lo desafíe por el liderazgo de su banda de bandidos! Ahora bien, algunos han intentado esto en el pasado, y los ha matado a todos... pero nunca ha respondido a un desafío de alguien como tú, ¿verdad?\
\
'¡Que este sea mi regalo de despedida para esta tierra! ¡Juntos podemos acabar con la amenaza de los bandidos en el Camino Verde!'","Habla con Melona junto al Camino Verde","El Maestro Buencorazón está al sureste de la entrada a las Ruinas de la Guardia del Sur.","'No... ¿qué estás haciendo aquí?'","Desafía a Maelgun Garrarroja a la batalla con el cuerno al oeste de la puerta de las Ruinas de la Guardia del Sur, y derrótalo","El Maestro Buencorazón, ciudadano preocupado, ha descubierto que el líder de los bandidos acepta desafíos a su liderazgo.","'¡Mis preparativos están casi completos, y estoy casi listo para seguir adelante! Pero han llegado a mis oídos noticias de algo extraordinario. He descubierto una forma en la que podría devolver a esta tierra algo de gran valor. ¡Soy caritativo ante todo, y mi generosidad no conoce límites! ¿Acaso no te recompensé con más monedas de las que merecías por el trabajo que hiciste para mí antes? Quiero decir, después de todo: te habrías enfrentado a esos bandidos incluso sin recompensa, ¿no es así? ¡Pero endulcé el trato con algunas monedas, y así todos ganan!\
\
'Parece que el líder de los asaltantes del Camino Verde es un hombre llamado Maelgun Garrarroja, y es un tipo muy malo. Está tan seguro de su liderazgo que ha dejado un cuerno sobre una mampostería al oeste de la entrada a las Ruinas de la Guardia del Sur, ¡y afirma que permitirá que cualquiera lo desafíe por el liderazgo de su banda de bandidos! Ahora bien, algunos han intentado esto en el pasado, y los ha matado a todos... pero nunca ha respondido a un desafío de alguien como tú, ¿verdad?\
\
'¡Que este sea mi regalo de despedida para esta tierra! ¡Juntos podemos acabar con la amenaza de los bandidos en el Camino Verde!'","La cazarrecompensas Melona ha subido por el Camino Verde, y ahora se encuentra al sureste de las Ruinas de la Guardia del Sur.","Qué extraño. El Maestro Buencorazón no está","El Líder de los asaltantes","'No... ¿qué estás haciendo aquí?'\
\
Melona, la cazarrecompensas, te mira consternada. Le dices que el Maestro Buencorazón y tú han acabado con Maelgun Garrarroja, líder de los bandidos que bloquean el Camino Verde. Ella sacude la cabeza con incredulidad.\
\
'¿Estoy condenada a sufrir tan mala fortuna? ¿Cuántas recompensas estoy maldita a perder por tu interferencia? ¿\\qMaestro Buencorazón\\q? ¿Te refieres a Geralt Buenaflor, rufián conocido?'\
\
Le dices a Melona que Geralt es un nombre muy común, que tienen muchas personas en el sur, y que seguramente es una coincidencia. Ella sacude la cabeza.\
\
'He estado cazando a Geralt y Eilian Buenaflor durante varios días, pero gracias a la herida que sufrí en la Pradera de Juncos siempre he estado un paso atrás. Mientras yo los cazaba, ellos cazaban sus propios objetivos: los hermanos Garrarroja, tres poderosos bandidos que juntos dirigían gran parte de la villanía presente en estas tierras. Ahora que los tres Garrarroja ya no existen, los Buenaflor son libres de ejecutar el siguiente paso de su plan: ¡tomar el control! No desean liberar estas tierras del control de los bandidos... ¡marido y mujer desean consolidarlo bajo su propio liderazgo!'\
\
Le dices a Melona que has conocido tanto a Eilian como a Geralt, y que estarías dispuesto a ayudarla a localizarlos.\
\
'¡No! Quiero decir... no, gracias, ${PLAYER}. Es solo que creo que podrías traer mala suerte. Solo he tenido mala fortuna desde que te topaste conmigo en la Pradera de Juncos, y temo que pueda empeorar. Lo entiendes. ¡De hecho, te recompensaré por mantenerte alejado! ¿Qué te parece?'","Maelgun Garrarroja derrotado"},
[12518]={"La Liga del Hacha necesita ayuda con sus actividades en el Bosque Salvaje de la Tierra de Bree.","Completa misiones en el Bosque Salvaje (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Completa misiones sin facción en el Bosque Salvaje para ayudar a la Liga del Hacha.","La Liga del Hacha (Diaria)","'El éxito de la Liga del Hacha depende de cada uno de sus miembros, y no podemos permitirnos el lujo de estar mal preparados cuando el Bosque Salvaje es nuestra única esperanza de una vida mejor.\
\
'Ayuda a la Liga del Hacha a superar las adversidades y me encargaré de que tus esfuerzos sean recompensados.'","Misiones completadas en el Bosque Salvaje (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Completado","Has ayudado a la Liga del Hacha en sus esfuerzos por todo el Bosque Salvaje de la Tierra de Bree. Todos los miembros de la Liga te agradecen tu ayuda.","Has ayudado a la Liga del Hacha"},
[12519]={"Edhan está justo fuera de la puerta trasera de la Posada de la Encrucijada.","Las cajas que estaban destinadas a la Posada de la Encrucijada fueron dejadas a lo largo del camino del este que sale de Herne, y Edhan te pidió que las llevaras al almacén dentro de la posada.","Edhan está exhausto por el trabajo que ya ha realizado, y se pregunta si le ayudarás con el resto.","'Muchas gracias por tu ayuda, {amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. No tengo mucho que ofrecerte, pero espero que esta recompensa te sea útil.'","'¡Una caja más, amigo! Realmente aprecio esto.'","Entregas la caja. Una menos, falta una","Recoge la caja restante junto al camino del este que sale de Herne","Habla con Edhan fuera de la Posada de la Encrucijada","'Estoy exhausto, amigo. Trabajo para Maddoc en la Posada de la Encrucijada, y mi trabajo es llevar cajas y suministros a la posada cada vez que son entregados. ¡Pero el conductor del carromato de las Tierras de Bree acaba de partir, y se negó a dejar las cajas más cerca que las afueras de Herne! Dijo que hay una mala sensación sobre el pueblo hoy, ¡y que no quería quedarse aquí más tiempo del estrictamente necesario!\
\
'¡Él hizo el mínimo esfuerzo, pero yo ya he hecho más de lo que debía! ¿Crees que podrías traer las dos últimas cajas al interior de la Posada de la Encrucijada y depositarlas en el almacén con la chimenea? Realmente apreciaría poder descansar mis brazos un momento, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}, y no lo olvidaría.\
\
'Las dos últimas cajas están justo donde el camino del este sale de Herne.'","Depositas la caja. ¡Esa era la última!","El mínimo esfuerzo","'¿Crees que podrías traer las dos últimas cajas al interior de la Posada de la Encrucijada y depositarlas en el almacén con la chimenea? Realmente apreciaría poder descansar mis brazos un momento, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}, y no lo olvidaría.\
\
'Las dos últimas cajas están justo donde el camino del este sale de Herne.'","Recoge una de las cajas junto al camino del este que sale de Herne"},
[12520]={"Talk to Andras in Avardin","The Ledger","Gather the items on the fourth page of the ledger","Andras is at Avardin, south-east of Andras' homestead.\
\
Andras is awaiting you and everything that you have collected from his homestead.","Mabon has marked up the ledger that you brought with notes about what is important and may still be found around the homestead.","'I have marked my dad's ledger with what I remember seeing over the last few days. I have also marked where you should be able to find the various things. Please gather them up and take them to him in Avardin.\
\
'We will be leaving here soon, and I will meet you there with him once everything is ready. Thank you for all that you have done for us.'","The items on the ledger may be found throughout Andras' homestead.\
\
The pages of the ledger detail out valuables within the homestead.","Gather the items on the first page of the ledger","Gather the items on the fifth page of the ledger","Gather the items on the second page of the ledger","'My son told me about everything that happened and how you aided him at the homestead. It seems that some old favours I earned were satisfied while you were there.\
\
'I am very grateful to you for keeping my boy safe and bringing these goods to me.'","Gather the items on the third page of the ledger"},
[12526]={"'Lômazar has been truthful with us up to this point, ${PLAYER}. While I have my doubts, it is not impossible that Sauron would have put such thought and effort into collecting many a valuable and powerful relic. You say that you have seen some of these already? Then perhaps we must act sooner than later in preventing The Black Word from finding any more lost trinkets of Sauron.'","Many lesser artifacts can be found scattered across Dor Amarth. Lômazar may have additional information about Dulgabêth's loyal.\
\
You should find any lesser artifacts you can while searching for Dulgabêth's loyal.","Lômazar explains to you all he knows of Dulgabêth's plans.","'I say again, you must give your promise to send me away from these lands. Even rotting in a dungeon until the end of days would be better than endless pain and torture at the hand of the Black Word.'\
\
You give your word that Lômazar will be treated fairly as a prisoner.\
\
'Good. Now listen closely, as I have not the strength nor will to repeat what I am about to say.\
\
'I do not know why only the most important and awe-inspiring bits fell to earth while much of the city remains. Dulgabêth the Black Word, known to you as the Mouth of Sauron, has claimed what still stands of Barad-dûr. He has many followers, myself once included. Now Dulgabêth seeks to rule all of Mordor and take Sauron's place, by use of powerful relics buried within the tower's walls. None will oppose him. His faithful servants are not to be trifled with either. Glúrugoth, the Hole-warden. Sapakár the Cleaver. Krassa-phûrsa, Bringer of Tears. These are all names that strike fear upon mention.\
\
'Do you now possess the knowledge you seek?'","Complete Treasures Forgotten","Complete Edge of The Abyss","You find nothing here","Talk to Lômazar","Thwarted Glúrugoth, the Hole-warden","Talk to Ingold","Thwarted Sapakár the Cleaver","Complete The Wrath of Glúrugoth","Found dusty artifacts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Search rubble for lesser artifacts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ingold can be found at the Ruins of Díngarth.\
\
You should speak with Ingold.","'Have you come to take me out from this place of my certain death or have you come to tell me only that my words rung true?'\
\
You explain to Lômazar that he will be taken out of Mordor once the situation in Dor Amarth has improved.\
\
'It seems I may be dwelling in this company for a time then. Be warned, it should be known that some of the relics Dulgabêth pursues are much more powerful than one of your ilk could imagine. You may have thwarted his efforts thus far, but let it be known, hidden objects lie in wait below the fortress of Barad-dûr.'","Lômazar is located at the Ruins of Díngarth.\
\
You should speak with Lômazar.","The Legacy of Barad-dûr","Thwarted Krassa-phûrsa, Bringer of Tears"},
[12527]={"'I am honoured that you could attend, ${PLAYER}. It was a bountiful feast, and I am glad to have shared it with you.\
\
'I do not know where your adventures shall take you next, but I am certain you will be prepared for it.\
\
'Be well in your travels, and know that you are always welcome in the halls of Durin's Folk.'","Talk to King Thorin III","King Thorin III has planned a great celebration for the Dwarves of Durin's Folk.","King Thorin III can be found in the Hall Under the Mountain.\
\
You have attended the celebration of Durin's Folk and should now speak to King Thorin III.","'Even in the face of such loss and devastation in the North, we of Durin's Folk must celebrate. We show gratitude for our families, for our friends, and for what coming joys remain hidden. My father, Dáin, understood this well, and I would honour his memory.\
\
'I sent invitations to all of Durin's Folk, and I hope that the last of our guests are arriving now. One has spent too long away from his kin, and I do hope he sees now that his return is welcomed by all.\
\
'You have served the peoples of the North, shown great bravery in far-off battles, and Gimli, son of Glóin, regards you as a true friend; you have earned a place at my table. Come, ${PLAYER}.'","King Thorin III can be found in the Hall Under the Mountain.\
\
King Thorin III has invited you to a great celebration of Durin's Folk.","'It is time. Come with me, ${PLAYER}!'","The Legacy of Durin's Folk"},
[12528]={"Faltharan is located at the steps to Tol Ciryarani.\
\
You should speak with Faltharan.","Assisted Lorvegil","Assist Siriel","Talk to Faltharan","Assist Celebros","DNT - Not Used","Faltharan listens intently to what his family told you.\
\
'Hmm... I understand. I'm not that surprised by how they all feel. There is much I would love to do before departing the city, but we do not have the time for everything.\
\
'I will be attending to the preparations. If my family has any tasks for you, then I would ask that you offer your assistance.'","Assist Lorvegil","Assisted Siriel","'${PLAYER}, we haven't much time left. The Gondorian Army intends to make its way upriver towards Pelennor. It pains me to say this, but we must abandon the city until the fighting is resolved.\
\
'I intend to send the surviving refugees to Dol Amroth, along with my family. I know that they will not like the news, but I would ask that you deliver it to them. Your actions have earned my trust, and I'm sure theirs as well.'","Faltharan is concerned with how his family feels about recent events, as well as their thoughts on the location of Lord Sirgon.","Assisted Celebros","The Legacy of Sirgon","Faltharan's family is located in the market east of Tol Ciryarani.\
\
You should assist Faltharan's kin with their tasks."},
[12529]={"Meregyth stands near the Mead Hall of Beaconwatch.\
\
You should speak with Meregyth and let her know what you thought of the tale of King Folca the Hunter and his battle with the Boar of Everholt.","Meregyth stands near the Mead Hall of Beaconwatch.\
\
Meregyth has offered to tell you the story of King Folca and his battle with the Great Boar of Everholt.","Meregyth is reminded by the Boar-tribe Orcs of the story of King Folca and his battle with the Boar of Everholt.","'Let me tell you the story, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo quest and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>","'Do you know, I never made the connexion until now? These Orcs must be the descendants of the White Mountain Orcs from King Folca's time. It appears that they took on the appearance of the boars, who were ultimately responsible for Folca's demise.\
\
'As if the situation were not already dire, these Orcs do not wish simply to attack, they seek vengeance.\
\
'We must attempt to speak with Cútha again. He must know of this.'","The Legend of Folca","Talk to Meregyth","'I cannot help but think back on a story that has been passed down to every child of the Mark: The Legend of King Folca the Hunter.\
\
'King Folca was responsible for driving the Orcs from the White Mountains. He would not allow any Rohirrim to hunt the beasts of the woods until this was achieved.\
\
'After the defeat of the White Mountain Orcs, he took it upon himself to hunt the fabled Boar of Everholt. Would you like to hear the story?'"},
[12530]={"You and Ithurga have confirmed that the replica was likely a misdirect and the real hammer is still out there.","The giant seems to be agitated by something stuck in its eye.","'After thinking about the reports you gathered and putting them together with what I know of this Marâkh, Mother of Tempests, I believe our best guess is an island in the north Jeb Khâtel. It is said to be such a perilous journey that not even the heartiest of freebooters dare travel there.\
\
'Again, I must caution, your life is more important than some old relic. Do not be hasty in this regard.\
\
'Go to the island in Jeb Khâtel. Learn what you can, and retrieve Marâkh. If you cannot do this, escape as quickly as possible. Live to tell the tale.'","Find the island of legend","Talk to Hûrlub the Bellower","'You are small thing. Why do you come here?\
\
'You not afraid? Everyone afraid. All stay away. Hûrlub always alone.\
\
'Crawlies! Crawlies hurt Hûrlub! Hûrlub cannot sleep!\
\
'Many leg ones. Always bully Hûrlub.'\
\
Hûrlub frowns.","The Legend of the Tempest","You have found a long path up a tall peak. The journey will be dangerous.","Climb to the top of the peak","A giant stands before you","Ithurga explained that he has deduced the final location of Marâkh, Mother of Tempests. It is in an island in northern Jeb Khâtel.","There is a long path leading up the peak"},
[12532]={"Talk to Ingold","You find nothing to report to Ingold here","You have fled the battle!","All is quiet here","The Lhingris Threat","Ingold can be found at the Ruins of Díngarth in Dor Amarth.\
\
You should speak with Ingold.","You should defeat the incoming spider swarm!","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not flee from where you stand</rgb>","Scout the location for spiders","You have successfully defeated the spider swarm","'You have successfully fended off a group of spiders descending the Morgai? I am glad you were our first line of defence! The scuttling creatures were no match for you.'","Scouting locations are along the base of the Morgai in Dor Amarth.\
\
You should scout the location.","Ingold has been getting reports that bands of spiders are crossing the Morgai from Lhingris into Dor Amarth. He asks you to patrol the border.","Stand your ground and defeat the spider swarm","You see a swarm of spiders approaching from the Morgai!","'I have heard tales of crawling things in the Morgai. Scuttling, venomous creatures roam through the valley. Some have recently spotted large spiders along the Morgai's ridge. I fear these horrid spiders are becoming bolder as they explore areas near the valley of Lhingris.\
\
'Will you go scout the base of the Morgai here in Dor Amarth in search of any intruders?'"},
[12533]={"Mundgeirr te ha dicho que la calidad que deseas otorgar a tu arma solo puede realizarse en la forja dentro de la Biblioteca de Acero.","Lleva una adamantita infundida a Mundgeirr","'Solo hay un lugar donde se puede forjar una calidad como la que buscas. Antes se conocía como la Biblioteca de Acero. Contiene tomos que detallan muchos de los secretos más finos de la herrería enana y está protegida contra el robo y la destrucción por antiguos encantamientos.\
\
'Sin embargo, desde que la redescubrimos, también ha sido encontrada por los Ghâsh-hai que la han tomado. No puedo estar seguro de lo que pretenden hacer con ella, pero no puede ser nada bueno.\
\
'Si deseas obtener tu calidad, tendrás que liberar la forja; sin embargo, antes de siquiera intentarlo, necesitarás traerme un adamantito infundido, que puede contener la calidad.'","'¡Te debemos mucho por preservar la Biblioteca de Acero! Me estremezco al pensar cuánto del conocimiento de nuestros padres se habría perdido si hubiera sido destruido por los Orcos.'","La Biblioteca de Acero","'¡Ah, has encontrado una Adamantita Infundida! Una vez que lo haya preparado, tendrás que llevarlo a la Biblioteca de Acero.'","¡La Biblioteca de Acero ha sido incendiada!","'¿La Biblioteca sigue intacta? Oh, qué buenas noticias. Es triste que seamos tan pocos, y no puedo enviar a nadie a estudiar los secretos que guarda... lamentablemente, los encantamientos nos impiden sacar cualquier cosa de la Biblioteca, pero al menos está a salvo de los Orcos...'","Mundgeirr se encuentra en el campamento del Mirador de la Gran Excavación, en Moria.\
\
Debes regresar a Mundgeirr para completar la mejora de tu arma.","'Tendrás que traerme una adamantita imbuida para que podamos comenzar.'","Mundgeirr te ha pedido que le traigas una adamantita infundida, con el cual podrá ayudarte a otorgar una calidad a tu arma. Desafortunadamente, no sabe dónde encontrar tal piedra.","'Las noticias se vuelven más sombrías por momentos, ${PLAYER}. Tengo un espía vigilando a los orcos de fuego en la Biblioteca... parece que están trabajando en algún tipo de arte oscuro allí, invocando espíritus de fuego desde las profundidades de Khazad-dûm hacia la Biblioteca. Eso solo puede significar una cosa: ¡tienen la intención de romper los encantamientos que protegen la biblioteca y destruir todo lo que hay dentro!\
\
Debes darte prisa si quieres detenerlos, y asegúrate de no dejar que invoquen demasiados de esos espíritus a la vez, o el encantamiento que protege la biblioteca se romperá y todo estará perdido.\
\
Habla conmigo de nuevo cuando estés ${PLAYER:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario, y no puede ser completada con una Comunidad.</rgb>","Habla con Mundgeirr para viajar a la Biblioteca de Acero","'¿No has sido capaz de potenciar la piedra? Sin una adamantita potenciada, no puedo ayudarte.'","Lleva la adamantita potenciada a Mundgeirr","Mundgeirr se encuentra en el campamento del Mirador de la Gran Excavación, en Moria.\
\
Mundgeirr te ha pedido que busques la Biblioteca de Acero, pero te advierte que una banda de orcos de fuego provenientes de las profundidades de Moria han tomado el control de la biblioteca."},
[12539]={"Lieutenant Gádhmal has been defeated!","Talk to Órug at Drenghól","Defeat Lieutenant Ogarbuk","The Lieutenants of Gorgar","'${PLAYER}, I have received word that Gorgar has bolstered his presence at Bagûd-mekhem.\
\
'It seems three of Gorgar's most trustworthy lieutenants have been sent to oversee his forces and lead a new front against the Gabil'akkâ. It remains unclear if Gorgar is even aware of the alliance between his forces and the small contingent of the Frost-horde gathered within Bagûd-mekhem.\
\
'If there are troubles between them, so be it. Nevertheless, the defeat of his lieutenants is of utmost importance!'","Defeat Lieutenant Gádhmal","Lieutenant Ogarbuk has been defeated!","In an effort to overcome the dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ, Gorgar has sent three of his mightiest lieutenants to oversee his forces at Bagûd-mekhem.","Lieutenants Ogarbuk, Bauzmát, and Gádhmal can be found at Bagûd-mekhem.\
\
After learning of their arrival at Bagûd-mekhem, Órug has asked you to defeat the lieutenants of Gorgar.","'It is done? Good!\
\
'Let that be a lesson to Gorgar and his Orcs!'","Defeat Lieutenant Bauzmát","Órug can be found at Drenghól in the War of Three Peaks.\
\
You have defeated lieutenants Ogarbuk, Bauzmát, and Gádhmal at Bagûd-mekhem. You should report to Órug.","Lieutenant Bauzmát has been defeated!"},
[12540]={"Lleva las ramas adecuadas a Merion en la puerta este de Musgovilla.","Puedes encontrar ramas adecuadas para reparar las defensas del pueblo al noroeste de Musgovilla, en la base de los árboles.","La Vida de un Guardia","'La incursión sobre Musgovilla por parte de esa banda de Uruks ha dejado nuestras defensas en un estado terrible. Si no fuera demasiada molestia, ¿podría pedirte que recojas ramas caídas de la base de los árboles fuera del pueblo? Con ellas podremos remendar los huecos de la empalizada exterior y reemplazar parte de la madera que se quemó durante el ataque.\
\
'Sé que no suena como una tarea muy importante, pero de verdad nos sería de gran ayuda. Con tanta gente buena herida y muerta durante la incursión, Eleri cree que deberíamos centrarnos en las pequeñas cosas sobre las que sí podemos actuar. Supongo que le encuentro sentido.'","Recolectó ramas adecuadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Podrías recoger ramas caídas de la base de los árboles fuera del pueblo? Con ellas podremos remendar los huecos de la empalizada exterior y reemplazar parte de la madera quemada durante el ataque.'","Recoge ramas adecuadas al noroeste de Musgovilla (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Gracias por estas ramas, ${PLAYER}. Me encargaré de utilizarlas para tapar los huecos en nuestras defensas, y quizá algunas de las ramas más grandes puedan usarse para fabricar herramientas; en los últimos tiempos han desaparecido objetos pequeños sin razón aparente, y necesitamos reemplazarlos.\
\
'Así ha sido la vida de un guardia de Musgovilla desde que me reclutaron. Si hay Uruks sueltos en la Ciénaga de los Cisnes, eso podría estar a punto de cambiar.'","Merion, uno de los guardias del pueblo de Musgovilla, intenta ayudar a reparar las defensas de la aldea tras la incursión Uruk.","Merion está esperando junto a la puerta este de Musgovilla."},
[12542]={"The Light and the Shadow Part 1: The Missing Chest","Return to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja with the missing chest","Search for Khôltekh's missing chest in Deshûkh","Speak with the merchant Rathâni in the Sail-haven","'I knew you were up to the task. Come, we have much to discuss.'\
\
Khôltekh takes the chest deftly, quickly handing it off to one of his guards.\
\
'I have a sense for these things. And, as promised, you have a greater role to play in the coming events. Tell me, what do you know of the Umbar-môkh? Wait, not here. You must accompany me to my house here in Umbar.'","'Clear skies and swift sails to you. Khôltekh? Ah, of course. The chest.\
\
'Yes, it was supposed to arrive two days ago. However the ship it was on was ransacked by Corsairs not far from port. The ship has only just come in, and half her cargo is gone. Namely the expensive half. I am afraid Khôltekh's chest was among the items not found. Khôltekh has always had good taste, and it seems the Corsairs agreed.\
\
'I do not know what is in that chest, but I do have a sense of where it might be. Corsairs and smugglers move freely in the Umbar-môkh. Seeing as how those items were freshly seized, it is most likely they are in Deshûkh, the Blood Market. That's in Dil-irmíz, the Berths. It is an area rife with thieves, smugglers and Corsairs, and it is where I would go if I was looking to offload freshly stolen goods. I would start there.\
\
'Be careful, that is a very dangerous area, and smugglers are not likely to part with their hard-won treasures with just a stern word.'","Return to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja, Hall of the Kindred, with the missing chest.","Khôltekh has asked you to talk to a merchant friend of his, Rathâni in the Sail-haven, about a missing chest.","Search for Khôltekh's missing chest in Deshûkh in Dil-irmíz.","'I hope you've met with clear skies and swift sails. I've a task uniquely suited for your gifts. Do well, and I may have a larger ask for you.\
\
'There's a chest with something quite precious to me locked inside. It was supposed to arrive two days ago. Two days have gone by, and only my irritation has arrived. It was supposed to arrive by ship. I suspect foul play and interference from smugglers in the Umbar-môkh.\
\
'Go see the merchant who was supposed to receive the shipment with this chest. Rathâni may have more insight into where this shipment has gone awry.'\
\
Khôltekh leans in close.\
\
'I am trusting you with this. Do not betray my trust, ${PLAYER}.'","Recovered Khôltekh's chest","Khôltekh has asked you to speak with Rathâni about a missing chest. She can be found near the market by the docks in the Sail-haven."},
[12543]={"Khôltekh has taken you into his trust, for now. He's asked you to accompany him to his house to speak more about his plans for Umbar.","'Only a fool trusts those he doesn't know. But we're good friends now, aren't we? I will trust you, for now. \
\
'You must come with me to my house here in Umbar. Well, one of them, anyway. I also make residence in Thargushakâl, the Shoreward Stone, but this house has many advantages. Namely, a much shorter walk.'\
\
Khôltekh roars in laughter, amused at his own joke.\
\
'Make ready, we will be off soon.'","Speak with Khôltekh when you are ready to go","The Light and the Shadow Part 2: An Audience with the Hall-father","'Ready? Excellent. These layabouts guarding me need some exercise anyway.\
\
'Keep a sharp eye, you might pick up some decorating tips. My house is one of the best furnished in all of Umbar.'"},
[12544]={"Return to Zihârax with the ring","'We must find Sêkhta. A snake with no head perishes quickly. Talk to Nûru, he has information on Sêkhta's whereabouts. One of my Umbar-môkh allies spoke with him recently.\
\
'Nûru can be found in Mekab-kuphâr in Khabârkhad. Go quickly, this Sêkhta is elusive, always one step ahead, like water through my hands.'","Zihârax has asked you to get his ring back from hoodlum in the market stands to the east.","The market cutthroats strike, attacking you!","'Aye, I know of this Sêkhta, the Blight. You'll want to speak with Zihârax in Dûlkar, the Shadow Market. It's located south-east of here, in Dil-irmíz.\
\
'I don't like this Zihârax, or many that Khôltekh consorts with. But we don't get to pick our allies down here, and his information has been sound in the past. He spoke with me this morning, told me he had important information, but that he would only tell Khôltekh or his appointed representative. I guess that's you.\
\
'One word of caution: the Dûlkar is not always a friendly place. Stick to the main market. If you go poking your nose in every stall, don't be surprised to find a sword blade pointing back.'","Speak with Khôltekh's contact Zihârax in the Dûlkar, the Shadow Market in Dil-irmíz. The Dûlkar is located south-east of Mekab-kuphâr.","Speak with Khôltekh's contact Zihârax in the Dûlkar in Dil-irmíz","Find the hoodlums that took Zihârax's ring","'Lower your voice. That name carries great weight here.\
\
'Of course I know Sêkhta. Everyone here does, don't be a fool. The difference is I have information Khôltekh wants. About Amârbo, Sêkhta's right-hand man.\
\
'Listen, I want to be of service to the Kindred and Khôltekh, but I have a problem. You see, this morning my prized ring was stolen from me by hoodlums. Can you believe that? I was going to ask Khôltekh for coin in exchange for this information, but you look like you can handle yourself in a fight and that ring means more to me than a bag of coins.\
\
'I was jumped to the east of here, right by the eastern market entrance. Get me my ring back, and I'll tell you what I know.'","The Light and the Shadow Part 3: A Flash of Gold","Return to Zihârax with the ring.","'I knew you could handle yourself. Sorry they attacked you. Thanks for getting my ring back, I don't feel whole without it.\
\
'All right, I'll tell you what I know.'","Speak with Nûru in Mekab-kuphâr about Sêkhta","Fight off the market cutthroats that have attacked you!","Speak with Nûru in Mekab-kuphâr in southern Khabârkhad about Sêkhta.","Khôltekh has asked you to speak with Nûru in Mekab-kuphâr in Khabârkhad. Nûru has information from an Umbar-môkh contact about Sêkhta.","Fight off the market cutthroats that have attacked you"},
[12545]={"Search for Amârbo in Deshûkh","The Light and the Shadow Part 4: Thick as Thieves","'Here's what I know. Amârbo, Sêkhta's right-hand man, has been seen spending his time in Deshûkh, the Blood Market.\
\
'Amârbo knows what Sêkhta knows. I know Khôltekh has been looking for Sêkhta's base of operations. Amârbo knows all this and more. Find him, and you'll make Khôltekh right pleased with you indeed.\
\
'I'd recommend you head over there now, I happen to know this is a time he likes to frequent Deshûkh. Thanks again for getting my ring back.'","You should investigate Deshûkh for signs of Amârbo. Deshûkh is located north-west of the Dûlkar.","Defeated Deshûkh smugglers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Search for Amârbo in Deshûkh, the Blood Market.","Zihârax, Khôltekh's contact, has told you an associate of Sêkhta's, Amârbo, has been seen in Deshûkh. You should investigate Deshûkh for Amârbo.","Defeat Deshûkh smugglers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja, Hall of the Kindred, with this information.","Ask Amârbo what he knows of Sêkhta and his whereabouts.","Return to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja with this information","'I yield! I am no fighter. I will tell you what I know!\
\
'Sêkhta has an outpost not far from here, to the south, from which his influence spreads all throughout Umbar-môkh. You cannot get past the door without a key, however. The way is barred, and the keys are scarce, and quite valuable. That is where you are likely to find him.\
\
'That is all I know.'","'The way is barred, and the keys are scarce, and quite valuable... I do so love a riddle!\
\
'You've done well, ${PLAYER}. but it seems our work has only just begun.'","Ask Amârbo what he knows of Sêkhta and his whereabouts"},
[12546]={"The Light and the Shadow Part 5: A Lock with No Key","The lock has a series of deep, narrow grooves carved into the stone","'You found some of Sêkhta's men guarding this door? No doubt there is something valuable or important to Sêkhta hidden inside. We must find a way to open it.\
\
'A series of deep, narrow cuts in the stone, you say? Interesting. Interesting.\
\
'I cannot think clearly here. Come, we must go to my house once more. We must figure out how to open this door, and to do that I need to think in peace.'","Look for a door within Dar Sêkhta with a suspicious lock","Look for an alcove or door with an unconventional lock.","Find Dar Sêkhta in Dil-irmíz","Examine the strange lock for clues as to its key.","'Ready? Let's be off then. Far too stuffy here. And the chairs aren't as nice. Ho ho!\
\
'The way is barred, and the keys are scarce and quite valuable... Hmmm... Hmmm....'","You have found Dar Sêkhta!","Accompany Khôltekh to his house, so he may think clearly on this key.","Khôltekh has asked you to investigate the area Amârbo told you about, where you will hopefully find Dar Sêkhta, and a clue as to Sêkhta's whereabouts.","'You should go to Dâr Sêkhta. Even if you cannot gain access, we may yet learn more about this key by examining the lock.\
\
'Amârbo, if he is to be trusted at sword-point, said it was quite close to Deshûkh. South of it, if I recall correctly? That is the place to start.'","Return to Dâr Laja with your description of the lock. Perhaps Khôltekh has a clue as to its key.","You see a nearby alcove with strange indentations in the wall","Return to Dâr Laja and tell Khôltekh your description of the lock","Speak with Khôltekh when you are ready to go","Khôltekh has asked you to look for Dar Sêkhta, and a suspicious lock there that might fit a mysterious key. According to Amârbo, it is located south of Deshûkh in Dil-irmíz.","Examine the strange lock for clues as to its key"},
[12547]={"'This is most troubling news. Why would a criminal have such scholarly books? And that saying...\
\
'Hmmm. \\qA candle flickers in the dark, and is extinguished.\\q Another riddle, it seems.'","'A wight's hand. All bone. That's the key.\
\
'The five narrow holes are for finger-bones. Luckily there's a great many crypt-walkers in Sektakhâb in Khabârkhad. You need one in exceedingly good condition, nothing broken, so it may take several tries to find one.\
\
'Find a suitable hand, take it to the door and find the whereabouts of this shadow. We need to put an end to the suffering of Umbari citizens at the hands of this villain.'","Go back to Dâr Sêkhta and insert the pristine wight's hand into the lock","Khôltekh has asked you to go to Sektakhâb in Khabârkhad and find a pristine wight's hand. He believes this is the key to Dâr Sêkhta that will open the way and find Sêkhta or necessary clues about him.","Khôltekh has asked you to find a pristine wight's hand in Khabârkhad. He believes that to be the key that is \\qscarce\\q but \\qquite valuable\\q that will open the way to Dâr Sêkhta's hidden area.","Return to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja with the clues you have found","Find a pristine crypt-walker's hand by defeating crypt-walkers","Enter the hidden area of Dâr Sêkhta","You hear a lock click behind the brick wall to your right, opening the way","You have found a pristine wight's hand","Enter the hidden area of Dâr Sêkhta.","Return to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja with the clues you have found.","The Light and the Shadow Part 6: A Helping Hand","Go back to Dâr Sêkhta and insert the pristine wight's hand into the lock."},
[12548]={"Return to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja with the book.","Speak with Ephrâti in Tilmakhím in Tâkhdar","'Just as I thought - each of these books show a fascination bordering on obsession with the Heirs of Castamir.\
\
'These robes - even stained in blood they speak to Umbari nobility. And these books, much more scholarly than one would think for a lowly criminal. And his writing style from the note, so neat, like he was trained or schooled in it....\
\
'I've got it! An archivist! An Umbari historian! It all fits. They are members of Umbari nobility, highly educated, trained in reading and writing. Sêkhta is an archivist!\
\
'Archivists live and work in the Tor-gardens. They are quite few in number. Hmmm... yes.\
\
'I have a plan. Come, we must go to the Tor-gardens at once!'","Return to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja with the book","Khôltekh has asked you to go find a bookseller in Tilmakhím. He believes she may have the missing volume to 'A History of Castamir and His Heirs' that you found in Dâr Sêkhta.","Speak with Khôltekh about his revelation","'Come, we must go to the Tor-gardens to expose this archivist where he lives and works. Sêkhta is there, I'm sure of it!'","'I have the book, but your coin is no good here. If I take it Mâramit, the purveyor of traps across the market, will have my head.'\
\
Ephrâti leans in close.\
\
'She and Khôltekh have an arrangement, if you get my meaning. You understand. Off with you then, I need to devise my next counterattack against these rats.'","Find a bookseller named Ephrâti in Tilmakhím, in Tâkhdar. Khôltekh is looking for the missing volume from the set you found in Dâr Sêkhta.","'I know not what \\qa candle flickers in the dark, and is extinguished\\q means.\
\
'Still, these clues help a great deal. There was a volume missing from the books you found. I wonder if the missing volume holds any secrets from Sêkhta. Would you go to Tilmakhím in Tâkhdar? There is a bookseller there who may have the missing volume. Ephrâti, I believe her name is.\
\
'We need every clue we can grasp to find this Sêkhta.'","Accompany Khôltekh to the Tor-gardens.","Speak with Khôltekh when you are ready to go","Speak with Khôltekh outside the Pot and Quill in the Tor-gardens about his revelation.","'The Candle! The Candle is a ship! They mean to commandeer the Candle of Umbar!'","The Light and the Shadow Part 7: A Candle Flickers in the Dark"},
[12550]={"'Donnvail está cubierto por la sombra del miedo, ${PLAYER}, y los Trév Gállorg aquí están atormentados. Mantenemos la cabeza agachada y tratamos de no llamar la atención sobre nosotros.\
\
'Los señores de Carn Dûm han enviado a esta ciudad crueles capataces para detener cualquier posibilidad de rebelión antes de que comience: Fûshath la Bestia, un terrible Gorthorog; Muiráthakh, el Juez Silencioso, el que profetiza doom y verdugo; y Gillë Andras, el Señor de las Fronteras del Oeste, cruel líder de los ejércitos que pisan Fasach-falroid.\
\
'No diré más. Busca a Garvan, más adentro en la ciudad. Él te dirá más, si es tan temerario como yo, y rezo para que no le digas a nadie que yo te di su nombre.'","'No tengo nada más que decirte, y no repetiré ningún nombre; hay demasiados oídos hostiles en esta ciudad.\
\
'¿Quizá anotaste lo que te dije? ¡Consulta tu diario y no atraigas más atención hacia mí!'","'Es lo que temía. Que la familia de Uthagan sufra por sus acciones es muy acorde con lo que sabemos de Muiráthakh.\
\
'Busca a Una en lo profundo de Donnvail, y que la mente de Uthagan encuentre alivio con nuestro eventual triunfo.'","'Hablas con valentía para ser ${PLAYERNAME:un forastero recién llegado[m]|una forastera recién llegada[f]} a Donnvail. ¿No temes a Muiráthakh ni a Fûshath la Bestia?\
\
'Uthagan, más adentro de la ciudad, podría ayudarte, pero habla con él con cautela; su familia fue recientemente \\qinvitada\\q a una cena en la casa de Muiráthakh, y no los he visto desde entonces. No sé si alguien los ha visto.\
\
'Debemos organizarnos si queremos golpear a nuestros amos Angmarim. Uthagan podría guiarte.'","'Has recorrido un largo camino hasta mí, ${PLAYER}, y espero que no haya sido demasiado doloroso. Donnvail no ha sido una ciudad pacífica desde que los señores de Carn Dûm enviaron aquí a sus esbirros.\
\
'Los pocos que nos oponemos a la sombra agradecemos tu ayuda. Este barrio será el corazón de la lucha. ¡Llama a tus aliados si los tienes y si están dispuestos a luchar contigo! Los enemigos que pronto enfrentarás no pueden ser derrotados por uno solo; harán falta muchos corazones para derrocar a los amos de esta ciudad.'","Uthagan está en la ciudad de Donnvail, al noreste de Fail-Á-Khro.\
\
Morven te ha dicho que hables con Uthagan, pero con precaución: su familia fue tomada recientemente por Muiráthakh, y ella no cree que hayan sido vistos desde entonces.","Morven está dentro de la ciudad de Donnvail, al noreste de Fail-Á-Khro.\
\
Garvan te dio el nombre de alguien que podría simpatizar con la causa, diciéndote que buscaras a Morven más adentro en la ciudad.","Uthagan derrotado","'Uthagan está más adentro en la ciudad, y puede que pueda ayudarte.'","'Lo siento, debe confundirme con otra persona. Solo estoy ocupado con mis asuntos.\
\
'Busca a Morven, más adentro de la ciudad. No puedo dejar que me vean hablando contigo, pero quizá ella esté dispuesta a escucharte.'","'¿Me hablas de rebelión? ¡Díselo a mi familia, que fue tomada por Muiráthakh bajo la acusación de que planeaban un levantamiento! Ese perro sabe que fui yo quien ayudó a Una, pero tomó a mi familia en su lugar, como advertencia para mí.\
\
'Hubo un tiempo en que te habría ayudado, pero ahora Una tendrá que luchar sola.\
\
'¡Te mataré yo mismo y te enseñaré algo sobre la desesperación!'","Búdan te envió a la ciudad de Donnvail para hablar con los Trév Gállorg que podrían levantarse contra los Angmarim.","'Encontrarás a Morven más adentro en la ciudad. ¡Ahora déjame en paz!'","'Lloro por Uthagan. Busca a Una en algún lugar profundo de Donnvail, y que su familia no haya sufrido en vano.\
\
'Debes irte ahora. Los guardias empezarán a sospechar.'","Uthagan habló de Una, que se encuentra en algún lugar de la ciudad de Donnvail, al noreste de Fail-Á-Khro.\
\
Aunque intentó matarte, Uthagan te dio sin querer el nombre de alguien con quien podrías hablar: una mujer llamada Una.","La Luz de la Esperanza","Habla con Uthagan","'Pobre Uthagan. ¿Habría alguno de nosotros soportado el tormento que debió sufrir?\
\
'Aun así, nos sigue ayudando: busca a Una en lo profundo de Donnvail.'","Garvan está en la ciudad de Donnvail, al noreste de Fail-Á-Khro.\
\
Búdan te habló de los tres líderes enviados a Donnvail por Carn Dûm: Fûshath la Bestia, Muiráthakh la Jueza Silenciosa y Gillë Andras el Señor de las Fronteras del Oeste. También te dijo que hablaras con un hombre llamado Garvan más adentro en la ciudad de Donnvail."},
[12551]={"Captain Agelbrit stands guard at a lonely gate-house on the upper edge of the Limlight Gorge. His duty is as much to keep unwary travellers out of the Gorge as it is to keep the beasts within from climbing out to threaten the folk of Stangard.","'You are headed west of Stangard? Well, let me give you a piece of advice, friend.... Stay clear of the Limlight Gorge if you know what is good for you.\
\
'I have heard tell of Orcs and the like raising trouble in the Wailing Hills... but I assure you they are not half as dangerous as the monstrosities wandering down in the Gorge these days.\
\
'If you do head out that way, just make sure to check in with Captain Agelbrit. You should at least know what you are getting into.'","The Limlight Gorge","'What is that? You want to explore the Gorge? That is folly and then some, unless you plan to lead a whole company of stalwarts with you.\
\
'But I see in your eyes that you are not the sort to be so easily dissuaded. Well, do not blame me when some troll uses you for a football, or a spider the size of a horse has you dangling as a snack in its larder.\
\
'Tell me, did the Men of Stangard put you up to this? Because if they did it is not funny any more. Three lads this week alone have gone down there, trying to prove their worth, and that will be the last we see of them. Enough is enough!\
\
'I will tell you what: you go talk with Sigelm over there... he has a tale or two to tell about the Gorge back before we stopped patrols down into it.'","Sigelm is near the Limlight Gorge Guardhouse.\
\
Captain Agelbrit has asked you to listen to Sigelm's tales of the Limlight Gorge before you explore the dangerous valley.","'Hold on a moment, stranger! I am sorry to take you to task, but I must ask what brings you this way?'","'So, do you still want to head down there? It is your life to lose, I suppose.'","Talk to Captain Agelbrit","Speak with Captain Agelbrit at the Limlight Gorge Guard-house.","'The Gorge? Oh aye, I have been down there many times. Not so much in the last couple of years, but we used to patrol it regularly.\
\
'Pretty place, really, but it has always been a bit queer. Strange things there. I would swear that the trees had moved from one patrol to the next, or that some boulder had shifted to face north, or all of the birds would suddenly get all quiet on a midsummer's day.\
\
'That was before those great cursed trolls arrived of course. They crawled up out of the rocks, or down from the mountains... I could not say which, but they are a handful for even a band of men.\
\
'Fortunately, they do not much like the sun... it has been overcast down in the Gorge a lot lately, but they are still too scared of it to wander as far from their caves as Stangard, so that is a blessing.\
\
'It was after the trolls arrived that we saw something that REALLY gave the men a nasty turn... we were watching from a safe distance as one of those great brutes was lumbering along, when it took a swing at some old fir-tree, and the accursed thing came alive! Vines and branches wrapped up round the troll, and there was such a to-do as we have never seen.\
\
'We had not been imagining that the trees down there wander about... they DO walk, you see, and they had been watching us all those years! That was the last patrol we did down there, and you could not pay any man of us to go back down there again.'","Talk to Sigelm"},
[12552]={"You should find the old sawmill in the Limlight Gorge and learn if Armund and his companions are still alive.","The dwarves sent a small expedition to try and rebuild the old sawmill in Limlight Gorge.","'Well, I do not know as I have any proper work for you.\
\
'The old mill is in rough shape, but nothing me and my folk cannot put to right with a bit of dwarf-ingenuity!\
\
'The only problem now is that all of the others seem to have wandered off and lost track of the time or some-such. None of them have come back from their jobs out in the Gorge....'","Talk to Armund in the old sawmill","The Limlight Mill","'Who is there?\
\
'We have not seen many travellers since we started work on the sawmill...are you looking for work?'","'Something you could look into while you are in the Gorge is a band of dwarves that headed down there about a week ago. You see, there is an old sawmill in the Gorge, along the river. It has been abandoned for a few years now because of the troubles in the Gorge.\
\
'These dwarves heard about the sawmill, and their eyes lit up...with greed, no doubt. They believed they were just the sort to get it working again and do business up in Stangard from it. A fine enough endeavour, if the Gorge were not crawling with all manner of dwarf-devouring beasts.\
\
'I do not guess that the trees themselves will be too kindly to folk trying to run a sawmill, either, now that I think of it. Anyway, if you should run into the dwarves -- and they are still alive -- see if you can convince them to come up out of there. It is not worth their lives to get a simple mill up and running. If they are dead...well, I would be obliged if you would let us know. There is not much we can do, but I like to keep track of such things.'","'You should seek the dwarves who passed into the Gorge.'"},
[12553]={"Defeated Khataj Mârsa Corsairs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Javish has asked you to initiate negotiations between a renegade Corsair group which poses a threat to the status quo in Mâr Naphra.\
\
The meeting location should be among the shallows to the south-east.","'Well, I should've seen that coming. Could never trust a Corsair, eh?\
\
'Anyways, I reckon we have no choice but to nip this in the bud. There's a reward in it for ya. Pay Khataj Mârsa a visit and take care of them before they cause more trouble for Mâr Naphra, would ya?'","'It didn't have to come to this. Us pirates need to stick together. If we don't, that'll be the best of us.\
\
'I appreciate you sticking your neck out. It was a difficult task, but you proved your worth.'","Javish is troubled by a group of renegade Corsairs who refuse to play nice with rules of Mâr Naphra.","Javish has no choice but to take Adranax's actions as an act of sedition. He asks that we punish the Corsairs before they can cause further chaos.\
\
Khataj Mârsa can be found south-east of Mâr Naphra.","The Corsairs at Khataj Mârsa have been punished. You should report to Javish your success.\
\
Javish can be found in Mâr Naphra.","'The rules here are simple. You follow them, and your life ain't forfeit.\
\
'Seems we got ourselves a crew of Corsairs who think they're better than the lot of us. I reckon we will need an outside party to resolve matters.\
\
'I've already set up the parley. Adranax is going to meet you at a cove south-east of Mâr Naphra.'","'What do we have here? You mean to tell me that Javish couldn't show up himself?\
\
'This is going to make things difficult. instead of betraying my good friend Javish, I've got to end some poor lackey's life.\
\
'This isn't personal, friend.'","Adranax planned to betray Javish all along. Javish should know that you had no choice but to defend yourself.\
\
Javish can be found in Mâr Naphra.","Talk to Javish","Talk to Javish in Mâr Naphra","Talk to Adranax at the agreed upon location","Defeat Corsairs in Khataj Mârsa (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Line in the Sand"},
[12555]={"'We could probably slay these vile cats from dawn 'til dusk and not see the end of them. We need to strike them where it will do the most harm.\
\
'Surely among the Khundolar at Lashkarg is one who trains these creatures. Hunt him out and defeat him. With their trainer gone, the cats may even turn upon their own.\
\
'Will you do this?'","Talk to Twiga at Etheburg in the Brown Lands","It is clear that the wild cats of the Brown Lands are anything but wild, and Twiga has a plan to do away with them.","The trainer of the Khundolar battle-cats may be found at Lashkarg, south-east of Etheburg in the Brown Lands.\
\
Twiga asked you to hunt down the trainer of the Khundolar battle-cats and defeat him.","'Have you dealt with the Khundolar's cat-trainer yet?'","The Lion's Eye","Defeated Sherkóz","Twiga is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, north-west of Lashkarg.\
\
You should return to Twiga with tidings of your victory.","Defeat Sherkóz","'You slew this Sherkóz? Did the cats turn upon the Khundolar?\
\
'Ah, I suppose it was too much to hope for. You have my thanks for your efforts, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[12556]={"'Berkha? Our new friend has brought you some delicious morsels to eat! Berkha? Oh dear. I lose track of him for five minutes and already he finds a way to escape....'","The Roc, Raghda-gûn, has taken in a little bird of another species.","Gather insects (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Raghda-gûn","The Little Bird","Gathered insects (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have gathered enough insects to feed little Berkha.\
\
Return to Raghda-gûn.","Raghda-gûn asked you to gather insects to feed to her little adoptee.\
\
Insects can be found underneath little stones scattered around the Raghda-gûn's nest.","'This would not be the first time someone's foolish greed brought trouble to my nest or danger to myself or one of my young. I appreciate your warning. I must nurse these eggs, which gives me less freedom to watch for interlopers.'\
\
You can't help but notice the duck waddling around her nest.\
\
'Ah, the chick here? Say hello to our guest, little Berkha! Say hello! Ah, he's shy. You know how children that age can be.\
\
'I found him alone not far from here. I do not know what became of his family, but if I did not adopt him as my own he surely would have died on these harsh isles. Though my kind are a far sight from his flock, surely our differences cannot be insurmountable. If you would like to be helpful to me, could you gather some insects for him to eat? I fear he is too small to be hunting on his own.'"},
[12558]={"'Ah, ${PLAYER}. These stones are perfect for skipping. I imagine that you have skipped a rock or two in your lifetime, have you not?\
\
'I will put these into Cútha's pocket sometime, and he will have a nice surprise when he finds them.'","The falls of Everholt lie to the south-west of Beaconwatch.\
\
Lady Answith wants to go to the falls in Everholt and collect several stones that would be suitable for skipping.","Lady Answith, the Thane's wife, knows that he can be unpleasant, but only because he allows himself to be consumed by duty and forgets the little things in life that he enjoys.","Collected skipping stones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Little Things","Talk to Lady Answith","'So you have met my husband, Cútha? I know that he can be a bit unpleasant at times, but you should understand that he is doing what he feels is right.\
\
'Sometimes he needs a gentle reminder to enjoy the little things in life. One of his favourite things to do is skip stones along the Mering-stream. Would you collect some stones that would be suitable for skipping?\
\
'There is a waterfall in Everholt, south-west of Beaconwatch that always has the best stones. I would go myself, but with all the trouble lately, I confess I do not wish to leave this area.'","Lady Answith is on a porch above the vendor's area north of the Mead Hall in Beaconwatch.\
\
You have collected skipping stones at the Everholt Falls and should now bring them back to Lady Answith.","Collect skipping stones (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12560]={"Dernstan is at Eaworth.\
\
Dernstan will be pleased to hear you defeated several goblins within the Living Deep.","'They will return, I have no doubt, but for tonight we can sleep without the ground rumbling.'","'When you are ready to brave the tunnels of the Living Deep, we can depart.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is an instanced public questing area.</rgb>","Defeated goblins in the Living Deep (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Living Deep: Goblin-sappers","Goblins can be found in the Living Deep.","<rgb=#FF0000>Completing Aiding the Eastemnet will cancel this quest</rgb>","Defeat goblins in the Living Deep (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Dernstan","The goblins within the Living Deep are attempting to destroy the forest from below.","'The Living Deep has been invaded by the sappers of the Enemy, foul goblins skittering about through the caves, assaulting the forest from below. The more of the forest that they claim, the greater their war-machine becomes.\
\
'To defend ourselves, we must strike at our enemy. Head into the Living Deep and defeat the goblins within.'"},
[12561]={"'Si eliminamos a los sapos, el resto se matará entre sí. ¡Estoy seguro de esto!'","Derrota a los sapos profundos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Águti en la Bodega Putrefacta","Águti se encuentra en la Bodega Putrefacta.\
\
Águti estará contento de escuchar que la población de sapos profundos ha sido reducida.","'Excelente trabajo, ${PLAYER}. Tengo fe en que pronto las criaturas de las Obras Hidráulicas ya no serán una amenaza, y podremos recuperarlo con facilidad.'","Los sapos profundos se pueden encontrar por todas las Obras Hidráulicas.\
\
Águti cree que cuando los sapos sean eliminados los lagartos y las arañas se comerán entre sí.","Águti ha determinado que los sapos profundos son la clave de la cadena alimenticia en las Obras Hidráulicas.","'He estudiado las muestras que me trajiste y he determinado cómo podemos eliminar a todas las criaturas de aquí con un solo golpe. Los sapos profundos son la clave para la supervivencia de los lagartos y las arañas. Atacar a los sapos será atacar a sus depredadores también.\
\
'¿Cómo, preguntas? Los lagartos no se ven afectados por el veneno de las arañas, por lo que las arañas no pueden debilitarlos, lo que los hace presas indeseables para las arañas. Además, los lagartos tienen suficiente astucia para evitar las telarañas de las arañas. Los sapos, por otro lado, son casi sin mente en contraste; tanto los lagartos como las arañas tienen poca dificultad para atrapar y devorar a los sapos.\
\
'Si eliminas a los sapos, las arañas y los lagartos no tendrán más opción que atacarse entre sí. ¿Lo harás?'","La fauna local es mortal","'Esto llevará un poco de tiempo, pero eventualmente podremos recuperar las Obras Hidráulicas de las criaturas que habitan aquí.'","Sapos profundos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12562]={"Libro de cuentas de Mason Espino recogido","Mason Espino está en el campamento de leñadores, al norte y este de la casa de guardia.\
\
Ted Abrojos te pidió que hablaras con Mason Espino, el capataz del campamento de leñadores de Combe. Puede que recuerde qué árbol era el Árbol de la Horca.","'¿El Árbol de la Horca? Oh, recuerdo haber visto algunas... hmm... ejecuciones en mi época. Creo... hmm... que anoté el lugar del Árbol de la Horca en mi libro de cuentas. Escribo todo lo que quiero recordar. Así que solo tengo que buscar en...\
\
Bueno... hmm... ¡vaya! Creo que dejé caer mi libro de cuentas en el bosque, no muy lejos de aquí. Sí, lo recuerdo. Nos sorprendieron unos Montebruno y dejé caer el libro en el camino. Apostaría a que un capitán de esos bandidos lo recogió.\
\
Hay varias hogueras al norte y al este, a lo largo del camino del bosque. ¡Quizá encuentres mi libro en uno de esos Montebruno! Tráelo de vuelta aquí... hmm... y buscaré eso que querías saber. ¿Un árbol, era?'","'¿Dices que el lugar del Árbol de la Horca está en el libro de Mason? ¡Bien, bien! Me encantaría ver ese libro, eh, bueno... la verdad es que no sé leer. Cuando lo tengas, será mejor que le pidas al viejo Espino que lo busque.'","'¡Ah, encontraste mi libro de cuentas! ¡Ahora puedo buscar eso... hmm... que querías!'","Mason Espino te espera en el campamento de leñadores que está al este y norte de Combe, al sur del bosque de Chet.\
\
Espino te envió a recuperar su libro de cuentas de los bandidos Montebruno acampados junto al camino. Debes devolverle el libro de inmediato.","'¡Diles a esos leñadores del campamento que no pueden ir talando árboles a lo loco así!\
\
Me doy cuenta de que la gente de Combe depende de la venta de esa madera para sobrevivir, ¡pero estamos hablando del legado de mi padre! ¿Cómo voy a encontrarlo ahora sin cavar agujeros por todo el bosque de Chet?'","El libro de cuentas del leñador","Lleva el libro de cuentas a Mason Espino","Recoge el libro de cuentas de Mason Espino","'Supongo que un Montebruno tiene mi libro de cuentas. Alguno de esos capitanes probablemente lo esté usando para planear sus movimientos en el bosque de Chet. Están acampados al este. Tendrás que recuperarlo de ellos si quieres saber... hmm... dónde está ese árbol.'","'¡Quizá los leñadores del campamento al este de aquí recuerden cuál era el Árbol de la Horca! ${PLAYER}, tienes que hablar con Mason Espino, el encargado allí. Él debe recordar cuál de los tocones era antes el Árbol de la Horca. ¡Debe recordarlo!\
\
El campamento de leñadores está junto a la carretera, al norte de la Casa Grande. Por favor, necesito ese dinero para empezar de nuevo.'","Ted Abrojos se angustió mucho cuando le dijiste que el Árbol de la Horca y todos los árboles que lo rodeaban habían sido talados.","Habla con Mason Espino en el campamento de leñadores de Combe"},
[12563]={"Attempt to talk to the Lone Lady","Talk to Glassiel","'The Lone Lady has turned against us? All is lost, ${PLAYER}...\
\
'She has always been the most distant of the Sisters, even in our stories of old... yet she was never so twisted as you describe!\
\
'What has happened to her after these long years? And what can be done?'","'I have something to ask of you, ${PLAYER}. Few others have heard me on this matter, but you seem the kind to heed the tales of strangers.\
\
'In my youth, I often travelled the lands of Lebennin and spent much time upon the banks of its rivers. I knew well of the legends of our people as did all other children of Lebennin, but that was not the reason for my wandering. My father had taken ill in summer, and the disease claimed him by spring. My mother went silent for a year's time, and all looked upon me as a child of madness and misfortune. My only respite was in walking the banks of the Five Rivers, and so I went.\
\
'The Erui was nearest to my home, and it, too, knew well of tragedy and death. It was there that King Eldacar slew the Usurper long ago, but many others fell and bloodied its shallows before the battle came to an end. It is said that the last of the Five Sisters, the Lone Lady of Erui, once looked upon our people with fondness, but the horrors that occurred in her waters led her to spirit herself away. It may seem a different tale from my own, but I have not yet reached its ending....\
\
'You see, I sat near the falls at the Crossings one day and was overcome by the sadness of my family's fate. As I dried my tears, I saw something that has not left my mind in all my years. I saw the image of a woman's face gazing upon me from behind the falls. I dashed into the water and called out, but as soon as I drew close to the falls, the face had gone. To this day, I know the Lone Lady appeared before me and ever since, I have held close my belief in the Sisters.\
\
'The Haradrim do not respect our lands or rivers as we do, and they do not know to fear the ire of the Five Sisters. The Lone Lady should not again suffer the blood of Men in her waters, and I ask that you seek her out at the Crossings as I once did. May she watch over Lebennin and keep us from the evils of war!'","River-stones can be found at the Crossings of Erui in eastern Upper Lebennin.\
\
You have found only a drowned Haradrim and should now search for the Lone Lady of Erui.","Glassiel can be found in Halach in south-eastern Upper Lebennin.\
\
The Lone Lady has given her waters form using pieces of ancient armour and has banished you from the Erui. You should bring these dire tidings to Glassiel.","The Lone Lady","The Lone Lady's face flushes with anger, and she does not respond to your words.","The waters of the Erui churn violently as the Lone Lady appears!","The Crossings of Erui can be found far to the north of Halach in eastern Upper Lebennin.\
\
Glassiel has asked you to search the Crossings of Erui for any sign of the mysterious Lone Lady.","This Haradrim lies drowned near a pile of river-stones as his brethren battle nearby...","Disturb the nearby pile of river-stones","Search the Crossings of Erui for sign of the Lone Lady","Distraught by many of the recent happenings in Lebennin, Glassiel hopes to call upon one of the Five Sisters for aid in these dire times.","The Lone Lady can be found at the Crossings of Erui in eastern Upper Lebennin.\
\
After disturbing a pile of river-stones, the Lone Lady has appeared in a rage. You should attempt to speak to her."},
[12564]={"'Hail, friend. I'm afraid nothing can distract that dog from watching the sea. On many mornings, I find that she has beaten me here! Sometimes she only leaves that spot once the moon has risen.\
\
'I decided to come prepared today with meat, just in case the dog was hungry. How about you take some to her?'","Handir has given you some meat with which to feed the lonely dog.","The dog happily bites into her meal","Feed the lonely dog","The Lonely Dog","'Well, would you look at that! Even the most stalwart of guards must take a break from their duty every now and then.'\
\
Handir's smile fades as he continues gazing at the dog. 'I wonder what she is searching for. Did she lose something? Someone? Perhaps her master left home for the war and never returned.\
\
'I suppose I ought to start asking around, see if anyone recognizes the poor beast. And if not... well, my family has room for another member!'","The dog watches the horizon, only sparing you a quick glance at your approach. Then she returns to her vigil.","You have found a lonely dog in East Pelargir.\
\
A nearby guard, Handir, has called out to you.","Talk to Handir","A nearby guard calls out to you","A lonely dog sits on a pier in Pelargir, always watching the horizon.","You have fed the lonely dog.\
\
You should talk to Handir."},
[12565]={"<rgb=#FF00FF>Look</rgb> next to Coldan","A vast and foreboding edifice rises against the mountain face","You should continue up the road that winds north from western Udûn.","Righted another Gondorian banner","You should continue up the road that winds north from western Udûn, righting any other banners that you find.","The soldier Coldan has asked you to stand beside him and look up toward the looming face of Ered Lithui.","'Have... have you come here to relieve me? Truly, I know not how long I have stood here. The winds at this height cut through my armour, and though a foul fog poisons the air, I feel as if every red, malicious eye in Udûn is fixed upon me where I stand.'\
\
The look-out shivers.\
\
'Why, you ask? Come stand by me, with your back to Udûn and your eyes up. What is it that you see?'","'That which you see is named Anglach, perhaps the greatest of forges in Mordor. I have stood and kept watch on it since yesterday, when Captain Lachír posted me here.'\
\
The look-out seems scared and miserable. You tell him to return to the Foothold and it is as if a great weight has been lifted from his shoulders.\
\
'Reason and duty have warred in me these many hours. Thanks to you, ${CLASS}, they may stop their contest and leave here, hand in hand.'","Captain Lachír's search party wandered the basin of Udûn, leaving men here and there to search in vain for some imagined treasure. After that, Lachír backtracked, leading his remaining company up the rising northward road.","'You wish to know where Captain Lachír has gone? That I can say, and better than you might imagine.\
\
'He set off east you see, after leaving us here, and was gone for some time. Then, some half a day later we saw him marching back along the road and our hearts leaped, only to sink again. They came not for us, nor were they returning to the Foothold. No, we watched them make their way down the central road, then turn up on the rising northward path. If you would find them, you must follow them there.'","The Gondorian banner stands proudly once again","Talk to the look-out","You should raise the fallen Gondorian banner that you found on the road that winds north from western Udûn.","The Lonely Look-out","A small, knocked-down Gondorian banner catches your eye - probably Captain Lachír's doing","Search the northward road","A lone look-out stands on a rocky outcropping south of the road","Raise the Gondorian banner","Continue up the road","You should talk to the look-out on the outcropping off the road that winds north from western Udûn, and learn what he knows of Captain Lachír.","Coldan the look-out stands on the outcropping off the road that winds north from western Udûn.\
\
You should talk to Coldan again, now that you looked and have seen the great edifice against the mountains.","This is the rising road that Captain Lachír took","Talk to Coldan","Continue up the road, fixing any other fallen banners you find","You should follow the road that winds north from western Udûn."},
[12566]={"El camino a Quiebra Larga","<rgb=#FF0000>Evita a los Fronteros de Lotho</rgb>","Habla con Fredegar Bolger en el agujero-almacén secreto","¡Has sido ${PLAYERNAME:detectado[m]|detectada[f]} por uno de los Fronteros de Lotho!","'Mmm, no conozco a este Bill Helechal. ¿Crees que podría estar aliado con Lotho?\
\
'No, lo dudo. Lotho puede ser un tipo desagradable, pero sigue siendo un hobbit, y no me lo imagino haciendo tratos con este tal Helechal.'","Le has enseñado una lección... ¿pero le servirá de algo?","'Si la Guardia de Allende espera desbaratar los planes de Lotho y sus Fronteros, ¡va a necesitar suministros, y yo tengo justo lo que hace falta!\
\
'Necesito que lleves estos suministros a los Fronteros en Quiebra Larga. ¡Pase lo que pase, no te dejes atrapar por los Fronteros de Lotho!'","Habla con el Frontero Tugo en Quiebra Larga","Enfréntate a Bill Helechal","'Iré donde quiera y haré lo que quiera, ¡y quien se interponga en mi camino lo pagará!'","La Guardia de Allende necesitará suministros para poner fin a los planes de Lotho.","Los suministros de la Guardia de Allende se encuentran en el agujero-almacén secreto en el bosque entre Gamwich y Quiebra Larga.\
\
Debes llevar los suministros de la Guardia de Allende a un Frontero en Quiebra Larga.","Hay un agujero-almacén secreto de la Guardia de Allende en el bosque entre Gamwich y Quiebra Larga.\
\
Debes hablar con Fredegar Bolger en el agujero-almacén.","Recupera los suministros de la Guardia de Allende del agujero-almacén secreto","Un Frontero de la Guardia de Allende se encuentra en Quiebra Larga.\
\
Debes hablar con el Frontero Tugo en Quiebra Larga.","Bill Helechal se encuentra cerca de Quiebra Larga en la Comarca Allende.\
\
Debes enfrentarte a Bill Helechal.","'Gracias por estos suministros. Fredegar ha sido de gran ayuda para nuestra causa.\
\
'Ya que te tengo por aquí, ¿te importaría ayudarme con algo? Hay un hombre llamado Bill Helechal merodeando por aquí cerca, y sospecho que no trama nada bueno. Su presencia pronto empezará a asustar a los niños. Así que espántalo... ¡por la fuerza!'"},
[12567]={"'Oh, thank goodness you've come!\
\
'I was on my way to report that I found a number of Orkish trebuchets and ballistae among the outer defences of Gundabad, and then some sneaky little goblin caught sight of me. After that, well, the odds were against me!\
\
'You know as well as I that a proud dwarf does not surrender! But... it is not an admission of defeat to buy one's self time to think! I broke my bonds not one minute after the Orcs threw me in this cage, but escaping this filthy camp will take more than just strength.\
\
'Why don't you destroy some of those siege-engines? That ought to get the Orcs riled up... and distracted enough to take their eyes off me!\
\
'Do not worry! I'll find somewhere safe... just not here!'","The Long Reach of Gundabad","You have destroyed many Orkish trebuchets and ballistae at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh.","You have destroyed many Orkish trebuchets and ballistae at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh.\
\
In addition to aiding the Gabil'akkâ, you also provided Darfin ample opportunity to escape his predicament unscathed.","Within the twin encampments of Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh, terrible siege-engines stand ready to fire on any who would dare to approach Mount Gundabad.","Completado","Destroy Orkish ballistae at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Destroy Orkish trebuchets at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Destroyed Orkish trebuchets at Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Orkish trebuchets and ballistae can be found in Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh.\
\
Darfin has asked you to destroy the siege-engines deployed in Hanksar-mokh and Kulûg-mokh. You should destroy Orkish trebuchets and ballistae."},
[12568]={"'Ah, ${PLAYER}, you have returned. It is good to see you again.\
\
'Gifemund will be happy to know his mine will be less difficult to reclaim. The White Hand encamped there would only have added to our difficulties here eventually.\
\
'Thane Nothmar arrived with his men shortly before you did, and we need to gather Gifemund and his men. The time has come for us to act.'","Mate Isernore is along the road between Gapholt and Woodhurst.\
\
White Hand scourge should be wiped out of Mate Isernore and out of the northern Stonedeans. The mine and its resources were not theirs to take.","Westan is on the bridge leading into Gapholt.\
\
Westan saw you coming and called for your attention.","The time has come to leave Gapholt and return to Woodhurst. You will need to pass over the bridge to begin your return journey.","Cross the bridge to leave Gapholt","Westan calls for your attention","The Long Road to Woodhurst","'On our way here from Woodhurst, we saw that the White Hand had taken Mate Isernore!\
\
'What can be done about them? They shot arrows at our caravan on the way by, and it seems like they could threaten Gapholt if left unchecked. The road to Woodhurst goes right by there!'","Westan tries to get your attention as you pass by...","Herubrand is in the cellar of the farmhouse in Woodhurst.\
\
You should return to Herubrand to inform him of your success in bringing aid from Gapholt and defeating the White Hand forces in Mate Isernore.","Thane Nothmar is ready to aid Woodhurst, as he promised. He will depart for Woodhurst shortly after speaking with those who will coordinate the defence of Gapholt during his absence.","Travel to Mate Isernore","Defeat the White Hand forces at Mate Isernore (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Mate Isernore is along the road between Gapholt and Woodhurst.\
\
Mate Isernore was once a mine owned by Gifemund, but was taken by the White Hand who crossed the Swiftwater River.","Talk to Herubrand","'I have gathered the men, and they await my order to depart. I must speak with those who are coordinating the defence while I am gone.\
\
'You seem eager to return to Woodhurst... feel free to depart when you are ready, and we will meet you there. I am a man of honour and will keep my word.'"},
[12569]={"Cinders dance, and all is quiet (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Long Wait","Soldiers can be found at Adambel.\
\
You should talk with the soldiers to pass the time.","'We wait for battle, and the wait is long. It seems longer still when the air is quiet and nothing moves! I must have patience, but I am not the only one who is restless. Look around you, and you will see many others grow weary of this endless waiting!\
\
'Let us brighten their spirits and take the stillness from their minds. How, you ask? Why, stoke the fires and share some stories. It will make the wait feel shorter.'","Fire pits can be found at Adambel.\
\
You should stoke the fires.","Stoke the fires (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk with the soldiers at Adambel (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talked with soldiers (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Habhûk can be found at Adambel.\
\
You should talk to Habhûk.","Habhûk does not like to remain idle for too long. The lull in battle has him on edge.","'For the first time in many days, I heard the low rumble of pleasant talk! There were tales of battles gone, happy memories of children, wives, and husbands waiting at home, loved ones all. Good memories were shared. Did you hear the same?\
\
'We have lasted this long, friend. One day this siege will end, but if it is not to be today, we will not let the passage of another restless day drive us to madness, and give the lie to those already spent. We will wait. One day we will win, and this waiting will be worth it.'","Talk to Habhûk"},
[12570]={"Niko se encuentra en Jänis-leiri, al oeste de Leijona-kotin.\
\
Deberías regresar con Niko y comunicarle tu éxito.","'Has demostrado ser un aliado valioso, Sivullinen. ¿Quizá podrías ayudarnos con una última tarea?\
\
'Cerca de aquí, en una zona boscosa que llamamos Leijona-kotin, habitan muchos kalpa-kita. Son bestias feroces y matan tanto a animales como a Lumi-väki. Quiero que vayas allí y reduzcas su número. Tal vez así se contenga cualquier agresión futura por su parte.\
\
'Encontrarás Leijona-kotin al este de aquí. Asegúrate de matar a su líder, al que llamamos Pitkä-hammas.'","'¿Él... está muerto? ¿De verdad? ¿Pitkä-hammas ha muerto?\
\
'Puedes regresar con Ora y decirle que su Maestro de la Caza te considera un cazador hábil, ${PLAYER}.'","Niko te ha desafiado a cazar a los kalpa-kita que acechan en Leijona-kotin, una zona boscosa al este de Jänis-leiri.","'¡Bien hecho! ¿Te guardaste un colmillo para ti?'","Los kalpa-kita pueden encontrarse en Leijona-kotin, al este de Jänis-leiri.\
\
Niko quiere que reduzcas el número de kalpa-kita de la zona y que, en especial, derrotes a un felino feroz llamado Pitkä-hammas.","Los colmillos más largos","Pitkä-hammas derrotado","'Encontrarás Leijona-kotin al este de aquí. Asegúrate de matar a su líder, al que llamamos Pitkä-hammas.'","Derrota a los kalpa-kita (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Kalpa-kita derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Habla con Niko","¡Has ganado la confianza del Maestro de la Caza de los Lossoth!","Derrota a Pitkä-hammas"},
[12571]={"The Looming Strife","Porókho would like to speak with you privately. Porókho is in Hêbatokh, the clan Morutágya camp in Ilmabiri, beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.","Talk to Belondor in Dâr Laja","After helping the grateful Morutágya clan with their requests, you feel that you have been dismissed. You should return to Belondor in Dâr Laja, the Meeting Hall and tell him what you learned.","Your work in the southern part of Ilmabiri, the sewers beneath the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl, appears to be complete.","'Welcome back, ${PLAYER}. What news do you bring?'\
\
You tell Belondor of the reaction of the Morutágya clan to the confirmation of Tumúldo's death, and the warning that there will be clan infighting for leadership. Belondor nods.\
\
'This sort of thing is not terribly common, but it isn't unheard of either. The Kindred will keep an eye on the situation. I will also learn what I can of this Umisúm person you spoke of. If she does manage to step up, she could become an important player in the politics of the city.\
\
'Thank you for your help, as always ${PLAYER}.'","'Come, ${PLAYER}, I would speak with you privately.'","Talk to Porókho","Porókho pulls you aside and speaks to you quietly.\
\
'I want to thank you for humouring us with these tasks. Even Gajóta,' he says with a warm chuckle. 'We really should get him a cat. Unfortunately, dark times lie ahead for us Morutágya. Tumúldo was our leader by right of birth, but he was also a great hero to our people and was well-loved. We would have readily followed Nakási, but she seems to have abandoned us for that khmêg Azagath.\
\
You can see on his face that Nakási's flight weighs heavy upon his heart.\
\
'They have a child, Umisúm, who would now be our leader by right of birth, but she will not go unchallenged. She is in her teen years and has yet to prove herself to our people. I hope for her sake that she is as cunning as her father and as fierce as her mother or she may not make it to adulthood. You know how families are.\
\
'I wanted to thank you for bringing us the letter from that ugly Gondorian. It is better to know than to be left wondering. There are difficult times ahead for all Morutágya, but we have survived worse. Now go. Leave these sewers and visit the baths. You stink.'\
\
He waves you off and you are clearly being dismissed."},
[12572]={"'We Iron-folk have turned the tide! Azog's doom is at hand!\
\
'It is time, Hermáth. My father leads our people to the gates of Moria. Let the coward answer at last for what he has done!\
\
'We are needed in the final charge, my friend! Come on!'","Talk to King Thráin at Muru Azog","'Swiftly now, my friend!'","Talk to Dáin at Muru Azog","Dáin can be found just outside Muru Azog at Azanulbizar.\
\
Azog has been slain at last, but victory was won at great cost. You should talk to Dáin.","'It is done! Azog is slain and the shade of my father might at last find peace!'\
\
King Thráin looks about Muru Azog, noting the countless dead Orcs arrayed before the gates of Moria.\
\
'Once the gates of Khazad-dûm are free of this Orkish filth, there will be time to consider where next our path leads.\
\
'May the name Azog be forgotten to the Orcs!'","King Thráin can be found just outside Muru Azog at Azanulbizar.\
\
Azog has been slain at last, but Dáin has fallen silent. You should talk to King Thráin.","The Lord of Moria","Talk to Dáin","After the horn-call of Grór sounded, Náin and the Dwarves of the Iron Hills charged forth to challenge Azog and put an end to the battle.","Dáin says nothing, his face still pale and etched with unease.","Dáin can be found at Durin's Stone.\
\
After overcoming Azog's forces at Durin's Stone, Náin Orcsfoe and the Iron-folk prepare to again make for the gates of Moria. You should talk to Dáin."},
[12573]={"Defeat Easterlings in the Brotherhood of the Pinioned (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El Señor de los Pinos","Followers of the Brotherhood of the Pinioned can be found throughout Osgiliath, and often wander far from their Easterling brethren.\
\
You recall Echil's mentioning of a \\qLord of Pinions\\q among the Easterlings who now form a brotherhood under him. You should seek out and defeat his followers to learn more of his whereabouts.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: You must defeat all five groups of Easterling followers to unlock the optional Lord of Pinions encounter.</rgb>","Defeated Easterlings in the Brotherhood of the Pinioned (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Lord of Pinions can be found in the north-eastern corner of Osgiliath.\
\
You have weakened the Brotherhood of the Pinioned, and should now confront the Lord of Pinions in Osgiliath.","Reuniendo un pequeño pero ferozmente leal grupo de seguidores entre las fuerzas de los Orientales gracias a su inexplicable afinidad con los crebain, un hombre extraño ha llegado a Osgiliath y busca desatar sus talentos contra aquellos que lo negarían.","Defeat the Lord of Pinions"},
[12574]={"Habla con Glavroleth en Echad Dúnnan","Gâmzhurm derrotado","'¡Los dunlendinos pronto serán expulsados de Eregion, gracisa a ${PLAYER}!'","El uruk Gâmzhurm se encuentra al sur y ligeramente al oeste de Echad Dúnann, al otro lado del Nan Sirannon.\
\
Debes usar el cuerno de desafío para invocar a Gâmzhurm, el líder de los dunlendinos, y derrotarle.","Glavroleth está en Echad Dúnann, al norte y ligeramente al este de Porth Cadlus.\
\
Deberías volver a ver a Glavroleth con las noticias de la muerte de Gâmzhurm.","'Aunque los dunlendinos fueron debilitados con nuestro asalto, no se han marchado de Eregion. Hay algo más que les mantiene aquí y dirige sus ataques.\
\
'Uno de los exploradores interceptó a uno de los dunlendinos que había desertado desu campamento. Le habló de un uruk-hai de Saruman que lidera el campamento y conduce a los dunlendinos a la locura.\
\
'Regresa a Porth Cadlus y desafía a este uruk a combate singular. Si se le derrota, muchos dunlendinos abandonarán las armas y volverán a su tierra natal.'","Los dunlendinos siguen en Eregion a pesar de su derrota, lo que indica la presencia de un poderoso líder.","'Deberías encontrar un cuerno en el campamento dunlendino para desafiar al uruk.'","El señor de Porth Cadlus","Utiliza el cuerno de desafío para invocar a Gâmzhurm y derrótale","'Con su líder derrotado, los dunlendinos no continuarán su asalto. Te lo agradezco de corazón, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[12575]={"Soltakh está en Fail-á-Khro, al norte de Aughaire y al sur de Dún Covád.\
\
Has derrotado a Gillë Andras, el Señor de las Marcas Occidentales, y ahora deberías llevar la noticia de tu triunfo a Soltakh.","'Gillë Andras probablemente ya ha sido enviado a Dún Covád; si atacas rápidamente, tú y tus aliados pueden enfrentarlo sin sus defensas.\
\
Dún Covád se encuentra en las colinas occidentales al norte de Fail-á-Khro.'","'¡Tus grandes hazañas han salvado a Aughaire de las garras de los Angmarim!'","'¡Si las órdenes que has plantado hacen su trabajo, el líder de los ejércitos que ahora amenazan Fasach-falroid puede estar ya condenado, ${PLAYER}, y ni siquiera saberlo! Se llama Gillë Andras, y es el Señor de las Marcas Occidentales.\
\
Incluso ahora, probablemente esté recibiendo sus nuevas órdenes: viajar a Dún Covád con una pequeña escolta para monitorear a los orcos en esa ciudad bajo su mando. Dejará las sólidas defensas de su mando en Donnvail y vendrá a las menores defensas de Dún Covád. Con tus aliados, puedes adentrarte en Dún Covád, al norte de aquí en las colinas occidentales, y derrotar a Gillë Andras aparte de sus lugartenientes. ¡A medida que este plan madura, Soltakh demuestra su valía! ¡Que Drostan sea olvidado!\
\
Derrota al Señor de las Marcas Occidentales, ${PLAYER}. Este golpe será un gran golpe para los Trév Gállorg, si tú y tus aliados pueden verlo hecho.'","Gillë Andras, el Señor de las Marcas Occidentales, se encuentra en la ciudad de Dún Covád, en las colinas occidentales al norte de Fail-á-Khro.\
\
Soltakh te ha pedido a ti y a tus aliados que derrotes a Gillë Andras, el Señor de las Marcas Occidentales.","'¡Nuestro plan se ha cumplido, ${PLAYER}, y has traído gran alegría a Soltakh, \\qEl Que Es Cambiado\\q!\
\
¡Ya estoy empezando a olvidar a Drostan! Hemos hecho grandes cosas hoy, ${PLAYER:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} , y te lo agradezco.'","¡Soltakh ha arreglado el traslado de Gillë Andras, el Señor de las Marcas Occidentales, a Dún Covád, donde se le puede enfrentar en condiciones más igualitarias!","El señor de las Marcas Occidentales"},
[12576]={"Talk to Malthellam in Morlad","Darkened by the absence of those lost in the War of the Ring, the Blackroot Vale has become a grim and mournful place, but hope remains that this new peace portends a better future under the rule of King Elessar.","'Halt!\
\
'By Lord Duinhir's edict, none are to enter the Blackroot Vale without his permission or without dire need. It is my duty to inform you that all others must be turned away, with my truest apologies. Have you an invitation from the Lord or some suitable cause for entrance?'\
\
You inform the guard that you have come to the Blackroot Vale on behalf of King Elessar. A flash of concern washes over the guard's face and he stammers as he begins to speak again.\
\
'I... yes... of course, you may enter the Blackroot Vale. Lord Duinhir bids a... gracious welcome... to King Elessar and all of his emissaries from Gondor... and the lands beyond!'\
\
The guard appears to have finally steadied himself, and he appears impressed with himself for managing such a diplomatic speech unrehearsed.\
\
'Even so, I must ask that you speak to the Steward of the Vale, Malthellam, in the town of Morlad, and seek his permission to remain in the Blackroot Vale. And, if it does not trouble you, please offer my apologies to the King for delaying you in your errand!'","Malthellam can be found outside his home in Morlad in the Blackroot Vale.\
\
You have been told to travel to Morlad to seek an audience with the Steward of the Vale, Malthellam, and gain the Lord's permission to remain in the Blackroot Vale.","'Ah, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'It has been some time since you were last in the Blackroot Vale, has it not? Much has changed, though I fear not all of it for the better, despite Gondor's victory in the War. Tingobel, at least, has been rebuilt after we routed what remained of the Orcs. But there will time enough to speak of these things, I think. It is my duty to inform you that the Vale does not allow for travellers without the permission of the Lord or without some suitable cause. Why have you returned?'\
\
You inform Uidor that you have come to the Blackroot Vale on behalf of King Elessar.\
\
'I see. That is cause enough for me, and I have not forgotten the deeds you've done for the good of the Vale. I will not stand in the way of your duties, my friend. If you wish to speak to someone on the authority of the King, you should talk to Malthellam. You remember him, do you not? He was the Steward of the Vale while Lord Duinhir served in the War, and though Lord Duinhir has returned, Malthellam has kept his role as steward and advisor while the Lord and Lady remain in grieving for their sons. If your business should demand an audience with the Lord and Lady, so be it, but for all other matters, I would not have you trouble him.\
\
'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}. May your errands be swift!'","'${PLAYER}...\
\
'It is good to see you well, and it gladdens my heart to know that you survived that terrible war with Mordor. The Blackroot Vale lost many—too many—of its sons in the defence of Minas Tirith and the battles that followed, as I am certain you know well. I must admit that I did not expect you to return to the Blackroot Vale so soon. You are, of course, welcome to remain here as long as you wish. Lord Duinhir has matters of his own to tend to, but I have the authority to grant you his permission. I must ask, though, what business brings you here?'\
\
You inform Malthellam that you have returned to the Blackroot Vale on behalf of King Elessar, who travels Gondor to see his new kingdom. Malthellam nods, but you sense a hesitance behind his gaze.\
\
'You must pardon my candor, but perhaps it is best that you have come in King Elessar's stead. The Vale mourns, and though it may indeed be a new time of peace, my people have found little of it.'","The Lord's Edict"},
[12577]={"The Lost Croft","Scavenged Orc-caches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Orcs can be found at the southernmost croft of Garsfeld, south-west of the town.\
\
Gísil wants you to take back the southernmost croft of Garsfeld.","Defeated Orcs at the southern croft (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Scavenge Orc-caches (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Gísil","Gísil can be found inside the Mead Hall of Garsfeld.\
\
You should return to Gísil with news of your success.","'The death of these Orcs has brought us nothing, except the smallest amount of time. My delay has cost my people dearly....\
\
'I need time to think, ${PLAYER}. Leave me.'","'${PLAYER}, to the south is one of our largest farmsteads. Since we know that the Orcs have already begun to invade from the south, I fear for anyone still dwelling there.\
\
'While they resisted my order to seek shelter in Garsfeld, I will not leave them behind when the rest of the crofters depart.\
\
'Travel to the south and fend off the Orcs... at least long enough to see if any have survived. I can only hope we are not too late....'","Gísil fears that the Orcs have already sacked the southernmost croft completely, but wants to try to gather any stragglers before the long journey south.","Defeat Orcs at the southern croft (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12578]={"'¿Qué? ¿Has venido del oeste para ayudarnos? ¡Habla con Avar de inmediato!'","'¿Las historias son ciertas? Entonces, ¡habla con alguien dentro de este \\qGabilshathûr\\q de inmediato!'","Hay muchos enanos dentro de Gabilshathûr.\
\
Has descubierto el asentamiento oculto de los enanos en Angmar, Gabilshathûr. Deberías hablar con alguien dentro del asentamiento y transmitir el mensaje de Torcuil.","'Si buscas la verdad detrás de las historias que he oído sobre los enanos perdidos, deberás cruzar Rammas Deluon y buscar su asentamiento al sur de Duvuinen.'","'¿Has venido por petición de los Montañeses del oeste? Bien, bien, alguien que no es nuestro enemigo, sino un amigo... o eso espero.\
\
'Supongo que fue una locura que nosotros, los enanos, viniéramos aquí hace años, pero estábamos hartos del dominio de los Duramano y dejamos Othrikar con la esperanza de encontrar gemas y minerales. En ese momento, el mal de Angmar estaba dormido, y más tarde prestamos muy poca atención a su creciente poder. Cuando sus ejércitos de orcos marcharon desde Carn Dûm, quedamos aislados.\
\
'Ahora estamos presionados por todos lados y podríamos usar tu ayuda si queremos sobrevivir en estas tierras malditas. No podemos ofrecerte mucho a cambio, pero si sobrevivimos, quizás algún día podamos aportar nuestra fuerza para derribar a Angmar.'","Habla con el líder de Gabilshathûr.","El asentamiento enano está al este de Rammas Deluon y al sur de Duvuinen.\
\
El mercader Torcuil te pidió que busques a los enanos perdidos y obtengas su alianza.","Encuentra el asentamiento oculto de los enano","Los Enanos Perdidos","'¿Has cruzado Rammas Deluon? La gente amistosa escasea por aquí, así que me alegra verte. Deberías informar a Avar que has llegado... estará muy complacido de verte.'","Torcuil agradeció la ayuda que has brindado a su gente y te contó que necesitan aliados adicionales si quieren sobrevivir bajo el duro dominio de Angmar. Te habló de una historia que ha escuchado sobre enanos que viven bajo la sombra de Angmar, y se pregunta si podrían convertirse en aliados en el futuro.","'Has hecho mucho por ayudarnos aquí en Tyrn Lhuig. No nos resulta fácil aceptar ayuda. De hecho, no hace tanto que habríamos rechazado tal ofrecimiento, pero ante el creciente poder de Angmar, esa ayuda es necesaria si queremos sobrevivir.\
\
'Aunque no soy un líder entre mi gente, puedo ver que necesitamos aliados.\
\
'Esos aliados podrían encontrarse al este, si las historias son ciertas. Se dice que más allá de Rammas Deluon hay un asentamiento enano. Podrían ser buenos aliados para mi pueblo contra Angmar en el futuro.'"},
[12579]={"'¿Qué? ¿Has venido del oeste para ayudarnos? ¡Habla con Avar de inmediato!'","'¿Has venido por orden de los Hombres del oeste? Bien, bien, alguien que no es ${PLAYERNAME:nuestro enemigo, sino un amigo...[m]|nuestra enemiga, sino una amiga...[f]} o eso espero.\
\
'Supongo que fue una locura para nosotros los enanos venir aquí hace años, pero estábamos hartos de la tiranía de los Puños Bourrus y dejamos Othrikar con la esperanza de encontrar gemas y minerales. En ese momento, el mal de Angmar estaba dormido, y más tarde prestamos poca atención a su creciente poder. Una vez que sus ejércitos de orcos marcharon desde Carn Dûm, nos quedamos aislados.\
\
'Ahora estamos acorralados por todos lados y podríamos usar tu ayuda si queremos sobrevivir en estas tierras desoladas. No podemos ofrecerte mucho a cambio, pero si sobrevivimos, tal vez algún día podamos prestar nuestra fuerza para derrocar a Angmar!'","'¿Las historias son ciertas? Entonces, ¡habla con alguien dentro de este \\qGabilshathûr\\q de inmediato!'","Búdan te ha dicho que hay otras personas que podrían necesitar tu ayuda en Angmar. Se habla de una enclave oculta de los enanos al este de Rammas Deluon. Si la leyenda es cierta, los enanos se han escondido bien, pero Búdan teme que Angmar no tarde mucho en descubrirlos.","El líder de los enanos se encuentra en Gabilshathûr.\
\
Has descubierto Gabilshathûr, el enclave secreto de los enanos en Angmar. Busca al líder de los enanos e intenta hablar con él.","'Si buscas la verdad detrás de las historias de los enanos de las que te hablé, tendrás que cruzar Rammas Deluon y buscar su asentamiento al sur de Duvuinen.'","Habla con el líder de Gabilshathûr.","Encuentra el asentamiento oculto de los enanos","'Te debemos mucho, ${PLAYER}. Nos has dado la esperanza de que algún día podremos librarnos del yugo de Angmar. Sin embargo, hay otros en estas tierras que también necesitan esa esperanza.\
\
'Hay rumores de que hay enanos al este de Rammas Deluon. Si es cierto, se han escondido allí durante mucho tiempo, pero a medida que Angmar extiende su mano, pronto podrían descubrir que ya no pueden esconderse.\
\
'Si deseas descubrir si estas historias son ciertas, viaja más allá de Rammas Deluon y busca a estos enanos perdidos. El salón de los enanos debería estar en algún lugar al sur de Duvuinen.'","Los Enanos Perdidos","'¿Has cruzado Rammas Deluon? La gente amistosa escasea por aquí, así que me alegra verte. Deberías informar a Avar que has llegado... estará muy complacido de verte.'","El enclave de los enanos se encuentra al este de Rammas Deluon y al sur de Duvuinen.\
\
Búdan te habló de un enclave oculto de los enanos en Angmar y sugiere que los enanos podrían necesitar tu ayuda."},
[12580]={"A small party of explorers set off for Dannenglor and have not yet returned, and Fernachar is anxious for word of their fate.","Talk to Fernachar at the Haunted Inn","'Dannenglor is to the north. You should follow the road there, for that is the path our friends took when they ventured thither.'","Los exploradores perdidos","Dannenglor is to the north of the Haunted Inn.\
\
Fernachar has asked you to search the ruins of Dannenglor for signs of the Elf-scouts who went that way. You should approach Dannenglor cautiously, following the road where the Elf explorers went.","Search near Dannenglor for the Malledhrim scouts","This blade surely belonged to an Elf, but it lies near a great stain of blood","'Hail, ${CLASS}; welcome to our meagre establishment. It is not much, but it is safer than the wild woods beyond that door. I hope you will be careful when you venture out again -- a small party of our own went out to explore, and they have not returned.\
\
'I will not deny that I am very worried for them. They espied the Elf-ruins to the north of here, which, if memory serves, was once the fair Elven-realm of Dannenglor. They left some days ago, and I fear the worst....\
\
'Will you search for them, and scout the ruins so that we know what we are up against? Be very careful -- I do not wish you to meet the same fate that they met.'","Fernachar awaits you in the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks, south of Dannenglor.\
\
You should speak with Fernachar and tell him of the worrying scene you beheld when you approached Dannenglor.","'Alas! This does not bode well. My fears are all but confirmed. Oh, ${PLAYER}...do you think there is any hope?'"},
[12581]={"'Hemos tenido muchos viajeros extraños en estas tierras, aunque ninguno tan extraño como la comunidad que recientemente pasó por Aughaire, buscando la tierra de Forochel. Esa tierra se encuentra al norte y al oeste de esta tierra, aunque nunca he visto las montañas de nieve, ni las costas congeladas del mar.\
\
'Tenían un viejo mapa que afirmaba que antiguas minas de enanos llenas de tesoros se encuentran en algún lugar dentro de la tierra de Forochel. Si viajaras a esas tierras, te pediría que buscaras a uno de su compañía y le brindaras ayuda si puedes. No parecían una compañía muy capaz, y me aliviaría saber que alguien como tú los cuidaría.\
\
'Forochel se encuentra al norte de Evendim, a través de Cirith Rhiw, al norte de Tyrn Fornech. Deberías comenzar tu búsqueda en el pueblo de Kauppa-kohta.'","'¿Has encontrado a la comunidad perdida? Deberías comenzar tu búsqueda en Kauppa-kohta. Escuché que discutían sobre ese pueblo como su primer destino.'","La comunidad perdida","Forochel se encuentra al norte de Evendim, a través de Cirith Rhiw, al norte de Tyrn Fornech. Deberías comenzar tu búsqueda en el pueblo de Kauppa-kohta.\
\
Helegdir te ha pedido que busques a un miembro de una comunidad de aventureros que se dirigió al Forochel, pasando por Aughaire, en Angmar.","'¿Helegdir te envió para asegurarse de que estuviéramos a salvo? Sí, sí, eso está muy bien, pero no es mi culpa, ¿sabes? Esos otros tontos se perdieron. Si tuviera mi cuervo, las cosas serían muy diferentes.'","Habla con Cenlieg","Helegdir te ha pedido que le ayudes a velar por la seguridad de un grupo de individuos conocidos como la Comunidad Perdida.","'Gracias por buscar a la comunidad perdida, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[12582]={"Gilanor of Ost Lontir seeks to assault the Corsair forces stationed at Edhellond, and has sent his scout, Dolvir, to learn more of their plots.","'Ah, you must be ${PLAYER}... Gilanor told me you would arrive soon.\
\
'It will not take you long to see what peril faces Gondor down in the Elf-haven. The Corsairs have moored three ships full of men, and have pillaged Edhellond to nearly nothing.\
\
'We must move quickly to save the history here, and even more quickly should we hope to quell the Corsair threat.'","DNT -- will not be seen","'We have weakened their forces near the beacon, we know their movements, and we know of their leadership... now is the time to strike at the heart of their force in Edhellond!\
\
'While you aided me, I sent a scout named Dolvir to observe the Corsairs moored at the Elf-haven. Seek him out, and aid him in ridding the coast of Corsairs. I will not allow that Umbarian filth to lay any further claim to our lands.\
\
'Go, ${PLAYER}! May we fight alongside one another before this war comes to an end!'","Dolvir can be found on a hilltop to the east of Edhellond.\
\
Gilanor has asked you to seek Dolvir outside Edhellond in hopes you can weaken the Corsairs' hold on the coast.","Talk to Dolvir","The Lost Harbour"},
[12583]={"'Please stranger, help me!'","Find Umfrë in the Mournshaws","You have rescued Umfrë","Talk to Umfrë at Echad Daervunn","'I would be grateful if you could find Umfrë and assure his safety.'","The Lost Hunter","Daervunn has befriended a Dunlending hunter by the name of Umfrë on the fringes of the Mournshaws after the hunter rescued him from a pack of vicious hounds. However, Umfrë has recently disappeared into the Mournshaws after giving chase to one of the hounds, and Daervunn is concerned that he may be in some danger...or even dead.","'Umfrë the hunter it was, who rescued me from a ravening pack of strange white hounds shortly after I entered the forest -- Cun Annun, he called them.\
\
'He seems a good Man, though when he realized I was a northerner he seemed dismayed. Nevertheless, he helped me tend my wound, and I had hoped to ask for his services as a guide through these woods. He left, though, in search of one of these hounds that he said had been terrorizing the people of his village of late. Yet a full day has since passed, and I have seen no sign of him. I fear he too may have been injured or killed beneath the forest's eaves.\
\
'My leg is still not fit to walk -- if you could find Umfrë and help him return here, I would be obliged, as I owe him a debt, and he may be the only one who can help us through this forest.'","Umfrë is lost somewhere in the Mournshaws.\
\
Daervunn asked you to find Umfrë the hunter, who disappeared into the forest, hunting for a Cun Annun that had been terrorizing his village.","Umfrë is at Echad Daervunn in the Mournshaws.\
\
You should return to Daervunn's camp and speak with Umfrë.","'My thanks to you, Duvodiad.\
\
'These woods have grown more dangerous than ever in recent days. These Cun Annun that hunt and kill Men and beast alike are a terror from our old wives' tales.\
\
'I do not know in truth what brings your people here, but I also in truth do not care to. Whatever your purpose, unless it is to bring harm to my people, I will help you if I may.'"},
[12585]={"Mapa minero de los Duramano reunido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El Capataz Nyrad puede encontrarse en el campamento duramano al norte de Othrikar. Regin está en Othrikar.\
\
Regin cree que Nyrad, el capataz anterior, robó el mapa, pero dejó los registros, ya que no podía leer las runas. Regin ha sugerido que podrías encontrar el mapa en la tienda del Capataz Nyrad o en el propio Nyrad.","Has encontrado el mapa robado por el Capataz Nyrad.","Obtén el mapa minero de los Duramano (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Las runas en los antiguos registros mineros hacen referencia a un mapa que parece estar perdido.","El mapa perdido","Devuelve el mapa a Regin.","'Creo que el mapa debe haber sido tomado por los Duramano. Deben haber dejado los antiguos registros que encontraste porque no podían leerlos. Pero apostaría a que el mapa está en manos del capataz duramano que solía tener mi puesto.\
\
'A menos que me equivoque, diría que el Capataz Nyrad está con muchos de los otros Duramano en su campamento al norte.\
\
'Es mucho pedir, pero si puedes recuperar ese mapa del Capataz Nyrad, ¡creo que al fin podremos encontrar el filón principal! Sospecho que encontrarás el mapa en un cofre dentro de la tienda del Capataz Nyrad en el campamento, aunque también podría llevarlo consigo.'","'¡Lo has encontrado! Es una noticia maravillosa. Déjame ver, déjame ver.'"},
[12586]={"Cabed has asked you to find something very important to him that he hid near Ost Celebrant during the Battle of the Field of Celebrant.","'So, you have found it. Thank you, I never thought I would see this again. This arrow was to be the symbol of our plight to the North-men. I was sent to deliver it at any cost, but I...I just could not do it.\
\
'I feared death, and now see what my cowardice has brought me. I later learned that one of the messengers survived and made it to the north...my shame has only grown.\
\
'But enough of this, there is more to be done.'","Cabed is atop a small hill along the southern road of Parth Celebrant.\
\
You should bring the red-tipped arrowhead to Cabed.","Cabed has sent you in search of a trinket he once carried. The trinket is located somewhere outside Ost Celebrant.","Find Cabed's lost trinket","The Lost Message","Talk to Cabed","'Have you found my lost trinket?'","'To understand the doom falling upon the Field of Celebrant, you must first understand our past.\
\
'Long ago, the kingdom of Gondor was besieged by a Horde of terrible Easterlings. They had forded the Great River at the Undeeps and sought to crush our forces here before sweeping into Gondor proper. While we fought valiantly, there was nothing we could do to stop the onslaught of Easterlings. My fellows and I were sent north to seek the aid of the North-men in desperation.\
\
'With us, we each carried a trinket. Before I fell, I buried the trinket in hopes that my failure would be forgotten. However, having returned, I know that can never be the case. I would ask that you seek it out. I buried it just outside the walls of Ost Celebrant. Perhaps it still remains there.'","You have found the rotting remains of a red-tipped arrow"},
[12587]={"Find the lost pages of the tome","'${PLAYER}, I will trust you with this task because you have been a friend to my people before. I want you to find the Secret Stone and return it to me. \
\
'The warnings were clear. This is a dangerous and powerful artifact. But, I believe the risk to be worth the danger. The craftsmanship of my people is fading, and we are desperate to find a solution. An ancient artifact of Khazad-dûm may BE that solution! At the same time, it worries me that this secret knowledge was just left out for anyone to find. Someone may have sinister intentions for it.\
\
'This may be an impossible task. For all we know, the Stone may be lost forever. But, should you manage to find it, please bring it to me. Perhaps the place to start is these missing pages. See if you can find any of them here, in Erebor.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> This difficult treasure hunt will require community teamwork and resources outside of the game itself. Good luck! </rgb>","King Thorin III thinks the lost pages of the tome may point the way to the Secret Stone.\
\
Perhaps one of the pages is inside Erebor.","Completado.","The missing pages of the tome have given you many clues to follow, but this is not the end of your adventure. The Secret Stone awaits!","King Thorin III thinks the lost pages of the tome may point the way to the Secret Stone.\
\
You should follow the clues of the rune scraps.","The Lost Pages","Completado","'Binakhrâm? That is our word for the Nameless. It sounds like you are on the right track!'","King Thorin III has asked you to try to locate an ancient relic known as the Secret Stone. But what dangers did the poem warn about? Can you solve this mystery on your own?\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This difficult treasure hunt will require community teamwork and resources outside of the game itself. Good luck! </rgb>"},
[12588]={"Talk to Náin the Slakeless","Deep in the Howling Pit, you found a strange artifact.","The Lost Pendant","Give Ashmâr-abân to Náin the Slakeless","'Hail, ${PLAYER}. What brings you to Járnfast?'\
\
You show Lord Náin the strange pendant you found in the Howling Pit.\
\
'Now where did you find that? I had thought it lost forever! Ashmâr-abân is an ancient heirloom of my line, passed down with the Black Mattock, to be forever held by the Lord of the Iron Hills. Perhaps I should say that was the idea, but it was lost with Lord Grár. I would never have thought it would one day be recovered from that foul pit, but here it is. Truly, it is a miracle. Here, let me show you its true form.'","The pendant you found in the Howling Pit has been revealed to be a lost artifact of Durin's Folk.\
\
You should give Ashmâr-abân to Náin the Slakeless.","Náin takes the pendant from you, holds it close to his heart, and murmurs something in Khuzdul you can't quite hear. The pendant begins to glow with a soft light. At the same time you notice that the pendant also emits a low tone, a soft humming sound. Náin hands it back to you.","The pendant gently thrums in your hand. Some ancient magic has awoken within it.\
\
'Ashmâr-abân has awoken once more. It belongs to you now. May it be a guiding light in the darkness.'","Ashmâr-abân has been transformed!\
\
You should talk to Náin the Slakeless."},
[12589]={"The Rohirrim must surely be nearby. You should try to find this Man, and see if he has strength enough to return to Walstow.","Winsig will be most interested to learn of this man's assault against you. \
\
Winsig can be found in the mead-hall of Walstow.","The Rohirrim snaps out of his stupor and looks deeply perplexed","Talk to Aldstan","You have happened upon more of the missing Rohirrim's belongings. If he can be found, Winsig would surely like to know of his findings at the East Wall.","'I know not what horror seized control of his mind like that. Once he wakes, I will speak with him.\
\
'Thank you for bringing him back to Walstow - I only hope that he shall recover from such a thing.'","Talk to Winsig","'No! Stay away from me!\
\
'My head... you meant to hurt me, he said! You are no saviour of Rohan!\
\
'Mordor will bring us glory, and you stand in the way!'","You have found more of the Rohirrim's trappings. You should seek out the Rohirrim nearby, and see if he has survived the Orc attacks.","The Lost Scout"},
[12590]={"'You have spoken to Coldan? He has decided to depart and take this news to Lothlórien. While I do not blame him for his excitement, I do wish that Coldan had consulted me first. My young apprentice has much to learn.\
\
'I assume you have also spoken to Legolas. He shares my impatience to retrieve Aiglos and remove it from Mordor.'","You relay the information to Coldan.\
\
'I cannot believe these words! To think this relic and pride of Elves has been recovered. I know what I must do then. I shall depart at once and inform those in Lothlórien of this news.'","Talk to Hithgol","Hithgol can be found at the Ruins of Díngarth.\
\
You should speak with Hithgol.","'I have seen the spear with my own eyes, ${PLAYER}. Not that I disbelieved you, but you understand it is hard to believe.\
\
'When you are ready to depart, we shall venture again to the site of Aiglos.'","Hithgol is convinced the spear you found is indeed the mythical Aiglos.","Habla con Legolas.","'Legolas has scouted the location of the spear and informed me that it is indeed the lost spear of Aiglos. I understand that you might not share the same enthusiasm as I, but let it be known to you that this relic is of great pride to all Elves. During the Second Age, Gil-galad wielded Aiglos on the slopes of Mount Doom, lending to the defeat of Sauron. I know this, for I was there.\
\
'Go, speak with my apprentice, Coldan. He should hear the news. Also I would like you and Legolas to retrieve the spear.'","The Lost Spear","Talk to Coldan","Coldan can be found at the Udûn Foothold. Legolas can be found at the Ruins of Díngarth.\
\
You should talk to Coldan and Legolas."},
[12591]={"Coloca la estatua de Elendil en el pedestal","La estatua perdida","'Siempre te daremos la bienvenida en Ost Forod, ${PLAYER}.'","'La estatua de Elendil que una vez se alzó en la isla de Tyl Ruinen ya no honra ese lugar con su presencia. Encuentra la estatua, independientemente de la condición en que se encuentre, y devuélvela a su pedestal.'","Hay un pedestal en las islas de Tyl Ruinen, en el medio del lago Nenuial, donde la estatua de Elendil que portas una vez se alzó. Tyl Ruinen está cruzando el lago desde la isla de Tinnudir.\
\
Mientras viajabas para reunirte con Gwindeth, Robin Sotopardo se ha encargado de reconstruir la estatua rota que recuperaste de los saqueadores en Tyrn Fornech. Esta es la estatua que una vez se alzó en Tyl Ruinen.","'Todavía estoy asombrado con este golpe de suerte, ${PLAYER}... ¡que vuelvas justo cuando he terminado de reconstruir la estatua rota de Elendil prueba que hay fuerzas del bien en este mundo que no han abandonado Evendim!\
\
'¡Lleva la estatua a las islas de Tyl Ruinen y devuélvela al lugar que le corresponde!'","'¡${PLAYER}! No pensaba volver a verte tan pronto, pero me alegra haberme equivocado. De hecho, parece que un viento azaroso te haya traído a mí en este día, porque tengo buenas noticias: ¡he terminado de reconstruir la estatua de Elendil de la que me trajiste los fragmentos!\
\
'¿Dices que sabías a dónde pertenecía esta estatua? ¡Maravilloso! ¡Harías bien en devolverla a su lugar, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Te daré la estatua y confiaré en que la coloques en el pedestal donde una vez se alzó. ¿Tyl Ruinen, dices? ¡Muy bien! ¡Ve con cuidado, y terminemos de reparar lo que los saqueadores de Evendim profanaron!'","Robin Sotopardo te ha dado la estatua de Elendil que ha reconstruido a partir de los fragmentos que le trajiste cuando estuviste en Ost Forod.","'¡Me llena de júbilo que juntos hayamos restaurado la estatua perdida de Elendil, ${PLAYER}!'"},
[12592]={"'Mi pico debe de estar todavía en la vieja cueva al sureste, en las Cumbres Invernales.'","Encuentra el pico perdido de Flosi","'Te agradezco por recuperar mi pico, ${PLAYER}'","La cueva está al sudeste del Mansión de Thorin, en las Cumbres Invernales.\
\
Convencido de que estaba cerca de una veta de oro antes de ser expulsado de la cueva, Flosi te pidió que recuperes su pico y que, además, elimines a algunos de los Rascacuevas de la cueva","Flosi está en las escaleras frente a la puerta principal del Mansión de Thorin.\
\
Debes devolverle el pico a Flosi y hacerle saber al viejo minero que ya debería ser seguro regresar a la cueva.","Derrota a los Rascacuevas en la cueva (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¿Puedes guardar un secreto? Estaba explorando una vieja cueva por allí, cuando me atacó una de esas feroces Rascacuevas. En la pelea, accidentalmente dejé mi pico atrás.\
\
'¿Podrías ir a buscar mi pico por mí... y ya que estás, acabar con algunos de esos Rascacuevas, para que pueda seguir excavando en paz?\
\
'La cueva está al sudeste, en las Cumbres Invernales. ¡Date prisa! Creo que estaba cerca de una veta de oro cuando me sacaron de allí'.","Flosi, un enano minero anciano, perdió su pico mientras excavaba en una vieja cueva infestada de Rascacuevas.","'Bueno, puede que la mina esté agotada, ¡pero al menos encontraste mi pico!'","'¡Ah, ahí está! Gracias, ${PLAYER}. Pero tengo malas noticias... un amigo me dijo que esa cueva ya está agotada. No hay más que oro de tontos ahí dentro.\
\
'Pero no te preocupes... ¡algún día encontraré mi propia veta!'","Rascacuevas derrotados en la cueva (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has encontrado el pico de Flosi","La Herramienta Perdida","Devuelve el pico a Flosi","'¿Encontraste mi pico? Lo necesitaré si quiero hallar mi veta. No tienes idea de cuántos años he estado cavando, tratando de encontrar un terreno propio.'"},
[12594]={"Recoge un artefacto antiguo del Ángulo","Narnien se encuentra en Gaerond, en la parte norte del Ángulo.\
\
Deberías llevarle los artefactos antiguos a Narnien.","¿Qué tesoros perdidos yacen bajo la tierra de Haudh Erthaid, la Tumba de los Reinos?","Artefactos antiguos recogidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Recoge artefactos antiguos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El Ángulo ha sido escenario de innumerables batallas a lo largo de los años. ¿Qué tesoros perdidos yacen bajo la tierra de Haudh Erthaid, la Tumba de los Reinos?","Recoge un artefacto antiguo.","Vuelve con Narnien","'¡Qué cosas tan interesantes me has traído! Estoy deseando aprender todo lo que pueda sobre ellas. Gracias por mantenerlas alejadas de quienes no saben apreciar ni su historia ni su valor artístico. Tienes mi agradecimiento'.","Este es un buen lugar para buscar artefactos antiguos","Se pueden encontrar artefactos antiguos en Ost Waeren y Tham Lumren.\
\
La elfa Narnien te había pedido que buscaras artefactos antiguos.","Los tesoros perdidos de Haudh Erthaid"},
[12595]={"'How lucky I am to have been found! Thank you for your aid, friend.'","Find lost refugees in southern Balewood (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Bruises and wide wounds mark this refugee. This must be the work of Wood-trolls...","Talk to Léodwald","'A cave? Oh, thank you... thank you, stranger!'","This refugee met his end at the hands of Orcs...","This refugee of Byre Tor succumbed to the cold...","The Lost of the Balewood","'I am certain that you have heard, but we were not the only ones who fled into the Balewood. Our kinsmen are lost in the forest, and I fear we may never see them again. They are ill-equipped to survive in such conditions, and the Orcs hounded us at every turn.\
\
'From what I have seen of you, you can handle such troubles, my friend.\
\
'If you could, please search for them. When we separated, we were not far from here, but I know not how far they may have wandered in the dark.'","Refugees from Byre Tor have taken shelter in a cave within the Balewood, but not all came there safely.","You have found a refugee of Byre Tor","'The cold bites at me, stranger. I must reach shelter!\
\
'Thank you for finding me in these bleak woods.'","Léodwald has asked you to seek out other refugees that fled into the Balewood and help them find the cave.","'It is sorrowful to hear of the fates that befell some of my kin, ${PLAYER}. This forest is a sorry place to meet one's end... and to such creatures....\
\
'Although I am glad to see these three among our number again, I fear that we, too, are simply awaiting a similar fate here. If you would remain here with us, I am certain there are more ways you can aid us still.'","The cave can be found to the east of the Orc roadway through the Balewood.\
\
You have found the six refugees of which Léodwald spoke. You should return to the cave and inform him of those that fell in the wilds."},
[12596]={"There is much work to do to rebuild the town of Hytbold.","The Lumber Mill: Enhancements I","Bring the Tokens of Hytbold to Oseg","Gather Tokens of Hytbold (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Hytbold is one step closer to being rebuilt and restored.'","'The Lumber-mill has been rebuilt, but there is much to do to get it fully functional and have it look like it belongs within our town. Bunks for the residents, crates and barrels for storage, and tools for the workers are all things that need to be added for the mill to begin full production.'"},
