[12605]={"You have found a mad dwarf in Thorin's Hall that may somehow be related to the Secret Stone.\
\
He asked you to find something in Nud-melek, inside Moria.","The Nauthlandir flower can possibly be found somewhere in Fangorn Forest.\
\
You should find the Nauthlandir flower.","You help the old dwarf drink the elixir. Almost immediately the life returns to his eyes. He blinks a few times, and looks at you, disoriented.\
\
'Where am I? What happened?'\
\
You explain the situation and tell him you think this was caused by the Secret Stone.\
\
'You must be right! That cursed stone! It draws the eye, and then steals your mind! I succumbed in a moment of weakness.... But that must have been years ago.'\
\
You tell him that King Thorin III has bid you find it and deliver it to him.\
\
'Thorin III? He is the son of Dáin Ironfoot? Oh my, it HAS been years. If the King wishes it, it will be so. I am Orring, one of the few to know of the existence of Abnubuzûr, the Secret Stone. I was one of its guards, before the madness took me. You will need to find the key, and the keyhole, but I know not where either are. The stone has surely been moved since my time, but perhaps Rúnvarth still holds the key? Alas, I do not know where to find him, either. I am sorry I could not be more help. Good luck on your quest, ${PLAYER}.'","Talk to Orring","Galathril resides within Lothlórien.\
\
You should talk to Galathril.","Orring can be found in Thorin's Hall.\
\
You should bring the medicine to Orring.","Talk to Galathril","Find the Nauthlandir","Galathril's eyes widen as you hand her the rare flower.\
\
'Incredible, ${PLAYER}! This may be the last Nauthlandir! Just a moment, I will create an elixir from the nectar.'\
\
She deftly extracts a few drops of nectar from the flower into a small glass phial, throws in a handful of dried herbs from a pouch at her hip, and swirls the mixture around. She stops the phial with a cork and hands it to you.\
\
'This will cure your friend's madness. Have him drink it.'\
\
She sighs gently. You see worry in her eyes.\
\
'I feel you are on a dangerous path, friend. Please be careful. I will do my best to grow more Nauthlandir, in the event they are needed.'","King Thorin III has asked you to try to locate an ancient relic known as the Secret Stone. But what dangers did the poem warn about? Can you solve this mystery on your own?\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This difficult treasure hunt will require community teamwork and resources outside of the game itself. Good luck! </rgb>","'Hail, friend. How can I help you?'\
\
You hand her the flower sketch you found in Moria.\
\
'I know this flower, ${PLAYER}.  It is known as Nauthlandir, Thought-clearer. Long ago, I used its powers to heal sicknesses of the mind. But, I'm afraid this species has all but died off as the forests have darkened. You found this in Moria?'\
\
You tell her of the mad dwarf you found whose ramblings led you to this sketch. Her expression turns serious.\
\
'I know the madness you speak of, ${PLAYER}. Before the dwarves were exiled from Moria, they came to us seeking aid. Several of them showed signs of this madness, but they were unable to cure it with their own medicines. It was as if a darkness had taken them and stolen their very minds. They would not speak of the cause, but it was clearly something fell, and powerful.\
\
'If you are able to find the Nauthlandir flower, I will be able to draft a medicine for your dwarf friend. But, I'm afraid I have not seen it for hundreds of years. Seek it in Fangorn Forest. It prefers to grow in the lee of large stones. If you do find it, please gently remove it, roots and all. I may be able to save the species. Good luck.'","Find someone who knows something about the flower sketch","Find a clue in Nud-Melek","The Mad Dwarf","You gently dig up the Nauthlandir flower","Inside Moria, you found an old sketch of a flower.\
\
You should find someone who knows something about this flower.","You have found a very old dwarf, sitting in the dark by himself. His eyes are glazed over, and he rambles to himself.\
\
'The Stone.... The Stone! Where did I?.... Who's there?!'\
\
You manage to calm him down, but he is no less incoherent in his ramblings.\
\
'Nud-melek.... Find it in Nud-melek!'\
\
He slumps down and becomes unresponsive."},
[12606]={"'Málur was captured by White Hand Orcs when he was quite young. He learned their speech and one of their captains taught him to read, finding it entertaining to have a slave speaking those foul words. He escaped some years later, having slipped a dagger into the captain's ribs before he left. He is a scholar now, but you should ask him some day about how many Orcs he slew on his way back to our people.'","Bring the journal to Málur Keenword","'Ah, welcome to Clovengap, ${PLAYER}! There is a dragon nearby!'\
\
You show him the journal and ask if he can read it.\
\
'Most certainly not! I have not wasted precious hours trying to decipher that filth when I could instead be studying dragons. Talk with Málur. In his younger days, while an Orc prisoner, Málur learned their foul language. He may best be able to help you with this text.'","The foul and fell scribblings of a madman may be the key to stopping the further spread of the corrupted crystals.","'Glad I am to hear that the crystals’ corruption did not spread to the sabre-tooth cats.\
\
'I was making headway with this cursed journal, but the writing has slipped into what I believe to be the Black Speech. Here, take the book up to Bazanmanar, and find Lore-master Rúni. He may be able to decipher these fell scrawlings. I shall meet you there.'","Talk to Rúni","The Madman's Journal","Málur Keenword is in Bazanmanar.\
\
Lore-master Rúni has directed you to speak with Málur about the journal.","Rúni is in Bazanmanar.\
\
Mother Amma has asked you to speak to Lore-master Rúni.","'Aye, I am Málur. A journal, you say? Well, give it here.'"},
[12607]={"La ira del guardián de la tumba ha sido apaciguada","Le preguntas a Colbert el Loco qué ocurrió aquí después de que intentara saquear las tumbas de Amon Amrûn.\
\
'Dos entraron y uno salió. Pero yo nunca salí, no realmente. Las sombras que se agitaron cuando tomamos el botín ahora se agitan en mi mente, siempre.\
\
'Nunca podré dejar Amon Amrûn. Como las sombras. Pronto no seré más que un fantasma errante, igual que ellas.'","Dile a Colbert el Loco que las sombras agitadas han vuelto a descansar","Has descubierto un cofre robado que seguramente enfureció a las sombras, y nada menos que el hermano de Colbert... muerto","Colbert te espera en su mirador al sur de Amon Amrûn.\
\
Deberías hablar con Colbert.","Encuentra el cofre de la herencia y devuélvelo a su tumba","'Mi cabeza... ahora está un poco más clara. La niebla se está disipando. Qué extraño.\
\
'Sabes, no fue muy sabio que mi hermano y yo viniéramos aquí y empezáramos a saquear tumbas al azar. Somos cazadores de tesoros profesionales, pero nos separamos del resto del grupo hace unas semanas. Buscábamos las riquezas del viejo Fornost.\
\
'Me pregunto si los demás siguen acampados donde los dejamos....'","La historia del loco","Amon Amrûn se encuentra en los Campos orientales de Fornost en las Quebradas del Norte.\
\
Deberías buscar en Amon Amrûn signos de lo que ocurrió para hacer que Colbert enloqueciera.","Colbert el Loco te ha seguido hasta Amon Amrûn, donde algo le hizo perder la razón tras despertar a las furiosas sombras de su tumba al intentar saquearla."},
[12609]={"'Something has driven to madness the sorcerers of Ordâkh you encountered here in An Shêru, ${PLAYER}. What can be the cause but the Thardúth, newly-awakened and testing their power? During the Dagor Carlanthir, even Inkanûsh struggled to repel the invasive voices of the servants of Morgoth dwelling within Utug-bûr. What ordinary Man of Ordâkh might hope to strive even half so well?\
\
'One of the slain sorcerers has given us a name to investigate: Damudûr. We must learn if this location hides the entrance to a vault of the Thardúth like we discovered at Utug-bûr.\
\
'I have heard mention of a Khanâg to the south-west where travellers gather. We should go to this place and see what we can learn of Damudûr.'","Arshûk is at Khanâg Gur.","Glorfindel asked you to approach Damudûr and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for some sign of the Thardúth.","'It is clear to me from Arshûk's account that the large Orcs he saw from afar were Utûgi. They must serve the Thardúth of Damudûr even as those that slew my brother served the Thardúth of Utug-bûr.\
\
'In Baharúd's memory will I continue to stand beside you, ${PLAYER}. The Utûgi may not fear a Kinta Elf such as Ulishár... but it may be they should.'","Emotion wars upon Arshûk's face as he wrestles with his fear","Ulishár is at Khanâg Gur.","'The Ordâkhai encamp outside Damudûr. They must be searching for something, but what that may be remains unknown to us.\
\
'I found someone who might know something of their purpose, but he is too terrified to speak any further on the subject. He is named Arshûk. Can you convince him to tell us what he saw at Damudûr?'","Retrieved fancy Ordâkhai blade from the camp of Kôth Rau","'What... what is it? What have you done?'\
\
You show Arshûk the fancy blade of Ordâkh and he looks at you in amazement.\
\
'You dared trespass near enough to Damudûr to retrieve this blade? That displays true courage, stranger!'","'I have heard mention of a Khanâg to the south-west where travellers gather. We should go to this place and see what we can learn of Damudûr.'","Glorfindel is at Khanâg Gur.","The Ordâkhai have established the camp of Kôth Rau outside Damudûr","Glorfindel catches your eye","The Madness at Damudûr","Arshûk takes a deep breath and gathers his courage","'Arshûk began to tell Ulishár about something he saw at Damudûr, but then he was overcome with terror and would say nothing more. Whatever he saw, we must prove to him we have the courage to protect him or he will say nothing.\
\
'One common element has emerged from the talk of the people with whom I have spoken, ${PLAYER}. Many of these folk have been impressed by the bright shine of the weapons wielded by the Ordâkhai, and by the gems and jewels that adorn their clothing.\
\
'Perhaps if you retrieve a fancy blade of Ordâkh from the camp of Kôth Rau, Arshûk will see you have the courage to oppose this kingdom, and protect him from its soldiers. Then it may be his tongue will loosen and he will confirm what I have come to suspect: that the Thardúth walk in An Shêru.'","'I want to help you, but... but...'\
\
Arshûk stammers with fright. Only when you place a reassuring hand on his arm does he calm sufficiently to make himself understood.\
\
'If I speak, will you protect me from the terrible creatures that stand behind the Ordâkhai? Can you prove to me you have the courage to oppose them?'","Arshûk stares at you with wild, terrified eyes","Climb the path south of Khanâg Gur toward Damudûr","Arshûk gathers his courage.","'I believe what Arshûk has told to us, but we know more about the Thardúth than he does, through no fault of his own. His fear of them is neither misplaced nor unfounded.\
\
'Nobles of Ordâkh are not accustomed to subservience. For them to behave so in the presence of the Thardúth indicates to me they have some knowledge of their powers or abilities. The Ordâkhai are right to fear them; perhaps they believe such demonstrations will keep the creatures they discovered at Damudûr under control. On this they must be wrong. The Thardúth intend to manipulate the Ordâkhai and seize control of their empire.\
\
'Each of these remain our foes. We will continue to oppose them, even as they prey upon each other. But Arshûk's tale has told me something else of use, ${PLAYER}. The madness that inflicted the others who strayed near Damudûr did not affect Arshûk. The Thardúth must be aware of an individual in order to invade his mind. This may be useful to us.'","'If I speak, will you protect me from the terrible creatures that stand behind the Ordâkhai? Can you prove to me you have the courage to oppose them?'","'As they faded from my view, but not my memory, never my memory, I heard them speak the name \\qEmax Dûl.\\q That is where the terrible creatures must be now, either the guests or the masters of Ordâkh.'","Retrieve a fancy Ordâkhai blade from the camp of Kôth Rau","Talk to Arshûk at Khanâg Gur","Bring the fancy Ordâkhai blade to Arshûk at Khanâg Gur","Glorfindel suggested you meet at Khanâg Gur north of Damudûr.","Meet up with Glorfindel at Khanâg Gur","Glorfindel suspects that Damudûr may have hidden the entrance to a lost vault of the Thardúth.","'Some folk say the cleft is held by Ordâkh, but others claim to experience terror of a deeper nature. You should make your way south and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for yourself, my friend.'","'In Baharúd's memory will I continue to stand beside you, ${PLAYER}. The Utûgi may not fear a Kinta Elf such as Ulishár... but it may be they should.'","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> towards the Ordâkhai camp outside Damudûr","'We were right to come here. Travellers speak of a cleft in the rocks to the south named Damudûr. I have learned little but the name, for stories of that place are muddled and confused. Most folk fear to go that way, but they are unable to explain why they fear it so. Some say the cleft is held by Ordâkh, but others claim to experience terror of a deeper nature.\
\
'You should make your way south, further along the road, and <rgb=#00FF00>look</rgb> for yourself. Ulishár and I will continue to speak to the people here in search of an answer to this central question: do the people fear the presence of Ordâkh at Damudûr, or a deeper evil?'","'It was a few nights ago. Under cover of the darkness, I crept near to the camp of the Ordâkhai soldiers. I thought I might be able to steal some of the unattended swords or other treasures. The Ordâkhai plunder the Ridge of Plenty for its wealth, and have always done so... how have they that right but I do not?\
\
'I was about to slip into the camp when something made me pause. Believe me when I tell you I know this for certain: had I not stayed my feet, I would not be alive today. For as I hesitated, a group of figures emerged from the cleft of Damudûr and passed by the light of a fire. From their attire, I knew four of them to be nobles of Ordâkh, but their manner was striking. Had they not been so richly-dressed I might have thought them servants. They cringed and capered before the two most severe creatures I have ever seen.\
\
'They were tall and gaunt, in appearance like the Kinta Elves you sometimes see throughout the Mûr. But where those folk possess a distant, preoccupied air, from these creatures I felt a sensation of intense hatred. A man and a woman they seemed in appearance, but the feeling of hatred radiating from them struck me as being quite otherworldly. They were flanked on two sides by great Orcs larger than any I have seen before; my blood ran cold and my breath stopped as they drew near to my hiding-place.\
\
'The clowning Ordâkhai nobility guided their companions past the fires and into the darkness of the enveloping night, and as they faded from my view, but not my memory, never my memory, I heard them speak the name \\qEmax Dûl.\\q That is where the terrible creatures must be now, either the guests or the masters of Ordâkh.'","Glorfindel believes that if you retrieve a fancy Ordâkhai blade from Kôth Rau, you will convince Arshûk to tell you what he saw.","Talk to Ulishár at Khanâg Gur","Glorfindel calls you over to him","Talk to Glorfindel at Khanâg Gur","'Perhaps if you retrieve a fancy blade of Ordâkh from Kôth Rau, near to the entrance of the cleft at Damudûr, Arshûk will see you have the courage to protect him. Then it may be his tongue will loosen and he will confirm what I have come to suspect: that the Thardúth walk in An Shêru.'","'I found someone who might know something of their purpose, but he is too terrified to speak. He is named Arshûk. Can you convince him to tell us what he saw at Damudûr?'","Wait for Arshûk to gather his courage","Ulishár is at Khanâg Gur, waiting to speak with you."},
[12611]={"Lady Vanyalos has returned to her hall in Imloth Melui.","Merenir is waiting by the centre fountain in Imloth Melui to speak with you in order to arrange the rescue of Lady Vanyalos.","'You have my thanks, ${PLAYER}, though they are not equal to the good you have performed for me and my house. If only I could tell you it will matter in the days ahead, but I cannot!\
\
'I dreamed I saw my husband Forlong, his hands covered in blood. I saw too my brother Denethor. He wore a fiery crown, and his expression was one of madness! This must mean that my husband is doomed to die, and my brother... I know not, but surely it is an ill omen.\
\
'I was taken by despair, ${PLAYER}, and would have died to the river or to the Orcs if you had not found me. Would that you could save my family from the visions I foresaw!'","Seemingly disturbed, Lady Vanyalos has left Imloth Melui, speaking strangely of dreams and visions to any she passed.","Talk to Merenir by the centre fountain in Imloth Melui","The Madness of Vanyalos","'Lady Vanyalos has always spoken of her visions as if she could see things hidden to others, and I had become numb to it after so long. But now she has left her chambers... indeed, she has left Imloth Melui altogether, and she called out to folk unseen as she went!\
\
'What has come over her? Why did no one hinder her flight? There are Southrons out there, and Orcs, and who knows what other dangers await in the brush?\
\
'${PLAYER}, I beg you: go after Lady Vanyalos at once, and bring her back to safety! Speak to me and we will choose separate paths to take, the better to find my lady!'","'I will search the high-lands, if you will search the banks of the river. Go swiftly, and may one of us find Lady Vanyalos before she walks heedlessly into harm!'","Talk to Lady Vanyalos in her hall"},
[12612]={"A medida que se acerca el día del solsticio de verano, los pueblos de la Tierra Media se reúnen para celebrar el gran Festival del Solsticio. ¡Disfruta del baile, la alegría y el amor con tu familia y amigos durante tres días!","A medida que se acerca el día del solsticio de verano, los pueblos de la Tierra Media se reúnen para celebrar el gran Festival del Solsticio. ¡Disfruta del baile, la alegría y el amor con tu familia y amigos por tres días más!","'¿Puedes creerlo? ¡El Solsticio de Verano ya casi termina!\
\
'Pocos han hecho tanto como tú por difundir el espíritu del Solsticio. ¡Gracias, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Si vuelves a acompañarnos, me aseguraré de preparar aún más regalos para el año que viene!'","'¡${PLAYERNAME:Bienvenido[m]|Bienvenida[f]}! ¿Has venido a unirte a la celebración del Solsticio de Verano?\
\
'¡Eso espero! ¡Zír Aktar es un lugar maravilloso para visitar durante las fiestas! Hay muchas actividades que disfrutar en nuestras hermosas playas, y además está Tâz Makhum, La Jarra Agrietada, nuestra posada y taberna de primera categoría, en la que te encuentras ahora mismo.\
\
'Para quienes deciden echar una mano a mi tripulación, puede que tenga regalos especiales para ofrecerles como muestra de mi agradecimiento.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Nota: Esta misión no se puede cancelar.</rgb>","La Majestuosidad del Solsticio de Verano","Habla con Faeleth en Minas Tirith (Solsticio de Verano)","Completa 'Una Afición por las Festividades (Avanzado)'","¡Son muchas las celebraciones y los ritos del Solsticio de Verano en la Tierra Media! ¡Únete a la fiesta y obtén regalos fabulosos!\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>(Hay doce días de misiones de participación 'Una Afición por las Festividades' y 'Celebrando el Solsticio de Verano'. ¡Planifica en consecuencia!)</rgb>","Completa 'Una Afición por las Festividades (Intermedio)'","Habla con el capitán Khâtaphos en Isla Remota, en las Islas Escudo","Has participado en innumerables celebraciones del Solsticio de Verano y has difundido un gran espíritu festivo.\
\
Deberías regresar con Faeleth en Minas Tirith (Solsticio de Verano) o con el capitán Khâtaphos en Isla Remota.","'¡${PLAYERNAME:Bienvenido[m]|Bienvenida[f]}! ¿Has venido a unirte a la celebración del Solsticio de Verano?\
\
'¡Eso espero! Aunque Minas Tirith soportó muchos días oscuros, esta nueva festividad ha animado al pueblo de Gondor y a las tierras lejanas. ¡Y ya era hora, diría yo! Entre innumerables bodas, banquetes, fiestas y demás actividades, es fácil dejarse llevar por el espíritu del Solsticio de Verano.\
\
'Para quienes encarnan ese espíritu y para quienes consiguen salir de las tabernas, quizás tenga algunos regalos especiales como muestra de nuestro agradecimiento.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Nota: Esta misión no se puede cancelar.</rgb>","Completa 'Una Afición por las Festividades (Final)'","Completa 'Una Afición por las Festividades (Intro)'","A medida que se acerca el día del solsticio de verano, los pueblos de la Tierra Media se reúnen para celebrar el gran Festival del Solsticio. ¡Disfruta del baile, la alegría y el amor con tu familia y amigos durante los últimos tres días!"},
[12613]={"<rgb=#FF0000>Mira</rgb> hacia el este desde un nivel inferior de Khadar-zarâm","Svanr se encuentra en las escaleras de Khadar-zarâm, en el oeste de Nud-melek.\
\
Debes volver a ver a Svanr.","Vuelve con Svanr","Un indicio de un olor desagradable te distrae de la vista hacia el sur","Los puntos de observación para contemplar la Segunda Sala se encuentran en las escaleras de Khadar-zarâm.\
\
Debes <rgb=#FF0000>mirar</rgb> los majestuosos árboles de piedra de la Segunda Sala, ya que esta es una oportunidad para contemplar algunas de las mejores obras de los enanos de la época de Durin.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión requiere emotes.</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>Mira</rgb> hacia el norte desde Khadar-zarâm","'¡Hola, ${PLAYERNAME:viajero[m]|viajera[f]}! ¿También te diriges a la puerta este? Anhelo caminar bajo el sol nuevamente, pues la oscuridad de Moria se ha visto contaminada por el mal durante los años de nuestra ausencia.\
\
'He venido aquí para hacer una peregrinación por los pasillos de mi padre, y estoy a punto de emprender la última etapa de mi viaje.\
\
'¡Únete a mí, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}! Pero primero, debes meditar sobre la majestuosidad de los árboles de piedra, pues la Segunda Sala es un lugar legendario.'","A través de las ramas de piedra, ves grandes y altos enanos tallados en la pared","<rgb=#FF0000>Mira</rgb> hacia el sur desde Khadar-zarâm","Svanr te ha pedido que observes los majestuosos árboles de piedra de la Segunda Sala.","La majestuosidad de los árboles de piedra","Este es un buen punto de observación","La vista es magnífica, pero (como el resto de Moria) la Segunda Sala está llena de enemigos","'Me alegra que hayas tenido la oportunidad de contemplar la belleza de esta vista antes de salir de Moria. Pero seguramente notaste que algo no estaba bien, ${PLAYER}... como yo también lo hice.'"},
[12614]={"'I thank you for your help, stranger. He looks much happier now. Telling him that he is handsome was a good touch.'","Groom the tired donkey","The Making of a Happy Donkey","You have watered and fed the tired donkey. Next, you should brush the dust from his coat.","Bring a bucket of water to the tired donkey","You have done everything you can think of to fulfil the donkey's needs. You should talk to his owner, Bangud, in Western Khanâg.","You have watered, fed, and groomed the tired donkey. Donkeys are social animals. Perhaps you should also talk to him and give him a compliment?","You have given the donkey some refreshing water. Next, you should find some fresh straw and give him something to eat. There is a stack of donkey feed on the north-west side of Western Khanâg.","'Excuse me stranger, have you a moment to spare? I have thrown out my back and I am unable to care for my donkey. We have just returned from a long journey and the poor animal needs tending to, but I am unable to do it.\
\
'Do you have a moment to help? He needs fresh food, water, and the dust brushed from his coat.'","Tell the donkey that he is very handsome","Water seems to be the donkey's most immediate need. There is a bucket of water near the north-eastern fountain in Western Khanâg.","Bangud, a traveller resting in Western Khanâg, has injured his back and is unable to tend to his tired donkey.","Bring fresh straw to the tired donkey","Talk to Bangud"},
[12615]={"Usa el brebaje para fortalecer tu determinación antes de entrar en el estanque","'Toma el brebaje que te di, ${CLASS}. Te protegerá de las luces del pantano y del agua que absorbe la vida de quienes la atraviesan.'","Nestawen ha convertido las hierbas que trajiste en una tintura que disipará los venenos malignos del estanque prohibido. Ha llegado el momento de expulsar la fuente de la enfermedad para que no pueda seguir causando daño a los viajeros desprevenidos.","Luces de pantano eliminadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Bien... ahora que has bebido el brebaje protector, deberías darte prisa en apagar las luces de ese pantano antes de que sus efectos desaparezcan.'","'¡Nos has prestado un gran servicio! Las luces que habitaban en ese estanque estaban absorbiendo la fuerza de todo lo que las rodeaba, volviéndose cada vez más malignas.\
\
'Te estoy muy agradecida por lo que has hecho, ${PLAYER}. Ha sido un acto valiente.'","Elimina luces de pantano (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El estanque contaminado se encuentra justo al sur de Estolad Mernael.\
\
Nestawen quiere que ahuyentes a las luces de pantano que habitan en el Bosque Ahogado y te ha proporcionado un brebaje que te protegerá de los efectos nefastos del agua.","Habla con Nestawen en Estolad Mernael","La malicia de las luces","Nestawen te dio un brebaje para tu inventario que te protegerá de las luces malignas que lentamente absorben la vida de todo lo que las rodea.\
\
Nestawen quiere que bebas la tintura que ha preparado para que te fortalezcas contra las luces del pantano.","Los efectos del agua no deberían interferir ahora","Nestawen se encuentra en Estolad Mernael, al norte del estanque contaminado.\
\
Vuelve con Nestawen de inmediato e infórmale de tu victoria contra las luces malignas del estanque.","'Estas plantas que recolectaste ya han demostrado su utilidad, mellon. Tienes un ojo excelente para detectar hierbas curativas; estoy muy impresionada.\
\
'Si deseas purgar esa zona del horror que la habita, deberías tomarte el resto de este brebaje. Ya ha demostrado sus efectos en el querido Alagos, pues puedo sentir que su presencia regresa. Pronto despertará. Bébelo y disipará los efectos de esa agua maligna.\
\
'Puedes aprovechar el tiempo que te da para ahuyentar cualquier amenaza que aceche allí. Algo contamina esa agua, convirtiéndola en veneno. Quizás puedas infundir miedo a la criatura que tiene un efecto tan terrible en ese lugar.'"},
[12616]={"'The men at the tower have long made me suspicious.'","'The tower near here has long been under the control of men I do not consider trustworthy. I have seen many carts of goods enter full and leave empty...things I believe intended for Stangard.\
\
'A few weeks ago, a longstanding friend of mine was enlisted to join them. Would you be so good as to find out what he knows? I fear to approach the tower, for I am wanted for treason at Stangard.\
\
'My friend's name is Swithulf.'","Gadda has a longstanding friendship with a guard at the tower near the abandoned farm.","Talk to Swithulf","The Man on the Inside","'You are a friend of Gadda? That is well. I do not feel any kindness towards the happenings surrounding this place, nor towards the men who serve here.'","Swithulf is at the tower near the farmstead.\
\
Gadda wants you to speak with his friend Swithulf and learn what transpires at the tower."},
[12617]={"The entrance to the depths of Isengard can be found through the door to the north of Orthanc.\
\
You have searched all that remains above ground in Isengard, but you should search the depths before returning to Quickbeam.","'Hoom... there is still the matter of Saruman, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'The Tree-killer fled into his tower, for the coward knew what I would have done had I caught him. My brothers and I crushed many Orcs, but I do not know if some remain hidden from our sight in Isengard.\
\
'You are small... and can fit where I cannot. Hoom... if you could ease my fears, I can begin my journey home.'","The Many Colours of Ruin","The remains of the ring of Isengard can be found surrounding Orthanc in northern Nan Curunír.\
\
You have searched the gate-house and should now search the flooded ring of Isengard for any sign of Orcs or other foes.","DNT -- Players will not see","Quickbeam grows concerned that the White Hand might yet recover from their defeat, and seeks your aid in exploring what remains of Isengard.","Search the depths of Isengard for Orcs","Slain by grievous wounds or crushed by debris, no Orcs remain here","Naught but crushed, damp tents and rubble remain outside Orthanc","Talk to Quickbeam","Search the flooded tents and wreckage for Orcs","Search the ring of Isengard for Orcs","Search the gate-house of Isengard for Orcs","The gates of Orthanc stand shut and impenetrable","'Ta-rum! The Orcs shall not bother us again!\
\
'Let the Tree-killer rot in his tower, or come forth and face us once more. All he has sown has been laid to waste.\
\
'Now then, ${PLAYER}. I have one more thing to ask of you before I journey to the forest.'","The gate-house can be found inside the southern entrance of Isengard.\
\
Quickbeam wants you to search what remains of Isengard for any sign of Orcs.","Search Orthanc's doorway for Orcs","Only shredded banners line the broken road that once surrounded Orthanc","The flooding depths shelter a few wounded Orcs, but little else...","Quickbeam can be found across the river Isen outside the eastern side of Isengard.\
\
You have thoroughly searched the ruins of Isengard and found only wounded and slain foes. You should return to Quickbeam."},
[12618]={"Talk to guards at each of Floodwend's gates (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'I am Etta, the principal counsellor and advisor in all matters of Floodwend. My son is young yet to bear all of the responsibilities of a Thane, and so I help where I must.\
\
'Radwig is not ready to ride into war, and war it is upon our fair fields and forests. We must invest all of our strength in defences, and dissuade the enemy from venturing near our city.\
\
'I think you will find that many agree with me, if you ask around.'","Etta is in the Mead Hall of Floodwend.\
\
You should speak with Etta.","This guard, like Etta, wishes to see the town well defended","This guard wishes to defend the town from attacks, as Etta counsels","Speak with Etta","'My mother and I are having a bit of a disagreement. I realize I am a newly-made Thane, but my father was a great man, and I aspire to do as he would have done. I believe we should ride out and meet our enemies on the field, and drive them from our lands.\
\
'Mother, on the other hand, wishes to shelter and hide here in Floodwend. I do not think my father would have wished this, but I do not reject my mother's counsel lightly. Will you ask my people what they think?'","Orcs cling to the forest in great numbers, but do not set foot beyond the trees' edge","The Many Opinions of Floodwend","Soldiers of Floodwend can be found guarding the three gates of the town.","The young Thane relents, and his mother appears satisfied that her counsel was taken","Speak with Etta and hear her counsel","'I suppose that is fair, then. If nearly everyone agrees that we should bolster our defences, then bolster them we must.\
\
'My mother was likely right in her counsel. I will follow her direction, but... perhaps you might be able to help me, since you are free to do as you will here.'","Thane Radwig of Floodwend and his mother Etta are not in agreement about the best approach for handling the enemies surrounding their town.","Etta believes that Radwig will fail if he rides into battle","There is a tower behind the Floodwend Mead Hall that offers a view of the forest.\
\
You should climb the tower and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> for something unusual.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You must perform an emote to advance this quest.</rgb>","Etta is in the Mead Hall of Floodwend.\
\
You should speak with Etta and hear her opinion.","'Things have been very quiet... almost too quiet, if you ask me. I have not seen much of anything lately, neither enemy nor ally.\
\
'Would you like to hear what I really think? The lack of Rohirrim coming to and from is more concerning than the lack of enemies.\
\
'We should bolster our defences, and quickly, if you ask me. I do not know what enemies move about our lands, but I am worried.'","This is a good location to <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> toward the forest","Return to Thane Radwig","'I am glad my son came around. Seeing to our defences is the only wisdom at such a time.\
\
'He wishes to be like his father, but his father died from his rash bravery.'","'The road to the south has been ominous for a while. I have been told the road towards the East Wall is crawling with Orcs and Uruks.\
\
'A number of Orcs seem to have moved into the forest right outside Floodwend of late, and I would guess that they came from the East Wall. We have defences already set up in the forest to deal with any foes, so I believe we should be on our guard here in Floodwend.'","Radwig, Thane of Floodwend, awaits you in the Mead Hall.\
\
You should speak with Radwig and tell him of the information you gathered.","The guard seems to be of the same mind as Radwig","Climb the tower behind the Mead Hall and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> to the forest","'I can hear the howl of Wargs coming from the forest to the north-west. There are some odd sounds coming from the forest to our south, as well, but for the most part things have been quiet at this gate.\
\
'I do not think the beasts will attack our city. I loathe sitting here idly and listening while they take over our forest. Why do we not ride out to rid our lands of the vile beasts?'"},
[12620]={"'This does not bode well for us or the White City, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Faramir and Boromir threw down the Great Bridge when last the Enemy tried to sack Osgiliath, but it appears that the Orcs have found a way to rebuild it... and allow it to bear the weight of enormous siege weapons.\
\
'It is no easy task to break a bridge, my friend. Let us return to the tunnels soon, and think on how we might slow their advance!'","The Morgul-host has constructed a crude span, allowing great beasts and siege weapons to cross!","Meldir can be found along the south-western walls of Osgiliath.\
\
You have discovered a great, crude span that can bear the weight of siege equipment now covering the ruined Great Bridge. You should return to Meldir.","The Great Bridge crosses over the Anduin in central Osgiliath.\
\
Meldir has asked you to investigate how the host of Minas Morgul is ferrying siege equipment across the once-broken bridge.","The March of Minas Morgul","'The host of Minas Morgul intends to siege the White City, but we do not yet know when the attack shall begin.\
\
'We observed the Orcs hauling supplies to the Great Bridge, and have heard a thundering from above in the tunnels, but we do not know their vile designs. They have built several siege weapons on the western bank, but the bridge is broken and cannot bear the weight of the Mûmakil or their siege weapons on the eastern bank. I do not believe they will strike until their weapons can cross the river unhindered!\
\
'If they have found a way to traverse the broken span, it could spell doom for Minas Tirith. Search the Great Bridge, and tell me of any Orkish craftwork you discover!'","Patrol the Great Bridge of Osgiliath","Concerned by the renewed advance of siege equipment across the Anduin, Meldir asks you to investigate the Great Bridge.","Talk to Meldir"},
[12621]={"Completado","Plant banners of the Gabil'akkâ on the march to Gundabad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have planted banners of Gabil'akkâ across the War of Three Peaks.","Planted banners of the Gabil'akkâ on the march to Gundabad (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","If the Gabil'akkâ are to reclaim Mount Gundabad, they must gain ground in the War of Three Peaks.","You have planted banners of the Gabil'akkâ from Zarkul-sulûn to Azgh-buzru, and in so doing, advanced the War of Three Peaks into the very shadow of Mount Gundabad.\
\
What trials remain before you?","The March of the Gabil'akkâ","'Before you depart Zarkul-sulûn, I have one more task for you.\
\
'In this time of battle and sacrifice, the dwarves that serve in the Gabil'akkâ look to the leaders among them. As you battle across Elderslade with our forces, plant banners where you have won victory over Gorgar the Ruthless and his Orcs. It is your example and your resolve that might turn the tide of the War of Three Peaks, my friend. Never forget that, ${PLAYER}!\
\
'Let them hearten the dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ! Let our banners march with us to the foot of Mount Gundabad!'","Good locations for banners can be found along the path to Mount Gundabad in the War of Three Peaks.\
\
Glóin has asked you to plant banners of the Gabil'akkâ across the War of Three Peaks as you march to Mount Gundabad.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: It is recommended that you complete this quest as you adventure across the War of Three Peaks.</rgb>"},
[12622]={"You should talk to Thurindol, who can be found in North Ithilien near the after-battle Cross-roads.","Talk to Mablung","Angbor receives word that it is time to march onward to North Ithilien.","Talk to Angbor","'The road through North Ithilien will be difficult. We must rely on Lord Faramir's Rangers to lead us among those hills safely. Why don't you speak with Mablung in Osgiliath about this?'","'Good, good! I am glad we shall have the Rangers for guides. Please go on ahead. I will remain here and make sure all our supplies and men are accounted for and ready to march. We shall meet again soon, I am sure of it.'","Seek out Thurindol in North Ithilien","The March to North Ithilien","'The Rangers of Ithilien are here to do our part in the march. You remember Thurindol, do you not? He has been scouting in North Ithilien for some time now. I have arranged for him to meet you near the Cross-roads. You are to travel with him ahead of the Host of the West.\
\
'First, however, you should speak with Angbor and relay these plans.'","You should talk to Mablung, who can be found in after-battle Osgiliath.","'${PLAYER}, thank you for meeting me here. Much has happened since you passed through South Ithilien. For our parts, we Rangers have ever moved, striking at the Enemy where we might. Bâr Húrin, alas, could not be defended and was lost. Men, too, we have lost, but I shall not dwell on that now.\
\
'Come, we have much to discuss if we are to shepherd an army through the lands of North Ithilien.'","You should talk to Angbor, who can be found at the after-battle Cross-roads."},
[12623]={"Talk to Mablung","Talk to Arodor","Search for Rangers of Ithilien within after-battle Osgiliath.","You should talk to Mablung, who can be found at the main Ranger encampment in after-battle Osgiliath.","Talk to Gladhir","'It is good to have you back upon the eastern banks of the Anduin. It was my honour to scout events of the battle before Minas Tirith and report back to Mablung. Many of us wished to join the fray, but wisdom and discipline counseled we few would better serve Gondor here. And truly, many a hurried messenger and routed, retreating foe fell to our hands.'","The March to Osgiliath","'I still cannot thank you enough for rescuing me on your journeys. It seems the secret of my capture did not stay a secret for long. Many a good-natured jest has been made at my expense. Still, I have kept true to my oath and given my all to thwarting the Enemy at every turn.'","Aragorn hopes there are still Rangers of Ithilien hidden within Osgiliath who could help guide his army on their northward march.","'Now then, let us speak of securing Osgiliath. We have done much to sweep the foes from this place, but some remain. While they do, they are a threat to the rear flank of Aragorn's host, to the guard of Minas Tirith, and to my men here. To truly purge our enemies here, we will need your help, my friend.'","'${PLAYER}, we are to march shortly. Is it true, as I have heard, that you are known to the Rangers of Ithilien? Will you search for any who might still hide among the ruins of Osgiliath? It is my hope that they might help guide us through Ithilien and on to the Black Gates of Mordor.'","Talk to Mírthel","Gladhir, Mírthel, and Arodor can be found at the main Ranger encampment in after-battle Osgiliath.\
\
You should speak with the other Rangers.","Search for Rangers in Osgiliath","'${PLAYER}, it is good to see you again. When last we spoke, Osgiliath was lost to the Enemy and war was at the doorsteps of Minas Tirith. We have watched the tides of battle turn from atop the Dome of Stars. We slew coward Orcs as they fled the battle, attempting to take shelter in the ruins. \
\
'But tell me, what word do you bring out of the White City? Why came you here?'\
\
You tell Mablung of the battle and Aragorn's plans to march to the Black Gate.\
\
'If this is the path they will march, then there is much to be done here in Osgiliath first. But before we speak of those matters, talk to the other Rangers here with me - Gladhir, Mírthel, and Arodor in particular. It has been too long and they will surely be glad to speak with you again.'","'Well met, ${PLAYER}! When I saw the darksome clouds finally give way, I shed my fears of the evils lurking in the Morgul Vale. I feel in my heart these great lands are not truly threatened any longer.'"},
[12624]={"View the statue at the after-battle Cross-roads.","The March to the Cross-roads","Talk to Angbor","This is a good place to <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> at the statue","With Osgiliath safe for passage, Mablung sends you on to assist Angbor at the Cross-roads.","'A vanguard of Lord Aragorn's Host has passed through Osgiliath and gone on to the Cross-roads. Angbor, Lord of Lamedon, leads these men in securing that place and preparing the way. I deem it is an undertaking that will require many hands.'","'Ah, ${PLAYER}, here we are, so close to the dreaded stronghold! If I did not have my orders from Lord Aragorn, I would march up to the gates of Minas Morgul and rap at the bars with my blade. Let them know fear for a change!\
\
'That is how I feel, yet my men still tremble and seem downcast when they glance that way. Have I told you how, when I ousted the Haradrim from Lossarnach, not a single of my men died? It is true.\
\
'Take a look at that statue up there. My men are restoring it rightfully to a symbol of hope.'","Talk to Angbor at the Cross-roads","The statue is certainly in need of repair","You should travel to the Cross-roads, which lie east of after-battle Osgiliath.","<rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> at Statue of the Fallen King","'As you can see, the Orcs defiled the statue. It is hard work, restoring hope when you have none of your own. Would you help these men out, and raise their spirits as they restore the statue? What do you say?'","Travel to the Cross-roads","You should talk to Angbor, who can be found at the after-battle Cross-roads."},
[12625]={"'¿Candelleth te envía? ¿Cómo le va a su compañía?\
\
'¡Ah! Parece que las preocupaciones del señor Elrond eran fundadas. El Tâl Bruinen y la carretera hacia Eregion están acosados por nuestros enemigos. En días como estos anhelo viajar por tierras lejanas, pues mi puesto se presta demasiado a la soledad y al tedio.'","El Guardián del Camino del Páramo Alto","Habla con Ringhul","En estos tiempos oscuros, los guardianes del camino custodian los rutas que llevan al valle oculto de Imladris.","Ringhul está en su puesto en el Páramo Alto, muy al norte y al este de Echad Candelleth.\
\
Candelleth te pidió hablar con Ringhul, Guardián del Camino del Páramo Alto, para obtener acceso a Rivendel.","'Has sido de gran ayuda para nosotros, ${PLAYER}, y estamos agradecidos. Nos alegraría seguir contando con tu ayuda, pero si sientes que ha llegado el momento de continuar tu viaje, te sugeriría que hables con Ringhul, montaraz de las marchas del Páramo Alto. Hazle saber que te envío yo y cuéntale tus hazañas... los amigos de Rivendel siempre son bienvenidos.\
\
'Para llegar al Páramo Alto, debes regresar al camino del Tâl Bruinen y seguirlo hacia el norte hasta la carretera principal en las Gargantas del Bruinen. Sigue la carretera principal hacia el este hasta el Vado del Bruinen y cruza el río, girando hacia el sur. Encontrarás un sendero que asciende hacia las colinas... te llevará al Páramo Alto y al puesto de Ringhul.\
\
'Adiós, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[12626]={"Las obras de reconstrucción de Puente de Caballetes continúan.\
\
Deberías supervisar la reconstrucción de Puente de Caballetes.","Habla con el vendedor servicial","Supervisa la reconstrucción de Puente de Caballetes","'Sí, había un hombre de pie detrás del puesto del mercado. Te vio examinando los productos de los vendedores y empezó a ponerse nervioso. Solo lo sé porque lo vi dando vueltas de un lado a otro. Luego se alejó hasta que casi se perdió de vista, y en ese momento echó a correr. Creo que se dirigía hacia los campos de Bree. Espero que esto te sirva de ayuda. ¡Me alegro de que te gusten mis mermeladas!'","¡Te encuentras con el hombre hablando con un orco a las afueras de Cotfast!","El mercado de problemas","'¡¿Has venido a Cotfast sin compañía? ¡No te voy a decir nada, ${CLASS}! ¡Gothtal me cubre las espaldas!'","'He estado pensando en nuestros problemas con Gothtal. Por ahora, sigamos dedicándonos a la reconstrucción de Puente de Caballetes y nos ocuparemos de ese tal Gothtal cuando sea el momento adecuado. Todavía queda mucho por hacer aquí, tanto en Puente de Caballetes como en el Bosque Salvaje.'","Habla con Aran Verduno","El vendedor se encuentra a las afueras de Cotfast, en el Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Deberías hablar con el vendedor.","Revisa el último puesto del mercado","El dueño de la fruta venenosa salió corriendo del pueblo en dirección al Bosque Salvaje.\
\
Deberías ir en su búsqueda e intentar alcanzarlo.","¡Estas frutas no tienen buen aspecto!","La Hermandad de los Leñadores ha accedido a ayudar a Puente de Caballetes a organizar un mercado de productos agrícolas en el centro de la ciudad.","Deberías seguirle para dar caza al vendedor que huye","En Puente de Caballetes se han instalado los puestos de los posibles vendedores.\
\
Deberías echar un vistazo a los productos de los vendedores.","Has inspeccionado los puestos del mercado (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'Tengo buenas noticias, ${PLAYER}. Tras el arduo trabajo de la Hermandad de los Leñadores y sus miembros, Puente de Caballetes pronto contará con un día de mercado mensual en el que campesinos y comerciantes acudirán a la ciudad trayendo consigo sus productos.\
\
'Para garantizar la seguridad de la ciudad, la Hermandad de los Leñadores ha estado investigando a cada vendedor. Hoy vamos a hablar con algunos de los granjeros de los campos cercanos a Bree. ¿Te gustaría hablar con el vendedor en nuestro nombre?'","En Puente de Caballetes se han instalado los puestos de los posibles vendedores.\
\
Deberías hablar con el campesino más cercano al puesto donde se encuentra la fruta en mal estado.","Aran Verduno se encuentra en Puente de Caballetes.\
\
Deberías hablar con Aran Verduno.","Echa un vistazo a los puestos del mercado (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Enfréntate al bandido problemático","El rastro de huellas conduce al Bosque Salvaje","El bandido problemático ha sido derrotado","'Ahora tenemos un nombre: Gothtal. También sabemos que este orco frecuenta el puesto avanzado de Cotfast, en el Bosque Salvaje. El intento de infiltrarse en nuestro mercado de la ciudad es una maniobra descarada por parte de este Gothtal. ¿Se ha vuelto loco? ¿Cuál es su plan? Espero averiguarlo pronto, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'¿Por qué no te tomas un rato para admirar los esfuerzos de la reconstrucción de Puente de Caballetes mientras yo pienso en nuestro próximo plan de acción?'","Encuentra y sigue el rastro de ese hombre","¡Se ha reconstruido otra parte de Puente de Caballetes!"},
[12630]={"Something is amiss in Lake-town.\
\
You should talk to the guard at the Master's manor.","'No admittance! The Master has died!'","'You are welcome in Lake-town, ${CLASS}, but I'm afraid you have come at a bad time. It's a delicate situation; if you must know, you shall have to go to the Master's manor and see for yourself.'","You hear a familiar whistle from somewhere nearby","Talk to Mervárth","Talk to the guard at the Master's manor","Something is amiss in Lake-town.\
\
You should make your way to the Master's manor.","'${PLAYER}! Good to see you again. You seem to have a knack for showing up where things have gotten interesting! \
\
'It does seem our dear old Master of Lake-town has died, but those guards are being awfully tight-lipped about the cause. He was the very picture of health just yesterday! And then there's a rumour going around that he was murdered....'","Lake-town citizens are milling about in front of the manor","Make your way to the Master's manor","You have just arrived at Lake-town, but it seems something is amiss. Make your way to the Master's manor to find out what happened.","The Master of Lake-town","Mervárth can be found near the Master's manor.\
\
You should talk to Mervárth."},
[12631]={"'Adder-fang escaped?\
\
'I feared he might, but I saw no sign of him leaving Caivád Sâr. Whatever trickery he employed, it is beyond my understanding. Let the wounds you dealt against him be a reminder that the Iron Crown holds no sway in Elderslade!\
\
'Do not fret, ${PLAYER}... Adder-fang won't elude us for long. I shall return to Annâk-khurfu and inform Commander Glóin of what has happened.'","Find some sign of Bandrauth Adder-fang in Tûr Ágal","Examine the pedestal and remain ready to confront Bandrauth Adder-fang","The dusty pedestal can be found in the highest chamber of Tûr Ágal.\
\
You have not found Bandrauth Adder-fang, but you have discovered a curious, dusty pedestal inscribed with Angmarim runes. You should examine the pedestal more closely.","'I trust Commander Glóin told you of our target?\
\
'Yes, Bandrauth Adder-fang is his name, and he seems to be well-known among the few Angmarim we've encountered in Elderslade. If what we have learned is true, he is a powerful sorcerer who once served the False King, Mordirith. It is curious, though, that none in the Gabil'akkâ have heard his name before.\
\
'Nevertheless, he would prove a deadly foe if the Iron Crown were to come to the aid of Gorgar's forces at the gates of Mount Gundabad. It is our task to ensure that he never can.\
\
'I have noticed he spends a great deal of time in that tower, Tûr Ágal. Find him, and defeat him for the good of the Gabil'akkâ!'","You have found no sign of the sorcerer, but a dusty pedestal draws your gaze...","Bandrauth Adder-fang can be found within Tûr Ágal at Caivád Sâr.\
\
Múta has asked you to find and defeat the Angmarim sorcerer, Bandrauth Adder-fang, in Tûr Ágal. You should search the tower for any sign of him.","Although his plans remain unknown to the dwarves of the Gabil'akkâ, scouts have discovered a terrible sorcerer of the Iron Crown, Bandrauth Adder-fang, overseeing the forces at Caivád Sâr.","Múta can be found outside Caivád Sâr in northern Elderslade.\
\
You wounded Bandrauth Adder-fang, but he was able to escape from his encounter with you. You should return to Múta and inform her of what has happened.","Talk to Múta at Caivád Sâr","The Master of Tûr Ágal","With the aid of fell sorcery, Bandrauth Adder-fang flees!","A harsh shout echoes nearby as Bandrauth Adder-fang attacks!"},
[12633]={"El Maestro de las Ruinas vaga por las ruinas de Nan Dhelu, al norte de Dol Vaeg.\
\
Cwendreda te ha recomendado que seas muy prudente al explorar Nan Dhelu y te ha prometido una recompensa si logras derrotar al monstruo.","Las ruinas de Nan Dhelu nunca han gustado mucho a los Eglain, pero desde la aparición de los Muertos en ellas, su preocupación va en aumento. Cwendreda, una valiente guerrera, fue enviada a investigar las ruinas; ahora, su misión recae sobre ti, mientras el terror comienza a hacerse palpable en estas salas que en otro tiempo fueron magníficas.","Habla con Cwendreda en Dol Vaeg","Derrota al Maestro de las Ruinas","'Saber que esa criatura ya no existe me devuelve un poco de esperanza. Hoy has sido de gran ayuda para los Eglain, ${PLAYER}, y te mereces tu recompensa.\
\
'Gracias de nuevo por todo lo que haces por mi pueblo.'","El Maestro de las Ruinas","Maestro de las Ruinas derrotado","Cwendreda se encuentra en Dol Vaeg.\
\
Cwendreda espera tu regreso, estará encantada de saber que has vencido al Maestro de las Ruinas.","'Soy una persona orgullosa, sin duda, pero también sé lo que es el miedo, y el Maestro de las Ruinas es la criatura más aterradora que he visto jamás. Vaga por las ruinas de Nan Dhelu acompañado de un esqueleto reanimado; es una criatura temible.\
\
'Si te encuentras con este monstruo, huye. Si decides luchar contra él y consigues derrotarlo, vuelve a verme, tendré una recompensa para ti.\
\
'El Maestro de las Ruinas merodea por todas partes, nunca permanece mucho tiempo en el mismo lugar.'","'Ten cuidado, ${PLAYER}. El Maestro de las Ruinas es la criatura más temible que jamás haya visto. Se recomienda precaución al explorar las ruinas de Nan Dehlu.'"},
[12634]={"<rgb=#FF0000>Talk</rgb> to the crowd gathered outside the manor about Smaug's bones","A crowd of people are gathered outside of the Master's manor in Lake-town.\
\
With Dagrun's reputation improved, now would be a good time to speak to the Men of Lake-town about Smaug's bones, on behalf of the Master.","Dagrun can be found in the Master's manor in Lake-town.\
\
You should assist Dagrun with her troubles.","The Master's manor stands before you","The Master of Lake-town should hear of this. That much is true","Find the Master of Lake-town","'I have dwelled all my life among the folk of Lake-town, and never has the gossip in the market been so pernicious and full of lies as these last days.\
\
'Why, they say I am of the bloodline of Othur! You know of Othur, do you not? He was Master of Lake-town in the time when Bard the Bowman was not yet king and Smaug slept, then awoke. Othur stole from Lake-town and fled, and his name is one of infamy and shame. They say his stolen wealth was not lost, but that I have it now and conceal it from all.\
\
'This is all nonsense, of course! But if I am to assist you in your puzzle, I must ask you to assist me in mine. I should not be at all surprised if they were somehow linked.'","Complete <rgb=#FF0000>'Underbelly of Deceit'</rgb>","The crowd has heard your words to leave Smaug's bones be and agrees","There is a lively debate among its residents about transporting Smaug's bones to Lake-town.","You should speak some more with Dagrun, who can be found in the Master's manor in Lake-town.","Complete <rgb=#FF0000>'A Question of Bloodline'</rgb>","'You're not one of those lot, then? Good. Why they wish to dredge up those bones and bearing them here to New Lake-town, I can't say! It was that dragon, after all, as set Old Lake-town ablaze. Or have they somehow forgotten the tales of their grandmams? \
\
'If you think you can make some sense of such rot and bother, go talk to Stafhild, over there. At the very least, he'll try to tell you why they believe the things they do.'","You should speak with Dagrun, who can be found in the Master's manor in Lake-town.","This is a good place to speak to the crowd","Talk to Dagrun again","You should speak with Dagrun, who can be found in the Master's Manor in Lake-town.","'Ah, ${PLAYER}. This has been an eventful day for you and for me and for Lake-town, has it not? But what is it? Is there some other matter about which you wish to speak?'\
\
You tell her briefly of the strange puzzle you followed from Loeglond, to Esgaroth, and finally to Lake-town.\
\
'Your problems and my own are much akin, friend. It would seem, new as I am as Master, that I have more than my fair share of opposition, and it has taken the form of such grumbling in the street as you have witnessed over Smaug's bones.'","Dagrun pauses and looks towards one of the windows","The Master's Dilemma","'Thank you once again, for all you have done, ${PLAYER}. You have been most helpful in assisting the best interests of Lake-town.'","Talk to Stafhild","Stafhild can be found in the unruly group in Lake-town.\
\
You should hear what Stafhild has to say.","Talk to Dagrun","'Why bring the bones here? Well, they're doing no one any good out there in the Lake, for one. And they have great value, or so I've heard tale. They could bring great wealth to Lake-town. Or put them up somewhere, and travellers like yourself will come from leagues away just to see them.\
\
'Don't you lecture me of that rot about ill luck. Why, that's a real bit of Smaug at the Dragonbone Inn... isn't it? I've always thought so, at any rate. The clear thing is, whoever begun this talk was thinking with their head for a change, and that's just the sort of thing Lake-town needs.\
\
'Really, someone ought to bring a petition to the Master!'","Complete <rgb=#FF0000>'The Master's Murder' quest arc</rgb>","You should assist the Men of Lake-town.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>The Trail of Rust quest arc will continue after completing The Master's Murder quest arc which begins with the Lake-town guard in front of the Master's manor in Lake-town.</rgb>","Find the Master of Lake-town."},
[12635]={"'¿Qué encontraste? ¿Un pergamino parecido a los que cuelgan del Árbol de la Fiesta? ¡Esto podría ser justo la pista que necesitamos para descubrir la identidad del misterioso organizador, ${PLAYER}! Dame eso y veré si lo es.'\
\
Waldo examina brevemente el pergamino y frunce el ceño.\
\
'Hay algo escrito, pero no consigo entenderlo. Si queremos resolver este misterio, parece que nuestro benefactor oculto quiere hacernos trabajar. Toma, te devuelvo el pergamino para que intentes descifrarlo. Buena suerte, ${PLAYER}.'","Cada año, en primavera, tiene lugar la Búsqueda del Tesoro del Aniversario para celebrar una ocasión muy especial. Pero ¿quién o qué ha sido responsable de estos curiosos sucesos?\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión será eliminada de tu registro cuando termine el festival actual.</rgb>","'Mi primo Lotho Sacovilla-Bolsón me dio la idea para esta búsqueda del tesoro. Verás, quería intentar crear un juego divertido para nuestros vecinos durante el festival. No estaba seguro de qué hacer, claro. Tenía algunas ideas y se las conté a Lotho, pero debió de pensar que eran demasiado pequeñas o poco ingeniosas. \\qMantenlos ocupados, Ebrulf,\\q me dijo. \\qHaz que toda la Comarca mire a todos lados excepto hacia mí y los míos.\\q Y le dije que tenía sentido, y que haría lo mejor posible. Mis juegos necesitarían algo de reflexión, por supuesto, y tendría cuidado de no hacerlos demasiado fáciles.\
\
'¡Lotho apoyó mucho mis planes! Una noche lo oí hablar con unos amigos suyos, y estaba tan entusiasmado... \\q¡Les daremos algo de qué hablar!\\q les dijo, y también \\q¡nunca lo verán venir!\\q. ¡Me puse colorado en ese mismo instante! No quería decepcionar a mi primo, así que puse aún más esfuerzo en planear mi búsqueda del tesoro y mantenerla en secreto.\
\
'Así que de nuevo te felicito, ${PLAYER}. ¡Espero que Lotho esté orgulloso de mí! ¡Estoy seguro de que lo estará!'","Has descubierto la identidad de la mente maestra detrás de las tarjetas colgadas del Árbol de la Fiesta y ahora deberías regresar con Waldo Retumbo.","Lobelia Sacovilla-Bolsón te ha llamado, claramente con intención de decirte unas cuantas cosas.","Estuvo cerca, pero lograste recuperar el pergamino para Waldo Retumbo.","Lobelia Sacovilla-Bolsón te lanza una mirada sospechosa y desconfiada","¡Ja, ja! ¡Me encontraste! Bien, ${PLAYER}, permíteme felicitarte, porque has resuelto mi pequeño misterio y no podría estar más contento. ¡Espero que hayas disfrutado de mi búsqueda del tesoro y que te hayas divertido! Todo fue idea de mi primo Lotho.'\
\
Ebrulf debe notar tu expresión de desconcierto, porque asiente con entusiasmo.\
\
'¡Es verdad! Mi primo Lotho Sacovilla-Bolsón me dio la idea para esta búsqueda del tesoro. Verás, quería intentar crear un juego divertido para nuestros vecinos durante el festival. No estaba muy seguro de qué hacer, claro. Tenía algunas ideas y se las conté a Lotho, pero debió de pensar que eran demasiado pequeñas o poco ingeniosas. \\qMantenlos ocupados, Ebrulf,\\q me dijo, \\qhaz que toda la Comarca mire a todos lados excepto hacia mí y los míos.\\q Y le dije que tenía sentido, y que haría lo mejor posible. Mis juegos requerirían algo de reflexión, por supuesto, y tenía cuidado de que no fueran demasiado fáciles.'\
\
'¡Lotho apoyaba muchísimo mis planes! Una noche lo escuché hablar con unos amigos y estaba tan entusiasmado... \\q¡Les daremos algo de qué hablar!\\q les dijo, y también \\q¡nunca lo verán venir!\\q. ¡Me puse colorado en ese mismo instante! No quería decepcionar a mi primo, así que puse aún más esfuerzo en planear mi búsqueda del tesoro y mantenerla en secreto.'\
\
'Así que, de nuevo, ¡te felicito, ${PLAYER}! ¡Espero que Lotho esté orgulloso de mí! ¡Estoy seguro de que lo estará!'","Busca cerca de Bolsón Cerrado a la figura sospechosa","Tienes en tu poder un pergamino misterioso que podría contener una pista para descubrir la identidad del misterioso organizador que llenó el Árbol de la Fiesta con cintas y tarjetas.","'¿Has resuelto el misterio? ¡Qué alegría, ${PLAYER}! ¡Cuéntame lo que descubriste, ahora mismo!'\
\
Le relatas todas las pistas que descifraste para encontrar a Ebrulf Sacovilla, el responsable de colgar las cintas y tarjetas. Waldo deja escapar un enorme suspiro de satisfacción.\
\
'Ni siquiera estoy enfadado con el joven señor Sacovilla por no seguir los procedimientos establecidos por el Comité de Organización de Fiestas. Al final, diría que esta búsqueda del tesoro resultó muy satisfactoria y valió el esfuerzo. Por ello te recompenso con varios de estos Fichas de Aniversario. Estoy muy impresionado de que resolvieras el misterio, ${PLAYER}. ¡Debiste recorrer toda la Comarca para llegar al fondo!'\
\
'¡Gracias otra vez!'","'Esta mañana muy temprano vi a una figura sospechosa merodeando cerca del Árbol de la Fiesta y, cuando me acerqué para verla mejor, ¡huyó colina arriba! Parecía dirigirse hacia Bolsón Cerrado, donde vivían el viejo Bilbo y el joven Frodo. Si vas allí, quizá encuentres algún indicio de nuestro misterioso organizador.'","'Esta mañana muy temprano vi a una figura sospechosa cerca del Árbol de la Fiesta y, cuando me acerqué, huyó colina arriba. Parecía dirigirse hacia Bolsón Cerrado. Si vas allí, quizá encuentres un indicio de nuestro misterioso organizador.'","Lleva el pergamino desechado a Waldo Retumbo junto al Árbol de la Fiesta","Sigue las pistas del pergamino para resolver el misterio","Has encontrado a Ebrulf Sacovilla junto a un montón de pergaminos al noroeste de Sobrecolina, en el Bosque del Fardo. ¿Es él el responsable de las travesuras que han preocupado tanto a Waldo Retumbo y al Comité de Organización de Fiestas?","'¡Tarjetas, tarjetas, tarjetas! El Árbol de la Fiesta sigue cubierto de ellas, y los procedimientos apropiados para planificar las actividades del festival aún no se han seguido, ¡para gran disgusto del Comité de Organización de Fiestas! ¿Cuánto tiempo ha pasado, ${PLAYER}? No puedo decirte con certeza cuánto llevamos lidiando con este suceso escandaloso, ¡pero sé que ha dominado todos mis momentos despierto! Y no estamos más cerca de descubrir quién ha montado este absurdo asunto que el año pasado por estas fechas.\
\
'¡O quizá sí! Esta mañana temprano vi una figura sospechosa merodeando cerca del Árbol de la Fiesta, y cuando me acerqué para verla mejor, ¡huyó colina arriba! Parecía dirigirse hacia Bolsón Cerrado, donde vivían el viejo Bilbo y el joven Frodo. Si subes allí, quizá encuentres algún indicio de nuestro misterioso organizador.\
\
'¡Por favor, ayúdame, ${PLAYER}! Después de todo este tiempo, estoy ansioso por llegar al fondo de este lío.'","Habla con Waldo Retumbo junto al Árbol de la Fiesta","'¿Qué tienes ahí? Te vi recoger algo y, como puedes ver, estás claramente en mi propiedad. ¡Dámelo o llamaré a los alguaciles!\
\
'Espera. ¿Es una de esas horribles tarjetas del Árbol de la Fiesta? ¡Alguien ha cubierto ese viejo árbol con ellas, y es una verdadera monstruosidad! ¡No puedo salir por la puerta de mi casa sin ver esas cosas estrafalarias! Seguro que fue ese Frodo o alguno de sus amigos... están intentando arruinar la vista y devaluar Bolsón Cerrado.\
\
'¡Oh, es terrible, simplemente terrible! ¡No quiero esa tarjeta ni nada que tenga que ver con ese festival indeseado! ¡Llévatela!'","Waldo Retumbo está junto al Árbol de la Fiesta, esperando encontrar alguna pista sobre la identidad de la figura sospechosa que vio.","Un pergamino como los que cuelgan del Árbol de la Fiesta ha caído junto al sendero","Waldo Retumbo vio una figura extraña merodeando cerca del Árbol de la Fiesta a primeras horas de la mañana, pero huyó colina arriba hacia Bolsón Cerrado cuando él se acercó.","¡Un hobbit está allí, sonriendo con suficiencia, junto a un montón de pergaminos!","Un pequeño pergamino ha caído junto al sendero cerca de Bolsón Cerrado. Parece muy similar a las tarjetas colgadas del Árbol de la Fiesta.","Habla con Lobelia Sacovilla-Bolsón","El Secuaz de la Mente Maestra","'¡No quiero esa tarjeta, ni nada que ver con este festival indeseado! ¡Llévatela!'","Recoge el pergamino desechado cerca de Bolsón Cerrado","Habla con Ebrulf Sacovilla"},
[12636]={"Golhador te ha advertido sobre los grandes mamuts de las Montañas Nubladas, algunos de los cuales parecen haberse aliado con los gigantes.","Golhador está en el campamento del Risco Alto.\
\
Golhador espera que regreses con anillos de colmillo que puedan arrojar luz sobre la naturaleza de la alianza entre los mamuts y los gigantes de las Montañas Nubladas.","Se pueden encontrar mamuts por todas las Montañas Nubladas, pero especialmente en zonas donde caminan los gigantes.\
\
Golhador ha expresado su preocupación de que los mamuts y los gigantes hayan formado una alianza y te ha pedido que le traigas los anillos de colmillo de plata que llevan los mamuts para examinarlos.","'Los mamuts nunca caminan en grandes números, pero a menudo se encuentran cerca de los gigantes. Si puedes recuperar algunos de sus anillos de colmillo, tal vez descubramos cuán fuerte es esta alianza.'","Los Maestros del Mamut","'Has hecho muy bien en traerme estos anillos de colmillo, . ¡Son realmente temibles! Sin duda fue un gigante terrible quien los colocó, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}. ¡Esperemos que nunca se acerque a este lugar, ni al campamento de los enanos al oeste!'","Lleva anillos de colmillo de plata a Golhador","'Si vas a escalar las montañas, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}, ten cuidado de evitar los grandes mamuts. Son peligrosos todos los días, pero últimamente los pocos viajeros que han pasado por aquí han mencionado una ornamentación inusual en las poderosas bestias: grandes anillos de plata fijados a sus peligrosos colmillos.\
\
Solo una raza podría colocar tales anillos y seguir viva, y esa es la de los gigantes. Esta alianza es de mal augurio, si es que es una alianza, y me preocupa no solo por la Casa de Elrond sino también por nuestros amigos enanos, que han establecido un campamento no muy lejos al norte.\
\
Si por fortuna logras derrotar a algunos mamuts, tráeme sus anillos de colmillo para estudiarlos. Debemos averiguar cuán profunda puede ser esta alianza entre grandes bestias y gigantes.'"},
[12637]={"The Materials of War","Las provisiones deben ser requisadas antes de que los corsarios puedan usarlas.","Los corsarios han comenzado a transportar suministros a Dol Amroth.","Collect supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12638]={"'Los Trév Duvárdain y los Trév Gállorg fueron una vez una sola tribu, pero con los años se distanciaron, fragmentados como les ocurre a veces a las tribus. Siempre hubo esperanza de que un día se reconciliaran, pero esa esperanza se ha esfumado.\
\
'Drostan habló del Clúcath, un combate ceremonial que se usaba para determinar la cadena de mando entre las distintas tribus. El último Clúcath se invocó hace muchos años con la muerte Násan, el guerrero de los Trév Gállorg, como resultado. Pero no es momento de hablar de estas cosas: nuestra victoria sobre las bestias de las colinas no debe ser manchada con tristes recuerdos. Me has ayudado con mi Fém, ¡y eso nos honra a ambos!\
\
'Ve ahora a ver a mi hermana Rona, y dile que pronto volveré a Aughaire. ¿Dónde me dijiste que estaba? ¿En la isla del centro de Aughaire, al este del trono de Crannog? Allí es donde la encontrarás entonces, espero. Lleva mi agradecimiento y no te preocupes por las provocaciones crueles de Drostan. La suya no es gente digna.'","'¿Tasgall está a salvo, y le has ayudado a completar su Fém con éxito? ¡Me llena de alegría que así sea!\
\
'¡Se lo contaré a Crannog ahora mismo! ¡Tienes mi agradecimiento y mis mejores deseos, ${PLAYER}, y también los de Tasgall, estoy segura de ello. Los Trév Gállorg no olvidamos hazañas como las que habéis logrado.'","El campamento de Tasgall está al norte de Aughaire y al sureste de Nád Nathair.\
\
Tasgall  y tú habéis tenido éxito en vuestra cacería de Bangrath y Murragrath. Te está esperando para hablar contigo.","'Hemos afrontado con valentía los peligros de Nád Nathair.'","'Tenemos lo que necesitamos para sacar a Bangrath y Murragrath de su escondite, ${PLAYER}. ¡Vayamos a Nád Nathair y usemos este cebo para poner fin a su amenaza!\
\
'¡Avísame cuando quieras ponerteen marcha! Debemos intentar no alertar a las criaturas de nuestra presencia o el plan fallará antes de empezar.'","El campamento de Tasgall está al norte de Aughaire y al sureste de Nád Nathair.\
\
Tasgall te está esperando para ir contigo en busca de Bangrath y Murragrath.","'¡Tienes mi agradecimiento y mis mejores deseos, ${PLAYER}, y también los de Tasgall, estoy segura de ello.'","La matrona y el maestro","Rona está en la isla central de Aughaire, al este del trono de Crannog.\
\
Tasgall ha quedado satisfecho con la ayuda que le prestaste y quiere que le digas a su hermana Rona que pronto volverá al asentamiento.","'¿Todo listo para marcharnos? ¡Dependemos el uno del otro en esta cacería, así que asegúrate de estar ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]}!'","Habla con Tasgall para viajar a Nád Nathair","'¿Tasgall está a salvo, y le has ayudado a completar su Fém con éxito? ¡Me llena de alegría que así sea!'","'Bangrath y Murragrath ya no existen, ${PLAYER}, y la historia ha terminado bien.'","Tasgall ha trazado un plan en el que él y tú atraeréis a Bangrath y Murragrath para poner fin a la amenaza que suponen."},
[12639]={"Derrota arañas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a la Matrona del Colmillo","Tu misión es matar arañas en Ushbarab y vencer a la Matrona del Colmillo cuando salga a defender su nido.","Arañas derrotadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Al noroeste de Maurûsh las arañas se vuelven más fétidas y fuertes. Hay un llamado de la coalición en Ub Nishir para eliminar a la matrona que lidera el nido.","Has derrotado a la Matrona del Colmillo","¡La Matrona del Colmillo emerge para defender su nido!","'¡Saludos! Hiciste bien en matar a la matrona. Ven, regresemos a Ub Nishir.'","Encuentra y derrota a la Matrona del Colmillo en Ushbarab.","El colmillo de la matrona"},
[12640]={"'Voy a empezar a preparar la cena, pero me pregunto si podría pedirte otro favor mientras me ocupo de la cocina.\
\
'La habitación de mi padre está en el segundo piso, pero en su estado, no hay forma de que pueda subir las escaleras. ¿Podrías desmontar su cama y volver a montarla en su biblioteca, en la planta baja? Seguro que se quejará, pero por el saco de dormir que hay ahí abajo, veo que, afortunadamente, ya lleva varias noches durmiendo aquí.'","Habla con Rhiangar","'¡Muchas gracias! Sé que le cuesta admitir que necesita ayuda, pero creo que al final me lo agradecerá.'","Lleva algo de tiempo, ¡pero la cama está montada de nuevo!","Desmonta la cama","Después de algún tiempo y esfuerzo, la cama ha sido desmontada.","La dolencia del alcalde Nevit ha empeorado, lo que le obliga a pasar largas horas durmiendo sobre un duro saco de dormir.","Rhiangar te ha pedido ayuda para desmontar la cama de su padre y poder bajarla al piso de abajo.\
\
La cama del alcalde se encuentra en la casa del alcalde, en Herne.","Has desmontado la cama de la habitación de arriba de la casa del alcalde. Ahora debes volver a montarla abajo, en su despacho.\
\
El despacho del alcalde está en su casa, en Herne.","Deberías decirle a Rhiangar que has trasladado la cama de su padre a la biblioteca.\
\
Rhiangar está en la cocina de la casa del alcalde en Herne.","La cama del alcalde","Monta de nuevo la cama del alcalde"},
[12664]={"'Are you ready to leave, ${PLAYER}? Come... let us return to Galtrev together.'","The Meaning of Alliance","'You fought bravely for our people, ${PLAYER}! You are a true hero... like the folk in the old tales. We owe you much!\
\
'Thanks to you, our people are slaves to the White Hand no longer. But I fear that Saruman will retaliate when he hears of what happened here.'","Tomos is at the outskirts of the Dragon-clan's encampment in western Pren Gwydh.\
\
You should speak with Tomos to travel to Galtrev.","'You have shown me what a true alliance should be, ${PLAYER}... and what Saruman has offered is no alliance. He has stolen our warriors and made us slaves. It is clear that the people of Dunland are nothing to him but thralls.\
\
'Let us return to Galtrev now. Perhaps with your help, I can demand a fair alliance from the White Hand peoples stationed in our village.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo instance and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>","Talk to Mari","It has become apparent to many that the White Hand alliance with the folk of Galtrev is not a fruitful one for the people of Pren Gwydh.","Accompany Tomos to establish a fair alliance between the people of Galtrev and the White Hand","Mari is in Galtrev, the main village of Pren Gwydh.\
\
You should speak with Mari in Galtrev."},
[12665]={"Derwent Correhuela se encuentra fuera del pueblo de Altapiedra, en Annúndir, en las Quebradas del Norte.","'Busca a Derwent Correhuela en el pueblo de Altapiedra, ${PLAYER}, en las Quebradas del Norte. Altapiedra se alza al final de un sendero en pendiente al noreste de Amon Raith. Una vez más, hacer buen uso de tus habilidades de lucha es la única forma de mejorarlas. ${PLAYER:Seguro[m]|Segura[f]} que quieres algún día igualar mi propia destreza, ¿no?'","'¡Ya van dos que te debo, ${PLAYER:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}! O los problemas siguen de cerca a un Luchador, o tú tienes un don para encontrarlos. Sea cual sea la verdad, ¡me alegra que hayas estado aquí! Pero ¿qué haré si Bill Helechal se entera de que sus amigos orcos no tuvieron éxito? No puedo seguir acobardándome cada vez que estalla una pelea...\
\
'Quizá adopte el estilo de combate que demostraste, ${PLAYER}, y trate de entrenar a la gente de Altapiedra en las artes de la lucha. ¡Puede que Rosa y Ned le tomen gusto y se conviertan en Luchadores naturales por derecho propio! Empiezo a preguntarme si Brom Barbadehalcón tenía razón respecto a este pueblo y si necesitaremos habilidades como las tuyas para defendernos.\
\
'Gracias otra vez, , y hazle llegar mi gratitud a Brom también. ¡Tuvimos suerte de que estuvieras aquí! La próxima vez que nos veamos, quizá formemos una dupla de luchadores que no tema ni a las espadas de orcos ni a las artimañas de villanos como Bill Helechal.'","A Brom Barbadehalcón le gusta presentarse como un Luchador duro y despreocupado, pero cuanto más trabajas con él, más te das cuenta de que su rudeza exterior es en gran parte una actuación.","'He recibido noticias de que Derwent Correhuela se ha metido otra vez en problemas, . No es que me importe demasiado, teniendo mis propias preocupaciones, pero como ${PLAYERNAME:Luchador[m]|Luchadora[f]} en ascenso deberías hacer todo lo posible por mejorar tu reputación entre la gente de las Tierras de Bree.\
\
'Al parecer, Derwent salió en busca de un nuevo hogar para su familia después de que te enfrentaras a los rufianes de Bill Helechal, pero el pueblo en el que se detuvo es quizá aún más peligroso que el que dejó atrás. ¿Por qué no vas a ver cómo está y compruebas si puedes ayudarlo? Me da miedo pudo haber mordido más de lo que puede masticar...\
\
Brom tose de repente.\
\
'¿Miedo? ¿Dije miedo? ¡Bah! ¡Brom Barbadehalcón no le teme a nada! Solo quise decir que Derwent quizá esté asustado y podría necesitar a un Luchador fuerte que lo ayude a asentarse. Búscalo en el pueblo de Altapiedra, , en las Quebradas del Norte. Tengo entendido que puedes seguir un sendero en pendiente al noreste de Amon Raith, bordeando las montañas, directamente hasta el pueblo. Una vez más, hacer buen uso de tus habilidades de lucha es la única manera de mejorarlas. Seguro que quieres algún día igualar mi destreza, ¿no?'","'¿Brom Barbadehalcón te envió a verme? Fue muy amable de su parte, ${PLAYER}, pero se equivoca: no tengo ningún problema y estoy disfrutando mucho de mi nuevo hogar aquí, en Altapiedra.\
\
'Y si mis vecinos tienen alguna necesidad o preocupación, estoy más que dispuesto a poner de mi parte para enderezar las cosas aquí; trabajé duro durante semanas en la Obra de Espinar. ¡Si aún estuviera allí, sin duda ya estaría terminada! Pero Bill Helechal y sus rufianes se encargaron de que no fuera así, ¿verdad?\
\
'Así que no hay problemas por aquí, pero si te interesa puedo darte un recorrido por el pueblo. ¡Es lo menos que puedo hacer, ${PLAYER:mi amigo luchador[m]|mi amiga luchadora[f]}!'","'Gracias de nuevo, ${PLAYER}, y hazle llegar mi gratitud a Brom también. ¡Tuvimos suerte de que estuvieras aquí!'","Derwent Correhuela se encuentra en el pueblo de Altapiedra, en las Quebradas del Norte.","'¿Derwent y su familia están prosperando en Altapiedra? Muy bien. En realidad no estaba preocupado, pero ya que ibas para allí de todos modos...\
\
'Le dices a Brom que en realidad no pensabas ir a Altapiedra y que solo viajaste hasta allí por su recomendación.\
\
'Sí, bueno, aun así debiste haberte preocupado por él. En cualquier caso, tengo una recompensa para ti. Que te ayude en las peleas que te aguardan, ya sea al servicio de quienes no pueden defenderse... o solo por diversión.'","La pelea en la plaza","Habla con Brom Barbadehalcón en la Cárcel de Bree.","Derwent Correhuela se encuentra fuera del pueblo de Altapiedra, al noreste de Amon Raith, en las Quebradas del Norte.","Brom Barbadehalcón se encuentra en la Cárcel de Bree.","'¡Por aquí, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}! Mientras caminamos, puedes contarme por qué Brom cree que Altapiedra es un lugar peligroso... ¡a mí me parece bastante tranquilo!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no puede completarse con una comunidad.</rgb>","Habla con Derwent Correhuela fuera del pueblo de Altapiedra","Habla con Derwent Correhuela de Altapiedra"},
[12667]={"El campamento de Callum está en el extremo occidental del Pantano de la Rana, al oeste de Bolgovado.\
\
A la luz de las revelaciones obtenidas del diario de Callum, Wilimar Bolger te ha pedido que vayas al campamento de Callum y lo detengas antes de que lleve a cabo su venganza.","Wilimar Bolger se encuentra cerca de su agujero en el lado noroeste de Bolgovado.\
\
Cuando llegaste al campamento de Callum, lo encontraste herido. Consumido por el dolor, contó cómo había huido de su escondite cerca de la casa de Wilimar, solo para asustar a un jabalí salvaje, que lo corneó. Siente que pronto sucumbirá a sus heridas y te dijo que le hicieras saber a Wilimar que no tiene nada más que temer.","'¡Vaya, qué alivio! Y, sin embargo, no puedo evitar sentirme mal por ese Callum.\
\
Verás, he leído más de su diario y su vida fue realmente lamentable. El lugar donde vive, muy al norte, parece ser un sitio oscuro y disputado. Nada que ver con la Comarca, y no ha tenido mucha suerte.\
\
Creo que merece un poco de compasión, si pudieras ayudarme con esto.'","'¿Así que el miserable hombrecito te envió para acabar con mi vida, verdad? Supongo que es lo justo. Mi vida ha estado maldita por la marca de deshonra sobre mi familia.\
\
Haz lo que quieras. No tengo fuerzas para defenderme, como puedes ver. Cuando ese hombre-rata encontró la flecha en su puerta, dio la alarma. Temía ser descubierto antes de estar listo, así que huí de mi escondite. Sin embargo, en mi huida, asusté a un jabalí y la vil bestia me corneó.\
\
Es solo cuestión de tiempo antes de sucumbir a la herida. Si no vas a matarme, al menos hazme el favor de decirle a Wilimar que ya no tiene nada que temer de mí. Los años cansados de mi vida están casi terminados...'","La amenaza enfrentada","'Por favor, date prisa, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}, y ve si puedes encontrar a ese Callum. ¡Solo tienes que convencerlo de que abandone esta misión de venganza! Según su diario, ha acampado al oeste de Bolgovado, en el extremo occidental del Pantano de la Rana.'","'¿Por qué te quedas aquí? Está claro que no represento ninguna amenaza y, evidentemente, no tienes interés en acabar con mi miserable vida.\
\
¡Vete! Dile al hombre-rata que no tiene nada que temer de mí. La venganza no se cobrará hoy...'","'¡Vaya, el autor de este diario, Callum, tiene un pasado oscuro! Parece que la muerte de su antepasado a manos de mi antepasado en aquella gran batalla fue una mancha negra para su familia. Llevaron esa marca durante siglos.\
\
Tras una serie de desgracias, que Callum atribuye a esa marca, decidió intentar borrarla matando a un descendiente de quien mató a su antepasado. Tras años de búsqueda, encontró la Comarca... ¡y a mí! La punta de flecha que mató a su antepasado fue la que dispararon contra mi puerta.\
\
Creo que sé dónde puedes encontrarlo. Describe el lugar donde ha montado su campamento, y parece que está al oeste de aquí, en el extremo occidental del Pantano de la Rana. ¡Tienes que detenerlo!'","Al leer el diario recompuesto, Wilimar ha descubierto que fue escrito por un Hombre llamado Callum. El antepasado de Callum fue asesinado en una gran batalla por el antepasado de Wilimar, y la familia ha llevado esa muerte como una mancha negra durante siglos. Callum ha decidido borrar la marca viniendo a la Comarca y matando a un descendiente de ese hobbit."},
[12668]={"Dagarm has returned to the trader's outpost along the road west of Elthengels.\
\
You have freed Dagarm, and he has asked you to speak with him upon your return to the trader's outpost.","Guthléod can be found within the trader's outpost west of Elthengels.\
\
Ofrith has suggested asking Guthléod about Dagarm's last known whereabouts.","Talk to Guthléod about Dagarm's whereabouts","You have discovered a trader bound to a post","'Dagarm mentioned that he was heading south-east, beyond the river, to look for some needed supplies. He surely should have returned by now. \
\
'I told him to be cautious, as it seems the enemy has been hiding all around us. Dagarm may have been caught off guard...if you go looking for him, do not make the same mistake.'","Talk to Dagarm at the trader's outpost","Ofrith has noticed that one of the men of the trader's outpost has been missing from camp for quite some time. Some have begun to worry that he has become lost or captured by Orcs.","Dagarm appears to have been captured by the Uruks in the camp beyond the river.\
\
Dagarm wishes to be released from his captivity within the Uruk-hai camp. You may be able to undo the ropes that bind him.","'My captors told me that their leader, Mauhúr, would have plans for me. I wager that I only live now because your arrival preceded his.\
\
'My thanks to you. You are the bravest ${RACE} I have ever known, of this I am certain.'","You have unbound Dagarm from the post","'One of the merchants in our camp has been missing for some time now. Dagarm is his name, and I have a growing concern that something may have happened to him.\
\
'Dagarm frequently speaks with Guthléod when he is in camp. Perhaps Guthléod may know where he has gone to.'","Search for the missing trader, Dagarm","Guthléod thinks that Dagarm travelled south-east along the stream","The Merchant Gone Missing","Free Dagarm from capture","Dagarm was last known to be heading south and east, beyond the river.\
\
Guthléod believes that Dagarm may have headed beyond the river and towards known enemy territory. He has cautioned you to be careful as you search."},
[12669]={"'¡Eres muy fuerte!'","Narnûlubat y Zogtark se pueden encontrar dentro de Noruidor.\
\
Tortrygg te ha pedido que encuentres y derrotes a dos de los líderes de los Ghâshfra, Narnûlubat y Zogtark.","Tortrygg está preocupado por la invasión de Norbar por los Orcos.","Derrota a Narnûlubat","'Eres alguien poderoso, pequeño. Mereces esta recompensa, aunque temo que tu éxito no haya sido suficiente para alejar a los Ghâshfra.'","Derrota a Zogtark","'¿Eres alguien que tiene nuestra amistad, pequeño ser? Entonces escúchame, soy Tortrygg de Norbar. Malvados Orcos de fuego vinieron del mundo de la superficie para conquistarnos y desatar el Gran Mal sobre nosotros. Nos matan, los matamos...no termina.\
\
'Te pido que nos ayudes a poner fin a esta guerra. Ayúdanos a expulsar a los Orcos de fuego. Si puedes matar a Narnûlubat y Zogtark, dos de los líderes de los Ghâshfra, los Orcos de fuego, los demás podrían irse.\
\
'¿Nos ayudarás? Narnûlubat y Zogtark se pueden encontrar dentro de Noruidor.'","Tortrygg se encuentra en el campamento de los Eldgangs dentro de la Grieta de Nûrz Ghâshu.\
\
Debes regresar a Tortrygg con noticias de tu victoria contra Narnûlubat y Zogtark.","'El mal invade nuestro hogar...ayúdanos a derrotarlo, ${PLAYER}.'","Zogtark derrotado","El mensaje","Narnûlubat derrotado"},
[12670]={"'You have defeated many of those cursed message-bearers, then? Good. Perhaps we shall make it to the field of battle undetected. My thanks, ${CLASS}.'","Defeated a message-bearer (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Déorwine","'If the Enemy has word of our passage, I am certain it is carried by Warg-riding message-bearers. We surprised one yesterday morn, and it bore some foul black scratching on some parchment, the meaning of which I could not fathom.\
\
'If you should espy any of these Warg-riders behind us in the Beacon Hills, I implore you to stop them, lest our force should be found out.'","Return to Déorwine in the camp in Taur Drúadan and tell him of the Warg-rider message-bearers you defeated.","Find and defeat Warg-rider message bearers in the Beacon Hills.","The Message Riders","You should defeat any Warg-rider message-bearers you find in the Beacon Hills.","Defeat Warg-rider message-bearers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12671]={"Competidores codiciosos derribados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has dejado caer tu poderoso garrote de enano por el shock de la vergüenza y la derrota","Dale un buen golpe a los compañeros codiciosos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Esta ronda ha terminado; no pudiste superar a tus compañeros a tiempo","Ahora deberías colocar tu garrote como una habilidad: la pelea comenzará pronto","No abandones los límites de la arena de combate","Coloca el garrote de enano en tus habilidades y espera a que comience la pelea","'¡Saludos! Este es un buen lugar para una pelea, ¿no crees? Sé que la cerveza más gloriosa de toda la Tierra Media, orgullo de la Liga de las Posadas, estará disponible para quien tenga la suerte de poner sus manos sobre ella primero. El truco es superar a todos los demás que codician esta cerveza, y espero que sean muchos. No hay cerveza en el mundo tan dorada, profunda o suave. Es suave, oscura y espumosa; enfría la lengua y calienta el corazón.\
\
'Si deseas tener alguna oportunidad, deberías empuñar un poderoso garrote de enano y mantener a los demás alejados. ¡Asegúrate de tener la preparación para luchar antes de entrar en el salón! Si abandonas los límites de ese nivel inferior allá, serás descalificado inmediatamente. ¡Buena suerte a ti, ${PLAYER}!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: El poderoso garrote de enano aparecerá en tu inventario. Deberías colocarlo en un espacio rápido para participar en la pelea. Este objeto no puede usarse fuera de los límites de la arena de combate.</rgb>","La arena de combate es el espacio reducido en el centro del salón, marcado por estandartes verdes. El garrote de enano está en tu inventario.\
\
Gísli Garrotefuerte te ha dado un arma excelente para defender tu premio. Debes entrar en la arena de combate mientras empuñas tu poderoso garrote de enano.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>ADVERTENCIA: Si abandonas la arena de combate después de entrar, soltarás tu garrote. El garrote no puede usarse fuera de los límites de la arena.</rgb>","Recoge la cerveza gloriosa antes de que los demás consigan la última gota","Habla con Gísli Garrotefuerte antes de que se acabe el tiempo","No entraste en la arena de combate a tiempo","No abandones la arena de combate","Se ha acabado el tiempo","¡El combate ha comenzado! Puedes empezar a golpear","El golpe más poderoso","Las personas codiciosas en la arena de combate reducida desean robar la gloriosa cerveza.\
\
¡Dale a los codiciosos que te rodean unos buenos golpes por su impertinencia! Ahora debes hacer lo que sea necesario para recoger la cerveza gloriosa para ti, pero ten cuidado: si abandonas la arena de combate por cualquier motivo, serás descalificado.","Gísli Garrotefuerte está en la arena de la Mansión de Thorin.\
\
Debes hablar con Gísli Garrotefuerte para presumir de tu excelencia en la recolección de la cerveza gloriosa.","Te han desafiado a recoger la cerveza más gloriosa de la Tierra Media, el premio de las celebraciones en la Mansión de Thorin.","'¿Has recogido ya la gloriosa cerveza? ¡No te respetaré hasta que lo hagas!'","Entra en la arena de combate antes de que comience la pelea. No abandones los límites","Los límites de la arena de combate se encuentran en el centro de la sala de cerveza de la Mansión de Thorin, marcados por estandartes verdes.\
\
Debes esperar a que comience el combate.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>ADVERTENCIA: Si abandonas los límites de la arena después de entrar, soltarás tu poderoso garrote de enano. El garrote de enano no puede usarse fuera de los límites de la arena.</rgb>","Has recogido la cerveza gloriosa","Has salido de la arena de combate. Puedes intentarlo de nuevo en 10 minutos, cuando comience la siguiente ronda","'¡Muy bien hecho, ${PLAYER}! Muy, muy bien hecho. ¿Podría... tomar un sorbo de esa cerveza? Si quieres compartir, te daré un gran regalo.'","'Ahora que empuñas el poderoso garrote de enano, ¡deberías entrar en la arena de combate y reclamar tu premio! No te detengas ante nada, ${PLAYER}; ¡no dejes que te desanimen!'"},
[12672]={"Se te ha acabado el tiempo","'No es en absoluto lo que esperaba, ${PLAYER}. Sospecho que quizás no te estabas concentrando en la tarea. ¡Inténtalo una vez más si tienes la determinación!'","Has derribado a un competidor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Ahora que empuñas el poderoso garrote de enano, entra en la arena de combate y muestra tu fuerza! ¡No te detengas, ${PLAYER}; no dejes que te disuadan de tu misión!'","Da un buen golpe a los demás competidores (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Esta ronda ha terminado; no pudiste superar a tus compañeros a tiempo","Ahora deberías colocar tu garrote como una habilidad: la pelea comenzará pronto","Los límites de la arena de combate se encuentran en el centro de la sala de cerveza de la Mansión de Thorin, marcados por estandartes verdes.\
\
Espera a que comience el combate.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>ADVERTENCIA: Si abandonas la arena de combate una vez comenzado el concurso, fallarás la misión.</rgb>","'¡Maravillosamente hecho, ${PLAYER}! Realmente maravilloso. Tu magnífica actuación merece un digno regalo.'","Coloca el garrote de enano en tus habilidades y espera a que comience la pelea","Gísli Garrotefuerte está en la arena de la Mansión de Thorin.\
\
Deberías hablar con Gísli Garrotefuerte para presumir de tu excelencia en el evento de la cerveza gloriosa.","Se te ha desafiado a participar en el concurso de la cerveza gloriosa de la Mansión de Thorin, donde los más poderosos compiten por premios y gloria.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando termine el festival actual. </rgb>","Habla con Gísli Garrotefuerte antes de que se acabe el tiempo","¡El combate ha comenzado! Puedes empezar a golpear","La arena de combate es el espacio reducido en el centro de la arena, marcado por estandartes verdes. El garrote de enano está en tu inventario.\
\
Gísli Garrotefuerte te ha dado un arma excelente para usar durante el concurso. Debes entrar en la arena de combate mientras empuñas tu poderoso garrote de enano.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>ADVERTENCIA: Si abandonas la arena de combate después de entrar, el garrote no podrá usarse fuera de sus límites.</rgb>","'¡Saludos! ¿Estás aquí para participar en los juegos de la cerveza gloriosa?\
\
'Toma este poderoso garrote de enano y prepárate para golpear a tus competidores.\
\
'Hay diferentes objetivos y requisitos para los concursantes; no dudes en hablar conmigo para conocer cada uno.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: El poderoso garrote de enano aparecerá en tu inventario. Puedes colocarlo en un espacio rápido para participar de forma más eficaz en el combate. Este objeto no puede usarse fuera de los límites de la arena.</rgb>","¡Demuestra a todos que eres ${PLAYERNAME:un competidor[m]|una competidora[f]} formidable y da a los demás participantes un buen golpe para hacerlos tambalear!\
\
¡Algunos competidores pueden detenerse para tomar la cerveza gloriosa; apártalos mientras puedas!","Entra en la arena de combate antes de que comience la pelea. No abandones los límites","El golpe más poderoso (Básico)","No entraste en la zona de combate a tiempo"},
[12673]={"Te han desafiado a recoger la cerveza más gloriosa de la Tierra Media, el premio de las celebraciones en la Mansión de Thorin.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando termine el festival actual. </rgb>","'Ahora que empuñas el poderoso garrote de enano, entra en la arena de combate y reclama tu premio. ¡No te detengas, ${PLAYER}, no dejes que te disuadan de tu misión!'","'¡Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}! Muy, muy bien hecho. ¿Podría... tomar un sorbo de esa cerveza? Si estás dispuesto a compartir, te daré un gran regalo.'","Se te ha acabado el tiempo","'¿Has recogido ya la cerveza gloriosa? ¡Quizás mis expectativas para ti eran demasiado altas!'","Has derribado a un competidor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Esta ronda ha terminado; no pudiste superar a tus compañeros a tiempo","Los competidores en la arena de combate reducida desean robar la cerveza gloriosa para sí mismos.\
\
¡Dale a los codiciosos que te rodean unos buenos golpes por su impertinencia! Ahora debes hacer lo que sea necesario para recoger la cerveza gloriosa, pero ten cuidado: si abandonas la arena de combate por cualquier motivo, serás descalificado.","Ahora deberías colocar tu garrote como una habilidad: la pelea comenzará pronto","No abandones los límites de la arena de combate","Coloca el garrote de enano en tus habilidades y espera a que comience la pelea","¡Increíble! Has recogido la cerveza gloriosa","Has dejado caer tu poderoso garrote de enano bajo el impacto de la vergüenza y la derrota","Recoge la cerveza gloriosa antes de que los demás consigan la última gota","Habla con Gísli Garrotefuerte antes de que se acabe el tiempo","No abandones la arena de combate","La arena de combate es el espacio elevado en el centro de la arena, marcado por estandartes verdes. El garrote de enano está en tu inventario.\
\
Gísli Garrotefuerte te ha dado un arma excelente para ganar tu premio. Debes entrar en la arena de combate mientras empuñas tu poderoso garrote de enano.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>ADVERTENCIA: Si abandonas la arena de combate después de entrar, soltarás tu garrote. El garrote no puede usarse fuera de los límites de la arena de combate.</rgb>","El golpe más poderoso (Experto)","Has abandonado la arena de combate. Puedes intentarlo de nuevo en 10 minutos, cuando comience la próxima ronda","¡El combate ha comenzado! Puedes empezar a golpear","Gísli Garrotefuerte está en la arena de la Mansión de Thorin.\
\
Debes hablar con Gísli Garrotefuerte para presumir de tu excelencia en la recolección de la cerveza gloriosa.","Dale un buen golpe a tus competidores (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Saludos de nuevo, ${PLAYER}. No toda la cerveza gloriosa se ha agotado, y hay una oportunidad de conseguir otro vaso antes de que termine el año. ¿Recuerdas cómo obtener este premio? Te lo recordaré. El truco es superar a todos los demás que codician esta cerveza, y espero que sean muchos. No hay cerveza en el mundo tan dorada, profunda o suave. Es suave, oscura y espumosa; enfría la lengua y calienta el corazón.\
\
'Si deseas tener alguna oportunidad, debes empuñar un poderoso garrote de enano y mantener alejados a los demás. ¡Asegúrate de estar listo para luchar antes de entrar en la arena! Si abandonas los límites, serás descalificado inmediatamente. ¡Buena suerte, ${PLAYER}!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: El poderoso garrote de enano aparecerá en tu inventario. Debes colocarlo en un espacio rápido para participar en la pelea. Este objeto no puede usarse fuera de los límites de la arena.</rgb>","Entra en la arena de combate antes de que comience la pelea. No abandones los límites","Los límites de la arena de combate se encuentran en el centro de la sala de cerveza de la Mansión de Thorin, marcados por estandartes verdes.\
\
Debes esperar a que comience el combate.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>ADVERTENCIA: Si abandonas los límites de la arena después de entrar, soltarás tu poderoso garrote de enano. El garrote de enano no puede usarse fuera de los límites de la arena.</rgb>","No entraste en la zona de combate a tiempo"},
[12674]={"'¡Saludos de nuevo, !\
\
'Toma este poderoso garrote de enano y prepárate para golpear a tus competidores. No abandones la arena o quedarás ${PLAYERNAME:eliminado[m]|eliminada[f]} de la competición.\
\
'¡Mucha suerte!'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: El poderoso garrote de enano aparecerá en tu inventario. Debes colocarlo en un espacio rápido para participar en la pelea. Este objeto no puede usarse fuera de los límites de la arena.</rgb>","La arena de combate es el espacio reducido en el centro de la arena, marcado por estandartes verdes. El garrote de enano está en tu inventario.\
\
Gísli Garrotefuerte te ha dado un arma excelente para usar durante el concurso. Debes entrar en la arena de combate mientras empuñas tu poderoso garrote de enano.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>ADVERTENCIA: Si abandonas la arena de combate después de entrar, soltarás tu garrote. El garrote no puede usarse fuera de los límites de la arena.</rgb>","Se te ha acabado el tiempo","¡Demuestra a todos que eres ${PLAYERNAME:un competidor[m]|una competidora[f]} formidable y da a los demás participantes un buen golpe para hacerlos tambalear!\
\
¡Algunos competidores pueden detenerse para tomar la cerveza gloriosa; apártalos mientras puedas, pero ten cuidado: si abandonas la arena de combate por cualquier motivo, quedarás eliminado de la competición!","Has derribado a un competidor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Gísli Garrotefuerte está en la arena de la Mansión de Thorin.\
\
Deberías hablar con Gísli Garrotefuerte para presumir de tu excelencia en la recolección de la cerveza gloriosa.","Esta ronda ha terminado; no pudiste superar a tus compañeros a tiempo","Ahora deberías colocar tu garrote como una habilidad: la pelea comenzará pronto","No abandones los límites de la arena de combate","Coloca el garrote de enano en tus habilidades y espera a que comience la pelea","'Ahora que empuñas el poderoso garrote de enano, entra en la arena de combate y reclama tu premio. ¡No te detengas, ${PLAYER}; no dejes que te disuadan de tu misión!'","Se te ha desafiado a participar en el concurso de la cerveza gloriosa de la Mansión de Thorin, donde los más poderosos compiten por premios y gloria.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000> NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando termine el festival actual. </rgb>","Has dejado caer tu poderoso garrote de enano bajo el impacto de la vergüenza y la derrota","Habla con Gísli Garrotefuerte antes de que se acabe el tiempo","'¡Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}! Realmente les diste un buen golpe. Por tu impresionante demostración de destreza física, mereces un regalo.'","No abandones la arena de combate","Has abandonado la arena de combate. Puedes intentarlo de nuevo en 10 minutos, cuando comience la próxima ronda","¡El combate ha comenzado! Puedes empezar a golpear","El golpe más poderoso (Intermedio)","Dale un buen golpe a tus competidores (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Entra en la arena de combate antes de que comience la pelea. No abandones los límites","Los límites de la arena de combate se encuentran en el centro de la sala de cerveza de la Mansión de Thorin, marcados por estandartes verdes.\
\
Debes esperar a que comience el combate.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>ADVERTENCIA: Si abandonas los límites de la arena después de entrar, soltarás tu poderoso garrote de enano. El garrote de enano no puede usarse fuera de los límites de la arena.</rgb>","'Vaya, no fue exactamente lo que esperaba.\
\
'Inténtalo de nuevo cuando te sientas con preparación para el desafío.'","No entraste en la zona de combate a tiempo"},
[12675]={"Thalfar se encuentra en el campamento situado en el centro de las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata, con vistas a Menem-berej.\
\
Deberías volver con Thalfar.","Se ha reparado una rueda dentada (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","A Thalfar le gustaría reparar los engranajes de Menem-berej, una plataforma situada en las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata que ha sido saqueada por los trasgos.","'Si me preguntas, nuestra mejor esperanza de encontrar mithril en las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata es recuperar y reparar la plataforma de Menem-berej.\
\
'¡Si pudieras empezar por restaurar las ruedas de la plataforma, sería de gran ayuda, ${PLAYER}!',","Repara ruedas dentadas en Menem-berej (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los engranajes se encuentran en la plataforma de Menem-berej, en el centro de las Vetas del Cuerno de Plata.\
\
Thalfar te ha pedido que repares las ruedas dentadas de la plataforma de Menem-berej.","'¡Ah, bien hecho! En un santiamén tendremos el Menem-berej de nuevo a punto.'","Los mineros de Menem-berej","'Hay que reparar las viejas ruedas dentadas antes de que podamos empezar de verdad nuestra expedición minera en esta zona.'","Vuelve con Thalfar"},
[12676]={"Muiráthakh, el Juez Silencioso, comanda la lealtad de muchos guerreros enviados desde Carn Dûm. Artagan quiere que sean eliminados.","Los secuaces de Muiráthakh","Ballesteros de la Corona de Hierro derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Más allá del arco este, los sirvientes de Muiráthakh protegen al Juez Silencioso y sus fallos ilegales. Lleva aliados y da un ejemplo de estos guerreros y ballesteros que lo sirven.'","'¡Los señores de Carn Dûm aprenderán a no jugar con nosotros!'","Guerreros de la Corona de Hierro derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Muiráthakh, el Juez Silencioso, vino acompañado de guerreros de Carn Dûm; ellos lo protegen y aplican sus decisiones. Mientras permanezcan en la ciudad, Donnvail nunca será libre.\
\
'Busca guerreros y ballesteros de la Corona de Hierro en el barrio que se encuentra más allá del arco este, ${PLAYER}. Lleva a tus aliados y derrota a estos sirvientes de Muiráthakh.\
\
'Debemos socavar su autoridad para liberar a Donnvail del yugo de Carn Dûm.'","'¡Donnvail pronto será libre, ${PLAYER}! ¡Estoy seguro de ello!'","Los guerreros y ballesteros de la Corona de Hierro se encuentran en el barrio más allá del arco este de los aliados de Una.\
\
Artagan quiere que socaves el dominio de Muiráthakh en Donnvail derrotando a sus sirvientes.","Artagan está en la ciudad de Donnvail, entre los aliados de Una.\
\
Has derrotado a muchos de los sirvientes de Muiráthakh y debes llevarle noticias de tu éxito a Artagan.","'Has hecho mucho para restaurar la paz en Donnvail, ${PLAYER}, y te lo agradezco. ¡Los señores de Carn Dûm aprenderán a no jugar con los Trév Gállorg!'"},
[12677]={"El cocinero extraviado","Bersi, un enano cocinero, se fue a recoger hierbas cerca de una gran guarida de arañas malvadas al noreste de Kheledûl, pero nunca regresó.","Encuentra a Bersi","'¿Has encontrado a Bersi? ¿No? Probablemente esté cerca de los nidos de arañas, al noreste de Kheledûl... ¡deberías darte prisa para asegurarte de que está bien!","Bersi probablemente esté en o cerca de la guarida de las arañas al noreste de Kheledûl.\
\
Nithi te ha pedido que busques a su amigo Bersi, que fue a recoger hierbas cerca de una guarida de arañas malvadas. Te recomendó que te dirigieras al noreste antes de llegar a Kheledûl para no arriesgarte a un encuentro con los Duramano.","'¿Podría molestarte un momento? Un amigo mío, Bersi, se fue solo a un bosque al noreste de Kheledûl para recoger hierbas para sus recetas. Le advertí sobre la amenaza de arañas malvadas en la zona, pero se rió de ellas.\
\
Bersi es un buen tipo y un gran cocinero, pero a veces puede ser un poco despistado. Mi molestia se ha convertido en preocupación. Tranquiliza la mente de un enano y búscalo, ¿quieres? Estoy seguro de que solo ha perdido la noción del tiempo, pero aun así...\
\
La guarida de las arañas está al noreste de Kheledûl, pero con esos malditos Duramano por ahí, te aconsejaría que tomes el camino largo alrededor del puerto.'"},
[12678]={"Thorlind can be found on the path south of Felegoth.\
\
You should talk to Thorlind.","Talk to Thorlind","The Missing Beornings","Beorning travellers and an Elf scout are missing in the forest. Thorlind, the chief hunter of Felegoth, is concerned that something troubling is afoot.","'Ah, there you are. Ready to begin?'","Thorlind can be found on the path south of Felegoth.\
\
You should find Thorlind.","Find Thorlind on the path south of Felegoth","Thorlind waves you over as you approach","'May I ask for your assistance, ${CLASS}? A matter has been brought to my attention, and I could use the aid of someone battle-tested, like yourself.\
\
'I am Thorlind, chief hunter of Felegoth. This is the situation: A pair of Beorning traders, siblings I believe, were present in Felegoth when King Thranduil ordered the realm closed. They left, taking the path west, but never reached The Forest Gate. I then sent one of my scouts, Glenneth, to find them. She, too, has gone missing. I fear they did not simply lose their way in the forest.\
\
'Meet me on the path south of here. We will follow their trail and see where it leads us.'"},
[12679]={"El niño desaparecido de Herne","'¡He visto a Cai! ¡Sí! Estaba sonámbulo, creo. Su rostro parecía dormido y murmuraba algo. Estaba intentando alcanzar la esfera brillante. No debemos seguir las esferas brillantes. La Dama del Lamento te atrapará. ¡Pregúntale a padre! ¡Le he contado todo lo que vi!'","Habla con Gurthern","'¡Mi niño! ¡Mi hijo ha desaparecido! ¡Por favor! ¡Ayúdame!\
\
'Todo estaba bien la última noche. Acosté a Cai a la hora de siempre, pero, cuando me he despertado esta mañana, ¡había desaparecido! Estaba intentando reunir el valor para dejar la posada y buscarle, pero los jinetes... ¡Los jinetes! ¿Y si se lo han llevado ellos? Por favor, ¿podrías preguntar a mis vecinos si alguien le ha visto? ¿Habrá podido ir a alguna de sus casas?'","'No, lo siento. No he visto al pequeño hoy. ¿Has preguntado a sus amigos? Están jugando en la posada.'","Moll afirma haber visto a Cai sonámbulo y te ha dicho que corrobores la historia con su padre.\
\
El padre de Moll, Rodric, está en la posada de Herne.","Pregunta si alguien en Herne ha visto a Cai","Una madre desesperada necesita ayuda para encontrar a su hijo perdido.","'Si, soy Gurthern. ¿Un niño desaparecido? No, no le he visto, pero dime todo lo que sepas. Quizá pueda ayudar.'","Rodric ha sugerido que le preguntes a Gurthern, el Dunlendino, si ha visto al niño desaparecido.\
\
Gurthern tiene una habitación arriba, en la posada de Herne.","Habla con Rodric","El hijo de Wenna, Cai, ha desaparecido, pero a lo mejor algún vecino le ha visto. Quiere que preguntes a la gente a ver si el niño está con ellos.\
\
Los vecinos de Wenna se encuentran en Herne.","'¿Un niño perdido? ¡Qué tragedia! Es la primera vez que oigo algo sobre ello. Voy a preguntar por aquí, pero no sé dónde está ese niño.'","'¿Qué? ¿Un niño desaparecido? Claro que no lo he visto. Debería de buscarlo ella misma y dejar de meter a los demás en sus problemas. Ya tenemos bastante con lo que está pasando.'","'Mmm. Sí, Moll me dijo que vio a Cai ir detrás de las esferas brillantes. Sinceramente, Moll es bastante imaginativa. No haría mucho caso a lo que ha dicho.\
\
'Si me preguntas, hay alguien que puede saber algo. Deberías hablar con el Dunlendino. ¡Su gente rapta niños todo el tiempo! Le preguntaría yo mismo, pero parece bastante peligroso. Pero no creo que sea un problema para ti, ¿no?\
\
'Está subiendo las escaleras, en su habitación. ¡Pero no le digas que te envío!'"},
[12680]={"El erudito Deluros está en la biblioteca de la Casa de Elrond en Rivendel.\
\
Has recuperado algunos fragmentos irregulares de reliquia. Quizá Deluros pueda usarlos para reconstruir el antiguo jarrón.","Lleva fragmentos irregulares de reliquia a Deluros","Los fragmentos perdidos","'Glorenglir no ha entendido el significado de estos fragmentos, ${PLAYER}, pero yo sí. Son restos de lo que debió ser un hermoso jarrón, creado hace mucho tiempo por algún señor Eldar.\
\
Si puedes recuperar más fragmentos de este jarrón, podría ser posible reconstruirlo. Su antigua gloria pudo perderse por descuido o necesidad, pero la historia nos deja una certeza: aunque esté roto, algo que fue bello puede volver a ser hermoso con cuidado y buena voluntad.\
\
Vuelve a la fuente del Bruinen y busca en los ventisqueros más fragmentos. Las piezas restantes seguramente serán muy irregulares. Si los desentierras tú mismo o confías en los acechadores de nieve de Glorenglir, lo dejo a tu elección. Sin embargo, advierto que la probabilidad de encontrar los fragmentos restantes será bastante baja.'","'Si puedes recuperar fragmentos irregulares de reliquia del mismo lugar al que te envió Glorenglir, quizá pueda reconstruir este antiguo jarrón.\
\
Puedes encontrar estos fragmentos irregulares en los acechadores de nieve, como antes, pero no tengo tanta confianza en esto como Glorenglir. Prefiero que busques en los ventisqueros cerca de la fuente del Bruinen, al norte de Rivendel en las Montañas Nubladas, para encontrar estos fragmentos.'","Los acechadores de nieve se encuentran cerca de la fuente del Bruinen y los ventisqueros de la zona también pueden contener los fragmentos irregulares de reliquia que busca Deluros.\
\
El erudito Deluros te ha pedido que recojas fragmentos irregulares de reliquia cerca de la fuente del Bruinen para que pueda reconstruir el jarrón que Glorenglir descartó tan fácilmente.","Los fragmentos que recuperaste de los acechadores de nieve de las Montañas Nubladas son de interés para el erudito Deluros, aunque Glorenglir no entendió su significado.","'Mientras estabas fuera, ${PLAYER}, pude reconstruir parcialmente el jarrón. ¡Es una cosa hermosa, incluso incompleta! Me pregunto quién lo hizo y las circunstancias que lo llevaron a quedar abandonado en pedazos bajo la nieve de las montañas.\
\
¡Veo que has traído algunos fragmentos irregulares contigo! Veré si alguno de ellos pertenece a este jarrón.'"},
[12681]={"Free Ubdun","You have found the brigand camp, and saw that they are holding a prisoner. You should defeat the brigands and free their prisoner.","You have freed Ubdun from being taken prisoner by brigands. He has returned to tend his goats and asked you to talk to Zidek in Western Khanâg.","'Excuse me, could I bother you for a moment? My partner should have been back by now and I am worried about him. I would look for him, but I cannot leave my shop. He took the goats out to graze and has yet to return. I told him not to go too close to Jirush, but I fear he has done it anyway.\
\
'There are some evil folk out that way, I told him, and of course, he says there are evil folk everywhere. He is not wrong, but I have heard some brigands have been camping in that area, and I do not like it. Would you check on him and see that he and the goats are safe? I am finding it difficult to focus on my work.'","Defeated Khûdi toughs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have found some goats","Talk to Ubdun","You found the brigand camp, and they are holding a prisoner","You have defeated the brigands and freed their prisoner, Ubdun the goatherd. You should return to where you saw the goats near Jirush and talk to Ubdun.","<rgb=#00FF00>Look</rgb> for the goatherd","'Where is Ubdun?'\
\
You recount the tale of what happened, and Zidek looks both relieved and frustrated.\
\
'I am glad he is safe, but curse him, he is probably right that there would be some sort of danger no matter where he took them. I do not know what else there is to be done. Thank you for your help, especially for saving Ubdun.'","Look near Jirush, to the south-east of Western Khanâg, for the missing goatherd.","Near Jirush, you have found goats without a goatherd. Was he harmed by brigands, as Zidek feared? You should find the camp Zidek mentioned.","Defeat Khûdi toughs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Find the missing goatherd","Find the nearby brigand camp","Zidek's partner, Ubdun, is out herding goats but should have returned by now. The butcher has asked you to ensure the goatherd is all right and thinks he may have gone in the direction of Jirush.","The Missing Goatherd","'Thank you for saving me! It was lucky you happened by.'\
\
You tell him it was no accident, and that Zidek had sent you to find him.\
\
'Bless Zidek, I hope he is not too cross with me. There is nowhere in the Khûd that is not dangerous, and the goats must be taken somewhere to graze. This patch of green is as good as any. Give my thanks to Zidek for sending you, and tell him I will return when the goats have had their fill.'","Talk to Zidek in Western Khanâg","There is nobody about","You have found goats near Jirush. You should look for the goatherd."},
[12682]={"'You return! What news of Rendis?'\
\
You let her know that the librarian is safe, and on her way back to the city with the medical tomes.\
\
'Holed away in a cave and lost track of time? That fool of a girl was always getting lost in a book! Well, I am equal parts annoyed and relieved. I will let Atharon know to expect her back. He and I will have a very stern talk with Rendis about all of this.\
\
'I suppose this is the best possible outcome I could have hoped for. You have my thanks.'","The cover of this book reads 'To Break and to Bind,' and seems to be about setting bones and how to make splints.","You found a cave-mouth","Return to Brunil","The binding of this slim book shows signs of heavy use, and its pages are dog-eared and creased. The title is 'Midnight in the Garden,' and its contents are enough to make one's cheeks redden.","Search the hillside for caves","'Hiding in a cave? All this time? What a fool that girl is. I insist you find her and bring her back at once. Come to think of it, even if you just return with the stolen books, that's fine with me. Hmph!'","After speaking with a couple of merchants in Imloth Melui, Rendis's intentions have become clearer. The path she chose to tread is one of danger, however, and it's unclear whether she or the precious tomes she carried away have survived.","Search for Rendis","This appears to be a compendium of various ancient texts, and presents and overview of medicine as it was practiced in ages long past. Flipping to a random page, you pause as you read a suggestion for applying spoiled sheep's milk mixed with week-old fish guts directly to a wound.","The Missing Librarian","The binding of this ancient book is cracked and warped with age. Its title has been worn away and lost with time, but its pages are full of drawings displaying organs and other things that are possibly better left inside one's body.","'Bags full of books, seeds, and a cart of food? I know for sure there were no parties or gatherings around the time she vanished, as we were preparing for potential invasion!\
\
'Just a moment - the merchant said she headed off west? Could she have... hmmm. There is a cave in that direction that Rendis has mentioned before. She was always insisting that the dry air within would be beneficial to some of our mouldier books.... But... you don’t think...?\
\
'Please, ${PLAYER}, the cave is west of here, someplace between Imloth Melui and Tumladen. You should take the south road out of the city and pass through the forest. I wish I knew more, but please, search for her there?'","While searching the hills west of Imloth Melui, you have come across a cave-mouth. You should explore the cave for any sign of Rendis or her books.","Rendis has been found and has promised to return to the city of Imloth Melui. She has asked you to inform Brunil of her whereabouts and plans.\
\
Brunil is in the Halls of Healing, in Imloth Melui.","This is 'Gondorian Herbology,' a book on remedies made from plants and herbs found across Gondor.","Atharon has suggested that Rendis may be hiding out in a nearby cave. You should search the forest west of Imloth Melui.","'Who- who are you?'\
\
You explain that Brunil and Atharon have sent you to find her.\
\
'Brunil and Atharon? They yet live? Oh, what a happy day this is! Uh, on that topic... what day is it, exactly?'\
\
Her mouth drops open with shock as you tell her the date.\
\
'How did so many days, nay, weeks pass? And you say that the war is over, and the Enemy is no longer a threat? My goodness. I came up here with some of our more essential medical texts, you see. I was sure the Morgul-horde would soon be on our doorstep and that Imloth Melui would fall to their flames. My beloved books... well, they are such important texts. I could not risk them, you see. I only meant to stay for a bit. I really did mean to check back and see if it was safe to return. Only, I suppose I got distracted reading.'\
\
She sighs, looking wistfully about the cozy cave.\
\
'Well, I suppose it is time to make my way back. Thank you for bringing me this news. I shall take some time to pack up my things. Please let Brunil and my teacher know that I am returning.'","This slim, unassuming book is entitled, 'Poisonous Plants of Pelennor and Beyond.'"},
[12683]={"Encuentra y defiende a Malloval","El Explorador Perdido","El halcón ha sido herido por una flecha y salta inquieto. Debe ser defendido de sus enemigos, o sin duda perecerá.","La presencia conjunta de tumularios y Corcur sugiere que los hombres de las colinas están aliados con quien sea —o lo que sea— que ha alzado a los Muertos. Uno de los hombres de las colinas podría portar un emblema o símbolo que indique a quién sirven...","Este sería un buen lugar para usar el silbato de Calenthon","Calenthon envió hace tiempo a su halcón Malloval a explorar las ruinas de Rhudaur en Nan Tornaeth, pero Malloval no ha regresado.","Las ruinas están sobre el campamento de Calenthon, al que se llega tomando el sendero hacia el norte y el este desde su campamento.\
\
Tras usar el silbato de Calenthon, oíste el grito de un halcón sobre las ruinas cerca del puente de Thoniant en Nan Tornaeth.","Localiza a Malloval","Completado","'Si aún no lo has deducido, Malloval es un halcón, veloz de alas y agudo de vista. Lo envié a averiguar lo que pudiera sobre la fuerza y los planes de los Corcur, pero no ha regresado.\
\
'Uso este silbato para llamarlo cuando vuela lejos entre los picos y valles...Tómalo y sube la colina hacia el sur. Sopla el silbato desde su ladera inclinada, y Malloval debería acudir a ti, o al menos responder a tu llamado con uno propio. Si es lo segundo, ve hacia él, pues es probable que esté en peligro.\
\
'Ten cuidado, ¡los Corcur son peligrosos en gran número!'","Has defendido con éxito a Malloval","Usa el silbato de Calenthon en la ladera sur","La ladera al sur de Calenthon sería un lugar ideal para soplar el silbato que te dio y llamar a Malloval.\
\
Calenthon te dio un silbato para invocar a su halcón, Malloval."},
[12684]={"Find whoever is responsible for this terrible act","The scouting party was last seen somewhere in central Elderslade.\
\
You should search for any signs of the scouting party.","'All dead and slain by Angmarim?! If I had known those evil Men were in league with Gundabad, I would have sent out war parties, not just an agile scouting party! There is no time to grieve now, my friend. We shall mourn and grieve after Gundabad is taken.'","The trail of blood seems to point in the direction of the ruins of Shakal-atrâd","The scouting party was last seen somewhere in central Elderslade.\
\
You should follow the trail of blood.","This does not bode well for the scouts","Examina la sangre","The Angmarim priest is performing a ritual with the recently slain!","Search for any signs of the scouting party","Shakal-atrâd can be found in central Elderslade.\
\
You should find who ever is responsible for killing the members of the scouting party.","Lóssi, a captain of the guard, is worried about a scouting party that has yet to report back to him.","Follow the trail of blood","Rásmar Blood-rue has been defeated!","It would seem the scouting party was killed and their bodies brought to Shakal-atrâd","Lóssi can be found at Annâk-khurfu.\
\
You should report back to Lóssi.","There was bloodshed here","Defeat Rásmar Blood-rue","Rásmar Blood-rue can be found in Shakal-atrâd.\
\
You should defeat Rásmar Blood-rue.","The Missing Scouts","The blood has been smeared across the old dwarf-watch","'Ah the great fighter. We meet again! I wish that I was in a better mood to regale stories with you, ${CLASS}. It is not so, for a scouting party under my command has gone missing.\
\
'We must find this scouting party. I know each of those who I send to scout Elderslade. They are all good dwarves and would do the same if either of us had gone missing. I know I shouldn't, but I fear the worst.'","The scouting party was last seen somewhere in central Elderslade.\
\
You should examine the blood.","Report back to Lóssi at Annâk-khurfu"},
[12686]={"Collect Ithamar's missing trinket","'Welcome to our camp. I understand that Lanbert has explained our situation to you? Dealing with these encroaching Orcs is frightening. Many years has it been since they have wandered openly outside of their caves.\
\
'During our last patrol, we encountered a small party of Orcs waiting in ambush, just south-west of the road. We managed to wound a few of them and escape, but in the skirmish, I dropped a small trinket. It may not be worth much silver, but it has personal value, and I miss it dearly.\
\
'I have orders not to leave camp...would you be willing to search for it on my behalf? It would mean a great deal to me.'","Collected Ithamar's missing trinket","'Oh, you have found it! Aye, this is it. Thank you, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'As soldiers, we are allowed very few personal comforts while on duty, making the loss of my keepsake even more difficult to endure. Having it in my possession once again has already raised my spirits.'","Return the trinket to Ithamar at the Cuthstan-camp","The Missing Trinket","Ithamar can be found at the Cuthstan-camp in Wailing Hills.\
\
Ithamar waits for the return of his treasured trinket.","Ithamar has lost a small trinket while on patrol and wishes to have his personal keepsake returned to him.","'Have you found my trinket, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'Search among the items left in the wake of the clash, a few paces south-west of camp. It may still be there if the Orcs have not discovered it.'","Ithamar believes that he lost his trinket in a skirmish that took place south-west of the road that leads east to Stangard.\
\
Ithamar would like for you to find his missing trinket and return it to him at the Cuthstan-camp."},
[12687]={"Bring the supplies to Hertha","Collect the supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have successfully defended the supplies!","The waggon is on the main road in Elderslade.\
\
You should defend the supplies from the raiders.","Hertha can be found at Shakal-atrâd.\
\
You should bring the supplies to Hertha.","<rgb=#FF0000>Do not leave the supplies unguarded</rgb>","You have left the supplies unguarded","The waggon is on the main road in Elderslade.\
\
You should collect the supplies.","The waggon is on the main road in Elderslade.\
\
You should more closely inspect the waggon.","The waggon is somewhere on the main road in Elderslade.\
\
You should search for the waggon.","This dwarf has been slain by an Orkish arrow!","'The waggon should have been here by now.'\
\
You ask to what waggon Hertha is referring.\
\
'There is a supply waggon coming from Limlók. Runerik is quite a punctual Beorning, so if the waggon is not here, I start to think that something is amiss! Would you search for the waggon in Elderslade for me? I would be happier if I knew the supplies were safe!'","Search for the waggon in Elderslade","Defend the supplies from the raiders","Make a closer inspection of the waggon","Hertha worries that a waggon of supplies from Limlók has not reached Elderslade yet.","The Missing Waggon","Collected the supplies (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","It looks as if the waggon broke down","'Blast, I knew it. I should have escorted that waggon myself! Of course we have the supplies, but at the loss of lives. We are here to help, not to hinder this war effort. I will make it up to these dwarves, I can promise you that.'"},
[12688]={"The Mission to Goblin-town","Skalla can be found in Vegbár, the Beorning outpost in northern Wolf-denes.\
\
You should talk to Skalla.","Help Langhár with 'Thinning Their Ranks'","Help Langhár with 'Interlopers from the North'","The Beorning scout near the Goblin-gate can escort you into Goblin-town.\
\
You should enter Goblin-town to disrupt the hobgoblins' takeover.","The goblins have split their loyalty between the Great Goblin and the hobgoblin invaders from Gundabad. An escalation to war is imminent, but it is in the best interest of the Free Peoples to make sure the Great Goblin has a fighting chance.","Langhár has asked you to find a way into Goblin-town to disrupt the hobgoblins inside.\
\
You should complete 'Watchers at the Gate' and find the Beorning scout near the Goblin-gate.","'I am not sure I have ever seen Skalla so concerned. There must be something we can do....'\
\
Langhár trails off, lost in thought. A wry smile suddenly crosses her face.\
\
'I have a crazy idea, ${PLAYER}, but it might just work. So, we have two goblin hosts to deal with, not enough Beornings to deal with either, and in the middle of it all the hobgoblins and the Great Goblin plan to fight it out? If their forces are closely matched, they might just kill each other off, and all we would have to do is mop up the survivors!\
\
'Based on what you saw in Waldfast, I think the Great Goblin is at a disadvantage in numbers. Perhaps we should even the odds?\
\
'I have some ideas for what we can do to pull this off. While you are dealing with things in Goblin-town, I am going to visit some good friends and see if I can get their help. Ask Skalla if he can help get you inside.'","This warlord must be the leader here","'Good to see you in one piece, ${PLAYER}. How fared your mission into Goblin-town?'\
\
You tell Skalla that you believe you were able to even the odds between the hobgoblins and the Great Goblin. You also saw the hobgoblin warlord, Shárnakh, while you were inside.\
\
'Shárnakh. At least we have a name for our enemy now. If you were successful, and it sounds like you were, the Great Goblin will want to press his advantage while he has it, before more forces from Gundabad arrive.\
\
'Langhár has not yet returned, and was rather mysterious about where she was going. I hope you are ready to face the goblins without her.'","The Beorning scout whistles to get your attention","Now that you have access to the Goblin-town throne room, you should do what you can to interfere with the hobgoblins' efforts there.\
\
You should complete quests inside Goblin-town, and find the hobgoblins' leader.","Skalla can be found in Vegbár.\
\
You should talk to Skalla.","Enter Goblin-town by speaking to the Beorning Scout","Talk to Skalla","Find the hobgoblins' leader","Help Langhár with 'Watchers at the Gate'","'So, you wish to enter Goblin-town. I overheard your plans. This seems incredibly risky, but I will not stop you. It may be our only path to success.\
\
'I have a scout stationed near the Goblin-gate. She will be able to get you near to where the hobgoblins have holed themselves up. Find her.'","Find the Beorning scout","Help Langhár with 'Informing the Masses'","'Yes, I can get you inside. Let me know when you are ready.'"},
[12689]={"Las Montañas Nubladas","Glóin ha acampado en las Montañas Nubladas y está intentando acabar con las amenazas del lugar.\
\
Glóin se encuentra en su campamento en el suroeste de las Montañas Nubladas.","Habla con Glóin en las Montañas Nubladas","'Hay mucho que hacer en las Montañas Nubladas, al norte. Los gigantes han empezado a vagar sin rumbo y hay trasgos por pululando de aquí para allá. Temo que nuestra frontera al norte ya no sea segura, ${PLAYER}. Un viejo amigo de los elfos, Glóin, tiene un campamento al norte de aquí, en la zona suroeste de las Montañas Nubladas.\
\
'Encuentra a Glóin en las Montañas Nubladas y mira qué puedes hacer para ayudarle.'","Glóin está atendiendo múltiples problemas en las Montañas Nubladas y le vendría bien algo de ayuda.","'Hay mucho que hacer aquí. Me alegro de que estés aquí para ayudarnos en nuestra causa.'"},
[12690]={"Lleva el granate potenciado a Mundgeirr","'¡Hola! Veo que sigues de una pieza. Excelente y, lo que es mejor aún, ¡has potenciado el granate! Un trabajo soberbio, sí señor.\
\
'Venga, dame esa piedra y ¡veremos si podemos otorgar la calidad que buscas!'","¡No has logrado expulsar a los orcos de las minas!","'¿Es que no has sido capaz de potenciar la piedra? Sin un granate potenciado no puedo ayudarte.'","Mundgeirr sabe de una antigua mina de mithril que alberga una forja de fundición, donde podrás sentar las bases de la calidad que buscas otorgar a tu arma. Desafortunadamente, una banda de orcos especialmente salvajes se ha apoderado de la mina y ha esclavizado a sus propios hermanos trasgos para explotar los filones agotados, con la esperanza de conseguir unos pocos y míseros fragmentos de mineral de mithril para sus amos.","'Si estás listo, los orcos también. Con suerte estarán tan ocupados cavando y gritándose que ni te verán... pero te hará falta mucha fuerte.\
\
'No olvides que necesitarás mineral de mithril para imbuir el granate; tendrás que tomárselo prestado a los orcos por el camino.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión es en solitario; no se puede completar en hermandad.</rgb>","Mundgeirr te ha pedido que le lleves un granate imbuido con el que poder ayudarte a otorgar una calidad a tu arma. Sin embargo, no sabe dónde encontrar tal piedra.","A Mundgeirr se le puede encontrar en el Campamento del Mirador de la Gran Excavación, en Moria.\
\
Mundgeirr te ha pedido que vuelvas a hablar con él cuando estés listo para buscar la forja, pero te advierte de que una despiadada banda de orcos y sus esclavos trasgos se han apoderado de la mina de mithril.","A Mundgeirr se le puede encontrar en el Campamento del Mirador de la Gran Excavación, en Moria.\
\
Debes regresar con Mundgeirr para completar la mejora de tu arma.","'¡Ah! Veo que has logrado echarle el guante a un granate imbuido.\
\
'Me llevará algún tiempo preparar la piedra. Cuando estés listo para partir hacia la mina, házmelo saber y te la devolveré.'","'Si lo que buscas es mejorar las habilidades de tu arma, hay un lugar en el que sin duda sentarás las bases para obtener tal habilidad.¡Hay una vieja mina de mithril, agotada hace mucho tiempo, pero en cuyo interior se encontraba una magnífica forja bendecida con poderosos hechizos para la fundición del mineral de mithril!\
\
'Por supuesto, ahora los orcos la tienen en su poder y han puesto a trabajar a sus hermanos trasgos como esclavos, intentando arañar los últimos retazos de mineral de la peor calidad. Dudo que sepan algo sobre la forja, o que les importe lo más mínimo, pero tendrás que abrirte paso a golpes entre ellos si quieres hacer utilizarla.\
\
'Sin embargo, antes de desafiar los peligros de la mina, deberías traerme un granate imbuido. Solo con una piedra así lograrás mejorar tu arma. Aunque me temo que no sé dónde encontrar un granate de esa clase.'","Lleva un granate infundido a Mundgeirr","Los esclavos del mithril","'¡Ah! Un trabajo excelente el de la mina. Confío en que la calidad sea todo lo que esperabas.'","'Necesitarás traerme un granate imbuido antes de que podamos comenzar.'","Habla con Mundgeirr para viajar a la mina de mithril"},
[12692]={"'Have you heard of the fabled underground realm, Thafar-gathol, the Grey Citadel? No dwarf has ever found it, but the lost realm is said to exist somewhere in these northern mountains. I have brought a moon-letter from the east with me. It is said this letter contains a clue as to the location of Thafar-gathol. The tale goes, if a great dwarf finds the Stave of Veluk-zámok, the path to Thafar-gathol will become clear.\
\
'Here, you may borrow the moon-letter, if you like. I am at an end with this riddle. I am no closer to finding the Stave now than I was before I came to Ered Mithrin.'","Hórin, a Zhélruka Dwarf tasked to dealing with outsiders, seeks assistance in deciphering an ancient moon-letter.","You should search in the Grey Mountains for the third location, described in moon-runes, on Hórin's parchment.","You tell Hórin how you followed the clues and learned the location of the Stave of Veluk-zámok. His eyes widen.\
\
'In Glimmerdeep, of all places, among the treasure of a dragon! Yet dragon and treasure are not to be found? And why not? Centuries upon centuries have passed. And yet dragons live longer than centuries....\
\
'Perhaps, perhaps not all hope is lost.'","This must be the location of the Stave!","You should search in the Grey Mountains for the location hinted at in Hórin's parchment.","Look for a clue in the Glimmerdeep","Read the moon-runes","It seems no dragon or its hoard remain here","The Moon-runes of Veluk-zámok","You should search in the Grey Mountains for the second location, described in moon-runes, on Hórin's parchment.","You should inspect the parchment that Hórin gave you.","You should read the moon-runes on the parchment.","Solve the parchment's second riddle","The Glimmerdeep can be found north of Skarháld in the Grey Mountains.\
\
You should examine the location in the Glimmerdeep mentioned on Hórin's parchment.","Inspect the parchment","Habla con Hórin","Solve the parchment's riddle","This must be the location","As you read, additional text appears!","Hórin may be in Skarháld or adventuring with you.\
\
You should talk to Hórin.","Solve the parchment's third riddle"},
[12693]={"The enemy hideout is in the culverts beneath the ruins of after-battle Osgiliath.\
\
You should enter the culverts and find the enemy hideout.","Defeated Kamábhil","Defeat foes in the culverts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Gladhir has just returned, and confirms that there are enemies hiding in a section of the culverts we had thought to be collapsed. The Variags were true to their word. I suppose it is up to us, then, to honour our half of the deal and let them pass unharmed through North Ithilien. I will send word.\
\
'${PLAYER}, take to the culverts. Defeat the forces gathered there and make sure they do not have the strength to make trouble for the Host of the West.'","Defeat Kamábhil","Return to Mablung","Enemigo derrotado (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The raiding party hides in the culverts of after-battle Osgiliath.\
\
You should defeat the Morgul raiding party.","You should return to Mablung, who can be found at the Ranger encampment in after-battle Osgiliath.","The Morgul Holdout","With the claims of the Variags confirmed, Mablung has asked you to defeat the enemies hiding within the culverts of Osgiliath.","'Good work. You have helped us secure Osgiliath and made safe passage for the Host of the West. I commend your work.'","Search the culverts for the enemy hideout","A large Morgul raiding party is hiding down here"},
[12695]={"Gather water from the Morgulduin, further upstream","The Morgulduin","The water appears to be somewhat clean","Speak to Rauniel by the banks of the Morgulduin","Sample water from a tributary into the Morgulduin","Sample water from the Morgulduin closer to its source","The Morgulduin River runs through Rath Dúath.\
\
You should find tributaries into the Morgulduin and sample the water there.","The Morgulduin River runs through Rath Dúath.\
\
You should sample the water of the Morgulduin, further upstream, past its tributaries.","Sample water from another tributary into the Morgulduin","Gather water from a northern tributary into the Morgulduin","'Faramir has asked me to continue studying the waters of the Morgulduin, but I have yet to learn what might be causing this corruption. You helped me retrieve river samples once before, might you do the same again? I am certain we will find the answers if we work together. Does a tributary passing through the city taint these waters, or does the problem lie near the river's source? Would you take water samples from nearby tributaries into the Morgulduin and a sample closer to the river's source for me? I would be most grateful for your assistance, my friend.'","'What interest have you with this river? Speak now, ${RACE}.'","Rauniel can be found by the banks of the Morgulduin in northern Rath Dúath.\
\
You should speak to the mysterious woman.","Gather water from a southern tributary into the Morgulduin","Someone watches you as you examine the corrosive and vile waters","Arodor seeks to know more about the Morgulduin River. He is specifically interested in finding a way to cure its putrid waters."},
[12696]={"'Antes de empezar, tendrás que traerme un zafiro imbuido. Solo una piedra así servirá para otorgar la mejora que deseas a tu arma.'","'El tiempo corre... Si no te marchas pronto, esas morroval carroñeras no te dejarán ni un par de tenazas con las que trabajar.¿Estás listo para partir?'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión es en solitario y no se puede completar en comunidad.</rgb>","Lleva el zafiro potenciado a Mundgeirr","Encontrarás a Mundgeirr en el campamento del Mirador de la Gran Excavación, en Moria.\
\
Regresa con él para completar la mejora de tu arma.","Mundgeirr te ha hablado de una antigua forja donde antaño se creaban algunas de las mejores armas de Moria. Sin embargo, poco después de que los enanos la redescubrieran, una horda de merrevail expulsadas de sus propias cavernas empezó a saquearla, llevándose las herramientas y los materiales de su interior.","Habla con Mundgeirr para viajar a la forja antigua","Mundgeirr te ha pedido que le lleves un zafiro potenciado para poder mejorar tu arma. Por desgracia, no sabe exactamente dónde encontrarlo.","Encontrarás a Mundgeirr en el campamento del Mirador de la Gran Excavación, en Moria.\
\
Te ha pedido que busques la forja de la que te habló, pero advierte que una banda desesperada de morroval parias se ha hecho con el control del lugar. Habla con él cuando estés listo para partir.","'¡Ah, ha sido una gran batalla!¡Haber ayudado a esas morroval carroñeras y rescatado la forja es todo un logo! Con ella a salvo y en nuestras manos, tendremos más posibilidades de resistir en Moria.'","Lleva un zafiro imbuido a Mundgeirr","'Sí, hay una forja con la calidad que buscas. La descubrinmos recientemente, pero al poco tiempo de reabrir las salas, una banda desesperada de merrevail expulsadas de las cavernas orientales irrumpió en el lugar y ahuyentó a mis hombres.\
\
Desde entonces, lo han estado destrozando y saqueando todo. Si logras entrar y evitas que escapen con las herramientas, podrás usar la forja para preparar tu arma como deseas.\
\
'Sin embargo, antes de que podamos siquiera plantearnos atacar a las merrevail, necesitas traerme un zafiro imbuido. Habla conmigo de nuevo cuando estés listo para partir.'","Las morroval proscritas","'Ah, veo que has conseguido un zafiro imbuido. Ahora tendrás que llevar esta piedra a la antigua forja de la que te hablé.'","'¿No has sido capaz de potenciar la piedra? Sin un zafiro potenciado, no puedo ayudarte.'","'¡Así que has logrado ahuyentar a esos merrevail y restaurar la forja!¡Bien hecho!\
\
'Ahora has potenciado la piedra, podré completar el proceso y ¡por fin podrás imbuir una mejora en tu arma!'","¡Las merrevail han escapado con el botín!"},
[12697]={"Collect Orders from Durthúl","Collect Orders from Rhanarch","The Most Valuable Commodity","'I have a task for you, if you are prepared to venture forth.\
\
'We are few here, and are lacking in information more than anything else. In enemy territory, information is the most valuable commodity. I need someone to find and remove lieutenants of the enemy and search them for any orders from Lhaereth. I believe you are best suited to this task as you have experience fighting the merrevail, and you are among the most skilled in our forces.'\
\
You ask Faeron if he has a task in mind for Dolenthol, as you can vouch for his skill in combat.\
\
'Dolenthol? I do not believe I am acquainted with him. Is he the Ithilien Ranger who arrived with you? If you say he is skilled, I will have him assist me with establishing message and supply lines with the lower tiers and Faramir's camp. Worry not, I will allow no harm to come to your friend.'","Faeron has asked you to find merrevail lieutenants and uncover orders from Lhaereth.\
\
You should find and defeat Ogolúm, Durthúl, and Rhanarch within the Circle of Madness.","The Circle of Madness has been invaded by Lhaereth's forces. Faeron thinks it prudent to discover what it is the winged-folk seek.","'Faeron will have me assist with establishing supply lines? Not quite the mission I was hoping for, but I understand the need. Be safe out there, ${PLAYER}. I will see you when you return.'","'Busca cualquier mención de Morloth en los tomos y pergaminos del Círculo de la Locura.'","Faeron can be found in Barad Elenath, the Star-gazers' Spire.\
\
You should talk to Faeron.","Collect Orders from Ogolúm","Dolenthol can be found in Barad Elenath, the Star-gazers' Spire.\
\
You should talk to Dolenthol.","Talk to Faeron","'Welcome back, ${PLAYER}. What have you discovered?'\
\
You show Faeron the orders Lhaereth issued to her lieutenants. He reads them with a puzzled expression.\
\
'I was correct, she is looking for something, but I do not know who or what Morloth is. The Halls of Black Lore, however... I have heard rumours of a great repository of dark knowledge held by the Witch-king somewhere in the city; this must be the same hall. If Lhaereth seeks this place, we must seek it as well.'","Talk to Dolenthol","'Find the Halls of Black Lore. Find a way in. Find its keeper.'","'El Círculo de la Sabiduría era bien conocido por sus jardines. Búscalo por todas partes.'"},
[12699]={"Help Grimbold rally his spirits","'Nothing you say to me can save Rohan, ${PLAYER}....'","Grimbold is at the Fords of Isen in the Westfold.\
\
You should help Grimbold to rally his spirits and answer the call to arms once more.","You must attempt to motivate Grimbold to rise again and fight, for the king and for Rohan.","The Mustering","You urge Grimbold to rouse himself.\
\
'Why? Why should I? Nobody will stand with me. Everyone has retreated, and the enemy cannot be kept out.'","Habla con Gandalf","'A little later than I would have liked, but I believe that this turn of events has been fortuitous.\
\
'I do not think I would have been able to gather them all without you, ${PLAYER}.'","Gandalf is at Erkenbrand's camp in the western Westfold.\
\
You should speak with Gandalf."},
[12700]={"The staff remains unbroken.\
\
You cannot leave it in the possession of the Angmarim, for they will use it for some evil purpose. You must take it with you. Perhaps Hórin will know of a place where this artifact can be made safe?","Once again examine the mysterious staff on the table in the Angmarim tent","You have found a mysterious staff in the main tent of Mullach Cagar. You feel it must be a powerful evil artifact.\
\
You should destroy the mysterious staff.","Search inside the tents at Mullach Cagar","This ornate staff has been placed in a prominent position in this central tent, surrounded by a runic circle and many-faceted crystals. What ill-intentioned ritual were the Angmarim performing here?\
\
Standing beside the staff makes you feel unpleasantly queasy; you are overcome with a sensation of great distrust. The purple glow of the gem mounted atop the staff fills your vision and you are falling, falling....\
\
You snap from your reverie. This is an artifact of evil, and you should destroy it if you can.","Find Mullach Cagar, the Angmarim camp south of Fellgát","The staff has completely rebuffed your attack.\
\
You should investigate the staff again.","You now have the mysterious staff in your possession. The nausea and paranoia it causes is slowly increasing.\
\
You should return to Hórin and Molkha on the frozen lake south-west of Fellgát.","The Angmarim have made camp south of Fellgát.\
\
You should find Mullach Cagar.","The Angmarim have been allowed passage into Welkin-lofts by the Frost-horde, but for what purpose did they come to these high peaks?","The staff is unaffected by your attack","Destroy the mysterious staff","You have found a strange staff. You feel uneasy standing near it.","'Our next objectives should be to investigate what the Angmarim are up to, and to do whatever damage we can to the nest of drakes above us. Molkha has located an Angmarim camp to the south-east, not far from here, called Mullach Cagar. I trust you, mighty ${PLAYER}, can handle a small group of Angmarim on your own. I am going to stay here with Molkha to attack this nest of drakes. If you would prefer to handle the drakes yourself before we move on, I will not stop you! Most importantly, I need you to find some evidence of why the Angmarim chose to come all the way up to the Welkin-lofts in the first place. They risked much to get this far.'","Talk to Hórin in the valley","You have discovered the Angmarim camp of Mullach Cagar.\
\
You should search the camp for clues to the Angmarim's purpose here.","You have found the Angmarim camp called Mullach Cagar","The Mysteries of Mullach Cagar","Examine the mysterious staff on the table in the Angmarim tent","As you pick up the staff, you hear faint whispering but cannot make out the words","You have found a strange staff in Mullach Cagar.\
\
You should investigate it more closely.","Take the mysterious staff from the table in the Angmarim tent","'${PLAYER}, you return! Did you find anything in Mullach Cagar? Wait... something about your demeanour has changed. What has happened?'\
\
You show Hórin the staff. His eyes widen and his skin blanches.\
\
'What in the name of the First Crafter is THAT?'\
\
You explain that you found it in the Angmarim camp and believe it to be a powerful artifact of evil. You tell him too that it resisted your efforts to destroy it.\
\
'Well, I think you were right to take it. We can't let the Angmarim keep such an artifact of evil. But I am no expert on the subject of fighting such magic! Who knows what might be unleashed if we did manage to destroy it? I think it might just be best for you to hold onto it for now. You are the most powerful among us, and we don't have time to cart it off to your Wizard-friend Gandalf! We have a war to fight!'","The mysterious staff cannot be destroyed through any means you currently have at your disposal.\
\
You have decided you must take the mysterious staff with you."},
[12701]={"Talk to Nestawen at Estolad Mernael","Nestawen can be found at Estolad Mernael, the Malledhrim camp in the Drownholt.\
\
You should speak with Nestawen immediately and tell her of the particularly fell pool in the Drownholt.","'How awful! I could not perceive the difference when I walked through that pool upon Alagos, for the evil of this swamp is overwhelming wherever I go. I wonder what troubles the waters there....'","'We are terribly distraught, randir. This dear one fell ill as we passed through the swamp-lands. It was day when we crossed the Drownholt, and Alagos bore me hither. But after a time his step became slower, and the moment we had successfully defeated the Orcs in a great skirmish, he collapsed where he stood.\
\
'He seemed to sleep, but alas, he recedes further from my calls every moment! I fear there is not much time to cure whatever malice ails him, ${PLAYER}. What wretchedness could affect him thus? The Drownholt is an evil place.\
\
'Until we know exactly where this began, I do not think we can help him. I fear to leave his side, though -- I am doing everything I can to hold him here. Could you go into the swamp and seek the source of this malady?'","'Please hurry, ${PLAYER}. I do not think I can keep Alagos with us much longer if I do not know more about what befell him in the swamp!'","There is a terrible rancour about this particular pool","One of the horses travelling with the Malledhrim has fallen ill, and the Elves begin to lose hope that he can be healed. His illness began as they passed through the Drownholt and has grown steadily more grave over time.","Nestawen rode upon Alagos on her route to Estolad Mernael.\
\
You should explore possible routes Nestawen may have travelled and look for anything out of the ordinary that could have induced the steed's strange illness.","Explore the Drownholt for the source of illness","La Misteriosa Aflicción"},
[12704]={"Rook is at his hut in Pren Gwydh.\
\
You should bring the eggs you collected to Rook in Pren Gwydh.","Craban roosting spots can be found in the lands of Pren Gwydh not far from Rook's Hut.\
\
You should search for crow-eggs so that Rook may train another flock of crebain from chicks.","The Mysteriously Dwindling Flock","'Ha! Perfect, ${PLAYER}, and excellent timing, for I was beginning to grow impatient.\
\
'I am now a great Wizard, you see, and it is all thanks to you!'","Collect eggs from crow-nests (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'It is very strange... my flock has significantly dwindled of late. I wonder where they all went off to? Very peculiar.\
\
'I was ready to become a great Wizard, but it seems that I have one more task -- I should look to replenishing my flock. I need eggs from craban-nests, and the sooner the better, but the wild crebain that guard them can be a bit... hostile.\
\
'You should go collect wild craban-eggs for me, ${PLAYER}. Make haste!'","Bring the eggs to Rook","'You can find craban-nests around this area, if you know where to look. The birds are wild, though! These crebain of Dunland are fierce.'","Now that you have used most of his trained flock feathers, Rook wishes to retrain a new flock, and looks for a collection of eggs to hatch.","Collected eggs from crow-nests (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12705]={"Gwyllion's Gate, the entrance to the path which leads to Gwyllion's hut, lies to the south of Gavar Cadlus.\
\
Grufudh told you to speak with Gwyllion, the Old Woman of the Mountain, if you wished to know the source of the White Hand banner.","Talk to Grufudh at Gavar Cadlus","'I have never seen such a banner, nor spoken with anyone who bore such a sign. If you found the banner near to Gwyllion's Gate, then there is one person and one person alone who may be able to help you.\
\
'You must speak with Gwyllion, the Old Woman of the Mountain. Her hut sits upon the side of the mountain beyond Gwyllion's Gate. All you have to do is follow the path.\
\
'Be wary though...the Old Woman of the Mountain is a Gurach, a witch from a lûth in the south. If you do not come in respect, she may take it ill.'","'You were waylaid by an Uruk-hai at the home of this Gwyllion, and he seemed to be guarding the old woman's hut? I fear this Gurach, as the Uch-lûth call her, is a sorceress in league with Saruman.'","Talk to Saeradan at Echad Saeradan","Saeradan is at Echad Saeradan, west of Gwyllion's Gate.\
\
You should return to Saeradan with news of your discovery of the Uruk-hai Filskûm at Gwyllion's hut.","'${PLAYER}, the banner you found is itself enough evidence that Saruman the White stirs trouble in this land, but the evils which you have encountered speak to a much more sinister plan.\
\
'You should go to Grufudh and learn if he has encountered any emissaries of the White Hand, and if so, what the emissary desired of his people.\
\
'Grufudh and his goatherds are at Gavar Cadlus to the east.'","The Mystery Deepens","Grufudh is at Gavar Cadlus, north-east of Echad Saeradan.\
\
Saeradan instructed you to speak with Grufudh about the banner of the White Hand that you found near Gwyllion's Gate.","Gwyllion's Hut","Talk to Gwyllion at her hut","Using the items and information you brought to him, Saeradan believes that it is a certainty that Saruman the White has a hand in the strange happenings in the Windfells."},
[12706]={"The townspeople of Halach have been receiving help from someone, but no one knows who.","'Please, put down your weapons, ${CLASS}. I mean you no harm, and I am alone. My fellow soldiers fled long ago.\
\
'You have come looking for me at the behest of the townspeople, yes? Rather, you have come looking for the one gifting them supplies. It is not much, compared to what my comrades and I raided from them during the war. But this is... repentance, I suppose.\
\
'I will return home eventually, but not before I see some of the harm undone.'","Irodon has asked you to investigate a boar wallow to the north-east of Halach.","Investigate the boar-wallow near Halach","Talk to Asórkho near the boar wallow","'${PLAYER}, welcome! As you can see, we've been hard at work rebuilding our home. My heart should feel light, but ever since the war's end, I have been troubled by a string of mysteries.\
\
'For the past few months, every now and then, someone has been leaving sacks of supplies at our doorsteps. Preserved boar meat, cut firewood, all harvested from the wild. The strange thing is, we don't know who is responsible. Of course, we were suspicious at first, but nothing about the supplies thus far has seemed amiss. I hope that the culprit is not a malicious person, but we cannot be too careful.\
\
'Now, I suspect the meat we have been receiving has been hunted from a nearby boar wallow, to the north-east. Perhaps our culprit is there right now. But very few people here would be able to defend themselves out there, and they are all busy protecting Halach.\
\
'Would you investigate the wallow for us?'","A Haradrim man calmly holds up his empty hands","You have found a Haradrim man near the boar wallow.\
\
You should talk to him.","The Mystery Supplier"},
[12707]={"'My sister is safe for the time being, ${PLAYER}, and the information she brought us was of great importance.\
\
'Something far more dangerous than Orcs lurks in the ruins upon the far side of that bridge -- a servant of the Nine, if Ianudirel has marked her guess correctly!\
\
'We need to deal with this quickly! My sister saw many fell spirits gathering to the call of this servant, and their power could prove a greater threat to us if it is allowed to build.'","'Greetings, my good ${RACE}. You are a welcome sight indeed in this dark place. I have been awaiting my chance to cross the bridge for nearly a day, but there are too many eyes searching for me -- and not all of them belong to Orcs....\
\
'Something terrible lurks on this side of the river, and I need to inform my brother of it!\
\
'What say we take our chances now? With the two of us, I think we will have a good chance of fighting our way across, even if we are discovered.'","Iavassúl is at Iavassúl's Watch in Taur Morvith.\
\
You should report to Iavassúl regarding his sister's rescue.","'Find my sister, ${PLAYER}. I have not heard from her since she went out to scout the land.'","'It seems I may have been overhasty in sending my scouts out across the bridge. One of them who goes by the name Ianudirel has not yet reported back, and I grow worried.\
\
'See if you can find her upon the far embankment. If she is not too sorely wounded or dead, then she should be trying to win her way across...but her path may be barred.\
\
'Also, while I know it is improper to say it under these circumstances...she is my sister, and I would be personally grateful if you are able to ensure her safe return.'","Ianudirel may be found on the far side of the river from Krul Lugu.\
\
Iavassúl has asked you to find Ianudirel, his sister, and help her to return safely, if she still lives.","Talk to Iavassúl at Iavassúl's Watch","Talk to Ianudirel to assist in her escape","The Narrow Way","The Elven scout Ianudirel was sent ahead to explore the far side of the river from Krul Lugu, but she has not yet returned."},
[12709]={"Talk to Gísling at the Mead Hall of Garsfeld","Collect food-stores around Garsfeld (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Greetings again, ${PLAYER}. I have faith in my father's plan, but in order not to place too heavy a burden upon Snowbourn, many of our rations must travel with the crofters. \
\
'Our rations are stored about the town, but I need you to gather them for me, so that Albryt, Odnoth, and I can begin stowing them for the journey.\
\
'Return to me when you have gathered the rations.'","Food-stores can be found scattered about Garsfeld and inside the homes of the town.\
\
Gísling wants you to gather food-stores in preparation to evacuate Garsfeld. He has asked that you try to avoid the attention of the crofters so as not to incite panic.","Gísling awaits your return in the Mead Hall of Garsfeld.\
\
You should bring the rations you collected to Gísling.","The Need to Survive","'We shall stow these rations away for the journey. Thank you for your aid, ${PLAYER}.'","Gísling requests your aid in making ready to evacuate the crofters from Garsfeld.","Collected food-stores around Garsfeld (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12710]={"The Nelegroth Broodmother","Collected spider remains (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Offering Stone can be found in one of the caverns of Torech Ungol, beneath Nelegroth.\
\
You should place the spider remains on the Offering Stone and then defeat the Nelegroth Brood-mother.","Defeat the Nelegroth Brood-mother","A note hangs from the board, signed by Legolas:\
\
'I have located a particularly elusive foe, the Brood-mother of Nelegroth. She does not reveal herself easily, but I have seen the local Orcs leaving their dead at an offering stone for her. It is then that she leaves her lair to feed. I suspect if you slay some of the Ungol spiders nearby and leave them on that stone, she will appear. Then, you can strike her down and rid Lhingris of another powerful enemy.'","Legolas has devised a plan for defeating the Nelegroth Broodmother and requests an adventurer's aid.","Ungol Weavers can be found in one of the caverns of Torech Ungol, beneath Nelegroth.\
\
You should defeat Ungol Weavers and collect their remains.","The Nelegroth Brood-mother descends from the shadows!","Place the remains on the Offering Stone","Collect spider remains (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated the Nelegroth Brood-mother"},
[12712]={"Defeated foes in Arandor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat enemies in Emyn Duir.","'Are you the one sent to train me? I look forward to learning all that you know! I was but a child when the war began, but now I am a man grown. Is it true that an Easterling horde is on its way?\
\
'Oh, I almost forgot, I have a note for you. I have been waiting here so... I may have already read it. I hope you do not mind! It says that many great warriors have joined the battle and we should assist them. I am ready to leave, whenever you are ready!'","Assist Huneric at Adambel with: Heraldry of The Thíuda","Take the new recruit with you as you assist those in Díngarth.","Defeat foes in Emyn Duir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Take the new recruit with you as you assist those in Echad-in-Edhil.","Use the whistle to summon the new recruit if you become separated","Defeated foes in Emyn Duir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Assist Huneric at Adambel with: Turning Defectors","A new recruit has come to Díngarth.\
\
You should speak with the recruit.","Assist Radigond at Díngarth","Defeat foes in Parth Daenath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You have been entrusted to train and mentor a new soldier.","The New Recruit","Defeat foes in Arandor (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Speak to the new recruit.","'Thank you, my friend. I have learned much in the time that we have spent together. I am now to report to Hildvar to continue my combat training. I am sure that we will soon fight side-by-side, and let our foes beware!'","Assist Hildvar at Díngarth","Assist Durin IV at Echad-in-Edhil with: Sauron's Presence Upon Parth Daenath","Assist Gelvira at Díngarth","After so many years besieging Mordor, the Great Alliance is still in need of new recruits. Upon entering Díngarth you receive a missive: you have been entrusted with a new soldier in hopes that you can mentor and train the young man. You should seek him out as soon as you are able.","Speak to the new recruit","Defeated foes in Parth Daenath (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Assist Durin IV at Echad-in-Edhil with: Heraldry of Durin IV","Take the new recruit with you as you assist those in Adambel."},
[12716]={"From this watch-post you can make out the old gardens of Vâr Nuchur","Maergrind, the Noble Gate of Máttugard, can be found in Gundabad.\
\
You should familiarize yourself with the foothold at Maergrind.","The Noble Gate","Greeted Quartermaster","From the watch-post you can just make out the Shalakibal, the old Water-square","The middle of Máttugard recedes into darkness, the pit of Ablak-zibdîn","The path from Maergrind to the Gates of Gundabad are well guarded","'I see you have explored Maergrind and peered toward the future of what awaits us! Now, onward! The expedition awaits!'","'Welcome, ${PLAYER}, to Maergrind, the Noble Gate of Máttugard. From this encampment we will bravely work to retake Gundabad!\
\
'Have a look around the Noble Gate, for it will give you a good view of much of Máttugard from here. If you are to lead any expeditions further into Gundabad, you will first need to get your bearings!'","Explore Maergrind (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Prince Ingór has established a foothold at Maergrind in Máttugard.","Prince Ingór can be found at Maergrind in Máttugard.\
\
You should talk to Prince Ingór.","Talk to Prince Ingór at Maergrind"},
[12717]={"Speak with Grimgar, grandson of Reeve Gárwig","'The battle looms near, and we are as prepared as we will ever be! We have Thrymm on our side, my brave daughter, and the brave kindred of our Reeve, Gárwig.\
\
'Will you speak with Gársig, the son of the Reeve, and make sure he has everything he needs? The Reeve's grandsons are here also, and ready to fight -- Humbald and Grimgar. Please help them however you can.'","'Another strong soldier to brave the Orcs' assault? Excellent!\
\
'As grandson of the Reeve, my duty is similar to that of a wandering hero such as yourself -- to assist where I am needed!\
\
'I relish a good fight. Let the Orcs come!'","Grimgar feels that Scylfig is well-prepared for the White Hand Orc assault","Speak with Cyneberg","The Noble Guard","'Yes, I believe we are quite ready to fight whatever dares to come our way.\
\
'I cannot wait to test my skill in battle alongside such great warriors of our realm!'","A number of nobles from the Reeve's family have taken up arms for the coming attack on Scylfig.","Cyneberg can be found sharpening her sword in Scylfig.\
\
You should speak with Cyneberg.","'Ah, welcome to the battle-ground! I do not need any help, but thank you for asking.\
\
'With the greatest strength of Wildermore's people gathered here, it would take a great army of Orcs to conquer Scylfig.'","'I am Gársig, son of Gárwig. Thrymm sent us warning not long ago of an unusual number of Orcs in the Writhendowns, and we have come to lend our arms to the defence of Scylfig.\
\
'The Reeve's kin are responsible for the protection of these lands. We suffer no enemy to pass our borders!\
\
'Thrymm is like a brother to me. I look forward to drawing swords with him once more.'","Gársig valiantly upholds his duty as a noble protector of Wildermore","The kin of the Reeve of Wildermore can be found in Scylfig.\
\
You should see if the Reeve's son or grandsons need any assistance.","Speak with Humbald, grandson of Reeve Gárwig","Humbald is excited to assist in the defence of Scylfig","Speak with Gársig, son of Reeve Gárwig"},
[12718]={"Le has enseñado una lección a Harry Madreselva... ¿pero le servirá de algo?","El camino a Nobotella","'La Guardia de Allende no tiene suficientes suministros para lidiar con la presencia de tantos Fronteros de Lotho. ¿Y si llevas algunos suministros a Nobotella? Hagas lo que hagas, ¡que no te pillen los Fronteros de Lotho!\
\
Te encontraré allí más tarde, una vez haya completado unos cuantos más de mis preparativos. Mi plan todavía está tomando forma, pero cuando esté listo será algo fuera de serie... ¡créeme!'","Enfréntate a Harry Madreselva","<rgb=#FF0000>Evita a los Fronteros de Lotho</rgb>","'¿Harry Madreselva? ¿Cuántos de estos Hombres han venido a la Comarca Allende? Quizá sí que están aliados con Lotho después de todos. ¿Cómo puede un hobbit, incluso uno como Lotho, rebajarse tanto? Aun así, parece que es lo que ha hecho, y ahora nos toca a nosotros pararle a él y a sus compinches.\
\
¡He preparado algo que hará justo eso!'","Fredegar Bolger se encuentra en el pueblo de Nobotella.\
\
Debes hablar con Freder Bolger en Nobotella.","Los suministros de la Guardia de Allende se encuentran en agujero-almacén secreto en el bosque entre Gamwich y Quiebra Larga.\
\
Debes llevar los suministros para la Guardia de Allende a Salga Pastoverde en Nobotella.","Salga Pastoverde se encuentra en Nobotella.\
\
Debes hablar con Salga Pastoverde en Nobotella.","Harry Madreselva se encuentra cerca de Nobotella en la Comarca Allende.\
\
Debes enfrentarte a Harry Madreselva.","¡Has sido ${PLAYERNAME:detectado[m]|detectada[f]} por uno de los Fronteros de Lotho!","'Más te vale moverte, desconocido. ¡Crúzate en mi camino y te arrepentirás!'","Habla con Salga Pastoverde en Nobotella","Habla con Fredegar en Nobotella","La Guardia de Allende necesitará suministros si quiere parar los descabellados planes de Lotho.","Recupera los suministros de la Guardia de Allende del agujero-almacén secreto","'Gracias por estos suministros. Confieso que sospechaba del Sr. Bolger cuando llegó, pero ha probado ser un buen amigo de la Guardia de Allende.\
\
'Ya que te tengo por aquí, ¿te importaría ayudarme con algo urgente? Un hombre llamado Harry Madreselva merodea por aquí cerca. Esperaba que te enfrentaras a él y lo mandases a paseo.'"},
[12719]={"'Sonidos extraños y sombras inquietantes nos rodean... ¿no te sientes ${PLAYERNAME:incómodo[m]|incómoda[f]}? Creo que proviene del norte. Hay una luz enfermiza en ese lugar.\
\
'He notado un gran aumento de gredbyg por aquí. Quizá su colmena esté allí arriba... ¿podrías ir a reducir su número? ¡Dormiré más tranquilo sabiendo que hay menos de ellos arrastrándose sobre mí mientras duermo!'","'¡Brrr! ¡Esos gredbyg me ponen los pelos de punta!'","El ruido de los gredbyg","Es probable que se encuentre una colonia de gredbyg en una colmena del Palacio de Náin, al norte de Lamab-dûm en la Gran Excavación.\
\
Thórhall quiere que elimines a tantos gredbyg como puedas.","'¡Ah! Un gran esfuerzo, ${PLAYER}. ¡Ojalá este fuera el final de ellos! Pero supongo que tendré que conformarme con esta valiente hazaña por tu parte. ¡Tienes mi agradecimiento!'","Has derrotado a un grodbog (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Regresa con Thórhall en Lamab-dûm","Thórhall está inquieto por los extraños sonidos que se oyen por todo Lamab-dûm y teme que procedan de los gredbyg que reptan por la zona.","Derrota gredbyg en el Palacio de Náin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Thórhall se encuentra en su campamento en Lamab-dûm, en la Gran Excavación.\
\
Deberías regresar con Thórhall e informarle de que la presencia de grodbog en la colmena del norte se ha reducido en cierta medida."},
[12725]={"Myrkworth se encuentra en Imlad Balchorth, en lo alto de una colina al norte de Gabilshathûr.\
\
Hwati te ha pedido que viajes a Myrkworth y hables con su primo, Eiláf.","Hwati en Gabilshathûr cree que su primo al norte, en Myrkworth, podría necesitar tu ayuda.","'Nos has sido de gran ayuda aquí, ${PLAYER}, pero mi primo Eiláf enfrenta un conjunto de problemas muy diferente al norte y también podría necesitar tu ayuda. Él está ayudando a supervisar un pequeño puesto avanzado que hemos construido allí. Se llama Myrkworth y se encuentra en Imlad Balchorth.\
\
'Si deseas seguir ayudándonos, viaja a Myrkworth y busca a mi primo Eiláf. Myrkworth está al norte de aquí, en lo alto de una colina en esas tierras traicioneras.\
\
'¡Ah, y si llegas a Myrkworth, dale mis saludos a Eiláf!'","'¿Ah, Hwati te envió, verdad? ¡Es un buen y sólido enano! No lo he visto en demasiados días. Pero habrá tiempo para hablar cuando el trabajo esté hecho...\
\
'Mientras que los orcos y trolls son una amenaza inmediata para Gabilshathûr, los Muertos de Angmar son una más sutil y peligrosa. Los enanos hemos venido aquí para intentar encontrar una forma de contrarrestar esta amenaza.\
\
'Habla con Gautar, Birgir u Oflár y mira si tienen algo para que hagas. Quizá, con el tiempo, yo también tenga una tarea para ti.'","'Mi primo Eiláf se encuentra en Myrkworth, que está en lo alto de una colina al norte, en Imlad Balchorth. ¡Cuidado con esas tierras, pues los Muertos de Angmar caminan por allí!'","El primo del norte"},
[12726]={"Melril can be found along the path leading through Tarlang's Crown, to the south-west of Sardol in Blackroot Vale.\
\
Harnion has asked you to seek Melril in northern Tarlang's Crown and aid the people of Blackroot Vale.","'${PLAYER}, something troubles me....\
\
'I worry that our efforts here might push more of the Corsairs into the vale in the north. We cannot allow them to move freely into Blackroot Vale... there are still many who dwell there and they are ill-prepared for combat.\
\
'I know of a hunter in Sardol named Melril. She is a hale hunter, and would be the first to stand against our foes in Tarlang's Crown. Seek her out, and aid in reinforcing our defences to the north!'","'Ah, ${PLAYER}! It is an honour to meet you.\
\
'I have heard much of your efforts in Blackroot Vale, and I am glad you have returned once more to aid us. Our situation grows more dire by the moment, so if you seek to help us, we could rest easier knowing the Enemy is being kept at bay.'","Talk to Melril in northern Tarlang's Crown","Harnion of Dol Amroth grows concerned that the forces in Tarlang's Crown will assault Blackroot Vale before moving on to the rest of Gondor.","The Northern Front","DNT"},
[12727]={"En los dias de la guerra contra Angmar hace mil años, un grupo de hombres del Rey Arvedui renegó al ser llamados a las armas. Arvedui maldijo a estos hombres, diciendo que no conocerían descanso hasta que cumplieran su deber. Hasta hoy, han caminado por los Campos de Fornost, atormentados por sus errores.\
\
'Ha llegado la hora para que estas sombras sean libres al fin. Reúne a tus aliados y busca al capitán Perjuro. Podrás encontrarle bajo los mismos muros de Fornost, al noreste de aquí en algunas viejas y desmoronadas ruinas de Arthedain.\
\
'Aunque ten cuidado: el suyo fue un destino aciago, y podría no ser amistoso con aquellos que le recuerden sus juramentos traicionados.'","Has derrotado al capitán Perjuro","La sombra del capitán Perjuro se encuentra al noreste del campamento de Mincham, en unas ruinas dispersas junto a los muros de Fornost.\
\
Mincham te ha pedido que encuentras a la sombra del capitán Perjuro y que lo instes, junto a sus seguidores, a cumplir su antiguo deber.","En los días del Rey Arvedui, el último rey de Fornost, una compañía de hombres del rey traicionó sus juramentos a Arthedain, permitiendo que Fornost cayera a los ejércitos de Angmar. Arvedui maldijo a estos hombres para que nunca descansaran hasta que hubieran cumplido sus juramentos.","Los Perjuros","Habla con Mincham","Habla con la sombra del capitán Perjuro","'Es nuestro deber ofrecer a las sombras de los Hombres libertad de su maldición y llamarlos para luchar contra Angmar... con más razón si son nuestros hermanos.'","Mincham te espera en su campamento.\
\
El capitán Perjuro te dijo que él y sus seguidores habían jurado lealtad a alguien llamado Amarthiel. Mincham podría saber qué significa esto.","'¿Qué? ¿Quién se atreve a interrumpir mi antigua vigilia?\
\
'¡Insensato! ¿Cómo te atreves a recordarme nuestros patéticos juramentos al cobarde Arvedui? ¡Ahora hemos hecho nuevos juramentos!\
\
'Seguimos a Amarthiel, y pronto barreremos a todos los insensatos vivos del Norte!'","'¡Ay! Lamento haberte enviado a esta tarea temeraria. Había esperado que la sombra tuviera una mente corrupta, ¡pero no tanto como para atacarte! Parece que los Perjuros ahora sirven al Enemigo en pensamiento y obra.\
\
'Amarthiel... me parece que he oído ese nombre antes. No debo hablar de tales cosas ahora, ¡pero en verdad son malas nuevas las que traes!'"},
[12728]={"Idmar is at his camp along the road in central Parth Celebrant.\
\
You should return to Idmar with news of your dealings with the maddened shades.","Upon noticing you, the Oathbreaker appears puzzled.\
\
'I am Thinnas, captain of the eastern front. What purpose do you have, coming here?'\
\
You question the Oathbreaker about his curse.\
\
'We did not think anyone would find out. But lord Cirion did... and he made certain we would never forget what we had done.\
\
'What need have you for this? Do you only seek to torment us more?'","As you acquire the Oathbreaker's attention, he glares in your direction.\
\
'Another? Why will you not leave us be?'\
\
Melethron's face contorts into a rage.","Melethron is at the northern Oathbreaker camp among his fallen men.\
\
Idmar asked you to speak with the shade of Melethron.","'Every attempt I have made to converse with these Oathbreakers has ended in violence. These men must have committed some sort of treacherous crime; elsewise, they would not have returned.\
\
'Most have nothing coherent to say, but I have heard the whispers of three names... Melethron, Thinnas, and Camlann. Perhaps they may have insight as to why their men have returned.\
\
'I have never been able to get close enough to speak to them, so you will probably have to fight your way to them. Be careful.'","'Speak with the Oathbreakers, ${PLAYER}, and learn what it is that they want....'","'You should return now to Idmar.'","Defeated Camlann","Confront and defeat Thinnas","The Oathbreakers of Parth Celebrant","As you approach Camlann, he looks visibly upset.\
\
'You have invaded our lands and slaughtered my men, and yet, you expect me to speak with you?\
\
'The frivolity of your charge is matched only by your foolishness. The fate that befell us is ours alone to face.'","Talk to Idmar","Thinnas is at the eastern camp of Oathbreakers near the Rushgore.\
\
Idmar has asked you to speak with the shade of Thinnas.","Defeated Melethron","Camlann is at the western camp of Oathbreakers near the border to Eorlsmead.\
\
Idmar asked you to speak with the shade of Camlann.","Confront and defeat Camlann","Medwine has attempted to converse with several of the Oathbreakers in the newly-risen force. However, he has only been met with violence.","Confront and defeat Melethron","Defeated Thinnas","'I take it your dealings with the Oathbreakers did not go well?\
\
'Yet, one mentioned Cirion? These men must have fought for Gondor at the Battle of the Field of Celebrant. Long ago, our forebear, Eorl, led Cirion to victory after arriving to save his forces from an onslaught of terrible Easterlings. It was a glorious moment in our past and paved the way for the formation of Rohan.\
\
'But how did these men come to be cursed? That battle was won, and Gondor was saved....\
\
'Here, take this, I think we may need to approach this differently now.'"},
[12729]={"Fonn está de vuelta en Tyrn Lhuig.\
\
Tras derrotar a Ulkrank, Bethad te pidió que le contaras a su amigo Fonn tus hazañas.","Sierpes derrotadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El explorador Bethad ha descubierto que la cueva de las sierpes es el hogar de un venerado anciano Gorthorog llamado Ulkrank.","'¡Tu derrota de Ulkrank fue una gran hazaña!'","'Mi herida ya está curada. No temas por mí. Volveré a Tyrn Lhuig por mi cuenta cuando sea el momento.'","Derrota sierpes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El Anciano","'¡Traes buenas noticias! Me alegra mucho saber que Bethad está a salvo, pues me había estado culpando por enviarlo solo a tal peligro.\
\
'Pero también has hecho una gran hazaña, amigo mío. Los Gertheryg son algunos de los luchadores más terribles de la Corona de Hierro, y si pueden ser desanimados aunque sea un poco por la muerte de su anciano, el Enemigo quedará muy debilitado. ¡Has logrado una gran victoria!'","'Descansaré un poco más y luego regresaré a Aughaire por mi cuenta. No temas por mi seguridad -- ¡debes ir a la cueva y derrotar a Ulkrank!'","'Me alegra que estés aquí. Fui herido por una de estas malditas sierpes y me he visto obligado a esconderme en los rincones oscuros de esta cueva durante algunos días. Pero ahora que mi herida está casi curada, he aprendido mucho espiando los movimientos de los Gertheryg.\
\
Esta cueva está habitada por un antiguo Gorthorog llamado Ulkrank. Es muy viejo... la criatura más vieja de este tipo que he visto. Los otros brutos parecen tratarlo con gran reverencia. Quizá sea su líder.\
\
Por mi parte, estoy listo para irme, pero si quieres, creo que puedes hacer más aquí. Mata tantas de estas viles sierpes como puedas y lucha hasta el fondo de la cueva donde habita Ulkrank. Cuando lo derrotes, dile a mi amigo Fonn en Tyrn Lhuig sobre tu victoria. Seguro que estará preocupado por mí.'","Ulkrank, el antiguo Gorthorog, se encuentra en algún lugar en las profundidades de la cueva.\
\
Bethad te ha pedido que explores la cueva hasta que puedas encontrar y derrotar a Ulkrank en persona.","'El antiguo Gorthorog no fue rival para ti.'"},
[12730]={"'Bien, has traído las costillas. Déjame prepararlas para ti....\
\
'Aquí tienes. ¡Dile al tío Adelard que las disfrute, pero que si come demasiadas tendrá que añadir uno o dos agujeros más a su cinturón!'","El favorito del Viejo Tuk","Adelard está esperando en los Grandes Smials, en Alforzaburgo.\
\
Después de que hayas recuperado las costillas que necesitaba Edilina Ganapié, ha preparado un plato de costillas de jabalí especiadas para que se las des a Adelard. Deberías llevárselas para que pueda intentar apaciguar al fantasma del Viejo Tuk.","'Ah, bien, has traído las costillas. ¡Y huelen delicioso! Edilina es una cocinera estupenda, ¿verdad?\
\
'Bueno, las llevaré a la biblioteca y espero que apacigüen al fantasma del Viejo Tuk. ¡Y así podré recuperar la paz!'","Costillas de jabalí recolectadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Oh, cielos! El fantasma sigue molestando mi biblioteca. De hecho, en cuanto puse un pie en la habitación, se armó un alboroto que me dio un gran susto. ¡Estoy tan alterado que no creo que pueda cenar esta noche!\
\
'¡Espera! ¡Comida! Como la mayoría de los hobbits, el Viejo Tuk tenía debilidad por la buena comida, especialmente por las costillas de jabalí especiadas. Debo admitir que a mí también me gustan mucho... Quizá si le preparamos un plato de costillas, logremos apaciguar a su fantasma.\
\
'Ve a ver a mi sobrina, Edilina Ganapié. Su madriguera está justo al este de los Grandes Smials y es una cocinera maravillosa. No le digas por qué necesitamos las costillas, no quiero causar pánico!'","Con el fantasma que aún molesta su biblioteca, Adelard ha ideado otra forma de apaciguar al Viejo Tuk: la comida. Se sabe que al Viejo Tuk le encantaban las costillas de jabalí especiadas, y Adelard cree que si le presenta un plato de estas costillas al fantasma en la biblioteca, este volverá a su descanso.","Se pueden encontrar jabalíes en las colinas al este de Alforzaburgo. La casa de Edilina Ganapié está justo al este de Alforzaburgo.\
\
Edilina Ganapié dijo que podía preparar las costillas de jabalí especiadas que quiere Adelard para apaciguar al fantasma del Viejo Tuk, pero que le faltaban las costillas. Te pidió que le trajeras algunas costillas de los jabalíes de las colinas más allá de Alforzaburgo.","Recoge costillas de jabalí (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡Oh, cielos! ¿Edilina necesita costillas antes de poder preparar el plato para el fantasma del Viejo Tuk?\
\
'Vaya... Bueno, hay muchos jabalíes en las colinas al este de Alforzaburgo. Deberías poder encontrar las costillas que necesitas entre todos esos jabalíes. ¡Pero date prisa! No sé cuánto tiempo más podré soportar a este fantasma en mi biblioteca.'","'Has traído las costillas para Adelard, ${PLAYERNAME:Frontero[m]|Frontera[f]} . Por favor, dáselas en los Grandes Smials, ¡con mis saludos!'","'¿Tienes las costillas? Debería haber muchos jabalíes en las colinas al este de Alforzaburgo. Solo necesito unas pocas costillas para preparar el plato del tío Adelard.'","Costillas de jabalí especiadas recolectadas","Lleva las costillas de jabalí especiadas a Adelard Tuk","Recoge costillas de jabalí especiadas","'Por favor, ve a ver a mi sobrina, Edilina Ganapié, aquí en Alforzaburgo. Es una cocinera maravillosa y debería poder prepararnos un plato de costillas de jabalí. Entonces podré dárselas al fantasma en mi biblioteca y apaciguar al Viejo Tuk.'","'¿Tienes las costillas de jabalí especiadas de mi sobrina Edilina? Era la comida favorita del Viejo Tuk, así que espero que el verlas en mi biblioteca apacigüe a su fantasma y me conceda algo de paz.'","Lleva las costillas de jabalí a Edilina Ganapié","El agujero de Edilina Ganapié está al este de los Grandes Smials.\
\
Adelard te ha enviado a ver a su sobrina, Edilina Ganapié, para que prepare un plato de costillas de jabalí especiadas para apaciguar al fantasma del Viejo Tuk, pero te ha advertido que no le digas la razón. No quiere causar pánico.","'¡Oh, cómo está el buen viejo tío Adelard! ¡Ya casi no lo veo!\
\
'¿Quiere unas costillas de jabalí especiadas, verdad? Bueno, tengo las especias, pero me faltan las costillas. Son bastante importantes para el plato, ¿no es así? ¡Ja, ja!\
\
'Pero no te preocupes, hay muchos jabalíes en las colinas al este de Alforzaburgo. Si me traes unas costillas, prepararé el plato que quiere el tío Adelard.'"},
[12733]={"Ingold has asked you to defeat the leaders of Fushaum Tûm.","Defeat Thorakó, the Hewer","Defeated Shatúrro, the Spear","Defeated Thorakó, the Hewer","A notice is pinned to the board, signed by Ingold:\
\
'We have detected a large presence of Olog-hai at Fushaum Tûm, and believe the leaders are planning an attack. A brave adventurer is needed to infiltrate the camp and defeat these powerful foes.'","'The encampment of Fushaum Tûm concerns me. There seems to be a large presence of Olog-hai there. I ask you to find those in command at Fushaum Tûm and defeat them.'","Ingold, a soldier of Gondor, has scouted Dor Amarth and is concerned with the growing numbers of foes gathering at the encampment of Fushaum Tûm.","The Olog-hai Lord","Defeat Shatúrro, the Spear"},
[12734]={"You see the silhouette of what appears to be an enormous boar","Find the trail of the rumoured boar","'I would normally not concern myself with rumours, but this one weighs heavily upon my mind. There is tell of a monstrous boar wandering the woods. I cannot help but think of the Boar of Everholt, which defeated Folca King all those years ago.\
\
'I do not have the time to chase rumours, but I would appreciate if you could look into this for me. Such a beast would be a dangerous thing. Let us hope that these are simply rumours....'","The boar was last rumoured to be in the wooded hills to the east of Aldburg.\
\
Arcil has asked that you follow the tales of a great boar, not unlike the Boar of Everholt, to see if it truly exists.","Talk to Arcil","The trail continues south into the woods.\
\
You should follow the trail of the great boar.","Arcil is in the Mead Hall of Aldburg, west of the woods.\
\
You should return to Arcil and let him know what you found in the woods.","Arcil is concerned about the rumours of a great boar wandering the woods, the likes of that which defeated King Folca long ago.","Search for evidence of the great boar","It was not an enormous boar, but this totem was made to appear as such","You saw the silhouette of what appears to be an enormous boar nearby and should approach with caution.","Found the trail of the rumoured boar","Continue to follow the trail of the great boar","The Once and Future King-slayer","The trail continues east into the woods.\
\
You should follow the trail of the great boar.","'I must admit that I am relieved it was not a great boar. I was raised learning the bravery of Folca King, and I confess that if the Boar of Everholt was able to best one of Rohan's greatest warriors, I feared for myself and others.\
\
'However, the fact that this totem was meant to frighten us is a little concerning. With the crude construction, it is possible some children made it as a jest. Let us hope that is the truth of it.'","Follow the trail of the great boar deeper into the woods","The trail of the rumoured boar leads up the hill, to the south."},
[12735]={"'Back so soon, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You explain that Aragorn wishes to find some way to put the shade of Arvedui to rest, and sent you to Elrond for his help.\
\
'We are in agreement. I knew King Arvedui in life. He deserves a better fate than to linger in the frozen wastes, tormented by his past. Relieving him of his burden will be no easy task, however.'\
\
Elrond furrows his brow, deep in thought.\
\
'Truthfully, I do not know how best to help him. In my experience, shades of Men often linger in the world because of something unfinished: an oath unfulfilled, an oath broken. Perhaps if you spend time with Arvedui, you will learn why he lingers, and find a way to relieve his burden. To that end, I have a request that might lead to salvation for the fallen king and also thwart the Enemy.'\
\
Elrond motions to the book on the table, and opens it to a page marked with a piece of tasseled cloth. You see that it contains a list of many dated entries, logging something. The seven-pointed star of Arnor illustrates one of the pages.\
\
'As you have seen, Angmar has committed many forces to Forochel, conscripting the local Gauredain into their ranks, sending more soldiers than necessary for the purpose we believed they possessed. They are searching for something, and I have finally found a clue as to what that might be. \
\
'This record recovered from Annúminas details significant troop movements from the years 500 to 600 of the Third Age. There, on that page, it states that a large contingent of soldiers and Prince Elendur himself moved an \\qitem of great importance\\q from Ost Forod into the North. It does not declare what this item is, or where precisely it came to rest. I have a suspicion as to what it might be, and if I am correct, it is surely what the Angmarim seek in the frozen wilds of Forochel.\
\
'First, I would ask you to seek the Ranger known as Lothrandir. I believe he is still among the Lossoth, and should you encounter the Angmarim in force, I fear you will have need of his sword-arm. Together, bring this information to Arvedui. As the King of Arthedain, he may know where this secret treasure was hidden by the Arnorians all those years ago.\
\
'If fate is kind, you will find the treasure before the Angmarim can seize it for their dark masters. If it is kinder still, you will also find a way to put Arvedui's spirit to rest. I wish you luck, ${PLAYER}.'","Lothrandir is with the shade of Arvedui at the shipwreck of the Thoroval.\
\
You should talk to Lothrandir.","Lothrandir is prepared to travel to the shipwreck of the Thoroval to meet Arvedui.\
\
Speak with Lothrandir at Sûri-kylä to enter 'Instance: Dúnedain Past and Present'.","'I would take a moment more of your time before you depart, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Though our mission to thwart the schemes of Amarthiel and Mordrambor must be our main focus, I sorrow that the shade of my ancestor lingers, burdened by great remorse. There must be something we can do to ease his spirit.\
\
'Please, speak with Lord Elrond on my behalf. If anyone among the living knows what can be done, it will be him.'","Talk to Lothrandir","Lothrandir can be found outside the village of Sûri-kylä in Forochel.\
\
You should find Lothrandir and explain Elrond's request.","Habla con Elrond","Complete 'Instance: Dúnedain Past and Present'","The One Who Lingers","'We will depart for the Thoroval when you are ready.'","Find Lothrandir in Forochel","Elrond can be found in his library in the Last Homely House.\
\
You should talk to Elrond.","'Hello, ${PLAYER}. What has brought you back to Forochel? Is everything well in Rivendell?'\
\
You explain Elrond's request to find the missing Arnorian treasure before the Angmarim, and to try to put Arvedui's shade to rest.\
\
'You bring tidings of high adventure, and it would be a great honour to assist you in finding a lost treasure of the Dúnedain, and to meet King Arvedui himself! We must not tarry here, then, if we are to find it before the Angmarim. Let us travel to the shipwreck of the Thoroval at once!'","Aragorn is concerned that his ancestor Arvedui lingers still in Middle-earth, haunting the wreck of the Thoroval.","'Lord Elrond's intuition was correct. King Arvedui was a valuable source of information, but the Angmarim are aware we seek Agoroth as well. How far do they lead us in this race?'"},
[12736]={"'Te saludo en tu momento de triunfo, ${PLAYER}. Los Orcos y los Angmarim han aprendido que su unión no será permitida. Por eso, te doy las gracias.'","Orcos Ongbúrz derrotados en Fasach-falroid (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Angmarim derrotados en Fasach-falroid (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Guirmán se encuentra en el Búth Luikh de Aughaire, al sur de Dún Covád.\
\
Has derrotado a muchos Orcos de los Ongbúrz y a sus aliados de la Corona de Hierro, y ahora deberías regresar a Guirmán para informarle de tus victorias.","'Orcos de la tribu de los Ongbúrz y sus aliados de la Corona de Hierro se encuentran en Fasach-falroid, al norte de Aughaire. Si eres capaz de enfrentarte a la ciudad de Dún Covád, en las colinas del oeste, encontrarás muchos de estos enemigos.'","Los Ongbúrz y la Corona de Hierro","Orcos de la tribu de los Ongbúrz y sus aliados de la Corona de Hierro se encuentran en la ciudad de Dún Covád y sus alrededores, al norte de Aughaire, en las colinas del oeste.\
\
Guirmán te ha pedido que combatas a los enemigos de los Trév Gállorg que se encuentran en Fasach-falroid.","Guirmán de los Trév Gállorg de Aughaire ha regresado de Fasach-falroid con noticias preocupantes de esa tierra.","'Salve, ${PLAYER}. Tus triunfos me llenan de alegría.'","'No se debe permitir que los Ongbúrz y los Angmarim prosperen en Fasach-falroid.'","Derrota a los Orcos de los Ongbúrz en Fasach-falroid (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a los Angmarim en Fasach-falroid (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Los Trév Gállorg hemos mantenido durante mucho tiempo nuestra vigilancia sobre las llanuras septentrionales de Fasach-falroid, pero somos demasiado pocos en estos tiempos difíciles para proteger toda la extensión.\
\
'Sin embargo, hemos visto lo suficiente para saber a qué nos enfrentamos: una unión de los Orcos de la tribu de los Ongbúrz y los Angmarim. Por separado, son peligrosos, pero juntos, luchando por un mismo amo, temo que puedan ser imparables.\
\
'Debes poner fin a su alianza, ${PLAYER}. Viaja al norte hacia Fasach-falroid y derrota a los Orcos del clan de los Ongbúrz y sus aliados de la Corona de Hierro. La ciudad de Dún Covád, al norte, en las colinas del oeste, seguramente tendrá muchos de estos enemigos para que los derrotes.'"},
[12738]={"'Escuché que el Maestro Gatson te envió tras esos orcos en los campos del sur. Ten cuidado... luchan como un lobo acorralado en un granero.'","'Últimamente ha habido orcos por aquí. Hasta ahora solo se han estado escondiendo y robando cosas, pero estoy seguro de que en cuanto se armen de valor, nos van a atacar. Supongo que soy demasiado terco para huir, y mis trabajadores, como Gilmar, son demasiado leales para dejarme, así que necesito que te deshagas de esos orcos por mí.\
\
Probablemente los encuentres merodeando por mis campos al sur. ¡Echa a esas criaturas viles de mis tierras!'","Gatson está en su granja, al norte de los campos.\
\
Has encontrado y derrotado a muchos orcos en los campos del sur de Gatson. Deberías regresar con Gatson y contarle tu éxito.","Orcos derrotados en los campos del sur de Gatson (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Esos orcos huelen la debilidad... Si logras ahuyentar a más, quizá lo piensen dos veces antes de molestarnos de nuevo.'","La amenaza orca","Se pueden encontrar orcos en los campos del sur de Gatson.\
\
El granjero Gatson acepta que los Montaraces no pueden ayudarle, pero aún le preocupa la seguridad de sus trabajadores. Espera que, al encargarte de los exploradores orcos que han estado robando en sus campos, puedas disuadir un ataque violento a su granja.","Exploradores orcos han estado merodeando por la granja de Gatson, robando comida, y Gatson está seguro de que es solo cuestión de tiempo antes de que ataquen su granja con fuerza.","'Has hecho bien, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Tenemos más problemas, pero al menos les diste una lección a esos orcos.'","Derrota orcos en los campos del sur de Gatson (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12739]={"'¡Nos salvaste! Estamos en deuda contigo.'","'¡Revisa tu arma, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}! Temo que los Orcos puedan estar sobre nosotros en unos momentos. Solo podemos esperar que no estén al tanto de nuestra fuerza aquí, y que sean solo un pequeño grupo de incursión.'","'Parece que derrotar a esos Orcos al norte no fue suficiente. Un explorador envió un mensaje diciendo que una banda de Orcos Blogmal y Krahjarn se está acercando a Gabilshathûr. ¡Deben haberse enfurecido por tu ataque!\
\
'Por favor, únete a los demás guardias y ayuda a defender Gabilshathûr. ¡Apresúrate! Hay poco tiempo para prepararse.'","El capitán de la guardia Gisur está en Gabilshathûr.\
\
Ayudaste a rechazar el ataque orco y deberías hablar con Gisur, ahora que el peligro ha pasado.","'¡Por la barba de Durin! ¿Viste eso? Ese grupo de incursión era mucho más pequeño que cualquiera que nos haya atacado antes. Tus esfuerzos no fueron en vano. Y quizás —después del revés que sufrieron hoy— lo piensen dos veces antes de volver aquí. Con suerte, su orgullo les impedirá contarle a sus amos que unos pocos enanos los derrotaron tan rotundamente.\
\
'Parece que, por ahora, estamos a salvo. Te damos las gracias, ${PLAYER}, y lo poco que puedo ofrecerte como recompensa, te lo daré.'","Habla con el capitán de la guardia Gisur cuando estés ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}.","La incursión Orca","Los Orcos se están movilizando contra Gabilshathûr.\
\
El capitán de la guardia Gisur te ha pedido que ayudes a defender Gabilshathûr de un ataque orco.","¡Gabilshathûr ha sido salvado!","Gabilshathûr está en peligro. Un grupo de incursión orco se dirige hacia el refugio enano y podría arrasarlo."},
[12740]={"You should let Horndir know that you have defeated many of the Orcs who were gathering and trying to regroup north-west of the Harlond.\
\
Horndir is in the Harlond.","The Orcs Above","Return to Horndir","'Greetings. I am Horndir, captain of the guard here in the Harlond. I hear you are looking to lend aid and were of great help during the war. Stragglers driven from the Battle of the Pelennor Fields have scattered throughout Lossarnach. Though their numbers have been decimated, they still stand to pose a threat and must be eliminated.\
\
'North-west of the Harlond, my scouts have reported a group of Orcs. They must be dealt with, lest they grow in number and become a danger once more.'","Stragglers driven from the Battle of the Pelennor Fields have scattered throughout Lossarnach. Though their numbers have been decimated, they still stand to pose a threat and must be eliminated.","'Thank you for the help. We are all looking forward to more peaceful days.'","Defeated Orcs at Taustrok (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Orcs at Taustrok (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Horndir has asked you to deal with the Orc presence at Taustrok before it grows in strength enough to threaten the Harlond.\
\
The Orcs have gathered at a small camp, north-west of the Harlond."},
[12742]={"'I evaded a number of Orcs on the journey here, but it seems some of them have followed me here. If you are as established an adventurer as you seem, perhaps you could do something about these creatures? They seem to be all over these Marshes by now, and they endanger my errand.'\
\
Artamir seems to mean no harm, but his presence here could threaten many fortunes. Did Frodo come this way? If he did, you should seek for sign of him while you hasten Artamir on his way.","'I was sent here by Denethor, the Ruling Steward of Gondor, on an errand of some importance, but it was entrusted to me in confidence and I should not speak of it now. I can tell you that it was a great honour to be selected for this errand, and that Denethor chose me personally, even before Faramir his son! I am certain that a successful end to this endeavour will elevate my stature in the Steward's esteem.\
\
'I evaded a number of Orcs on the journey here, but it seems some of them have followed me here. If you are as established an adventurer as you seem, perhaps you could do something about these creatures? They seem to be all over these Marshes by now, and they endanger my errand.'\
\
Artamir seems to mean no harm, but his presence here could threaten many fortunes. Did Frodo come this way? If he did, you should seek for sign of him while you hasten Artamir on his way.","Artamir has asked you to defeat Orcs throughout the Dead Marshes, for the creatures seem to have followed him here and are making completion of his errand more difficult. Furthermore, if Frodo did come this way, the Orcs drawn here by Artamir's presence could complicate matters.","Defeat Orcs in the Dead Marshes (7/8)","You rescue a crumpled parchment from the Orc before the swamp claims it","You found a parchment in the clutches of an Orc in the Dead Marshes, and should bring it to Artamir at his camp.","Defeated Orcs in the Dead Marshes (${NUMBER}/8)","'You did not find anything? Not a single thing?'","The Orcs Have Orders","You have faced many Orcs in the Dead Marshes, but there are more out there and you should defeat them for Artamir.","Bring the crumpled parchment to Artamir at his camp in the Dead Marshes","Defeat Orcs in the Dead Marshes (${NUMBER}/8)","'You found something? Let me see what you found!'\
\
Artamir takes the crumpled parchment from you and unfolds it, but in mere moments he shakes his head.\
\
'This is written in the speech of the Orcs, and no reputable Man of Gondor ever studied such words. My father never trusted the written word to begin with; Ilcamir was a man of action and of deeds, and I am no different than my sire!\
\
'But I can tell you this much, even without knowing the words themselves: this parchment contains orders for the Orcs. They have been sent to this dreary land, much as I have been. But for what purpose?'\
\
Artamir's brow is creased in thought as he considers what goal the Orcs might have within the Dead Marshes, but your worry is deeper than his. Did Frodo come this way? And does the Master of the Orcs know it?","Artamir son of Ilcamir has come to the Dead Marshes, and the sooner he leaves them the better!"},
[12744]={"Zagdúr clears her throat, causing Shúkurz to smile sheepishly","Find the Orcs of Jeb Khâtel","'You aren't the first outsider who's found their way here. But you'd better make sure you don't become the last, you hear? Try anything funny, and we'll gift you an arrow to the throat.\
\
'If you've got important Mâr Naphra business, head up the hill and talk to our elder, Zagdúr. She'll sort you out.'","You feel the weight of many eyes scrutinizing your every move...","A man named Phocas seems intent on tracking down Orcs in Jeb Khâtel.","'Hail, stranger. You're not from around these parts, are you?\
\
'Have you, by chance, ventured north to Jeb Khâtel and encountered Orcs? I've heard nothing beyond mere whispers, but it is my duty to find them. Alas, everyone here is rather... tight-lipped on the matter.\
\
'If you manage to locate these Orcs, I'll happily pay you for the information.'","Talk to Zagdúr","You have found Kafagur's elder, as well as a familiar Orc by her side -- Shúkurz.\
\
You should talk to him.","Zagdúr has politely interrupted your reunion with Shúkurz.\
\
You should talk to her in Kafagur.","Your presence in Kafagur has not gone unnoticed, but many of the Orcs seem unwilling to talk to you.\
\
You should find someone who is willing.","Find someone in Kafagur who is willing to talk to you","'Well, stranger, if you are friends with Shúkurz, then I can push aside some of my wariness for now. What brings you to Kafagur?'\
\
You tell her of the Man in Mâr Naphra who sent you to look for the Orcs.\
\
'Judging by his words, he is an outlander like you -- far from home, and far from his friends. The few in Mâr Naphra who trade with us would never tell him of Kafagur.\
\
'I shall inform our guards to watch out for this man, in case he harbours ill intentions. As for your intentions, however...'","You've found an Orc in Kafagur named Grúshul who wishes to speak with you.\
\
You should talk to her.","The Orcs of Jeb Khâtel","Talk to Shúkurz","'${PLAYER}?! You're the last person I expected to see here!\
\
'Don't worry -- Zogmauk, Lumbag, Muzmák, and Shulgolb made it out of Gundabad safely with me. We only just recently arrived ourselves! Some of the folks here weren't too keen on us staying, but we got that all smoothed out. And -- '","Grúshul has given you permission to meet with the elder, Zagdúr.\
\
You should find her in Kafagur.","The large Orc beckons you over with a grimace","Find Zagdúr in Kafagur","Talk to Grúshul","With a start, you recognize the Orc next to the elder","Phocas has asked you to head north to Jeb Khâtel and find the Orcs that dwell there."},
[12745]={"Los orcos se encuentran en Nan Wathren, al sur de las Quebradas del Norte.\
\
Debes derrotar a un buen número de orcos en Nan Wathren.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Se recomienda una Pequeña Comunidad.</rgb>","Desolladores Tarkrîp derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los orcos de Nan Wathren","Derrota a Tiradores Tarkrîp en el oeste de Nan Wathren (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Has derrotado a un buen número de orcos en el oeste de Nan Wathren.","Has derrotado a un buen número de orcos de Nan Wathren.","Tiradores Tarkrîp derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Completado","Al dirigirte al extremo de la garganta de Nan Wathren, ves que ha caído completamente en las manos de los orcos Tarkrîp.\
\
Un sendero traicionero y difícil continúa más allá del puente.\
\
Debes derrotar a los orcos de Nan Wathren, pero lleva compañeros contigo si vas más allá de este punto, ya que el peligro es mortal a partir de aquí.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Se recomienda una Pequeña Comunidad.</rgb>","Los orcos se han apoderado de los cañones de Nan Wathren, y deben ser expulsados.","Derrota a Desolladores tarkrîp en el oeste de Nan Wathren (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12746]={"Luchadores Tarkrîp derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota Luchadores Tarkrîp en Nan Wathren occidental (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los orcos de Nan Wathren","Has derrotado a un buen número de orcos de Nan Wathren.","Los orcos de Nan Wathren se vuelven más fuertes y crueles a medida que avanzas por el paso.\
\
Debes derrotar a los Degolladores y Luchadores Tarkrîp que encuentres en tu camino a través del extremo oriental de Nan Wathren.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Se recomienda una Comunidad.</rgb>","Has derrotado a un buen número de los orcos más fuertes de Nan Wathren oriental. Estos enemigos eran duros y numerosos, y tu valiente empeño por rechazarlos te ha granjeado gran renombre entre los Pueblos Libres de la Tierra Media.","Completado","Los Degolladores y Luchadores Tarkrîp se encuentran en Nan Wathren oriental, en el sur de las Quebradas del Norte.\
\
Debes derrotar a un buen número de Degolladores y Luchadores Tarkrîp en Nan Wathren.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Se recomienda una Comunidad.</rgb>","Los orcos de Nan Wathren se vuelven más fuertes y crueles a medida que avanzas por el paso.","Degolladores Tarkrîp derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota Degolladores Tarkrîp en Nan Wathren occidental (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12747]={"Destroyed Orkish totem (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'With luck we managed to be in Ethring before the Orc raiding party arrived. Will luck always be on our side though? We must continue to do our part and secure the Vale.\
\
'${PLAYER}, let us cross the river Ringló in Ethring and head east towards the Orc camp mentioned by the unfortunate woodcutter. If we perchance upon any Orkish structures, let us destroy them. They shall not defile our Vale any longer!'","Burn Orkish banners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Arvaethor has asked you to accompany him to the White Mountain Orc camp and destroy any signs of Orc encroachment upon the Vale.","Burnt Orkish banner (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You should speak with Arvaethor.","Orc structures can be found north-east of Ethring.\
\
Destroy Orkish structures in Ringló Vale.","The Orkish Path","'There was not an Orc presence in this part of the Vale when I patrolled here last. I know not the numbers and strength of the foes we will encounter in this Orc encampment.'","Speak with Arvaethor","Destroy Orkish totems (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12749]={"Larus Fragmentoagudo descubrió que había un segundo cofre, que aún permanece perdido.","Larus Fragmentoagudo cree que el segundo cofre está dentro de un edificio en la colina a tu izquierda al acercarte a la fortaleza controlada por los Duramano en el paso de Gabilazan desde el norte. Gabilazan está al sur del campamento donde se encuentra Larus.\
\
Larus Fragmentoagudo está muy preocupado de que Heikki Vigilaoro registre cosas poco favorables sobre él si no logras recuperar un segundo cofre enano desde las Montañas Nubladas.","'¿Cómo pude haber pasado esto por alto? ¡Había una segunda página en los registros de Heikki! ¡Describe un segundo cofre, ${PLAYER}! Heikki no es el tipo de enano con el que quieras quedar mal, porque lo recordará — lo escribirá en uno de sus libros y nunca te dejará olvidar que lo decepcionaste. Si no consigo ese segundo cofre, no me sorprendería que alguien encontrara sus registros dentro de cuatrocientos años y pensara mal de Larus Fragmentoagudo, hijo de Tralli.\
\
'Así que tenemos que encontrarlo, ${PLAYER}. Déjame revisar este papel y decirte dónde debería estar. Ah, la fortaleza enana entre los Riscos Altos, al sur. Es la fortaleza que custodia Gabilazan, y está llena de esos inútiles Duramano.\
\
'Quizás quieras tomar el paso más occidental hacia el Risco Alto. Busca un edificio en una colina a tu izquierda al acercarte a la fortaleza. El cofre debería estar justo dentro, ¡así que no te demores!'","'¿Quién se atreve a entrar en la tumba de Halmur Modelapiedra, hijo de Vithurr de antaño? ¡Ni siquiera un duramano sería tan insensato como para entrar aquí! Conocen la historia de los Modelapiedra y tiemblan de miedo. Pero tú eres diferente...\
\
'Vienes por el cofre, ¿verdad, ${RACE}? ¡Solo tienes unos momentos para contarme tu historia antes de que te parta en dos!'","Reúne el segundo cofre","El Otro Cofre","'El segundo cofre estará dentro de un edificio en una colina a tu izquierda al acercarte a la fortaleza duramano en el paso de Gabilazan desde el norte. Viaja allí y recupera ese cofre, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[12750]={"The Outcast","A boar is hitched outside of the tavern. Sâdikiz is probably inside.","'It is true that I am largely responsible for the opening of the doors, such as it is. I did not do it entirely on my own, though. Many in Jiret-menêsh felt as I did, and I also found the courage to stand up to Châmelek Gêta from trading letters with a friend.\
\
'His name is Sâdikiz, and he is a Temámir who was banished from Jiret-menêsh many years ago. He also pushed for opening the doors and was so wilful that he angered Châmelek Gêta. She dubbed him \\qthe Sky-hungry\\q and cast him out from the city, telling him that if he craved the sky so much, he could go die under it.\
\
'I expect she thought he did just that, but the world is not as perilous as she believes. He has had many adventures and has returned to An Shêru. He can often be found in Khanâg Gur.\
\
'You should meet him! I admire him in many ways. He may yet prove to be a valuable ally to you, as he has been for me. Look for his boar. If you see it, he cannot be far.'","Sâdikiz the Sky-hungry can be found at Khanâg Gur. Mêshaget said to look for Sâdikiz's boar.","Talk to Sâdikiz the Sky-hungry","Instance: The Outcast completed","Sâdikiz the Sky-hungry can be found at Khanâg Gur. You should go there to find him.","Travel to Khanâg Gur","You saved Sâdikiz from being beaten by two bullies who claimed he owed them money. You should talk to Sâdikiz in Khanâg Gur, outside of the tavern.","Mêshaget said he received encouragement to fight for the opening of the doors of Jiret-menêsh through correspondence with Sâdikiz the Sky-hungry, a Temámir who was banished by Châmelek Gêta many years ago. Mêshaget thinks you should meet Sâdikiz, whom he considers a dear friend.","Complete Instance: The Outcast","You have arrived at Khanâg Gur","'As you may have overheard, I currently owe a debt to some of the locals. It seems that they are not particularly patient and sought to speed my repayment. You have spared me from many bruises, or perhaps worse!'"},
[12751]={"Laugi should be somewhere near Zarkul-sulûn in southern Elderslade.\
\
Gunvald has asked you to look for his missing brother.","Find the missing scout","'Hail, ${RACE}. 'Tis good to see a friendly face. I would rise to greet you, but I need a moment to catch my breath.\
\
'I am indeed Laugi. I was on my way to scout the camp ahead when I was beset upon by the enemy. I made a good accounting of myself, but one of them nicked me before they fled.'","'Hail, friend. I am Gunvald, one of Ausma's scouts. I heard that you will be assisting us, for which I am very glad indeed. My brother, Laugi, went scouting near the Zarkul-sulûn ruins and was due to return some time back. If you could look for him, I would much appreciate it. I am sure he is fine, of course, but... well, it is not like him to be so overdue. I would go myself, but I must stay here to assist Ausma.'","The Overdue Scout","A wayward brother who went scouting should have checked in quite some time ago."},
[12752]={"'The honey jar gives me hope that the stories of Zigilmarn, the fabled Clovengap honey-wine, are true!'","The Overgrown Vineyard","'The jar you brought back from Dashât-zahar is fascinating in so many ways! Look here, see those stains? That be honey or my chin is bald! It has long been thought that our ancestors here tended bees! I believe you found a jar of honey intended for sale at the market.\
\
'Right, let us return to the map. The honey jar gives me hope that the stories of Zigilmarn, the fabled Clovengap honey-wine, are true! I read that there were vineyards on the far shores of the Kurdushâlak. See what you can find, if you please? I shall meet you across the river, at Hagbuth.'","The vineyards may be in eastern Clovengap.\
\
Gerja has asked you to locate the fabled vineyards of Clovengap.","'Welcome back! Did you find the vineyards?\
\
'Come, come! Show me on the map.'","Overgrown trellises stretch across multiple tiers","The vineyards of Gundabad were once renowned throughout Middle-earth.","Gerja Defthand is in Hagbuth, in eastern Clovengap.\
\
You should let Gerja Defthand know that you found the vineyards.","Talk to Gerja in Hagbuth","Search for the vineyards"},
[12753]={"'This is how I see it, and pardon my speaking thus, Stéthi. There are two impurities we've got in this slag. First-wise, there's no one to do the deed. Second, there's someone, somewhere, who knows the signal flags and maybe doesn't want the deed done.'","Kurtil stands near the dwarves and corpse, behind a cart high up the path in northern Udûn, above Maudhúl Vôr.\
\
Hear what Kurtil has to say.","The dwarves stand behind a cart high up the path in northern Udûn, above Maudhúl Vôr.\
\
The trail of footprints led straight from signs of a bloody struggle to two dwarf-forgeworkers standing over a corpse. You should speak to them.","Talk to the dwarves","Search for Ushkbál","You should search for Ushkbál the Overseer in the great foundry, on the northern side of Udûn, above Maudhúl Vôr.","The corpse and dwarves are behind a cart high up the path in northern Udûn, above Maudhúl Vôr.\
\
You should inspect the overseer's corpse to verify the dwarves' claim that he bears sword-wounds, while they hold only hammers.","'We must seek Ushkbál the Overseer, then. It is he who will accomplish what we seek.'\
\
Paying no heed of any surprise on your face, Kurtil thinks for a long moment.\
\
'He has agreed, agreed to talk to us at least, and there is hope for more. Surely, he is found at his post, north of here by the great foundry, which lies above Maudhúl Vôr.'","This footprint is fresh - you are on the trail","Clear signs of a struggle and of bloody deeds! A conspicuous footprint lies nearby","The wounds are indeed incisions, not made by blunt instruments","Talk to Kurtil","The Overseer's Post","Talk to Slárnur","This is the place - now to find the Overseer","It seems an overseer named Ushkbál is the key to this mysterious meeting, somehow.","The dwarves are behind a cart high up the path in northern Udûn, above Maudhúl Vôr.\
\
You should talk to the dwarves, now that you have verified that the overseer's corpse bears sword and not blunt wounds.","Talk to Stéthi","'Stéthi, you explain. I'll botch it up, properly. Besides, I'm still catching my breath from dragging old Ushkbál all the ways up here.'","'You speak to them, yes? I think that best.'","You have not found Ushkbál the Overseer, but you have found signs of a bloody struggle. You should follow the footprints leading from the place and see where they lead.","Kurtil arrives just behind you to witness the scene. 'Talk before fight,' he hisses.","''Twas not us who did this thing. I know full well how it may look. We only dragged him here, out of the sight of prying eyes.\
\
'Hoy, you there, Kurtil! I know you by face and by name. Whatever trouble you're up to this time, you must bow to plain truth: Who in the northern 'works would touch a hair on Ushkbál's ugly pate? None, that's who! No overseer we'd more gladly work for, neither.\
\
'Besides, you see we carry only hammers and these wounds be swords' work, plain to see. Look yourself, ${RACE}.'","Inspect the corpse","Follow the footprints","'The great foundry lies north of the road below, above Maudhúl Vôr. You go and seek Ushkbál the Overseer on the good legs you have. I follow behind.'","'If it is so, then it is so, yes? The dwarf speaks true.'","'Yes, yes, yes. The iron is hot now, but cooling, cooling...'\
\
For a moment, Kurtil seems lost in thought.\
\
'We need only someone to go. Who to fill the post? No, not I, Nurnhoth that I am. Who am I? No one. Will Gradrágh go? Ha ha. We know the answer to that, my friends. What of you, Slárnur? You will not. A shame!\
\
'No Orc, nor dwarf, nor Nurnhoth here among us...'\
\
Then a smile slowly spreads across Kurtil's face, lighting the twinkle back into his eyes, which fix on you.","'Now then, that's settled, I hope! A smouldering shame about Ushkbál, though! We know not if it were one of the enforcers or some wild-frenzied soldier who stuck him through, but there you have it. He was our hope and he's gone.\
\
'Well, and if you are here then you followed the signal flags, too, just as we. Let us work the iron together, we four, while it's got any heat left. Perhaps the work might be salvaged. If only we can think what to do now that we are on our own. What say you Kurtil? ${RACE}?'","'Look and you will see. No hammer felled Ushkbál.'"},
[12754]={"Cordially <rgb=#00FF00>bow</rgb> to Anórohir","Travel to the Eyrie with Anórohir","Gwaihir the Wind-lord can be found at the Eyrie.\
\
You should talk to Gwaihir.","Cordially <rgb=#00FF00>bow</rgb> to Gwaihir","'Our paths cross once again, ${RACE}. I saw you once in the Garden of Galadriel, and now you fly high above your station to the very Eyrie of my people. It is most curious to me that you keep turning up, small one.'","Travel to the Carrock","The Carrock can be found on the western edge of the Beorning-lands in the Vales of Anduin.\
\
You should seek out Varthmath atop the Carrock.","Talk to Varthmath atop the Carrock","'I have made my decision. The Elves say they will help us, but only rarely do I see them leave the shelter of the woods, and I hesitate to call on them for aid. The dwarves and Men that live in the north have their own problems, as do we, and neither can be a help to the other while his own lands remain unsecured!\
\
'I have not spent this time idly, ${PLAYER}. No, there is a solution, and it lies on the very edge of my land. On the edge... and upwards! I speak of the Great Eagles' Eyrie. Those noble birds have aided my people before, and they may do so again.\
\
'You are a friend of Gandalf the Wizard, and he is one who has the respect of the Eagles. Speak to Gwaihir the Wind-lord on behalf of my people and request their aid. I will send Varthmath ahead to call upon the Eagles for a meeting.'","The Pact of Paws and Wings","'${PLAYER}, there you are. I have requested a summons. Anórohir has agreed to take only one of us up to the Eyrie. I think it should be you, for you are a friend of Gandalf, and that may help the Great Eagles decide to side with us!\
\
'I would recommend that you speak with courtesy to the Eagles. Consider a proper bow at the outset, and be sure to make use of as fine speech as you are able!'","Anórohir can be found atop the Carrock.\
\
You should travel to the Eyrie with Anórohir.","Atop the wind-swept peak you see some familiar friends","'Ah, I believe Grimbeorn awaits us with his reply. Speak to the lord of the Beornings and learn what he has to say. Let us hope it will be good tidings for my father and for the Elves of Felegoth.'","Gwaihir the Wind-lord can be found at the Eyrie.\
\
You should be polite to Gwaihir.","Habla con Grimbeorn","Grimbeorn can be found at the Beorninghús in the Beorning-lands.\
\
You should talk to Grimbeorn.","Varthmath must have already climbed to the top of the Carrock","Talk to Gwaihir the Windlord","Gwaihir awaits your word","Grimbeorn looks to the skies for assistance in the Vales of Anduin.","Anórohir is on the Carrock.\
\
You should be polite to Anórohir."},
[12755]={"Léofmar will be all right. It would be wise to continue your search for sleeping Ents","Another Ent sleeps here, surrounded by smoke, fires, and grief. What harries this poor creature's home?","'I rode my horse to the edge of the wood, but I would not let him follow me inside. I came here to hide... and to die. My poor steed should not meet the fate of a coward.'","Léofmar is in Fangorn.\
\
You should speak with Léofmar.","Talk to Léofmar again","Léofmar's horse has responded at once to your summons, ready and willing to bear his master to safety.","'My steed! I cannot believe it, ${PLAYER}. I cannot believe that you found him. I had not even hope that he was near, the foolish beast.'\
\
You tell Léofmar of the small boating camp on the edge of Fangorn, where he will likely be welcomed with his bow and arrows.\
\
'I will go there now, ${PLAYER}; thank you. I am blessed, not cursed, to have so many good folk and creatures looking after me. I will not be afraid anymore.'","You should search for other sleeping Ents in the forest, heading north-east from Léofmar's location.","You should whistle for the horse you met earlier, now that you have found his lost master","The horse you met appears, clearly relieved to be reunited with his master","Find a new sleeping Ent in the north","<rgb=#FF0000>Whistle</rgb> for Léofmar's horse","Listen to Léofmar's tale","'I will tell you all, ${PLAYER}. You will regret ever helping me; I know it.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo instance, and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>","Léofmar is ashamed of his behaviour, wracked by guilt. Could his crimes have been so great that he deserves the curse he believes is coming to claim him?","You should <rgb=#FF0000>whistle</rgb> for Léofmar's horse.\
\
You must be standing near Léofmar in order to do this.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You must perform an emote to advance this quest.</rgb>","Léofmar is in Fangorn.\
\
You should speak with Léofmar and hear his tale.","'I will tell you my tale of woe, ${PLAYER}, but I promise that you will wish to undo all of the kindness that you have done for me when you hear of my cowardice.\
\
'Let me tell you first that I am no soldier. I have never been a brave man. My duties in my home called me to take the city-watch for a night, and I did that duty at least, but I am ashamed to speak of what came after....'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This is a solo instance, and cannot be completed in a fellowship.</rgb>","Léofmar is in Fangorn.\
\
You should talk to Léofmar once more.","Reassure Léofmar that you do not think his crime so terrible","The Pain of Regret"},
[12764]={"Has explorado el límite de Nan Wathren.","Como no se ha encontrado rastro del maestro de pociones que creó el potente somnífero, el Capitán Pasolargo te ha pedido que amplíes tu búsqueda a un territorio más peligroso: Nan Wathren.","'Me pregunto, ${PLAYER} -- ¿encontraste al creador de la poción repugnante mientras explorabas los campamentos orcos?'\
\
Le dices al Capitán Pasolargo que no tuviste suerte.\
\
'Ah. Eso es realmente una mala noticia, porque significa que la influencia del enemigo se extiende más de lo que pensaba. Tengo la inquietante idea de que Nan Wathren ha caído en manos de los Orcos.\
\
'El paso de Nan Wathren es un lugar peligroso incluso en el mejor de los casos. Si deseas ayudar a Puente de Caballetes de una vez por todas, debes eliminar la presencia Orca De nan wathren.'\
\
<RGB=#Ff0000>Nota: Nan wathren es una zona peligrosa. sería prudente viajar allí en compañía de una comunidad.</rgb>","El Paso de Nan Wathren","Encuentra y entra en el peligroso paso de Nan Wathren","Has llegado al límite de Nan Wathren.\
\
Puedes entrar si lo deseas, pero será un camino peligroso.","Completado","Nan Wathren está al noreste de Puente de Caballetes.\
\
Deberías dirigirte al paso de Nan Wathren para buscar la fuente de los problemas de Puente de Caballetes.","Nan Wathren se encuentra más allá de este puente...."},
[12765]={"'No sé qué planean los infiltradores, ${PLAYER}, pero tuvimos mucha suerte de que escuchara parte de sus planes. Debes ir a su escondite y usar la contraseña para entrar y frustrar sus planes antes de que terminen sus preparativos.\
\
'La contraseña es \\q¡Otro infiltrado está aquí!\\q\
\
'Su escondite está en Bree, al sur de la Escalinata Alta.'","'¿Qué es eso? \\q¿Otro infiltrado está aquí?\\q Bien. No te reconozco, pero nuestro grupo ya es bastante grande, así que no me sorprende. Los que hagan falta, ¿verdad?\
\
'Quizá podríamos haber elegido una mejor contraseña, supongo, pero al menos es fácil de recordar.'","La contraseña","El escondite de los infiltradores está en Bree, al sur de la Escalinata Alta. Un portero está frente a la entrada y solo te dejará pasar si repites la contraseña.\
\
Benegar Vallelargo escuchó a dos Hombres desaliñados hablar de un grupo secreto que planea una sorpresa malvada para Bree y quiere que te infiltras entre los infiltradores.","'Bueno, quizá no asesinato, pero sonaban muy serios, ¡y me temo que no pasará mucho antes de que sus planes se cumplan!\
\
'Estaba agachado aquí en el barro, buscando tortugas, cuando dos Hombres mal vestidos salieron chapoteando hacia la isla. Parecían no querer ser vistos y miraban constantemente por encima del hombro, hacia Bree. Pensé al principio que venían a buscar tortugas en mi mejor lugar para atraparlas, ¡pero entonces empezaron a hablar! ¡Y sus palabras! ¡Ay, ay!\
\
'Hablaron de un grupo que se ha infiltrado en Bree y que está reuniendo fuerzas, observando y esperando. Y cuando estén listos, están planeando una sorpresa para la aldea, ¡una que la gente de Bree no olvidará pronto! \\qCulver el Ingenioso está afilando su hoja\\q, dijo el más desaliñado, \\qy Garrett el Retorcido tiene toda la cuerda que necesitaremos.\\q\
\
'Se marcharon después de eso, pero no antes de hablar de la contraseña que los infiltradores usan para entrar en su escondite. Es \\q¡Otro infiltrado está aquí!\\q, y si se la dices a su portero, podrás entrar y detenerlos antes de que estén listos. Su escondite está en Bree, al sur de la Escalinata Alta, y su portero está frente a la entrada. ¡Deténlos, ${PLAYER}!'","Benegar Vallelargo escuchó a dos Hombres desaliñados hablar de una 'sorpresa' para Bree, y ahora quiere que te infiltras en su escondite y detengas sus planes.","Habla con el portero del escondite de los infiltradores y dale la contraseña"},
[12766]={"Fallen boulders can be found on the pass to the Men Angrún.\
\
After clearing a number of loose stones, you should now attempt to break the boulders that have fallen upon the pass to the Men Angrún.","Clear loose stones from the pass to the Men Angrún (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Determined to follow the dark road to the Grey Mountains, the Zhélruka seek to clear a massive rockslide from the northern pass leading to the Men Angrún.","The boulder resists your efforts!","'Bah!\
\
'The dark road is the swiftest course to Dómekh, and I am not prepared to give up so easily. If I must scale this rockslide to walk the Men Angrún, I shall do it!\
\
'You may go, ${RACE}. I will find a way through.'","Loose stones can be found upon the northern pass to the Men Angrún in the Ironfold.\
\
Wishing to avoid passing through the lands of the King under the Mountain, Ingór has asked you to aid his company in clearing the way to the Men Angrún.","Attempt to break boulders that have fallen upon the pass to the Men Angrún","'Have we not travelled far enough to satisfy that stuffy Longbeard smith?'\
\
Ingór studies your face and notes your confusion.\
\
'Do you not remember me? You sent my company away to continue on our journey, and so we have. Indeed, we would have travelled further, but the northern pass to the Men Angrún is sealed by stone and debris!\
\
'To speak plainly, I do not wish to travel through the lands of the King under the Mountain. We of the Zhélruka seek to make our pilgrimage to Dómekh in the old ways, unhindered by politics. There are old wounds between our peoples best forgotten, and I would not see them renewed by the manner of our passage to Dómekh.\
\
'Will you aid us in clearing the loose stones and boulders from the way to the Men Angrún?'","Cleared loose stones from the pass to the Men Angrún (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Path Better Taken","Talk to Ingór","Ingór can be found on the pass to the Men Angrún.\
\
You have attempted to break the fallen boulders upon the pass to the Men Angrún, but they resisted your efforts. You should talk to Ingór."},
[12767]={"Habla con Daegennan en Gwingris","Sierpes derrotadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}. Creo que con eso sus números están lo suficientemente reducidos para que al menos en un futuro próximo las provisiones lleguen sin problema.\
\
'Sin embargo, hay todavía más por hacer.'","'Saludos, ${PLAYER}. Te doy la bienvenida a Gwingris.\
\
'Como puedes ver, nuestro puesto avanzado está escaso de suministros. Me temo que el siguiente envío desde Rivendel tardará mucho en llegar, y sin esos suministros nos será difícil aguantar contra las fuerzas del Enemigo.\
\
'Las entregas anteriores se han encontrado con algunos problemas en el valle hacia el este de aquí, debido a las sierpes. Si pudieras dedicar algo de tiempo en diezmar el número de estas criaturas, podremos conseguir reabastecernos más fácilmente en un futuro.'","Derrota a las sierpes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Malvadas sierpes amenazan las rutas desde Rivendel al puesto de avanzada élfico de Gwingris.","Pueden encontrarse sierpes en los valles al este de Gwingris.\
\
Daegennan te ha pedido que ayudes a despejar de sierpes las rutas entre Rivendel y Gwingris.","El camino de Rivendel","'Quienes traían entregas desde Rivendel a menudo hablaban de sierpes que habitan en el valle lejos hacia el este de aquí. Comienza tu cacería allí.'","Daegennan está en Gwingris, al oeste de los valles de las sierpes.\
\
Deberías volver a ver a Daegennan en Gwingris."},
[12768]={"'Sé que hiciste lo que te pedí, . Los enanos pueden reclamar estas antiguas salas, y son bienvenidos a ellas. No siento afecto alguno por estos pasajes sombríos. Lo que extraño es el aire frío y puro de las montañas. Algún día, cuando los orcos se hayan ido y los enanos también se hayan ido, regresaremos al hogar que dejamos hace tanto tiempo y correremos por las laderas de las montañas, y allí encontraremos alegría.\
\
'Ese día aún no ha llegado, ${PLAYERNAME:primo mío[m]|prima mía[f]}, pero llegará, y entonces nuestro audaz ancestro estará orgulloso de nosotros.'","'Lo hiciste bien, ${PLAYERNAME:primo mío[m]|prima mía[f]}. Los orcos y trasgos creían estar a salvo en las salas de esta ciudad maldita, pues la estirpe de Beorn estaba en la superficie y muy lejos. Ahora saben que nuestro alcance es grande, pero quiero que sepan que no somos simples visitantes. Tenemos un derecho sobre las laderas de las montañas que se alzan sobre estas salas, un derecho más fuerte que el de los enanos sobre estos pasajes sombríos.\
\
'Sal de estas salas y abre camino hacia la superficie. En la cima de Zirakzigil, <rgb=#FF0000>ruge</rgb> nuestro legítimo dominio sobre los cielos, . Encuentra un lugar lo bastante impresionante, un punto de referencia con algo de majestuosidad, desde el cual llevar a cabo este acto. Quiero que todos, enanos y orcos por igual, sepan que la estirpe de Beorn reclama las laderas de las montañas y no teme a nada.'","'Sal de estas salas y abre camino hacia la superficie. En la cima de Zirakzigil, <rgb=#FF0000>ruge</rgb> nuestro legítimo dominio sobre los cielos, ${PLAYER}. Encuentra un lugar lo bastante impresionante, un punto de referencia con algo de majestuosidad, desde el cual llevar a cabo este acto. Quiero que todos, enanos y orcos por igual, sepan que la estirpe de Beorn reclama las laderas de las montañas y no teme a nada.'","El rugido resuena en el aire frío y puro de las montañas, como una advertencia para cualquiera que se oponga a tu pueblo","Orcos derrotados en los confines más lejanos de Moria (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Varthmath se encuentra en La Guardia Orca, en las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo.\
\
Has hecho lo que Varthmath te pidió y ahora deberías informarle de tu éxito.","El camino de regreso","Los restos de la terrible criatura ofrecen un espectáculo impresionante","'¡Combate contra orcos por todos los confines más lejanos de Moria, ${PLAYER}, y enséñales a temer a la estirpe de Beorn!'","Has seguido a tu primo Varthmath hasta las profundidades de Moria, donde los enanos de la Guarnición de Hierro buscan expulsar a los trasgos que habitan su antiguo reino.","Varthmath te ha pedido que encuentres un lugar en las laderas de Zirakzigil desde el cual puedas rugir tu dominio sobre las montañas. Quería que encontraras un punto de referencia lo suficientemente impresionante en el que hacerlo.","Derrota orcos en los confines más lejanos de Moria (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Se pueden encontrar orcos por las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo, Nud-Melek y las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Tu primo Varthmath te ha pedido que derrotes orcos en las profundidades de Moria para enseñarles a temer a la estirpe de Beorn.","Encuentra un punto de referencia impresionante en la cima de Zirakzigil y <rgb=#FF0000>ruge</rgb> tu dominio sobre las montañas","'Ah, ${PLAYERNAME:primo mío[m]|prima mía[f]}, ¡es bueno ver un rostro conocido! Hice venir a Sterkist hasta aquí, pero parece que te envió a ti en su lugar. No lo culpo por haber decidido no venir. Yo no habría entrado en esta oscuridad si hubiera tenido elección, pero esa es precisamente la situación. ¡Son esos enanos! Incitan a los trasgos innecesariamente y despiertan criaturas del mal que deberían permanecer dormidas.\
\
'Sabes que Beorn y su estirpe se originaron en las montañas. Las montañas que se alzan sobre estas salas malditas son el verdadero hogar de nuestro pueblo, por derecho. Estos enanos agitan a los trasgos y las criaturas se desparraman por todas las montañas. ¿Cómo podemos esperar recuperar algún día nuestro territorio si está constantemente amenazado por enanos u orcos?\
\
'¡Combate contra orcos por todos los confines más lejanos de Moria, , y enséñales a temer a la estirpe de Beorn!'","Habla con Varthmath en La Guardia Orca, entre las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo","Varthmath se encuentra en la Guardia Orca, entre las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo."},
[12769]={"Talk to Kholnedák","Search Aegollant for shoddy stones","Dingási has asked that you travel south to Arnach, and speak with Kholnedák, the supervisor in charge of the town's storage and shipping of stone.\
\
Kholnedák can be found in Arnach.","While inspecting the shoddy stones in Aegollant, you were set upon by brigands. One of the bandits dropped a crumpled note, the details of which Kholnedák will be eager to read.\
\
Kholnedák is in Arnach.","'You return! Tell me, what did you find?'","Kholnedák has asked you to investigate the bandit camp Aegollant, and to search for signs of the shoddy stones.\
\
Aegollant is in Lossarnach.","You found a pile of the shoddy stones!","Examina la piedra","'Ah, ${PLAYER}, it is as we feared. Our stock within has also been seeded with poor quality stone. If I were a betting dwarf, and I am, I would say that we might find some answers in Aegollant, where a group of bandits has set up camp.\
\
'Down the hills and across the road they linger, attacking passersby on the road and stealing from the town when they can. The Captain of the Guard, Baranor, has been planning to rout the swine, but his forces are stretched a bit thin at the moment.\
\
'You seem like you can take care of yourself. Why not search their camp? Look for more of these blocks, or any other clues that might tell us who is responsible for the deception.'","You found a crumpled note!","Within the ruins of Aegollant, you have found piles of the shoddy blocks which were snuck into the dwarves' superior piles of stone.\
\
You should investigate the blocks.","Return to Kholnedák","Dingási suspects that the supply chain may have been corrupted with more of the poor-quality stone. You are tasked with travelling to Arnach to check on the inventory stored there.","The Path of Stones","Kholnedák has asked you to meet her near the northern farms in Arnach.","Talk to Kholnedák near the northern farms","'Greetings, stranger. You come from Dingási? You are timely, as I was readying to send word that we had a partial wall collapse here.'\
\
As you inform her of the bad blocks her face grows troubled.\
\
'Dire news indeed, and I feel the fool for not having noticed if our stock was tainted. I will check the stores immediately! Our stone is currently stored within a local barn. Meet me near the northern farms.'","'Glad am I that you have destroyed so many of those shoddy blocks, yet troubled too, that there were so many. I have had my workers check the stores we have here, and there were indeed more of the poor blocks mixed in among the ones of greater quality.\
\
'I ordered the inferior blocks destroyed, but I need to trace the dilution of our stock to see from whence they came. Will you go south to Arnach and speak with my colleague, Kholnedák? Have her check the town's stores to see if they too have been infiltrated.'"},
[12770]={"Ruingal ha sido derrotado","Hugi está en el campamento frente a las Forjas de Khazad-dûm.\
\
Debes regresar con Hugi e informarle de tu éxito.","'¡Excelente trabajo, ${PLAYER}! Ahora, tu recompensa.\
\
'Sin duda habrá más Maestros del Saber que necesitarán tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}. No dejes de volver a verme antes de entrar en las Forjas de Khazad-dûm si alguna vez te encuentras acompañando a un Maestro del Saber novato.'","Muchos Maestros del Saber buscan la Senda de la Maestra Antigua, pero no todos pueden alcanzar sus objetivos por sí solos.","Ruingal se encuentra en las Forjas de Khazad-dûm, al sur del Cruce de las Cenizas, en las Profundidades Llameantes, al este de las Obras Hidráulicas.\
\
Hugi te ha pedido que ayudes a un Maestro del Saber a enfrentarse al espectro de fuego Ruingal para cumplir con la Senda de la Maestra Antigua.","La Senda de la Maestra Antigua: Echando una mano","Habla con Hugi afuera de las Forjas de Khazad-dûm","'Saludos, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Hablo en nombre de mis compañeros Maestros del Saber al pedir tu ayuda para una tarea nada pequeña.\
\
'En las Forjas de Khazad-dûm mora un espectro de fuego conocido como Ruingal. Por lo visto, ha causado no pocos estragos desde los días en que el Daño de Durin llegó a Moria.\
\
'Si ayudas a uno de mis hermanos Maestros del Saber a derribar a esta vil criatura, tendrás nuestra eterna gratitud y un pequeño símbolo de nuestro aprecio.'","Derrota a Ruingal"},
[12771]={"Ayudaste a un capitán a completar \\qEn peligro\\q","Ayuda a un capitán a completar \\qEn peligro\\q","Fil-gashan se encuentra en la zona suroeste de las Profundidades Llameantes.\
\
Waden te ha pedido que ayudes a otro capitán a completar su tarea final en Fil-gashan.","Waden se encuentra justo afuera de Fil-gashan, en la zona suroeste de las Profundidades Llameantes.\
\
Con tu tarea completada, deberías regresar junto a Waden con noticias de tu éxito.","'Saludos, ${PLAYER}. Hay muchos capitanes que buscan el Camino de las Manos Sanadoras, pero no todos pueden cumplir su tarea en soledad. Deberías procurar ayudar a tus compañeros capitanes en su camino.\
\
'El mayor peligro al que se enfrentarán se encuentra en Fil-gashan.\
\
'Ve ahora y demuestra tu honor.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>;Esta misión solo puede completarse ayudando a un capitán en su misión de clase, \\qEn peligro.\\q</rgb>","Muchos capitanes buscan el Camino de las Manos Sanadoras, pero no todos pueden alcanzar sus objetivos en soledad.","Habla con Waden afuera de Fil-gashan","'You have done well, ${PLAYER}. You are truly a worthy captain.'","El Camino de las Manos Sanadoras: Echando una mano"},
[12772]={"Pinzalarga derrotado","Nils se encuentra en su campamento, fuera de Skûmfil.\
\
Deberías regresar con Nils para informarle de tu éxito.","Derrota a Pinzalarga","El camino del Campeón Marcial: Echar una mano","'Saludos, ${PLAYER}. Hay muchos guerreros, pero pocos Campeones cuyos actos perduren en la memoria. Hay Campeones así que buscan demostrar su valía en Skûmfil.\
\
'Incluso los héroes más grandes necesitan amistades que los apoyen, y mis camaradas Campeones no son la excepción. Si estás a la altura del desafío, quiero que te unas a uno de esos Campeones y entres en Skûmfil. Una vez dentro, ayuda al Campeón a derrotar al grodbog conocido como Pinzalarga.\
\
'Si tienes éxito, regresa a verme... si no, bueno, dudo que puedas regresar.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión solo puede completarse ayudando a un Campeón en su misión de Rasgo Legendario \\qHeroicidades.\\q</rgb>","Pinzalarga se encuentra en Skûmfil, al este del Refugio Sombrío, en las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Ayuda a un Campeón a dar muerte al grodbog Pinzalarga.","'¿Es realmente una carga ayudar a un Campeón que lo necesita?'","'Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}. Me pregunto si tus propios actos llegarán a convertirse en leyenda por tu papel en esta victoria.\
\
'Toma esto con mi gratitud... has hecho algo importante.\
\
'Además, asegúrate de hablar conmigo antes de volver a Skûmfil. Es probable que haya nuevos Campeones que necesiten tu ayuda.'","Muchos Campeones buscan el camino del Campeón Marcial, pero no todos pueden alcanzar sus objetivos en soledad.","Habla con Nils en su campamento"},
[12773]={"La Senda del Puño Magistral: Echando una Mano","Habla con Breguthryth afuera de las Excavaciones Tenebrosas","Derrota al Capitán Demente","'Saludos, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Los Vigilantes como yo nos esforzamos por purgar el mal de nuestras tierras allí donde lo encontremos y allí donde llamemos hogar.\
\
'El antiguo hogar de los enanos necesita con urgencia nuestra ayuda. Muchos Vigilantes buscan cumplir la Senda del Puño Magistral, pero no pueden hacerlo solos.\
\
' Si estás ${PLAYERNAME:dispuesto[m]|dispuesta[f]} a prestar una mano en esta tarea, quiero que ayudes a tus compañeros Vigilantes a dar muerte a la criatura conocida como el Capitán Demente. Regresa conmigo cuando la tarea esté hecha, y me aseguraré de que recibas tu recompensa.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta misión solo puede completarse ayudando a un Vigilante en su misión de rasgo legendario \\qSalvaguardia\\q.</rgb>","Muchos Vigilantes buscan seguir la Senda del Puño Magistral, pero no todos pueden alcanzar sus objetivos en solitario.","El Capitán Demente solo puede ser invocado dentro de las Excavaciones Tenebrosas, situadas en las extensiones surorientales de las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Breguthryth te ha pedido ayudar a un Vigilante a derrotar al Capitán Demente.","Breguthryth está afuera de las Excavaciones Tenebrosas.\
\
Debes regresar con Breguthryth e informarle de tu victoria.","Capitán Demente derrotado","'¡Excelente trabajo, ${PLAYER}! Con el Capitán Demente muerto, nuestros esfuerzos por ayudar a los enanos a recuperar Moria avanzan un paso más.\
\
'Acepta esto en nombre de los Pueblos Libres de la Tierra Media. Hoy has hecho un gran servicio a todos nosotros.\
\
'Si alguna vez vuelves por aquí, asegúrate de hablar conmigo antes de entrar a las Excavaciones Tenebrosas. En estos días oscuros abundan los enemigos por abatir, y muchos Vigilantes necesitarán tu ayuda.'"},
[12774]={"'Nunca deberías darle la espalda a un saqueador que necesita ayuda... ¡deberías averiguar qué puede ofrecerte a cambio de tu asistencia!'","Unur derrotado","Hardsnel se encuentra justo afuera de la Sala Decimosexta, al norte de las Fundaciones de Piedra.\
\
Con Unur derrotado, deberías regresar junto a Hardsnel con noticias de tu éxito.","Habla con Hardsnel","El camino del bromista: Echando una mano","'Has hecho un buen trabajo, ${PLAYER}. Eres de verdad ${PLAYER:un saqueador digno de llamarse amigo.[m]|una saqueadora digna de llamarse amiga.[f]}'","Muchos saqueadores buscan el camino del bromista, pero no todos pueden alcanzar sus objetivos por sí solos.","'Saludos, ${PLAYER}. Muchos saqueadores buscan el camino del bromista, pero no todos pueden cumplir su cometido en soledad. Deberías procurar ayudar a otros saqueadores en su camino.\
\
'El mayor peligro al que se enfrentará uno de ellos se encuentra en la Sala Decimosexta.\
\
'Ve ahora y demuestra tu honor.'","Derrota a Unur","La Sala Decimosexta se encuentra al norte de las Fundaciones de Piedra y al sur de Sigin-Tharâk.\
\
Hardsnel te ha pedido que ayudes a otro saqueador a completar su tarea final en la Sala Decimosexta."},
[12775]={"Eniel está en el campamento justo al sur de la Gran Escalera.\
\
Con el líder de la Mano Blanca derrotado, deberías regresar con Eniel.","Regresa con Eniel","'Has hecho un buen trabajo, ${PLAYER}. Eres, sin duda, ${PLAYER:un compañero valioso[m]|una compañera valiosa[f]} para los demás Cazadores.'","El Camino del Trampero: Echando una mano","Muchos Cazadores buscan el Camino del Trampero, pero no todos pueden alcanzar sus objetivos sin ayuda.","Derrota a Drâgh","'Saludos, ${PLAYER}. Muchos Cazadores buscan el Camino del Trampero, pero no todos pueden cumplir su cometido por su cuenta. Deberías procurar ayudar a tus compañeros Cazadores en su senda.\
\
'El mayor peligro al que tu camarada deberá enfrentarse se encuentra en la Gran Escalera.\
\
'Ve ahora y demuestra tu honor.'","Drâgh ha sido derrotado","La Gran Escalera se encuentra justo al norte del campamento donde conociste a Eniel.\
\
Eniel te ha pedido que ayudes a otro Cazador a completar su tarea final en la Gran Escalera.","'Si encuentras a un cazador que necesite tu ayuda, deberías brindársela.'"},
[12776]={"Mother Amma is in Bazanmanar, in the north-east Clovengap.\
\
You should tell Mother Amma what you found in the ruins of Frósthel.","'Is this skull not astounding? I believe it once hung far over this area. Who knows how long ago it fell and shattered.'","Drakes can be found in Frósthel, in north-west Clovengap.\
\
The sarrowstone enchantment has infected the drakes. You must defeat them lest the corruption spread!","'Now then, I know not what to make of these fragments of torn paper that you collected. They look like they could form a map, but the writing on them is incomprehensible to me. Lore-master Rúni borrowed the journal and its translation as soon as he heard mention of dragons. Bring the fragments to him and see if he can decipher their meaning.'","You have gathered fragments of torn paper from the corrupted Angmarim sorcerers. Could they, together, be a map?","Defeat crystal-encrusted drakes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Rúni","Investigate the drakes at Frósthel","Lore-master Rúni is located in Bazanmanar.\
\
Mother Amma has asked you to speak to Lore-master Rúni.","Defeated crystal-encrusted drakes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Path to Corruption","Defeat the cold-drake nest matron","Return to Mother Amma","Lore-master Rúni is in Bazanmanar, in the north-east Clovengap.\
\
Mother Amma has asked you to see what progress Rúni has made.","'My friend! This journal is amazing! It belonged to an Angmarim by the name of Bruidalg the Bloodletter.\
\
'Look here, he wrote, \\qThe way is secret, secret is the way. Only with the four shall the secret way be secret no more.\\q Bruidalg continues on, rambling about, \\qThe bones, the bones are leaking. The master is in the muck, the master and the bones and the crystals. All in the muck, dragons in the mire. Never will I breathe clean air again.\\q\
\
'Fascinating, no? Could there be a dragon here in Clovengap? Aside from our frosty lady, that is. But another, perhaps? A second dragon?! Mired in the muck somewhere? By Durin's beard, this is too exciting.\
\
'Oh! I almost forgot. The journal mentions experiments on some of the frost-drakes that followed Hrímil into Clovengap. They have taken up residence at Frósthel, a set of ruins across the river. You go deal with that, and I shall have a look at the fragments you brought me.'","'Corrupted drakes? Terrible news! Glad am I that you have dealt with this situation, my friend.\
\
'The lore-master has been asking after you. Do go see if he has made progress with the ripped paper fragments.'","The drakes have been corrupted!","Drakes can be found in north-west Clovengap.\
\
There may drakes to which the corruption has spread. Rúni has asked you to investigate.","'Ah! You return. Tell me of the drakes!'"},
[12777]={"Enter the hidden gate of Lûghash and find Spakorth","An uneven dirt path leads onto the stones of Lûghash...","The Stout-axes of Mordor have long dwelled within Lûghash and they have reshaped the Flaming Spire to serve their own needs.","You spot Spakorth standing amid the shabby dwarf-barracks of Lûghash...","The hidden gate of Lûghash can be found in an alcove high above the main gate, accessible by a rear pathway leading onto the Spire.\
\
You have discovered the hidden gate of Lûghash and should now enter the Flaming Spire and find Spakorth.","'Hail, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'We stand before the main gate of Lûghash, but you must not enter it. The Mistress has watching-stones guarding the inside of the gate, and if you are detected, she shall bring her wrath down upon us all!\
\
'Many years ago, she allowed us to construct a second, hidden gate leading from our barracks out to the parapet far above us. We grew weary of her spirits lingering near us and begged her to keep the watching-stones away from our barracks. We did not expect mercy, but she relented, and set them only as guards within the main gate.\
\
'Do you understand? You must enter through the hidden gate if you are to remain beneath the Mistress's notice. It is not hidden in the ways of the dwarves, ${PLAYER}, but it is hidden from the Spire's face.\
\
'Behind the Spire, you will find a dirt pathway leading onto Lûghash itself. You must follow our lamps of crystal to a small, shadowed alcove. It is there you shall find the hidden gate.\
\
'Go now! I must still speak to the Mistress to calm her fears about the spirits you drove back to the Spire, but once that is done, you shall find me in the barracks on the central level of the Spire.'","A few, small crystal lamps rise about the stones of Lûghash and lead upward...","The Path to the Flaming Spire","The hidden gate of Lûghash can be found in an alcove high above the main gate, accessible by a rear pathway leading onto the Spire.\
\
Spakorth has described the path to the hidden gate of Lûghash. You should find the rear pathway, climb the tower by following the path of crystal lamps, and seek the hidden gate in a shadowed alcove.","Spakorth can be found in the dwarf-barracks on the central level of Lûghash.\
\
You have entered Lûghash and should now speak to Spakorth.","You have found the hidden gate of Lûghash, and Gimli is eager to enter the Spire!","Find the rear pathway onto Lûghash","'Ah! At last you have come!\
\
'I spoke to Mistress Zôreth, and she was pleased to learn that the \\qstrange invaders\\q were driven out. She wishes to focus on her research in the heights of the Spire, so I do not think we need worry about her for now.\
\
'Now that that's all settled, I have a few duties to perform about the Spire. If you would aid me with some of them, perhaps Gimli shall have more time to ask me his questions!'","Find the hidden gate of Lûghash upon the parapet","Talk to Spakorth in Lûghash","Find the trail of crystal lamps"},
[12779]={"'${PLAYER}, it has become more and more difficult to get a clear view of Wulf's Cleft, for the Dunlendings have increased their patrols in this area. If we are to learn the current state of their muster in Wulf's Cleft, we must engage these patrols and clear a way.\
\
'Travel south along the western edge of the mountains between the Isendale and Wulf's Cleft. The Dunlending patrols can be found in the valleys and mountain passes.\
\
'When you have cleared a path, return to me.'","'Stop the Dunlending patrols, ${PLAYER}!'","Garrun is encamped to the north of Cuvnerth.\
\
You should return to Garrun and let him know that any Dunlending patrols have been scattered.","Talk to Garrun in the Isendale","Garrun reports that a number of Dunlending patrols watch the passes between the western edge of the Isendale and Wulf's Cleft.","Dunlending patrols can be found in the valleys and mountain passes south of Garrun's camp.\
\
Garrun asked you to engage the Dunlending patrols along the western edge of the Isendale and clear a path to Wulf's Cleft.","'Good, ${PLAYER}, good. This means we can resume our vigil and perhaps bring reinforcements to the passes.'","Defeated Dunlending patrols (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Dunlending patrols (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Patrol Ends"},
[12780]={"Habla con Hórin","Fellgát has been cleaned up and is ready for more dwarves.\
\
You should talk to Hórin in Fellgát.","Hórin has asked you to help Dréri and Náth prepare the camp for incoming reinforcements.\
\
You should complete quests for Dréri and Náth.","'We have come to these high peaks in search of the hobgoblin leader Warlord Dushtalbúk and his advisor Loknashra. Ausma's scouts spotted them leaving the Stonejaws and marching in this direction with a sizeable troop of soldiers. We do not know their goal here, or why they left the safety of their stronghold, but this is an opportunity we cannot pass up! If we catch Dushtalbúk out in the open on these mountain slopes, we can deal a major blow to Hrímil's forces.'\
\
His face hardens, and he looks towards the sky, still haunted by his previous experience with the Dragon.\
\
'We must defeat the leaders of the Orcs, hobgoblins, and whatever else remains under her sway before engaging Hrímil directly. She is more than enough for an entire army to handle on her own, trust me.\
\
'Judging by the state of this place, we are on the right track. The hobgoblins must have passed through here and abandoned this camp. We cannot pass on such an advantageous defensive position for our own base of operations, so I must ask you to help clean up this mess. I know this is beneath your station, ${PLAYER}, but we are short-handed. Reinforcements will be arriving shortly, so this place needs to be in better shape! Dréri and Náth will take charge of this effort.\
\
'In the meantime, Ausma's apprentices Kyrstig, Molkha, and Klúso have gone ahead to locate the hobgoblin force. It is a shame Ausma could not join us herself, but she is still injured from her attack on Dushtalbúk. After we sort this place out, you and I will go looking for the hobgoblins.'","'Good work, ${PLAYER}! Fellgát looks much more like a proper camp now, and worthy of the Gabil'akkâ! Dréri and Náth will stay here until reinforcements arrive and we locate the hobgoblins, but you and I have some mountain-trekking to do.'","The Peaks of the Welkin-lofts","Completed quests in the Welkin-lofts for Dréri and Náth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Complete quests in the Welkin-lofts for Dréri and Náth (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Hórin is leading an expedition into the peaks of Welkin-lofts to search for Warlord Dushtalbúk and Loknashra."},
[12782]={"Help Adnoth, the stable-hand","Return to Thane Mildrith at the Mead Hall of Elthengels","Thane Mildrith's people are located within the walls of Elthengels in the eastern section of the Norcrofts.\
\
Thane Mildrith has asked you to aid her people in their tasks of protecting the town from further attack.","'I must commend you for helping me and my people. It is said that in the most trying of times the true worth of a person's character can be seen, and I have seen a great deal of good in these men.\
\
'I am still learning how best to serve Elthengels as Thane. I cannot be the strong warrior that my husband was, nor can I be the fearless vindicator that my dear son Pendulf was, but you have shown me that I have the ability to garner support and to rally the people of this village. This is a most generous gift you have given me.'","You have helped Elfwyn with his task","You have helped Adnoth with his task","Thane Mildrith is found at the Mead Hall of Elthengels.\
\
Thane Mildrith has promised to reward you for helping her people with their various tasks.","'My people are in need of aid, ${PLAYER}. Elthengels has survived a tremendous Orc-assault, but it has come at a great cost. My husband and son have perished, the countryside is ravaged, and many yet lay dead or dying. Without reinforcements from Théoden King or that coward Reeve Athelward, the end of our time here draws ever nearer.\
\
'If you offer me your assistance, I will gladly take it. We must band together, and take aid from wherever it may come.\
\
'The people of Elthengels are now my only concern. Our time for grieving must be brief. I will not let them give in to sorrow or concede defeat while they yet live...but there are many within the walls of this village that are in need of help. If you are able to resolve their troubles, return to me, and I shall see that you are rewarded.'","The People of Elthengels","Thane Mildrith of Elthengels needs aid in managing the many pressing issues of her people in the wake of the Orc-assaults.","'There are many people who seek guidance and aid. Seek out Elfwyn the healer, Baldthorne the blacksmith, Adnoth the stable-hand, and Wuscrad the garrison commander. They may all be found within the walls of Elthengels.'","Help Baldthorne, the blacksmith","You have helped Wuscrad with his task","Help Wuscrad, the garrison commander","Help Elfwyn, the healer","You have helped Baldthorne with his task"},
[12783]={"Llega al arroyo con Penny y refréscate. No te dejes atrapar por hobbits parlanchines. ¡Solo te retrasarán!","¡Has frustrado a un hobbit parlanchín!","Reúne los suministros del picnic.","Llega al lugar perfecto para el picnic con Penny. ¡El trébol a lo largo del camino podría distraerla y causar un retraso!","<rgb=#FF0000>¡Oh no! ¡Toda tu comida se ha arruinado!</rgb>","Provisiones de picnic reunidas (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Has recogido zanahorias (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Reúne los suministros del picnic (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Carga a Penny con los suministros del picnic","¡Qué gran día para un picnic!","Disfruta de un maravilloso picnic","'¡Ah, ${PLAYER}! Empezaba a preguntarme dónde te habías metido. Bueno, de todas formas, ¡debería darte las gracias por invitarme! Ahora mejor nos damos prisa. Tenemos un camino por delante - y no demasiado rápido, tampoco, si nos topamos con muchos curiosos en el camino - y me gustaría haber terminado de comer antes del té de la tarde!\
\
'Como puedes ver, he reunido una buena cantidad de cosas. Ahora ayúdame a recogerlas y cargarlas en el poney mientras intento pensar qué falta. ¡Estoy bastante seguro de que estoy olvidando algo de gran importancia!'","El picnic perfecto","Descarga el poney","De alguna manera, las provisiones sobrevivieron al calor, al agua, a los espejismos y al camino sinuoso por la carretera y la colina en perfectas condiciones. Rápidamente, y con hambre, colocas las cosas sobre la manta que el alcalde Pieblanco ha extendido.","Refrescarse en el siguiente punto de agua","'Ahora no dejes caer nada. ¡Rápido, carga el poney con todo eso!'","Habla con Fosco Campolejano","'Si deseas tomar prestada a la vieja Penny para tu picnic, no veo ningún problema con eso. Es de buen carácter y trotará sin problemas si eres amable con ella. Hay zanahorias en el camino que son un buen tentempié para el viaje. ¡Evita el trébol, o se tomará todo el día con ello!\
\
'Asegúrate de que se detenga y se refresque tanto en el arroyo como en el abrevadero en el camino. Quiero que esté sana y fuerte mañana para la recolección de manzanas. Ahora, si me disculpas, ¡hace más calor aquí que en el horno de un Took! ¡No entiendo por qué tú y el Alcalde eligieron hoy para su salida!'","Llega al lugar perfecto para el picnic","Carga tus provisiones en Penny.","¡En camino al lugar del picnic!","<rgb=#FF0000>¡No dejes que tu comida sea devorada por hobbits hambrientos, insectos o arruinada y empapada por la lluvia!</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>Penny ha sucumbido al calor!</rgb>","Haz un picnic en la manta de picnic","'Bueno, vamos, recoge las cosas y cárgalas en el poney mientras pienso. ¡No es fácil recordar lo que has olvidado!'","Llega al punto de agua con Penny y refréscate un poco más.","Elimina el trébol que distrae del camino","¡Delicioso! ¡Encantador! ¡Perfecto!","El picnic se ha salvado. ¡La lluvia incluso refrescó un poco el ambiente!","Cargas cuidadosamente las provisiones del picnic en el poney de Fosco Campolejano y pronto estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]} para partir hacia el lugar del picnic.","Has quitado algo de trébol","Haz un picnic en la manta de picnic.","'Como dije, sé gentil con Penny y ella será buena contigo. ¡Dale zanahorias pero evita los parches de trébol si alguna vez quieres llegar a tu destino!'","Ahuyenta a los hobbits hambrientos con una ligera <rgb=#00ff00>bofetada</rgb>","<rgb=#FF0000>¡Penny no debe sucumbir al calor!</rgb>","Llega al arroyo y refréscate","Frustra a los hobbits parlanchines","Has llegado al lugar del picnic y has encontrado a Will Pieblanco esperándote. ¡Es hora de desempacar las cosas del picnic y preparar el festín!","'¡Ahora eso fue un festín delicioso, y bien vale la pena la aventura! ¡Quizás vayamos a otro picnic pronto!'","¡Has frustrado a un hobbit hambriento!","Habla con Will Pieblanco","Disfruta de un picnic encantador sin una sola interrupción.","Dale algunas zanahorias a Penny","¡Penny está bien alimentada, descansada y lista para la última etapa de la expedición!","Habla con el granjero Fosco Campolejano y el alcalde Will Pieblanco.","Recoge zanahorias para Penny (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Dale algunas zanahorias a Penny."},
[12784]={"El pícnic perfecto - Diario","Completa \\qEl pícnic perfecto\\q","Un pícnic al día - ¡qué mejor manera de pasar el verano!","'Si traes de vuelta a Penny feliz y bien alimentada, te daré una recompensa extra. ¿Qué dices?'","Completado \\qEl pícnic perfecto\\q"},
[12786]={"Tílsa Pasofuerte necesita ayuda para elegir un regalo.","'¿Qué me gusta en un mathom, preguntas? ¡Mientras más pequeño mejor! Cuando tienes tantos amigos y conocidos como yo, terminas con la casa llena de mathoms. Me gusta mantenerlo todo ordenado, así que los mathoms más pequeños ocupan menos espacio, ¡lo que me fastidia menos, también!'","Habla con el cartero Ciervotrébol","'A juzgar por tu atuendo, debes ser una persona de gusto distinguido. ¡Quizá seas la persona apropiada para ayudarme! Estoy aquí para visiar a una amiga. Es la primera vez que me invita a su casa, así que me gustaría llevarle un regalo, un \\qmathom\\q como lo llaman por estos lares. El problema es que no consigo decidir qué regalarle. Me aterra darle un regalo mediocre. ¿Podría preguntar por el pueblo para saber qué entiende la gente por un buen mathom?'","Tílsa Pasofuerte está en las afueras de Campotieso.\
\
Vuelve con Tílsa Pasofuerte.","Pregunta a la gente de Campotieso sobre qué sería un buen mathom.","Habla con Frothard Tuk","'Rojo. Me gustan las cosas rojas.'","El regalo perfecto","Habla con Tílsa Pasofuerte","'¿Un buen mathom? Bueno, cualquier cosa, supongo. Si recibiera un mathom que no me gustase, ¡simplemente se lo daría a otra persona! Personalmente, aun así, me gusta recibir mathoms relacionados con mis aficiones. Los mejores mathoms que he recibido nunca son un martillo, un paquete de gasa y una espada corta.'\
\
...\
\
'Son tres aficiones diferentes, por supuesto.\
\
'¿Por qué preguntas? ¿Me estás ofreciendo algo? Una cuchara nueva de madera sería genial. Perdí la vieja en un 'incidente de molido de grano', como me gusta llamarlos.'","Habla con Henepa Nudotorcido","'Interesante... utensilios de cocina, cosas pequeñas y cosas... ¿rojas? Un tercio de esa información es muy útil.\
\
'Sabes que mi amiga es cervecera, quizá una cuchara de madera podría ser un buen regalo. Oh, ¿y sabes qué? No se me da mal tallar madera. Quizá podría hacerle yo misma una. ¿Es apropiado tallar una cuchara de madera? ¡Supongo que lo averiguaré!\
\
'Gracias por ayudarme. Me alivia tener una dirección que seguir.''"},
[12787]={"El día de la fiesta de Bingo finalmente ha llegado.","Bingo está fuera de su agujero hobbit en Cavada Grande, al norte del Ayuntamiento.\
\
La cena de Bingo fue un éxito rotundo, y desea agradecerte toda tu ayuda.","'Bueno, veamos... todavía tengo algunas cosas que terminar para estar listo, pero quizá lo más sencillo sea que salgas y atiendas a mis invitados.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no puede completarse con una comunidad.</rgb>\
'","La Receta Perfecta","Habla con Bingo fuera de su hogar en Cavada Grande","'¡El gran día finalmente ha llegado, mi ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}! Aún me quedan algunos preparativos para dejar mi hogar presentable para les invitades, ¡pero ya casi está todo listo! Avísame si estás ${PLAYERNAME:dispuesto[m]|dispuesta[f]} a ayudar.'","Habla con Bingo dentro de su agujero hobbit para preparar la fiesta","'Bueno, ${PLAYER}, no sé muy bien qué decir. Hemos pasado por tantas cosas juntos en este viaje... Debo confesar que me entristece ver que llegue a su fin.\
\
'He hecho muchísimas amistades en esta aventura, y creo que la concurrencia a mi fiesta demostró que eran aún más de las que yo mismo imaginaba cuando escribía las invitaciones. Pero ninguna es tan querida para mí como tú, . Eres ${PLAYER:un auténtico[m]|una auténtica[f]}  y ${PLAYER:un amigo[m]|una amiga[f]} leal. ¡Siempre serás ${PLAYER:bienvenido[m]|bienvenida[f]} en mi humilde hogar!\
\
'Debo ocuparme de terminar mi libro y, una vez hecho eso, ¿quién sabe? He probado el sabor de la aventura, y ¿qué es un libro sin una secuela? Oh, solo estaba bromeando, . Bueno... en su mayor parte.\
\
'¡Hasta pronto, mi buen amigo! Volveremos a vernos, y espero con ansias las historias que nos contaremos ese día.\
\
<rgb=#00FF00>Bartolín ha llegado frente al hogar de Bingo en Cavada Grande.</rgb>\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>¡Gracias por jugar La balada de Bingo Boffin!</rgb>","Bingo está dentro de su agujero hobbit en Cavada Grande, al norte del Ayuntamiento."},
[12788]={"Talk to Léothred","'${PLAYER}, what happened? Are you all right?'\
\
You tell Léothred and Fróthi about your vision and how you saw Karazgar befriending Fram for nefarious reasons. This was not the first time that Karazgar's rust had given you a vision of the past!\
\
'This Karazgar that you and Fróthi speak of, he has had his claws in the north for many years, yes? I suspect if he did indeed befriend Fram, his intentions were not honourable!'","Examine the strange rock","The Perilous Pact","The strange rock reminds you of something. It reminds you of the trail of rust left behind by Karazgar. This however is hardened, like a stone. You touch the rust-coloured rock and a suddenly a vision overcomes you.","For Léothred and Fróthi, the truth of how Fram slayed Scatha begins to take form.","Léothred can be found following Fram's map in Elderslade.\
\
You should talk to Léothred.","'There must be a reason the map and the trail of cairns led us here, to this location. We should search the surrounding area again. Perhaps, in exhaustion from our journey, we overlooked something.'","A strange rock can be found near where Fram's map end.\
\
You should examine the strange rock."},
[12789]={"It appears that this Zhélruka died fighting something large.","The path to Stormwall is north-east of Skarháld.\
\
You continue on the path to Stormwall, keeping an eye out for the missing Zhélruka.","Set out on the path to Stormwall","Find the missing Zhélruka (3/4)","This Zhélruka died from many bites","This Zhélruka has been mauled by some beast","The Perilous Path","Five unprepared Zhélruka have set out for Stormwall, against Agátur's dire warnings, in search for the lost realm of Thafar-gathol.","The path to Stormwall is north-east of Skarháld.\
\
You should set out on the path to Stormwall, keeping an eye out for the five Zhélruka.","'You must go after those five Zhélruka, ${PLAYER}. They are fools or, what is their word for it? \\qDraks!\\q But the fate they hurry towards, unprepared as they are, is too harsh a punishment for folly.'","This Zhélruka was burned by something","You see a dwarf up ahead!","Find the missing Zhélruka (${CURRENT}/4)"},
[12792]={"Come tartas (2/6)","Lleno y pegajoso de tarta, ahora deberías hablar con el Maestro de las Tartas.","¡Se acabó el tiempo!","'¿Ya estás ${PLAYERNAME:lleno[m]|llena[f]}? ¡Apenas has comenzado!'","Tartas comidas (6/6)","Tartas comidas (2/6)","Tartas comidas (4/6)","'Bien, bien... casi a mitad de camino.'","'Ah, todavía tienes un poco de tarta en la cara...'","Come tartas (4/6)","Come dos tartas más dentro del tiempo asignado.","Come una tarta más dentro del tiempo asignado.","'¡Esto es bastante perturbador de ver, te lo aseguro!'","Termina antes de que se acabe el tiempo.","Tartas comidas (3/6)","'¡Vamos, a comer! ¡Te estás quedando atrás!'","'¿Vienes por más, eh? Lo siento... solo un premio por concursante.'","Tartas comidas (1/6)","'¡Bien hecho, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}! ¡Te las arreglaste para acabar con esas tartas justo a tiempo!\
\
'Como ganador del concurso de comer tartas, puedes reclamar tu premio. Por supuesto, también tienes un título maravilloso que lo acompaña: ¡${PLAYERNAME:Campeón[m]|Campeona[f]} del concurso de tartas!'","Come tres tartas más dentro del tiempo asignado.","'Bueno, bueno. ¡Si no es el ${PLAYERNAME:campeón[m]|campeona[f]} del concurso de tartas de Bree!'","Come cuatro tartas más dentro del tiempo asignado.","Tartas comidas (5/6)","Come tartas (0/6)","'¡Ya casi terminas! ¡No te molestes en masticar, solo acaba!'","Es hora del concurso de comer tartas en la feria de los Campos de Bree. ¡Vengan todos y disfruten!","Come tartas (5/6)","'Oh, vaya, te ves un poco acalorado. ¿Te sientes mal?'","El concurso de comer tartas","Come cinco tartas más dentro del tiempo asignado.","Come seis tartas más dentro del tiempo asignado.","Come tartas (1/6)","Come tartas (3/6)","'¿Estás aquí para el concurso de comer tartas? ¡Maravilloso! Te explicaré las reglas...\
\
'El objetivo es comer cualquiera de las seis tartas que hay en la mesa. Grandes o pequeñas, no me importa. ¡Pero asegúrate de avisarme cuando termines antes de que se acabe el tiempo!\
\
'¿Quieres comenzar?'","'¡Buen día para ti también!'"},
[12793]={"Albin Cotonorte está en el recinto del mercado de la Granja de Cotonorte.\
\
Albin Cotonorte se alegrará de saber que la hierba para pipa está lista.","'¡Una buena hierba para pipa garantiza un buen mercado!'","'El dulce aroma de la hierba para pipa fresca es casi tan agradable como el olor de un pastel recién horneado... casi.'","'Estamos listos para el mercado. Las tres mezclas tienen un gusto y un sabor excepcionales, y tenemos suficiente para que dure al menos el primer día, ¡suponiendo que no nos lo fumemos todo nosotros primero!\
\
'Ve al recinto del mercado y avisa a Albin Cotonorte de que la hierba para pipa para el mercado ya está lista.'","La hierba para pipa está lista","La hierba para pipa es algo que los hobbits se toman muy en serio. Nadie visitaría un mercado a menos que tuviera un suministro y variedad adecuados.","Habla con Albin Cotonorte"},
[12796]={"Do not leave the Culling Pit or become defeated","Defeat the giant Gethin","The banner is on the arena floor at Avardin in the Starkmoor.\
\
Use the banner to summon forth your first opponents, then defeat them.","'You must have dealt with drakes before. I know of no Dunlending who has stood before them and lived to tell the tale. You impress me.\
\
'Our champion is next. A Dunlending because he decided he wanted to be one and none of us dared to deny him... the giant terror of the hills.\
\
'I hope you have brought your friends. This battle will not be easy.'","Geralht is at the Culling Pit in Avardin.\
\
Geralht will be pleased to discuss your victory.","The Pit -- Battle III","You have failed the Culling Pit battle","'Perhaps the giant was not as great as he claimed....'","The Pit in the Starkmoor serves as a proving ground for conscripts. Those strong enough to withstand it join the army in Wulf's Cleft; those too weak are sent to dig in the mines.","Talk to Geralht at the Culling Pit in Avardin"},
[12797]={"'You have defeated the best that Dunland has to offer, but we are not the only ones who live in these lands.\
\
'Isengard is the greatest power here, and now I fear your accomplishments here have awakened its wrath. Prepare yourself.\
\
'I hope that you have brought your friends. This battle will not be easy.'","'I must say that I am impressed, indeed.'","Do not leave the Culling Pit or become defeated","The banner is on the arena floor at Avardin in the Starkmoor.\
\
Use the banner to summon forth your first opponents, then defeat them.","Geralht is at the Culling Pit in Avardin.\
\
Geralht will be pleased to discuss your victory.","The Pit -- Battle IV","You have failed the Culling Pit battle","The Pit in the Starkmoor serves as a proving ground for conscripts. Those strong enough to withstand it join the army in Wulf's Cleft; those too weak are sent to dig in the mines.","Defeat the forces from Isengard","Talk to Geralht at the Culling Pit in Avardin"},
[12798]={"You should see if you can discover any sign of Ondor the Dwarf near the entrance to the Pit of Iron in the north-east Heathfells.","'Oh, there was one other thing - one of my men spotted a dwarf heading into a cave north-east of here.\
\
'We think that may be where the Orcs around here have been coming from, but we haven't been able to spare any men to check it out. You may want to take a look around....'","El foso de hierro","You spot something lying next to the cave entrance...","Find some sign of Ondor","Captain Féarn mentioned that one of his men spotted a dwarf poking around the entrance to a cave north-east of Dol Baran. From the description it sounds like it might have been Ondor.\
\
Knowing how excitable Ondor can be, there's a fair chance he's gotten himself in some sort of trouble up there, and it might be a good idea to scout out the entrance to that cave."},
[12799]={"Talk to Molkha","You have located the hobgoblin fort in the Pit of Stonejaws.\
\
You should talk to Scout-master Ausma in Bárgstad.","'You must be ${PLAYER}! I have heard a great deal about you! I am Kyrstig of the Longbeards. I am eager to fight beside such a renowned ${CLASS}!'","The Pit of Stonejaws","Talk to Kyrstig","Scout-master Ausma has asked you to introduce yourself to her apprentices.\
\
You should talk to Kyrstig, Molkha, and Klúso in Bárgstad.","'Welcome to the Pit of Stonejaws, ${PLAYER}. We have reason to believe that the hobgoblin seat of power lies within these jagged caverns. We also believe that their leader, Warlord Dushtalbúk, and his advisors are currently here, holed up in their fort to avoid the growing unrest between the enemy forces.\
\
'Our mission here is to locate their fort, discover the scope of their power, and if we are very fortunate indeed, slay the warlord himself. The timing is vital. If we can remove Dushtalbúk from the table before the hobgoblins and Orcs reconcile their differences, they may be unable to organize again before we deal a decisive blow and win this war. \
\
'Because of this mission's importance, Prince Durin has personally asked me to oversee it. You, ${PLAYER}, will also be instrumental in our success. I have not come alone, however. I have taken on three apprentices that I would like you to meet. I have been teaching them the ways of stealth and of the dagger. Go, introduce yourself. I expect they will be excited to meet you, for they have heard tell of your exploits!'","'So you are ${PLAYER}? I am Klúso of the Stout-axe clan! Ausma has told me much of your skills. I look forward to seeing them in action myself!'","Find Shakhajât","Talk to Scout-master Ausma","'${PLAYER}, was it? I am Molkha of the Zhélruka. The others seem quite excited to work with you. If your presence betters our chance of surviving this dangerous mission, I suppose I am pleased as well!'","Help Scout-master Ausma with \\qJust a Warm-up\\q","Somewhere in the heart of the Stonejaws is the hobgoblin fort Shakhajât.\
\
You should find Shakhajât and help Ausma with \\qJust a Warm-up\\q.","Scout-master Ausma and her apprentices have arrived in the Pit of Stonejaws to investigate the hobgoblins' seat of power.","Talk to Klúso","'All warmed up, ${PLAYER}? What do you have to report?'\
\
You tell Ausma that Shakhajât lies at the centre of the Pit of Stonejaws, little more than a dagger's throw from Bárgstad.\
\
'Good work. Now for the next step: locating our warlord.'","A large Orc-fort lies before you. This must be Shakhajât","Now that you have met the new scouts, you should decide upon your course of action in the Pit of Stonejaws.\
\
You should talk to Scout-master Ausma in Bárgstad.","'My apprentices are an interesting assortment, to be sure. They show promise but lack experience, which I hope to correct during this mission. But enough of the pleasantries. We have work to do.\
\
'We arrived only slightly ahead of you, giving us the time to make camp but little else. Our next step is reconnaissance. I will send you and those three out into the caves to scout different areas of the Stonejaws. Your first mission is this: find the hobgoblin fortress known as Shakhajât. Do not stray too near, lest you ruin the advantage of our surprise!'"},
[12801]={"You should talk to Párgrub.","'This is it! Are you ready, strong ${RACE}?'","Now that you have been entered into the pit-fighting tournament, you should show these Orcs what you can do!","Párgrub can be found near Thorzhaf.\
\
You should speak with Párgrub about the match.","Talk to Párgrub","'Oh no, Párgrub ruined. Bet against you every time. Thought you would die a horrible death, Párgrub did. Now you win every fight and Párgrub have nothing. Such failure.\
\
'At least other Orcs think you work for Párgrub now. Maybe you come back and fight again sometime and this poor snaga will bet on you for once!'","The Pit-fighter -- Day Three","'Now it's the last fight. Párgrub has only one chance left to bet big. All this poor snaga's supplies but the bucket of armour scrap will go! You will, err, win for me, yes?'"},
[12803]={"Hasta se encuentra en la Bodega Putrefacta, en las Obras Hidráulicas de Moria.\
\
Debes hablar con Hasta para descubrir qué necesitará para preparar un señuelo destinado a la criatura que hay detrás de los inquietantes rumores.","Habla con Hasta","'Hethuwen examinó más detenidamente la muestra que reuniste antes y encontró resultados inquietantes. ¡Por lo visto, la fuente de la sustancia es una criatura viva!\
\
'Si esa criatura continúa existiendo, sin duda pondrá en peligro los esfuerzos de los resistentes enanos aquí en las Obras Hidráulicas, y quizá en toda Moria. Tengo un plan, ${PLAYER}, que sin duda nos ayudará, pero llevará algo de tiempo ponerlo en marcha.\
\
'Atraeremos a la criatura fuera de su escondite, y tengo razones para creer que será muy grande. Se necesitará una gran cantidad de ingredientes para preparar un señuelo que resulte lo bastante apetitoso. Háblame de nuevo y te diré lo que necesitaré. Oh, y... corre la voz entre tus amigas y amigos que puedan ayudarte. Vamos a necesitar muchísimos ingredientes.'","'Excelente; bien, empecemos. Hay mucho que hacer y muchos elementos que preparar.'","Hasta te ha informado de sus planes para enfrentarse a la misteriosa criatura que se oculta tras los desagradables rumores en las Obras Hidráulicas.","El Plan"},
[12805]={"'We rarely receive visitors of any sort in Limlók. Hertha visits from time to time, when she is not guarding the pass, but she grew up here and this is her home. Now then, what of Hunulf? He left here against my better judgment.\
\
'I see, I am saddened to hear of his passing. His companion Vaskorn is still here in Limlók, resting from his wounds. He will recover. You should speak with him, by the well.'","Vaskorn can be found at Limlók in the Floodfells.\
\
You should talk to Vaskorn.","Talk to Runerik Knotbeard in Limlók","Limlók, the last northern settlement of the Beornings, could fall to the forces of Gundabad at any moment.","Talk to Vaskorn in Limlók","'${PLAYER}, is that you? Yes, I was attacked by a Warg-rider on my journey from the Thornholt to Limlók. I will recover in time. Is it true that Hunulf is dead? If only I could have made that journey with him, he would still be alive. Poor Hunulf, a true friend.\
\
'I am glad that Hunulf was able to warn you about what we have seen. It has grown ever dire in the Thornholt. Fiskvat, that fool, refused to leave with us. He stayed behind due to his stubbornness and love for the Thornholt honey! I fear he will likely perish. Threkmóth the elder sadly died on our journey to Limlók. He was slain by the Taurogrim. The Taurogrim have been greatly angered by recent events. I believe the intrusion of the Orcs of Gundabad and purifying of the woods by the Elves has pushed them into an absolute frenzy.\
\
'Oh and ${PLAYER}, you can trust the dwarves here. They saved my life multiple times on our journey. Perhaps you know them from your time in Ered Mithrin?'","Runerik Knotbeard can be found in Limlók.\
\
You should talk to Runerik Knotbeard.","'Now then, I hope you are a fighter. The Orc assaults would not be much trouble for Limlók, were it not for the additional Warg attacks. Limlók will fall soon if something is not done.\
\
'I will not be making your stay a comfortable one, for Grimbeorn has sent you to assist us. And assist us you shall.'","The Plight of Limlók"},
[12806]={"The final vessel can be found upon the bridge to Eithel Gwaur in Rath Dúath.\
\
You should pour water into the vessel for Rauniel.","Rauniel can be found upon the bridge to Eithel Gwaur in Rath Dúath.\
\
You should talk to Rauniel.","The Plight of Rauniel","Retrieved an urn","Foulness is purged from the vessel as you pour the water into it","The urn Rauniel seeks can be found at Shakam Moz in the hills of eastern Rath Dúath.\
\
You should retrieve the urn for Rauniel.","Retrieve the urn from Shakam Moz","Talk to Rauniel upon the bridge to Eithel Gwaur","Pour water into a vessel upon the bridge to Eithel Gwaur","'Noble ${RACE}, there is but one more ward on the far side of the bridge. The urn you seek has been recently taken by merrevail, but they know nothing of the urn's significance. Scale the eastern peak and retrieve the final urn. We have come this far, have we not? I have no one else to assist in my freedom. You must seek out the final urn.'","'Again you are successful? I did not think you possessed such resolve, fair ${CLASS}. I am glad you are the one to rescue me. Still, there is more to be done before I am able to escape my bonds.'","Rauniel, the maiden of the Ithilduin, needs your assistance in destroying the wards that block her escape from a treacherous prison."},
[12807]={"Cure poisoned foxes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cure poisoned rabbits (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cure poisoned squirrels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cure poisoned frogs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cured poisoned squirrels (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Completado.","Cure poisoned birds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Plight of the Innocent","Poisoned animals can be found north of the path in Eryn Lasgalen.\
\
You should cure animals poisoned by the Taurogrim.","The animals of the forest have fallen victim to the vile poison of the Taurogrim.","Cured poisoned frogs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Cured poisoned birds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The Taurogrim have returned and again they threaten the beasts of Eryn Lasgalen with their vile poisons. As you well know, Thorlind has crafted a draught to counteract their poisons.\
\
'We do not have much to spare, but I would ask that you offer it to any creatures suffering the Taurogrim's poison.'","Cured poisoned foxes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Completado","As Thranduil expected, Thorlind's cure has continued to prove effective in curing the many sickened animals tainted by the Taurogrim in Eryn Lasgalen.","Cured poisoned rabbits (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12808]={"'There is but one way to solve the mystery of who these people are, and that is to speak with them. Let us approach with caution and greet them with kindness, and see what comes of it. Go on, I will be right behind you.'","Talk to Faeron","Talk to the guard","Talk to Nabatínu","Faeron has offered to assist the Jatsakóri and will meet you back at the Rangers' camp south of Gadim-ûn. You should go to the Ranger camp and talk to Rhadrog.","The Plight of the Játsakori","'And who are you, strangers, who traverse this land without fear? You are no Ordâkhai, and this one is a Man of the West who makes no effort to hide his origin. If you are enemies of Ordâkh, know that you are among friends.\
\
'If your heading is further west, then I must caution against it. Only death and danger lie in that direction.'","'You surmise correctly that we are enemies of Ordâkh. We are capable warriors, however, and would travel west no matter the danger, should our business take us there. It was only a short time ago that we were in the cursed land of Mordor. I have my doubts that An Shêru has more danger to offer than the very lair of the Enemy.\
\
'Tell me more of this danger to the west. I search for signs of an evil blight infecting the land, covering it in rot and sickness.'","Nabatínu, who leads the people inside Gadim-ûn, a place in north-eastern An Shêru, has identified himself as an enemy of Ordâkh, and recommends against going any further west into An Shêru. You should talk to Faeron about what Nabatínu has said.","Faeron suggested talking to these people to learn more about them. You should talk to the guard at Gadim-ûn, a place in north-eastern An Shêru.","Talk to Rhadrog at his camp","The guard has directed you to speak with his leader, Nabatínu, inside Gadim-ûn, a place in north-eastern An Shêru.","Nabatínu has told you that he and the others here were once thralls of the Ordâkhai and have now found their freedom. They work to free the others still bound in thralldom. You should discuss the situation with Faeron.","Faeron has asked Nabatínu, leader of the people inside Gadim-ûn in north-eastern An Shêru, if he knows of any areas of blight in An Shêru. You should talk to Nabatínu to hear his answer.","Following tracks in the sand has led you to a group of unknown people.","'Alas, no, there is not enough life remaining in An Shêru for such rot to take hold. No, the danger I speak of comes in the form of a new breed of Orc, with size and strength unlike any other I have known. They patrol the roads, killing any they come across, though they often take some prisoner. I shudder to think what becomes of those poor souls.\
\
'There are also two strongholds of Ordâkhai of an unusual sort. They are zealots who do not believe Barkhûsh is truly defeated. They continue to worship him and believe that upon his return, he will reward their loyalty with power untold. They are fools, but are dangerous fools. They are led by a coven of Bokhór, witches with the power to ensnare Men's will.\
\
'In fact...'\
\
The man looks around at his fellows, dirty and hungry, living uncomfortably within a crypt.\
\
'We were all once such thralls. Játsakori, we were called. Our wills were taken from us, and we were forced to work in mines for the Ordâkhai. I was able to break my mind free from their spell at the moment Barkhûsh was defeated, as the casters of the spell suffered a moment of weakness. I was able to escape, and since then, I have been helping as many people as I can break free from thralldom.\
\
'Many have left to seek life and healing elsewhere, but those of us who remain do so intending to free the others. We have found the last of our number increasingly difficult to save. Their minds are bound tightly with the evil magic.'","'Ah, you return. I was just talking to Faeron. It seems we came here looking for one foulness only to find another. I agree that something must be done. It's time to break camp.'","Faeron turns to you, looking deeply concerned.\
\
'I don't like this, ${PLAYER}. These people need our help. Let's return to camp and speak with Rhadrog.'\
\
He turns back to face Nabatínu.\
\
'We must return to two of our company, camped to the south. With your permission, I would like to bring them here, and together we will do what we can to help you. You aren't the only ones who have been forced into labour by evil. King Elessar did not leave the Nurnhoth or the Stout-axes to suffer, and I would not leave yours, if I can help it.'\
\
Nabatínu nods his consent.\
\
'Good. ${PLAYER}, I will meet you back at the camp.'","'Who... who are you?'\
\
The man nervously grips his weapon, but does not threaten you with it. You tell him that you are travellers and are curious about them.\
\
'There is no such thing as a traveller who just happens to be passing through here. But I think you should speak to our leader, Nabatínu. You will find him within.'"},
[12809]={"Halson Fondocuba, posadero de El Arado y las Estrellas, participa en la fiesta de fabricación de cerveza de las Cuatro Cuadernas.","'¿Has recuperado el yeso de esos trasgos ya?'","Wilcome Tunelero está en Scary, al este de Tejonera. La posada El Arado y las Estrellas está en Tejonera, al oeste de Scary.\
\
Halson Fondocuba, de El Arado y las Estrellas, te ha enviado a Scary para buscar un envío de yeso que se ha extraviado.","'¿Tuviste que enfrentarte a trasgos por ese yeso? ¡Has superado mis expectativas, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}! ¡Te mereces una cerveza de la casa por eso!'","'¿Oh, trasgos se han llevado mi yeso? Eso es malo. Muy malo. No supongo que puedas recuperarlo de ellos, ¿verdad?'","'¿Podrías ir a Scary para hablar con Wilcome sobre ese yeso?'","Los trasgos que robaron la carreta que transportaba el yeso venían de los Valles Rasgados, al norte de Tejonera.\
\
Parece que los trasgos se han apoderado del yeso destinado a El Arado y las Estrellas. Deberías viajar a su campamento y buscar la carreta perdida.","'¿Vienes de parte de Halson? Tengo una historia triste que contar, así que más vale que sea a ti.\
\
'Envié a uno de mis hombres a la posada El Arado con una carreta para llevarle el yeso a Halson y traer unos barriles por aquí, pero volvió en pánico.\
\
'Al parecer, fue emboscado por trasgos justo cuando estaba a punto de llegar a Tejonera. ¡Imagínate, trasgos en la Comarca! Tuvo que abandonar la carreta y apenas logró escapar. Se lo conté a uno de los Fronteros de aquí, pero aún no han hecho nada.\
\
'Tal vez si encuentras a esos trasgos por la zona de Tejonera, también puedas encontrar la carreta que transportaba el yeso. Mi hombre dice que los trasgos parecían venir del norte, por si eso te sirve de algo.'","'¡Bienvenido a El Arado y las Estrellas! ¡Pasa un rato con nosotros y relájate! ¡Prueba nuestra famosa cerveza negra de los Wooly-foot!\
\
'¿Verdad que está buena? Pero déjame contarte, tengo un problema con la fabricación de cerveza con el que podrías ayudarme. Se acerca la fiesta de fabricación de cerveza de las Cuatro Cuadernas, y quiero preparar mi mejor cerveza negra de los Wooly-foot para el concurso. Pero verás, ¡necesito mi ingrediente secreto! Utilizo yeso en polvo para quitarle el sabor amargo a la cerveza.\
\
'Normalmente lo pido en la cantera de Scary, no muy lejos de aquí al este, pero no ha llegado. ¿Podrías ir a Scary y preguntarle al viejo Wilcome Tunnely qué ha pasado? ¡Te lo agradecería mucho!'","Recogido el yeso en polvo","Recoge el yeso en polvo","El Arado y las Estrellas","Lleva el yeso a Halson Fondocuba"},
[12810]={"'Veo que has fracasado en Kheledûl...'","El puerto saqueado","'¡La muerte de Gellir ha sido vengada y hemos recuperado nuestro tesoro! ¡Tu nombre vivirá en nuestras canciones!'","'Has apaciguado la memoria de mi hermano, ${PLAYER}. Gracias.'","'¡Muy bien hecho! Creo que mi hermano estaría satisfecho con este precio de sangre. Enviaré estos tesoros a la Mansión de Thorin, y quizás podamos usarlos para derrotar a los Duramano de una vez por todas!'","Cajas de tesoro recuperadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Las cajas de tesoro se encuentran en el puerto fluvial de Kheledûl, al este de Gondamon.\
\
Askell ha ideado un nuevo plan para castigar a los Duramano por la muerte de Gellir. Te Ha pedido que asaltes la ciudad portuaria de kheledûl Y recuperes las cajas de tesoro robadas a los barbiluengos por los Duramano.","Lleva las cajas de tesoro a Askell","Recoge cajas de tesoro (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Aunque nosotros, los barbiluengos, pudimos expulsar a los Duramano de la mayoría de nuestras granjas después de que revelaran su verdadera naturaleza malvada hace dos años, todavía son demasiado fuertes para que podamos enfrentarnos a ellos en el campo.\
\
El último bastión importante de los Duramano en ered luin es el puerto fluvial de kheledûl. es en Kheledûl donde Se concentra gran parte de su fuerza restante, y es en kheledûl donde Almacenan sus riquezas robadas, los tesoros que nos arrebataron durante los largos años de su tiranía en la Mansión de Thorin.\
\
Has demostrado ser ${PLAYERNAME:un guerrero capaz y un verdadero amigo[m]|una guerrera capaz y una verdadera amiga[f]}. si puedes Asaltar kheledûl y recuperar los tesoros robados, no solo estarás dando un golpe por el pueblo de Durin, sino que también estarás dando un duro golpe en nombre de mi hermano.'","Insatisfecho con la muerte de los Duramano que mataron a su hermano, askell Quiere ahora perjudicar aún más a los Duramano Recuperando sus tesoros robados."},
[12812]={"Talk to Doron","Cabed hopes that the Easterling-blade and the red-tipped arrow will force action to be taken against the inhabitants of Ost Celebrant.","Idmar is horrified that an Easterling lurks in Parth Celebrant and demands that you speak with Doron","Talk to Idmar","'I have done all that I can to aid you. This arrowhead and blade should be all you need to spur your allies to action. If it does not, I fear the field will again fall to the enemies of Gondor.\
\
'Take this to them with haste, each moment you do not act only gives the enemy more time to prepare.\
\
'Consider my duty fulfilled, even if my spirit remains. Farewell.'","'Was Cabed willing to aid you? I know he despises me for my actions, but as you know, I only did what I thought was best....\
\
'What is this? Why have you brought the blade of my enemy here? Tell me at once!\
\
'So, an Easterling has invaded our ruins. I will not fall victim to the same folly twice, ${PLAYER}. Journey to Ost Celebrant with me, and together, we will drive him from this land.\
\
'There is no time to wait for your allies, you must go now, before it is too late. I will meet you at the gates, make haste!'","'Take these items to Idmar and Doron.'","'Take this item to Doron.'","'You have returned...I was beginning to worry. You were gone for some time...what is that you are carrying?'\
\
Idmar glances with wonder at the red-tipped arrowhead, but then suddenly notices the blade you hold.\
\
'This arrowhead is very important to my people, and I will have it sent to Stangard. It must be hung in the mead-hall to honour our ancestors' service. But...where did you get that blade? Speak quickly.\
\
Idmar looks deeply disturbed after learning that it was just outside Ost Celebrant.\
\
'This is unsettling news, ${PLAYER}. Bring this blade to Doron, immediately. I will muster my men and hope that we receive more support from Stangard. Go now!'","The Point of It All","Idmar is at his camp along the road in central Parth Celebrant.\
\
You should bring the items to Idmar.","Doron is among his men on the crest of the hill in western Parth Celebrant.\
\
Idmar wants you to speak with Doron regarding the Easterling."},
[12813]={"Feed Spearflower to one of the goats in Imloth Melui","Talk to Brunil in the Hall of the Gentle Hand","Feed Dusk-flower to one of the goats in Imloth Melui","'Ah, one of the ingredients disagreed with the constitution of our goat? Which component was to blame, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'The Maresfoot? I see. That is delivered daily! I think we may be closing in on our culprit.'","'I do not question the efficacy of your search, ${PLAYER}! I think the true problem here is that our sneak must be even more stealthy than I supposed!\
\
'I think perhaps I have gotten ahead of myself. We need to ask the right questions, and I think we should start with the most basic one of all. If I wanted to poison that healing draught, how would I go about doing it? Why, I would taint one of the components that goes into it!\
\
'I have collected the ingredients that go into the mixture, and I give them to you. Will you take them to the field beneath the long stairs, in the northern area of town, and feed them to the goats there, one by one? I think the goats will tell us if one of these ingredients is tainted.'","The goat did not enjoy the Maresfoot! Is this ingredient to blame?","The goat readily eats the herb out of your hand. You watch it closely after it's done.","The goat stares at you blandly.","The Poison Test","Brunil can be found in the Hall of the Gentle Hand, on the western side of Imloth Melui.\
\
You fed all the ingredients in the draught to the goats, and the Maresfoot seemed to be disagreeable. You should return to Brunil with what you have learned.","Feed Maresfoot to one of the goats in Imloth Melui","The goats can be found north-east of the Hall of the Gentle Hand, at the bottom of the long stairs.\
\
Brunil has asked you to feed each ingredient in the healing draught to a goat, one after another.","Brunil has isolated the ingredients in the medicine that worsened the condition of her patients, and she thinks one of them might be poisoned.","The goat stares at you for a moment, but you are unable to hold its attention."},
[12814]={"The Poison's Cure","The poisoned patients can be found throughout the Hall of the Gentle Hand in Imloth Melui.\
\
You should administer the compounded cure to the patients who drank the poison.","Talk to Brunil in the Hall of the Gentle Hand","'We need to act quickly if we are to save those who drank from the tainted healing draught. A high concentration of Beruthiel's Rue has only one cure, but they are fortunate that I know where to find it!\
\
'Beruthiel's Rue can be countered with a mixture made primarily of Dewleaf, which can be found on the bluff above the River Erui, to the south-west of the town's entrance. Pick as much Dewleaf as you can and return to me with haste!'","Bubbles form in the cure as you add the Dewleaf to the mixture","'You have finished delivering the cure to my patients? You have the healer's touch, ${PLAYER}, and I am delighted to tell you so! I am certain that you reached everyone in time, and have reversed the harm caused by Egind's folly. You have my thanks, and his as well, I am sure.\
\
'But there is no time to rest! Merenir came here to find you, for he has a troubling report.'","Gave the cure to a patient (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","The healer's workbench is right by Brunil in the Hall of the Gentle Hand. It is where she makes all of her medicines.\
\
Brunil has prepared the cure, and it will be complete once you add the Dewleaf. The cure waits for you on the healer's workbench.","Return to Brunil in the Hall of the Gentle Hand","Brunil wants you to hurry and help her cure the patients that drank the tainted healing draught.","Collected Dewleaf (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I have troubling news to report, ${PLAYER}, and I came to seek you at once!'","Merenir has come to the Hall of the Gentle Hand with a troubling report.","Brunil can be found in the Hall of the Gentle Hand, in Imloth Melui.\
\
You should tell Brunil that the cure has been administered to all the poisoned patients.","Talk to Merenir in the Hall of the Gentle Hand","Brunil can be found in the Hall of the Gentle Hand, on the western side of Imloth Melui.\
\
You have collected as much Dewleaf as you could find, and should bring it to Brunil.","Dewleaf can be found on the bluff above River Erui, south-west of the entrance to Imloth Melui.\
\
Brunil has asked you to fetch as much Dewleaf as you can in order to counteract the poison her patients consumed.","Administer the cure to sick patients (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","'You have returned, and with impressive haste! Very good, ${PLAYER}! I have prepared the mixture, and it waits now for the Dewleaf you collected. Make use of the healer's workbench here and the cure will be ready!'","Add the Dewleaf to the cure at the healer's workbench in the Hall of the Gentle Hand","'Orcs, ${PLAYER}! Orcs!'","Collect Dewleaf south-west of Imloth Melui (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12816]={"Los Hombres de Bree desean ayudar a los hobbits en su concurso anual de pesca permitiendo a los pescadores capturar peces del estanque junto a la granja.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando finalice el festival actual.</rgb>","Atrapa tantos peces como puedas en veinte minutos.","'No deberías demorarte demasiado aquí, ${PLAYER}, ¡pues tu tiempo ya se está agotando! Buena suerte.'","El estanque de pesca se encuentra al este de la granja de Andrath.\
\
Will Marjacierva te ha pedido que captures peces para el Festival del Lithe de los hobbits.","'¡Qué día tan hermoso! Las flores están en plena floración, las abejas zumban por todas partes, hay toda clase de criaturas correteando y los peces están en su mejor momento. Deberías atrapar algunos para el Festival del Lithe.\
\
'Fui el año pasado y lo único que tenían eran peces de los enanos. ¡Fue terrible! Demasiado duros… no se podía masticar nada. ¡Nuestros peces son los mejores, aquí mismo, en Bree!\
\
'Los mejores peces se encuentran en este mismo estanque. Estoy seguro de que los granjeros te dejarán pescar aquí durante un tiempo.'","El estanque"},
[12817]={"Himril takes full account of all the materials you delivered.\
\
'Many thanks, traveller.\
\
'This should account for the missing materials from my ledger. You may go on your way.'","Building materials collected (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","All of these building materials should account for what is missing from Himril's records. You should return to Himril.\
\
Himril is in Imloth Melui.","Talk to Himril","'Greeting, traveller. Welcome to Imloth Melui.'\
\
She files through papers, showing you little concern.\
\
'I am surveying the land, and the damage done to it is spread far and wide from here to Pelargir.\
\
'We seem to be missing a few crates of building materials. If you are keen to lend your aid, could you perhaps visit Arnach to the south and see if there are any materials that have been left behind?\
\
'Our efforts to restore Gondor are vast, and a few items being unaccounted for is nothing new.'","The Power to Rebuild","An Elf surveys building materials in an effort to hasten the progress with which the land is restored.","Collect building materials (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Himril has asked you to travel to Arnach to the south and search for building materials."},
[12818]={"Find and challenge Sors,  Eiviona, or Owein","You have beaten the experienced Dunlending fighter","Mair is by a large rock in the northern half of the village of Tûr Morva in Tâl Methedras.\
\
You have defeated an experienced fighter of the Falcon-clan and should return to Mair.","'Many clans have joined with Saruman, ${PLAYER}, and the Hebog-lûth may need to face them before it is all over. We need every advantage we can get, and my father the Brenin thinks that you and your Ranger friends are just such an advantage.'\
\
Mair assesses you shrewdly.\
\
'I am not so certain. Are there any fighting skills in the North worth knowing? Find some of our most youthful fighters and challenge them to combat. That will tell me if my father is right to think so highly of your skills. I speak of Yevan, Olwen, or Wundod. If you cannot defeat any of those youths in combat, you have nothing to teach us.'","Mair has asked you to teach the warriors of the Falcon-clan fighting skills from the North.","'Can you defeat one of our more experienced fighters? Seek out and challenge Sors, Eiviona, or Owein, here in Tûr Morva. They will be more of a challenge, I trust.'","'Well now, perhaps you do have things to teach us in the ways of combat. I am listening.'","You have beaten the youthful Dunlending fighter","Talk to Mair in Tûr Morva","'Your defeat of the youth proves little, ${PLAYER}, but it does prove this: you have some small skill in combat. More than one of our unskilled youths, at the least.'\
\
Mair studies you appraisingly.\
\
'How will you handle one of our more experienced fighters, I wonder? Seek out and challenge Sors, Eiviona, or Owein here in Tûr Morva. They will be more of a challenge, I trust.'","'Defeating Yevan, Olwen, or Wundod will tell me if my father is right to believe that you have anything to teach us in the ways of warfare. They are youthful and inexperienced.'","'Mair expects us to fight? I am not afraid of you! I will show you the strength of the Hebog-lûth, though I be but a fledgling in the art of combat!'","Mair is by a large rock in the northern half of the village of Tûr Morva in Tâl Methedras.\
\
You have easily defeated a youthful fighter of the Falcon-clan and should return to Mair.","Find and challenge Yevan, Olwen, or Wundod","'Do you think that you can defeat me? I have seen service in war, Duvodiad. I am not a fresh-faced youngling untested by combat. Prepare yourself!'","'I am no fighter, I am a singer of songs! I am not the Olwen you want! You are looking for my sister, I think. She is outside our home, to the north, near Penrod.\
\
'Do not worry, it happens a lot. I do not know what Mother was thinking.'","Yevan, Olwen, and Wundod can be found in Tûr Morva.\
\
Mair has challenged you to defeat one of the youthful fighters of the Falcon-clan in combat.","Sors, Eiviona, and Owein can be found somewhere in Tûr Morva.\
\
Mair has challenged you to defeat one of the more accomplished fighters of the Falcon-clan in Tûr Morva.","The Practiced Arm"},
[12819]={"Defeat Celebrant relic-thieves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'You should return to your captain, Idmar.'","Defeated Celebrant brigands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Drive the brigands from Parth Celebrant, ${PLAYER}.'","Defeated Celebrant relic-thieves (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Before you go, I have one more thing to ask of you. I have sent you to request the aid of the Horse-lords. Should they fail to move against these invaders, I demand that action be taken.\
\
'These wicked Men have invaded our land, and such indifference to their occupation is intolerable. Travel to the south and find them in their camp. Give them no quarter....'","Talk to Idmar","Defeat Celebrant brigands (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Price They Pay","Defeated Celebrant archers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Celebrant archers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Doron is concerned that no action will be taken against the brigands which rob the Field of Celebrant and has implored you to defeat many of the wicked Men.","The brigands have gathered to the south inside of a large camp known as Hordfierd.\
\
Doron has asked you to defeat many of the brigands which have invaded Parth Celebrant.","'It goes without my saying, but thank you for ridding us of those brigands. It is most unusual that an Oathbreaker would ask you to take action against anyone, much less someone deserving of our ire.\
\
'Our work is not yet finished...we must make the Field clear of these thieving roustabouts.'","Idmar is at his camp along the road in central Parth Celebrant.\
\
Doron sent you to speak with Idmar, following your attack upon the brigands."},
[12820]={"Mientras la vil hechicería del Señor Oscuro eleva Barad-dûr cada vez más sobre las tierras de Mordor, terribles temblores han desprendido las piedras de la Torre Oscura.","Rompe los escombros caídos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Estás destinado a servir mediante el trabajo al Señor Oscuro.","Se pueden encontrar escombros caídos por todas las mazmorras de Barad-dûr.","El precio del progreso"},
[12822]={"'${PLAYER}, it is good to see you. Tell me, how is Ningêna? I am happy that things are progressing at Sûru.\
\
'I must confess, I have a problem for which I hope to gain your assistance. We have a prisoner by the name of Khûldim. He was once the Umûn, the Lord here, sent by the Empire of Ordâkh to keep the Ambarûli under their evil thumb. He was responsible for much suffering.'\
\
Girhâzi clenches her teeth, visibly still angry about things this man has done.\
\
'The pashâg surrendered to us instead of fighting, and now we are stuck deciding what to do with him. Some want him executed for his crimes. Others think we should ransom him to the Ordâkhai, as surely he comes from a rich family.\
\
'Amâsu thinks he may have a use, though. She believes he may have information for which we have been looking, but so far, we have learned nothing from him. You should talk to Amâsu though, she can explain better than I.'","Talk to Khûldim Umûn","The Prisoner Problem","Talk to Girhâzi","'How dare he insult our food!'\
\
She rubs her chin thoughtfully.\
\
'He expects to be tortured, does he? I have an idea.'","You have found the prisoner, Khûldim Umûn","'Ah yes, Khûldim Umûn.'\
\
Amâsu spits out his name like just saying it befouls her tongue.\
\
'That man has a corrupted heart and is... was, a steadfast follower of the One Who Sees All. I weep for his mother, who must live knowing that this heartless creature is what her child became. But I am nonetheless glad the Dumûri gave him mercy, as I believe he uncovered a secret during his time as overseer, and I would have him tell it to us.'\
\
The old woman clears her throat and her demeanor shifts into that of a teacher.\
\
'Throughout the majority of Ambarûl's history, we have been ruled over by invaders from foreign lands. Our land is valuable for its fertility, and we are too few to be able to field an army large enough to defend ourselves. The Empire of Ordâkh is only the latest in a long history of tyrants.\
\
'One thing that the Ordâkhai did that the others did not was forbid the teaching of reading and writing to any Ambarûli. With knowledge comes power, and they wanted to deny us that. When we lost our literacy, we lost our history and our culture. The Old Way was forgotten and we have become a people who does not truly know who we are.\
\
'Not all literacy was lost, however. When this was first enacted, a woman swore an oath that she would teach another of a younger generation, in secret, so that all would not be forgotten. This oath has been passed on to me, and I have passed it to Girhâzi. What has also been passed on is the tale of the Dubarâkh, a hidden library where the books telling the stories of our people have been saved. Unfortunately, the location of this library has been lost to time.\
\
'I believe that during his time as overseer, Khûldim learned the location of the Dubarâkh. It is vital to the survival of our culture that it is found. This is the only lead we have. Please, speak to Khûldim and see what you can learn. He is held here in the lodge.'","Amâsu has told you that she believes Khûldim Umûn knows the location of the Dubarâkh, a hidden library archiving the history and culture of the Ambarûli people. You have talked to the prisoner and should now return to Girhâzi.","Talk to Amâsu","Girhâzi has asked you to speak to Amâsu about the prisoner.","Girhâzi has asked for your help in dealing with an Ordâkhai prisoner, the former overseer of Ambarûl, Khûldim Umûn.","Amâsu has told you that she believes Khûldim Umûn knows the location of the Dubarâkh, a hidden library archiving the history and culture of the Ambarûli people. She has asked you to talk to the prisoner in the cell on the west side of the lodge and see what you can learn.","Find where the prisoner is held","'What is this, a visitor? Introduce yourself, stranger. Who are you, and why are you here?'\
\
You give him your name and tell him you came to question him. He leers at you for a moment and then begins to laugh.\
\
'You are a fool, ${PLAYER}, sent on a fools' errand. Why should I tell anyone anything? My secrets are keeping me alive. If I tell you what I know, these people will lose the only reason they have to not execute me. All I have to do is keep my mouth shut and await rescue.'\
\
Khûldim leans closer and sneers at you.\
\
'You know, where I come from a man in my position would be properly tortured. Instead, you torture me with your poor company and mildly unpleasant food. You are all weak and pathetic.'\
\
You inform him that nobody is coming to rescue him and take your leave."},
[12823]={"Use the horn to draw Dargum's attention and defeat Grazadh","The Nink-hai leader can be found at the end of the mountain pass in the mountains.\
\
Langfrith has asked you to infiltrate the Orc camp and defeat the leader of the tribe.","The Prisoner Returns","You have defeated Grazadh, but Dargum has escaped","'It is regrettable that their leader was able to flee, but if this Dargum has truly fled from the Nink-hai encampment, the result is much the same to me. Without a task-master's commands, the remnants of their tribe will likely disband their plot and set out for easier prey.\
\
'Knowing that this danger has subsided, I must now concentrate entirely on the coming siege of Faldham. Praises upon you, ${PLAYER}. You are a worthy ally.'","Explore the Nink-hai camp along the mountain path east of Faldham.\
\
Langfrith has asked you to infiltrate the Orc camp and overthrow the leader of the tribe.","Langfrith awaits oustide the mead hall of Faldham.\
\
Langfrith will wish to know of the events that transpired when you confronted the Nink-hai leader.","You have encountered Dargum, the Nink-hai leader","Enter the Nink-hai camp and locate their leader","The Nink-hai threat looms ever present. Langfrith believes that the only solution will be to defeat the Nink-hai Orc's task-master.","'My focus lies upon the Nink-hai Orcs, plotting and scheming in the eastern mountain passes. They are a new but unsettling threat to the Elfward. There is but one course of action if we are ever to delay their treachery: to confront and defeat their leader.\
\
'You must breach the enemy camp, ${PLAYER}. Locate and overthrow the Nink-hai task-master. His defeat should throw the lackeys into a state of panic and chaos, granting us an opportunity to better prepare our defences before dealing with the rest.'","Return to Langfrith and inform him of Dargum's escape","The horn has drawn Dargum's attention"},
[12824]={"'Anurandir regresó y me habló, ¡apenas podía creer su historia! Eres verdaderamente alguien de gran habilidad. Anurandir volvió a sus deberes en la naturaleza, pero tu rescate no será olvidado pronto.'","'¡El rescate de Anurandir no será olvidado pronto!'","Habla con Dornhador","Salva a Anurandir","Anurandir ha escapado de Barad Morlas","Anurandir fue capturado por semiorcos, y depende de ti salvarlo.","'Yo... soy el líder de los rastreadores de Echad Eregion... hemos estado vigilando de cerca a los semiorcos de Barad Morlas. A través de nuestra vigilancia hemos marcado las idas y venidas de sus mensajeros, suministros... incluso interceptado órdenes.\
\
'Fui capturado, por favor, ayúdame a escapar. Temo que pronto volverán para torturarme para obtener información.'","Regresa a Dornhador en Echad Eregion.\
\
Informa a Dornhador que has rescatado a Anurandir.","Lleva a Anurandir a un lugar seguro.","El Prisionero de Barad Morlas"},
[12825]={"Talk to Dervorin","Dervorin wants to know why lumber production is so slow.\
\
Talk to Dravron about why his camp is not putting out lumber.","'Hmph. Dervorin wishes to know why lumber has not been leaving this camp? It is because it's not profitable enough for me to send any!\
\
'The longer I withhold the product of these forests, the more the price of it will increase. Only when it is guaranteed to make me wealthier than the Lord of the Vale himself will I begin to sell!\
\
'What gives me the right? My family holds a claim to this land per an agreement with the Lords of the Vale from generations ago. Dervorin is welcome to revoke it but without cause, he will lose face. Go tell him that I will operate my lumber camp as I see fit.'","Dravron mentioned that his leadership of the camp stems from a land claim passed down through his family.\
\
Report this finding to Dervorin in Ethring.","'He claims to own the land itself per an agreement with my forebears? I find this suspicious....'","Talk to Dravron","'My friend! I have not set eyes upon you since our time together at Minas Tirith. I feared you dead, but I am glad to have been proven wrong.\
\
'I returned home safe some weeks ago, and have been dealing with a frustration ever since. I don't know if you are aware that the Ringló Vale produces much of the timber used in Gondor. Yet I arrived home only to find that the nearby lumber camp has been laying idle! I tried to speak to the owner of the camp, a surly man named Dravron, but he's only offered middling excuses. I could step in as acting Lord of the Vale, but I am loath to wield my power so heavy handedly, at least not yet.\
\
'Say, you are a fine conversationalist. Perhaps he would be more open with you than he would me. Find the camp up the hill, north-east from Ethring. See if he'll tell you why he's dragging his feet up there!'","Dervorin is frustrated with the lack of output from the nearby lumber camp.","The Problem with the Lumber Camp"},
[12826]={"'¡Siempre oí que los Elfos eran criaturas temibles y extrañas, pero tu amigo me parece más bien divertido! Te aseguro que ningún Elfo pintó este cuadro, ¡pero tomaré eso como un cumplido a mi arte! Sí, soy la pintora, y he pintado muchas de las plantas y animales que he visto en los bosques y campos de la Comarca. No conozco la palabra que usó para describir esta flor; nunca la había oído antes. Sin duda es algún término élfico lleno de significado, pero a los hobbits nos gusta dar nombres que lo dicen todo a la primera. ¡Este cuadro representa un girasol, por supuesto!\
\
'Crece una buena cantidad de ellos en el borde de un campo al norte de la Casa del Bosque, si quieren ir a verlos por ustedes mismos. ¡Y dile a tu amigo Elfo que agradezco sus amables palabras sobre mi pintura!'","'Hay flores por toda la Comarca. Aquí en Casa del Bosque cultivamos varias variedades. Lamento no poder ayudarte más.'","La Promesa de los Girasoles","Habla con Edlothon en el campo cerca de Casa del Bosque","'¡Deberías hablar con Marjoram! Siempre está pintando flores, plantas y animales, y puede que haya visto esa flor élfica que estás buscando. Vive aquí, en Casa del Bosque.'","'¡No sé qué decir, ${PLAYER}! Si no fuera imposible, diría que el artista no pintó esto de memoria, ¡sino del natural! Esta pintura representa una Anarlossë, ¡exactamente como la recuerdo! ¿Cómo puede ser? ¿La pintó uno de los míos? ¿Cómo llegó este cuadro a un pueblo hobbit? Los hobbits viven más que los Hombres, pero no tanto como para haber visto jamás una Anarlossë y pintarla con tal precisión. ¡Las últimas murieron hace muchísimo tiempo, y solo uno de los míos podría haber pintado esto!'","Habla con Haerandel en el Recinto del Festival","'¡Has regresado, ${PLAYER}! ¿Encontraste a mi hermano a tiempo? ¿Y había algo de verdad en el rumor de que alguna variedad de la Anarlossë podría sobrevivir aún en la Comarca?'\
\
Le cuentas a Haerandel acerca de los girasoles y de la decisión de su hermano de permanecer en la Tierra Media por ahora. Él te observa pensativo y, tras un momento, una sonrisa suaviza sus rasgos.\
\
'Estoy dividido. No deseaba contradecir la decisión de mi hermano, pues sé que no fue una elección fácil, y la lamentaba hondamente. No quería hacerlo cambiar de opinión ni obligarlo a quedarse.\
\
'Pero cuando partiste en su busca, cuando pareció que la Anarlossë quizá florecía aún en algún rincón de la Comarca, confieso que pensé en qué diría si él decidiera quedarse. ¿Podrían volver nuestros días de viaje? ¿Adónde iríamos?\
\
'He encontrado el destino perfecto, ${PLAYER}. Le sugeriré a mi hermano que dejemos que nuestros pies errantes nos lleven a las tierras del sur. Hay un supuesto maestro de hierbas en Minas Tirith al que propondría visitar. Posee una buena cantidad de ideas equivocadas que Edlothon y yo estamos más que preparados para corregir. Partiremos en primavera, con el paso ligero y el ánimo renovado, en otro viaje como los de antaño.\
\
'Gracias por ayudar a mi hermano y a mí, ${PLAYER}. Quizá el sol nos sonría, y nuestros caminos vuelvan a cruzarse en tierras lejanas. Hasta entonces, ¡adiós!'","Edlothon está junto a una hilera de girasoles en un campo no muy lejos del pueblo hobbit de Casa del Bosque.","Haerandel está en el Recinto del Festival de las Tierras de Bree.","Habla con Marjoram Cosechalana en el pueblo de Casa del Bosque","Encontraste a Edlothon antes de que su compañía de Elfos alcanzara su destino, y ha decidido prestarte atención en este asunto de pétalos, flores y relatos.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro cuando finalice el evento asociado.</rgb>","'¿Buscan girasoles? ¡Justo terminé una pintura de otro ayer! La apoyé contra la pared allí para que se secara. ¡Échale un vistazo y dime qué te parece!'","Investiga la cuestión de la Anarlossë en el pueblo de Casa del Bosque","'El pueblo de Maderzal queda justo debajo de nosotros, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Habla con los hobbits del lugar y averigua qué saben de la Anarlossë de antaño.'","'¿Podrían dejarme descansar en paz? Solo sé que las flores son bonitas, pero si buscan un conocimiento más profundo, no tengo nada que ofrecerles.'","'¿Girasoles? No sé nada sobre eso. Mis disculpas.'","'¿Cómo expresar esto, ${PLAYER}? ¡Mi corazón salta de alegría al verlas! Siento como si hubiese retrocedido en el tiempo, no al día en que la Anarlossë luchaba por sobrevivir, sino a los días en que florecía con fuerza. Haerandel y yo caminamos juntos entre estas flores, en los reinos del Norte y del Sur, con la vista fija en el horizonte y la mente danzando ante las promesas del futuro. Verlas de nuevo me devuelve aquellas alegrías, y los pesares que siguieron a las guerras de Sauron quedan olvidados. La promesa de los girasoles era tan brillante como sus pétalos, y muchos viajes nos aguardaban aún.\
\
'Cuando Anárion cayó y Arnor decaía, la Anarlossë desapareció del mundo. Y sin embargo, de algún modo, una semilla debió llegar a esta región. La imagino surcando el aire en la primavera, llevada por la brisa, hasta caer en esta tierra protegida. Aquí echó raíces, y su linaje prosperó lejos de ojos ajenos. La Anarlossë sobrevivió.'\
\
Edlothon contempla en silencio los girasoles.\
\
'Estaba listo para partir. Mi corazón lloraba por dejar atrás a mi hermano, pero sabía que lo vería de nuevo cuando él también alzara velas hacia el Oeste. Pero esta visión ha despertado en mí algo que no sentía desde nuestros viajes juntos, hace tanto tiempo. ¿Cuántas maravillas siguen ocultas en la Tierra Media? Vuelvo a sentir la llamada del camino.\
\
'Creí que no podía quedarme más tiempo, pero ahora pienso que mi hermano y yo podríamos disfrutar aún de otro viaje por la Tierra Media antes de partir juntos a las Tierras Imperecederas, como alguna vez imaginé. ¿Podrías llevar este mensaje a Haerandel por mí? Pasaré un tiempo aquí en contemplación, y pronto lo alcanzaré.\
\
'Tienes mi gratitud, ${PLAYER}, por recordarme lo que una vez valoré. Y no solo eso: también me has devuelto la esperanza en lo inesperado, en las maravillas que aún pueden aguardarnos tras la próxima curva o detrás del siguiente árbol. Me has devuelto la promesa de los girasoles, y no sabía cuánto la extrañaba.'","Habla con Edlothon en el pueblo de Casa del Bosque","'¿Un campo bordeado por flores como las del cuadro? Guía el camino, ${PLAYER}, ¡aunque me cueste creer lo que dice esta hobbit!'","'Esa flor misteriosa suena como un girasol para mí. No del tipo púrpura con el centro amarillo brillante, ¡la otra variedad! Marjoram pinta muchas de ese tipo, así que si quieren saber más deberían hablar con ella. Vive aquí en Casa del Bosque.'","'Hmm... suena a palabra élfica. ¡No quiero saber nada de ello!'","'No soy un experto en flores, lo lamento. Mi especialidad es repartir el correo y, entre nosotros, estos hobbits tan curiosos hacen que ese trabajo sea más difícil de lo que debería. ¡No sé cuánto más podré soportarlo!'","'¿Qué tiene que decir esta hobbit? ¿Sabe el nombre del Elfo que pintó este cuadro?'","'No sé nada sobre... ¿cómo llamaste a esa flor? ¿Anarlossë?'","Marjoram Cosechalana te contó que flores del sol bordean un campo agrícola al norte de Casa del Bosque.","Una hilera de girasoles bordea el campo, y Edlothon las observa con asombro en los ojos.","'Creo que mi hermano y yo podríamos encontrar alegría en otro viaje por la Tierra Media antes de partir hacia las Tierras Imperecederas juntos, como siempre pensé que lo haríamos. ¿Podrías llevar este mensaje a Haerandel por mí? Pasaré aquí un tiempo en contemplación y luego me uniré a él.'","'Girasoles bordean un campo justo al norte, si quieren verlas ustedes mismos. ¡Y dile a tu amigo Elfo que agradezco sus amables palabras sobre mi pintura!'","'¿Me preguntas por una flor élfica y ni siquiera notas las que están plantadas justo frente a mi puerta? ¡Qué grosería! ¡Buen día!'","Este cuadro sí se asemeja bastante al Anarlossë descrito por Haerandel.","Edlothon te ha pedido que hables con los hobbits de Casa del Bosque para averiguar si la legendaria Anarlossë logró sobrevivir al declive del Reino del Norte.","Una hobbit cercana ríe alegremente y hace una reverencia entusiasta.","Edlothon te ha acompañado al pueblo hobbit de Maderzal, donde encontraste indicios de una flor que recuerda al legendario Anarlossë.","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:seguro[m]|segura[f]} de haber entendido lo que dijo esa hobbit? Por amor a mi hermano Haerandel te daré crédito en esto, aunque me parezca una fantasía imposible. Hay un pueblo hobbit justo debajo de nosotros, y entiendo que quienes viven allí lo llaman Casa del Bosque. Ve y habla con ellos, y averigua si poseen flores como las que describes.\
\
'Mi decisión está tomada: la primavera será el momento de mi partida. Pero no tengo tanta prisa como para ignorar una pregunta de mi hermano. Los viajes que compartimos en nuestra juventud me son muy queridos, como él lo es. Ve a Casa del Bosque y aclara este asunto. No puedo demorarme demasiado, pero dedicaré un momento a esta búsqueda. ¡Me tiene el espíritu inquieto!'","Marjoram Cosechalana desea hablar contigo y con Edlothon.","Encuentra los girasoles en el campo al norte de Casa del Bosque"},
[12827]={"'Ho there friend! Please, you must help me!'","You should find the prospector's shack down in the Limlight Gorge.","Find the prospector's shack","'We had a small band of prospectors and fortune-hunters pass through Stangard a month or so ago. They had bought some old dwarf-made prospector's map of the Gorge...it must have been twenty-years-old or more, if it was not fraudulent.\
\
'They wanted to head down into the Gorge and investigate the old prospecting sites. We told them not to waste their time, but I guess they had already spent much coin on that fool's map, so they insisted on heading down all the same.\
\
'For the first week or so, they got on all right -- set up some sort of camp, made a few runs into town for supplies -- but we have heard nothing recently. It has been a while, and I do not have high hope that you will find them alive, but if you can find out what happened to them, it would take some weight off my mind.'","Prospectors have dared the dangers of the Limlight Gorge, determined to reap the mineral bounty of the Gorge.","You should speak with the remaining prospector from the expedition.","'Forgive me for my desperate plea, stranger, but my expedition has fallen to ruin, and most of my companions have been set upon by trolls.\
\
'I pray that you can aid me, for my livelihood, too, is in ruin, unless I can salvage something from this disaster.\
\
'Everything was going well, too...until the trolls caught us.'","Talk to Brid","The Prospector's Shack","You found the prospector's shack"},
[12828]={"Assisted Offram with Blankets for the Winter","'I am glad that you have considered the plight of my people. Indeed, I do have more tasks for you.\
\
'On your last venture, you brought me a large quantity of aurochs-meat, hides, and ivory. I need you to take these materials and help me provision the garrison and the town.\
\
'Will you do this?'","Assisted Offram with Making Meat-pies","Talk to Offram outside the Vendor Hall in Eaworth","'My thanks to you, friend ${PLAYER}. Your assistance will help Eaworth stand strong against the siege.'","Assist Offram with Making Meat-pies","Assist Offram with Blankets for the Winter","The Provisioner's Assistant","Assist Offram with Horns for Battle","Offram was pleased with your hunting prowess and offering of meat, hides, and ivory from the aurochs of the Vale.","Assisted Offram with Horns for Battle","Offram stands guard outside the Vendor Hall at Eaworth.\
\
Offram has asked you to help provision the garrison and town of Eaworth.","Offram stands guard outside the Vendor Hall in Eaworth.\
\
You should return to Offram with news of your successes."},
[12829]={"¡Clic! ¡Clic! ¡Clic! ¡Clic! La bóveda esta desbloqueada","Bávor Piedraroja está al otro lado de la Mansión de Thorin, hacia el sur.\
\
Ahora que has resuelto el acertijo de la bóveda enigma, deberías recoger el tesoro y llevarlo de vuelta con Bávor Piedraroja.","Recoge el contenido de la bóveda enigma","¡Clic!","La bóveda está al otro lado de la Mansión de Thorin, al norte y subiendo las escaleras.\
\
Acciona las palancas de la bóveda en el orden correcto. Si cometes un error, vuelve con Bávor Piedraroja para reiniciar los engranajes.","La Bóveda enigma","'Por favor, no me digas que no había nada en la bóveda.'","Lleva el contenido de la bóveda enigma a Bávor Piedraroja","Tomas una gran roca negra y tosca de la bóveda.","Acciona la segunda palanca","Ahora que has ensamblado todos los engranajes, es hora de abrir la bóveda.\
\
Encontraste estas pistas grabadas en las caras de los engranajes:\
\
El hacha muerde profundo antes del primer amanecer.\
\
El sol se alza después de que la luna se ha ocultado.\
\
Una joya puede encontrarse a la luz del sol.\
\
Las joyas solo se encuentran tras mucho esfuerzo.\
\
Antes que todo, puede verse la luz plateada de la luna.","'Asegúrate de consultar los acertijos. Debemos estar seguros de accionar las palancas en el orden correcto. ¡Oh, esto es muy emocionante!'","Acciona la tercera palanca","Acciona la cuarta palanca","Acciona la primera palanca","'¡Por fin! Está funcionando... creo.\
\
'Tendré que quedarme aquí para cuidar de esta máquina. Tú ve y abre la bóveda. Está bastante lejos —al otro lado de la Mansión de Thorin— al norte y subiendo las escaleras. Las cadenas y los cables recorren las paredes — ¡una verdadera obra de arte!\
\
'Asegúrate de accionar las palancas en el orden correcto, o tendrás que volver aquí para que reinicie los engranajes. Quizás esas pistas que encontraste en los cofres te ayuden con el orden.'","'¿Esto estaba en la bóveda? ¿Esto?\
\
Bávor observa incrédulo la roca negra. —¡Asombroso! ¡Fantástico! ¡Increíble!\
\
'Escucha, nadie sabía con certeza qué estaba sellado en esa bóveda. ¡Este es uno de los mayores tesoros de todos los enanos!\
\
'Oh, sé que no parece gran cosa, pero la historia cuenta que Durin mismo extrajo esto de Gundabad, la montaña donde despertó por primera vez. ¡Es el primer trozo de mineral jamás extraído por el padre de nuestra estirpe! Este es el artefacto más antiguo de los enanos y sirve como símbolo de nuestra herencia. Has desenterrado un verdadero tesoro con todo tu esfuerzo, y mereces todo nuestro agradecimiento.'"},
[12830]={"La llegada masiva de refugiados a Archet ha causado una escasez de suministros, y la intendente del capitán Helecharroyo, Peg Pruner, tiene dificultades para abastecer a los refugiados.","'Peg está al norte de aquí, justo subiendo por la carretera.'","Debe completarse antes de la \\qIntroducción.\\q","'¿El condestable Cardoso te envió? Me aseguraré de agradecérselo. Personas dispuestas a ayudarnos son justo lo que necesitamos hoy.\
\
Si estás ${PLAYERNAME:dispuesto[m]|dispuesta[f]}, tengo trabajo para ti.'","'Peg Pruner, la intendente del capitán Helecharroyo, necesita ayuda para reunir suficiente comida para los refugiados que han llegado a la ciudad desde que los bandidos comenzaron sus ataques.\
\
Ahora que la traición de Calder Cob ha sido revelada, gracias a ti, debemos asegurarnos de velar por la seguridad de la gente que ha perdido sus hogares y medios de vida. Si tienes tiempo o ganas de ayudar, ¿por qué no visitas a Peg y le ofreces tu ayuda?\
\
Peg está reclutando voluntarios en el extremo norte de la plaza principal de Archet. Solo sigue la carretera principal hacia el interior del pueblo.'","La intendente","Peg Pruner está en el extremo norte de la plaza de Archet.\
\
El condestable Cardoso mencionó que Peg Pruner podría necesitar ayuda para reunir comida para los habitantes desplazados de Archet."},
[12834]={"Râsabur has worked up the courage to challenge Eshen-erêz, the Bone-queen.","(Optional) Use the Aradûni Horn to call for Râsabur and begin the fight","'We have done it, ${PLAYER}! Our actions have made Idagâl safer for our army as well as the people who live here.\
\
'I will be heading on to the Dawn-warden to regroup with Captain Hanâbu. If you are heading that way, I hope to see you there. May we fight side-by-side again one day!'","Râsabur needs your help defeating Eshen-erêz, the Bone-queen.\
\
You should go to the centre of Ushumût, signal Râsabur by blowing the Aradûni Horn, and then defeat Eshen-erêz, the Bone-queen.","Talk to Râsabur","Defeated Eshen-erêz, the Bone-queen","Defeat Eshen-erêz, the Bone-queen","The Queen of Bones","You have defeated the Bone-queen.\
\
You should regroup with Râsabur near the rock where you first met.","'I have identified the leader of this drake nest. She is called Eshen-erêz, the Bone-queen, the largest of the wild-drake matrons. I watched her breath dissolve a man down to the bone.... I believe if we can defeat her, the rest of these drakes should scatter!\
\
'Go to the centre of the nest, blow the horn to signal me, and we will challenge her together. May fortune smile on us. For Damakhêra Ardu!'"},
[12835]={"'¡Date prisa! Debes destruir a la reina grodbog antes de que ponga más huevos.'","'¡Es un alivio haber expulsado a esos malvados gredbyg de Nud-heden!'","Nud-heden nunca se recuperará hasta que la reina grodbog sea eliminada.","Reina grodbog derrotada","Habla con Auti en Guardia Orca","La reina grodbog está en Nud-heden, en el interior del Agujero Chirriante, al sureste de Guardia Orca.\
\
Auti está convencido de que la infestación grodbog no será resuelta hasta que su reina sea derrotada.","'${PLAYER}, hemos hecho mucho, pero solo hemos demorado lo inevitable. Mientras la reina grodbog viva, esto se seguirá repitiendo. No, debe ser eliminada. Es la única manera de hacer que dejen de venir.\
\
'Vuelve a Nud-heden, al interior del Agujero Chirriante, al sureste de aquí. Una vez allí dentro encuentra a la reina grodbog y derrótala. Solo entonces nos dejarán en paz.'","'Gracias, ${PLAYER}. Ahora podemos empezar a reclamar el edificio y hacer que se convierta en lo que una vez fue. Khazad-dûm no volverá a su antigua gloria de una vez, pero piedra a piedra brillará una vez más.'","Derrota a la reina grodbog","Auti está en Guardia Orca, al noroeste de Nud-heden.\
\
Auti se alegrará de oír de que la reina grodbog ha sido derrotada y que los insectos han abandonado Nud-heden.","La cámara de la reina"},
[12836]={"Nud-heden tiene ahora la oportunidad de ser reclamada por alguien que no sea los gredbyg. ¿Volverán los enanos a llamar este sitio su hogar?\
\
Khazad-dûm no recuperará su gloria de una sola vez, pero, piedra por piedra, volverá a brillar.","'¡Es un alivio haber expulsado a esos malvados gredbyg de Nud-heden!'","Nud-heden nunca se recuperará hasta que la reina grodbog sea eliminada.","Reina grodbog derrotada","La reina grodbog de Nud-heden está poniendo huevos y cuidando de las larvas. Está creando un enjambre para protegerse, mientras sigue reproduciéndose ilesa.\
\
Debes derrotar a la reina grodbog de Nud-heden.","Derrota a la reina grodbog","La reina grodbog fue derrotada","Mientras la reina grodbog siga viva, los enanos nunca recuperarán su antiguo y honorable hogar. Hay que acabar con ella. Solo entonces este lugar podrá estar en paz.","La cámara de la reina"},
[12837]={"No lograste llegar a la rueda de agua a tiempo","'¿Llegaste hasta aquí en menos de dos minutos? ¡Increíble! ¡Dervel dijo que sería imposible!\
\
'Sí, me apostó a que un recién llegado no sería capaz de lograrlo, y todos los que fallan ayudan a llenar sus bolsillos. ¡Por fin alguien fue capaz de hacerlo!\
\
'Supongo que eso significa que debería recompensarte por este logro. Oh, no es ninguna molestia. ¡Vale la pena solo por ver la cara de Dervel cuando le diga que realmente lo lograste!'","Llega a la rueda de agua situada en el fondo del barranco antes de que se acabe el tiempo","Dervel Crintach te desafió a llegar, antes de que se acabe el tiempo, a la rueda de agua situada en el fondo del barranco en el que está construido Glyn Helyg","El Camino Más Rápido","Addo Benchuth está esperando para hablar contigo sobre tu logro","Dervel Crintach ha hecho una apuesta y quiere involucrarte en ella","¡Lo lograste!","Habla con Addo Benchuth junto a la rueda de agua","'Mejor date prisa. ¡La rueda de agua está muy por debajo de nosotros!'","'He concertado una apuesta con el viejo Addo Benchuth, que vive abajo, en el fondo del barranco en el que está construido Glyn Helyg. La apuesta es esta: que un recién llegado al pueblo no puede bajar hasta la rueda de agua, muy por debajo de nosotros, en menos de dos minutos.\
\
'¿Me ayudarías con esta apuesta? Es un largo camino hacia abajo, y los puentes pueden ser confusos, así que tendrás que ser ${PLAYERNAME:astuto[m]|astuta[f]}. Pero no tomes el camino más rápido... después de todo, no querrás romperte los huesos.\
\
'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:listo[m]|lista[f]}? ¡Buena fortuna para ti!'"},
[12840]={"Defeat Mordor Black-arrows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","An elite raiding party of Uruk-hai wander the Beacon Hills searching for the Rohirrim. Their tracking has taken them to the main road towards Taur Drúadan and soon they will be upon the Rohirrim War-stead if they are not dealt with swiftly.","You have defeated the Uruk-hai raiding party, and protected the Beacon Hills and the Rohirrim from their blades and arrows.","Defeated Mordor Warriors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","An elite raiding party of Uruk-hai can be found in the eastern edge of the Beacon Hills.\
\
You should defeat the Uruk-hai raiding party.","Defeated the Mordor Warleader","Defeat Mordor Warriors (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Completado","An elite raiding party of Uruk-hai have been wandering the Beacon Hills, searching for the Rohirrim.","Defeat the Mordor Warleader","The Raiding Party","Defeated Mordor Black-arrows (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated the Uruk-hai raiding party."},
[12841]={"Summon the soldiers for Huneric (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Summoned soldiers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Huneric, Lord of the Thíuda, has noticed forces gathering at Mokh Darga and wishes to halt the imminent raid before it can form.","'You fought well, and we gained the upper hand in today's battle. Maybe tomorrow we will do the same in the war and the siege will be ended! If not tomorrow, let us hope it will be soon.\
\
'The Storm of Wrath is on its way. We must be ready.'","Talk to Huneric","Soldiers can be found sleeping in their tents in Adambel.\
\
You should summon the soldiers for Huneric.","Huneric can be found in Adambel.\
\
You should talk to Huneric.","'A raiding party gathers in Mokh Darga, formed of warriors from all across the Corpse-fields. They seek to raid Adambel, or I am not called Hundred-slayer! And I am so named, so heed my words and my warning!\
\
'Our greatest chance in stopping this raid is to catch it by surprise. Take up sword and spear, and let us go with haste to swift and honourable victory!'","The Raiding Party","'The Storm of Wrath is nearly here, but that is not the only threat that endangers the Great Alliance. Indeed, the Ghâzab Bôron may serve to inspire our other foes to take the lead and seek to bring us down before the Storm even arrives!\
\
'Gather the men. Something looms on the horizon, and we may need more soldiers for the danger that comes this way!'"},
[12842]={"Tras un largo viaje de muchas millas, has llegado por fin a la aldea de Archet. Aragorn fue visto recientemente viajando en las cercanías de este tranquilo pueblo.","'Debo decir, ¡eres alguien muy alto! ¿De dónde has venido y cómo te llamas? ¿${PLAYER}? Ese es un nombre bastante inusual. ¿Qué asuntos te traen a Archet? Tenemos nuestros propios problemas, y poca necesidad de que forasteros traigan los suyos.'\
\
Le dices a la mujer que has viajado desde lejos buscando al montaraz Aragorn. Ella piensa por un momento y luego niega con la cabeza.\
\
'Es cierto que estuvo aquí, pero se ha marchado. Se fue justo antes de que los bandidos Montebruno lanzaran su ataque sobre nuestra aldea, reduciéndola a este estado. Podríamos haberlo usado en la defensa. A decir verdad, también podríamos haberte usado a ti, si hubieras llegado un poco antes. Pareces ser fuerte.\
\
'No sé adónde ha ido ahora el montaraz, pero Jon Helecharroyo podría saberlo. Él ha asumido el mando del proceso de reconstrucción, ahora que su padre ha fallecido. Lo encontrarás frente a los restos de la taberna, imagino. Lo vi allí más temprano.'","'Bueno, ¡debo decir que nunca esperé ver a alguien de tu gente por estas tierras! Eres de la línea de Beorn, ¿no es así? Tu estatura y tu porte me parecen inconfundibles. Nunca había conocido a alguien de tu familia hasta hoy, pero he oído hablar de tu pueblo por montaraces y otros habitantes de la naturaleza.'\
\
Le cuentas a Jon Helecharroyo por qué has venido a Archet, y él asiente.\
\
'Sí, Aragorn estuvo aquí, aunque en estas tierras se hace llamar Trancos. Se fue con cierta prisa, pero oí de otros que lamentaba hacerlo y deseaba quedarse para ayudarnos con nuestros problemas. Se dirigió a Bree, a menos que haya oído mal.\
\
'¡Pero espera, ${PLAYERNAME:mi alto amigo[m]|mi alta amiga[f]}! No te apresures a marcharte aún. Vienes a nosotros en nuestra hora más oscura, cuando los bandidos Montebruno han quemado nuestra aldea y matado a muchos de nuestros amigos. Mi propio padre pereció en la noche, abatido por los Montebruno y sus odiosos aliados del norte... de Angmar. Sé que deseas encontrar a Aragorn, pero si realmente compartes sus ideales, dedicarás un momento aquí o allá para ayudar a quienes lo necesitan. La experiencia te hará más fuerte, y juntos podremos impedir que otras aldeas sean quemadas en nombre del mal. Piénsalo, .'","El Rastro del Montaraz","'El montaraz Aragorn estuvo aquí, es cierto, pero se marchó antes del ataque de los Montebruno. No sé adónde fue, pero Jon Helecharroyo podría saberlo. Jon está a cargo de reconstruir la aldea ahora que su padre ha muerto.'","Habla con Jon Helecharroyo frente a los restos de la taberna, en la aldea de Archet","Jon Helecharroyo está frente a los restos de la Taberna del Tejón Loco, en la aldea incendiada de Archet.\
\
Letty Colazorro te ha dicho que hables con Jon Helecharroyo sobre el paradero de Aragorn, quien dejó la aldea de Archet poco antes de que fuera atacada por los bandidos Montebruno. Jon está a cargo de reconstruir la aldea ahora que su padre ha muerto.","Ayudando a la gente de las Tierras de Bree te volverás lo bastante fuerte como para encontrar a Aragorn"},
[12843]={"'Nethúr en Esteldín querrá hablar contigo, ${PLAYER}.'","'¿Has estado ya en el campamento de nuestros hermanos en las Quebradas del Norte? La antaño noble Esteldín sigue sirviéndonos con honor incluso hoy, como base para que nuestros Montaraces se entrenen y se preparen mientras las fuerzas de Angmar descienden desde los yermos del norte.\
\
'No es que aquí no necesitemos tu ayuda, pero quizás quieras hablar con Nethúr en Esteldín: he oído que la situación allí se ha vuelto muy grave, pues los orcos acampan en número cada vez mayor y amenazan con abrumar a nuestra gente.'","Los Montaraces de Esteldín","'¿Calenglad te envía? Ja, y pensar que creí que quizá necesitarían tu ayuda aún más que nosotros... pero es cierto que la situación aquí tampoco es de mi agrado: los orcos nos superan enormemente en número, y es solo cuestión de tiempo antes de que los últimos bastiones del Norte sufran un ataque.'","Nethúr está en Esteldín, lejos al este de Evendim.\
\
Calenglad te envió a hablar con Nethúr.","Calenglad de Tinnudir te ha pedido que hables con Nethúr de Esteldín, en las Quebradas del Norte, acerca de los Montaraces de Esteldín y de las fuerzas orcas que descienden desde Angmar."},
[12844]={"Duindir is located in the western section of Southern Ithilien.\
\
You should speak to the Ranger on the path outside of the ruins.","The Western Post can be found on top of the western cliffs in Southern Ithilien.\
\
You should search tents at the Western Post for information as to the Rangers' whereabouts.","Luntil beckons you to speak with her.","You hear the sounds of men coming from the nearby ruins","A Ranger has been bound and interrogated by the Haradrim!","The path from the Western Post leads north-east, further into Southern Ithilien.\
\
You should explore further up the road into South Ithilien. Perhaps you will find the elusive Rangers there.","Luntil offers to row you across the Anduin to the tree-covered hills of South Ithilien. There, you hope to make it to Osgiliath without significant delay.","Duindir is located in the western section of Southern Ithilien.\
\
You should rescue the Ranger from the Haradrim.","Search the tents for any information (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Quickly stranger, untie me so that I may live another day. Curse these damned Haradrim!'","Duindir is located in the western section of Southern Ithilien.\
\
You should investigate the sounds coming from the ruins.","The Western Post can be found on top of the western cliffs in Southern Ithilien.\
\
You should speak with a Ranger at the Western Post.","'Now that we stand at the base of the Emyn Arnen, do you see the beauty of these lands? This rugged beauty is my home. My parents lived here for as long as they could but the threat in the east grew too great and we fled to Lossarnach when I was young. I vowed to do everything I could to save Ithilien so that one day my children may live here in peace. Now I ask of you: protect these lands.\
\
'The Rangers have a camp-site - the Western Post - just north of here. Tell them I sent you to aid them. Some of the Rangers can be stubborn, at times, but I know they are in need of someone like yourself.'","'My thanks for helping me out back there. I was on routine patrol with a comrade when we were ambushed. One moment we were fighting back to back and the next our foes fell back - a clever ploy! - and we pursued them separately. Before I knew it, I was surrounded, alone, and taken as you found me.\
\
'Now forgive me, but I must ask what brought you to these wooded shores?'\
\
You explain that you are trying to reach Faramir with important information, and also that Luntil sent you to the Rangers' camp to lend what aid you could.\
\
'I look into your eyes, ${RACE}, and see that you speak the truth. Alas, I can help you little, for I have not seen Faramir nor heard of his whereabouts for many weeks. I hope for your sake that the information is important enough to traverse these lands. Southern Ithilien is crawling with the Morgul-host.\
\
'Now, let us speak of the debt you owe to Luntil. She is wise in many ways, and I will confess your help is sorely needed, so I deem that I should not release you from your word.'","Search for any Rangers","Duindir is located in the western section of Southern Ithilien.\
\
You heard signs of a struggle there, but found only Haradrim. You should search the ruins for signs of any Rangers.","Rescue the captured Ranger","Luntil insists that the Rangers will help provide safe travels through Ithilien","'It is not chance that brought you to this hidden landing place. I can see it in your eyes: you wish to cross the Anduin into Ithilien. The currents are swift in these parts, but you are in luck, as I can take you there. My name is Luntil and I ferry provisions to the Rangers that protect these lands. I admire their courage and they are grateful for my assistance to their cause.\
\
'Climb into the boat when you are ready to cross the Anduin. I have one small favour to ask of you when we reach the shores of Ithilien. I ask nothing more in payment.'","You hear sounds of a struggle as you enter the ruins. The place is crawling with Haradrim!","Luntil's boat can be found hidden amongst the reeds on the shores of the Anduin in Lossarnach.\
\
Luntil has asked you to step aboard her boat when you are ready to travel to Southern Ithilien.","Luntil can be found on the shores of the Anduin in Southern Ithilien.\
\
You should speak to Luntil about the favour she asked in exchange for ferrying you across.","Speak to Luntil","The Rangers of the South","You find nothing of interest","There doesn't seem to be anyone at the camp-site","Explore further up the road","Speak with Gladhir","Cross the river by boat","Speak to a Ranger at the nearby camp-site","Investigate the sounds coming from the ruins"},
[12845]={"Lleva las órdenes de los Angmarim a Esko","Los Angmarim están acampados cerca del Mur de Hierro, al noreste de Pynti-peldot.\
\
Esko te ha pedido que registres los campamentos de los Angmarim en busca de pruebas de la Joya de Hielo.","Los Angmarim están acampados cerca del Mur de Hierro, en las montañas de Forochel, muy al este de la bahía.\
\
Esko te ha pedido que registres los campamentos de los Angmarim en busca de alguna prueba de la Joya de Hielo.","'Ahora que conoces la historia del Jä-koru, creo que ha llegado el momento de abordar el asunto presente.\
\
'Uno de mis espías afirma que los Angmarim planean traer el Jä-koru de vuelta a Forochel próximamente... pero no sabemos cómo ni cuándo lo harán.\
\
'Como seguramente habrás notado, hay un campamento de Angmarim cerca del Mur de Hierro, que es la ruta más probable que utilizarían para traer el Jä-koru hasta aquí… suponiendo que haya permanecido en Angmar todos estos años. Si entras en combate con los Angmarim allí, quizá encuentres a alguno que sepa algo sobre el Jä-koru o, al menos, pruebas de su paso si ya lo han traído.'","'¿Aún no has encontrado ninguna pista del Jä-koru? Por favor, continúa con la búsqueda… ¡no podemos permitirnos fallar!'","Busca pruebas de la Joya de Hielo","'¡Ah! ¡Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}! ¡Por fin tenemos el Jä-koru casi en nuestras manos!\
\
'Según estos documentos, ya se encuentra aquí, en Forochel. Los Angmarim planean conservarlo aún durante algún tiempo para usarlo como amenaza contra los Hylje-heimo y seguir manipulando al Consejo hasta que sus aliados entre los Susi-väki y los Kivi-väki nos hayan hecho suficiente daño como para obligarnos a pedir la paz… y someternos a la esclavitud de Angmar. Solo entonces renunciarán al Jä-koru.\
\
'Evidentemente no podemos permitir que esto ocurra. Si logramos capturar el Jä-koru y entregarlo en secreto a los Hylje-heimo, podremos asegurar su apoyo en el Consejo y unir fuerzas con los pueblos del Sur a tiempo para detener este mal antes de que nos consuma a todos.'","Esko te contó la historia de la Joya de Hielo y cómo los Angmarim la están utilizando como instrumento de presión contra los Lossoth.","Esko se encuentra en Pynti-peldot, al suroeste del Mur de Hierro.\
\
Has encontrado un conjunto de órdenes que indican cuándo y dónde será introducida la Joya de Hielo en Forochel. Deberías llevarlas a Esko de inmediato.","'Los hombres de Angmar son malvados y nos perjudican al retener el Jä-koru.'","Has encontrado órdenes relacionadas con la Joya de Hielo","El rescate de Angmar"},
[12846]={"'Another chance to lose my head. What a fine day this is turning out to be!'","'You must go with Gondrad and see the ransom paid. Tarry not. I have much work to do, and would dwell on what may become of my sons no more than I must.'","To ensure the return of her sons, Glánhar requires Jarl Akhiz's brooch to complete the ransom.","'That is the camp there, just as he told us it would be. You go on and steal back his brooch. I will remain here, doing my best to keep my head attached to my shoulders.'","Found the stolen brooch","The rival Jarl's camp is near the Firien Wood, west of Ost Rimmon.\
\
Search for the stolen brooch among the camp.","Now that you have the stolen brooch, you should bring it to Gondrad, who waits near the camp in the Firien Wood.","Searched the chest","You have found the rival captain's camp","'Why, there it is. And you don't look terribly bruised or bloodied, for all that. Things are going well for us so far, aren't they? It's how I know our luck must be about to turn.'","Talk to Gondrad","Find the stolen brooch","Find the rival Jarl's camp near the Firien Wood, in the western Beacon Hills.","'This cunning wolf has named his price and I fear it must be paid. I ask the two of you to take this gold and to fetch the stolen trinket, and see if you can indeed buy back my sons from these men.\
\
'It did not escape me that he first offered three sons for ransom and now counts but two. Yet I will not dwell on it. There is no time for grief or fruitless worry, now. We must act. \
\
'But I beseech you both - show caution! You are treating with scoundrels and must be cunning yourselves - and cautious, beside. I would give much to see my sons alive before me, but your lives are not among the things that I would give.\
\
'Now go.'","The Ransomer's Rival","'Those look very much like the men who assailed us before the meeting, do they not? I wonder if they will like you rifling through their things.'","Meet Gondrad near the rival captain's camp"},
[12847]={"Heal scarred trees (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Thorlind","The Ravages of the Taurogrim","Healed scarred trees (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Thorlind can be found near Tholkát in Eryn Lasgalen.\
\
You should talk to Thorlind.","'So many trees were damaged! Thank you for doing what you can, ${PLAYER}. We must find a way to rout this ancient enemy, before they can defile the forest further.'","Scarred trees can be found near Tholkát in Eryn Lasgalen.\
\
You should heal scarred trees.","The Taurogrim are a destructive force, poisoning wildlife and destroying plants as they spread. Thorlind has asked you to heal the trees that have been scarred by their ravaging.","'The Taurogrim have no regard for the natural order. They ravage the land where they spread, destroying the wildlife. We cannot allow this to continue. If you find any trees that show scarring from their brutal attacks, please use this salve to heal them.'"},
[12848]={"El cuervo te mira con expresión desolada, pero de pronto bate las alas con furia y se lanza hacia una abertura en las rocas.","El cuervo de Cenlieg está ahora a salvo.","Encuentra y rescata al cuervo de Cenlieg","Habla con Cenlieg","Cenlieg, el Sabio, ha perdido a sus compañeros y se encuentra varado en Kauppa-kohta. Envió a su cuervo para encontrar rastros de ellos, pero el ave no ha regresado.","El cuervo de Cenlieg puede encontrarse cerca de un afloramiento rocoso al suroeste de Kauppa-kohta.\
\
Cenlieg te ha pedido que encuentres a su cuervo desaparecido.","'Cómo consiguió perderse entre los huargos sigue siendo un misterio para mí, pero evidentemente no fue culpa mía.\
\
'Parece indicarnos el camino hacia los acantilados helados del oeste. Creo que mi comunidad debió pasar por allí hace uno o dos días. Pienso que podremos seguir su rastro en cuanto Linden recupere el ánimo.'","'Por favor, si encuentras a mi cuervo podremos averiguar en qué dirección marcharon mis compañeros por última vez.'","'¿A través de los árboles, dice? Que basta con atravesar la línea de árboles. ¡Ja! De ese modo estaríamos vagando durante una semana o más. Mi atajo es la única forma de llegar a… oh, mil disculpas.\
\
'Verás, mis compañeros y yo nos dirigíamos a… en fin, eso no viene al caso. En su precipitación, tomaron un camino que no deberíamos haber seguido, y parece que he perdido su rastro.\
\
'Enseguida envié a mi cuervo hacia el afloramiento rocoso situado al suroeste para ver si quedaban huellas en la nieve. Hasta ahora no ha regresado. Iba a ir a buscarla, pensando que quizá se hubiera quedado atrapada entre los árboles, pero mi amigo oso, Linden, no se encuentra bien y necesita de mi ayuda aquí. Si te diriges hacia ese lugar, ¿podrías buscarla?'","El cuervo","Cenlieg se encuentra en Kauppa-kohta, al noreste del afloramiento rocoso donde encontraste al cuervo.\
\
Has encontrado al cuervo de Cenlieg, pero se ocultó rápidamente presa del pánico. Tal vez deberías volver a hablar con Cenlieg."},
[12849]={"The Ravens of the North","'What do you want?'\
\
You politely explain King Thorin's wish to rebuild a friendship with the ravens.\
\
'Ah, so he thinks he might put all to rights now, does he? He did not seem so concerned about the minds of the ravens when Dáin was King Under the Mountain. He must know the truth of it. You see, the line of Carc nears its end. Roäc is dead, his children are dead, and now Arcah, daughter of Croär, is all that remains. I tend her lesser kin as best an old dwarf may, but she is the last chief of the great ravens, and it has been many years since we last spoke in the forgotten ways of Durin's Folk.\
\
'She has gone elsewhere... beyond my sight. I do not know if she will ever return, but if the King Under the Mountain wishes to heal the wounds of time and once again share true friendship with the ravens, it will be no simple errand.\
\
'I can speak with them if they would still hear me, but they will not listen without the offerings that once adorned their homes. I have seen sparkling trinkets borne by the Easterlings come to the North, and I believe the ravens may find them to their liking.\
\
'Bring me those trinkets, and we shall see if the ravens still desire friendship with Durin's Folk.'","Deliver the trinkets to Dís at Ravenhill","'I cannot give the King Under the Mountain what he seeks... not without time.\
\
'The ravens must decide if such an offering pleases them, and perhaps one day the younger Dwarves of Durin's Folk will witness the return of Arcah and the friendship that was lost.'","Dís has long tended the ravens that still dwell in the heights of Ravenhill, but the once-strong friendship between the ravens and Durin's Folk has faded nearly to naught.","Collect Jangovar trinkets for the ravens of Ravenhill (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Trinkets are carried by many of the Jangovar in the North.\
\
Dís has suggested that renewing the old practice of offering shiny trinkets to the ravens might aid in rebuilding a friendship between Durin's Folk and their kind.","Dís can be found at Ravenhill.\
\
You have gathered many trinkets from the Jangovar and should now deliver them to Dís.","Collected Jangovar trinkets for the ravens of Ravenhill (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12850]={"Return to Erna","Talk to Víthog","'The Bilitang? You have returned it to us? Ah, ${PLAYER}. This means more than you can know. You have restored what is most prized to us. You have also restored our faith in the good-will and honesty of Dale.\
\
'You must know that the twisted, faltering strength Athálrik gained from the memory-cloth was a misuse. It is not a weapon, nor was it meant to be anything of the kind. It is a long song of memory, woven by Sangemêkh after Sangemêkh across many lives of the Chayasír, and the song gives strength. A strength meant to sustain, and bring together, and give hope. In truth, I do not think many would become as Athálrik did, handling the Bilitang un-trained. I think there must have been some sour knot within his heart from long before.\
\
'But thanks to you, all is right again.  You may go and tell the Regent Queen in Dale that she will see no more trouble from the Chayasír.'","Bring the memory-cloth to Turáh","'Did you think I would run and hide in the timbers? I saw all, aye, and heard as well. The lad has come to a bitter end. It fills me with sorrow, but I hold nothing against you, ${CLASS}.\
\
'There was always anger in Athálrik's heart... but not such anger as this. What put that there? Ah, I may never know. I have seen much sorrow in my life, and I have never known a true cause to any of it.'","You should return Queen Regent Erna, in the Great-keep in Dale, with the news that Athálrik chose death over justice.","You should bring the memory-cloth back to Sangemêkh Turáh, in the refugee camps in the hills east of Dale.","You should talk to Víthog, the old forester in the highlands west of Lake-town.","The old forester Víthog will lead you to Athálrik, where you can confront him for his accused crimes.","You should talk to Víthog, who has approached after your confrontation with Athálrik.","'Aye, I know his visits home are not to me, though I am the closest thing to family Athálrik ever had. I know also he has been troubled of late. Troubled as I have ever seen him. \
\
'My eyes are still keen, and I see as much that is good as is stern in your face. I will take you to him. I hope you will do him some good. Ah, but what am I? I am an old man and I am given to worry.'","The Reach of Justice","The Queen Regent and young king listen to your account.\
\
'The news you bear is grave indeed. It is troubling that Athálrik could not be brought to face due and proper justice.\
\
'However, I judge your dealings in the matter honest, and your course of action the necessary one. And for your service in the protection of Dale, we thank you.'","'Come then, let me lead you to the place Athálrik goes. Whatever is troubling the lad... I hope you do him some good.'"},
[12851]={"A fresh shipment of building materials has arrived in Halach.","The Rebuilding Process","Gorhir has asked you to take a crate to Irodon, who is supervising rebuilding efforts in the centre of Halach.\
\
You can take the crate from the pile next to Gorhir.","Talk to Gorhir","Pick up a heavy crate from the pile","You've delivered the crate to Irodon.\
\
You should confirm with Gorhir at Halach's harbour.","'You hauled such heavy cargo without even breaking a sweat. Impressive work!'","'Thank you, friend! I expect Gorhir will want to know the materials have been delivered.'","'Look at all of these crates, ${PLAYER}! Filled to the brim with building materials, too!\
\
'Would you mind taking this one over to Irodon? He should be supervising rebuilding efforts in the centre of town.'","'Would you mind taking this crate over to Irodon? He should be in the centre of town.'"},
[12852]={"Travel to Parth Gladló to search for Haradrim","With renewed spirit, Éomer, King of Rohan, has decided to send Elfhelm to lead an attack against a band of Haradrim who has fled into Talath Anor.","Talk to Elfhelm at Parth Gladló","Habla con Éomer","Defeat Haradrim at Parth Gladló (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Some of the Haradrim have fled north on horse! We must pursue!'","Many Haradrim are encamped here","You should talk to Elfhelm at Parth Gladló, north of the after-battle Pelennor.","'Men patrolling the northern parts of the Pelennor have spotted a large group of Haradrim hiding out in Talath Anor. We cannot let them remain. We must act swiftly and surprise their forces. Will you accompany Elfhelm on this ride? He has volunteered and could certainly use your expertise.'","Travel to Parth Gladló, north of the after-battle Pelennor, to search for Haradrim.","Defeated Haradrim (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Reclamation of Talath Anor","You should talk to Éomer at Aragorn's Pavilion on the after-battle Pelennor.","'I am glad you and Elfhelm were able to scatter the Haradrim encampment. Do not worry overmuch about those who slipped away to the island fortress of Cair Andros. It is only a matter of time before we must recapture Cair Andros for Gondor, and then their day of reckoning shall come too.'","You should defeat Haradrim at Parth Gladló, north of the after-battle Pelennor."},
[12853]={"Talk to Reeve Athelward at the Mead Hall of Cliving","'The Norcrofts will be safer for my Riders and for those evacuating, without the Orcs suddenly raining arrows down upon them.\
\
'You are well-deserving of this reward.'","Defeated Orc-archers in the Norcrofts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Red Fields lie to the south-east of the city, in the area between Cliving and Elthengels.","'My Riders have spoken with me about a section of the Norcrofts, between Cliving and Elthengels, that they have branded the Red Fields, for the blood-stained grasses that have become an all too common sight there.\
\
'These plains are so dangerous due to the ever-present threat of mounted Orc-archers. Even the most seasoned rider can be struck with an unlucky or unexpected arrow and become mortally wounded.\
\
'Clear as many of the mounted Orc-archers from this land as you can, and I will ensure that you are rewarded for your endeavours.'","The Red Fields","Reeve Athelward resides in his Mead Hall, at the eastern edge of Cliving.\
\
You have overcome the mounted Orc-archers that have been terrorizing people in the Red Fields.","The bands of Orc-archers that roam across the fields between Cliving and Elthengels have been terrorizing the people of the Norcrofts. Their territory has become so dangerous and violent that it has been nicknamed the Red Fields.","Defeat Orc-archers in the Norcrofts (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12856]={"The pendant can be found on a table next to Fastred inside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.","Talk to Fastred","The Reeve Restored","Pick up Fastred's pendant","Fastred wishes to speak with you about your victories in the Sutcrofts, and the great work you have done for the safety of his people.","'Treasure that as a reminder of all you have done for the people of the Sutcrofts.\
\
'We must rebuild in wake of this attack, but rest assured, our strength will never waver, and no Orc will ever claim these lands again!\
\
'Glory for Rohan... may your courage never falter!'","'Well? What do you say?'","Fastred can be found inside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.\
\
You should speak again with Fastred.","The delicate pendant has beautiful etchings of wheat wreathing a bold red gemstone... a true token of the Sutcrofts","'You have done a great many things for the people of the Sutcrofts, ${PLAYER}. I wish to reward your tenacity with a symbol of our appreciation.\
\
'On the table there is a pendant, a pendant of the Sutcrofts. Take it, for you have earned it most thoroughly.'"},
[12857]={"The Reeve of the Entwash Vale","Burnoth awaits you outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
You should speak with Burnoth when you are ready to accompany him into the Mead Hall.","You have met up once more with the Riders Four outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth.","Burnoth awaits you outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth.\
\
You should speak with Burnoth regarding Reeve Ingbert's response.","'Hail and well met, friend ${PLAYER}. It appears our paths run along similar courses. I did not believe things had become so dire within the borders of the Riddermark, but I see from the Orc-encampment outside Eaworth that the situation here is worse than I imagined.\
\
'I am sore distressed to bring word of the Khundolar to Reeve Ingbert, but if he does not join in the muster, I fear the Eastemnet will fall. Will you accompany me to meet with him?'","'The situation here is far worse than I imagined. If we do not help the Reeve against these Orcs, I fear Eaworth and the Entwash Vale will fall!'","Talk to Burnoth to accompany him into the Mead Hall of Eaworth","Burnoth has agreed to help the Reeve in exchange for a conscription to the muster of the Eastemnet","Talk to Burnoth outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth","'Let us meet with the Reeve and see what he has to say.'"},
[12858]={"'${PLAYER}, we meet again! We have been here for a few days, but have been unable to speak with Reeve Athelward. He has not refused to see us, as Aldor Harding, but has passed naught but excuses through his doorward.\
\
'Perhaps you will once again speak on our behalf? An impending invasion by a horde of Khundolar Easterlings is not a matter to be taken lightly.\
\
'If you could, either convince Athelward to speak with us directly or relate our tale to him as best you may.'","Talk to Burnoth in Cliving","The Riders Four have come to Cliving to warn Reeve Athelward of the impending invasion of the Khundolar.","Reeve Athelward is in the Mead Hall of Cliving.\
\
Burnoth has asked you to relate his message regarding the Khundolar invasion to Reeve Athelward.","Burnoth is encamped with his Riders outside the Mead Hall of Cliving.\
\
You should return to Burnoth with Athelward's reply.","You relate Athelward's words to Burnoth, and he pauses in thought.\
\
'In truth, I am troubled, ${PLAYER}. You have said naught to discourage me, but I find Athelward's response queer in these dark times. Does he truly seek to host a feast for a few ragged Riders?\
\
'Nay, this is troubling indeed... I must consider our best options.'","'Greetings! Have you found your stay in Cliving a pleasant one... or at least eventful?\
\
'Yes, I know of the Riders of whom you speak. They are retainers of Lord Éomer? Had I known sooner, I would have greeted them with a warmer welcome.\
\
'Let a feast be prepared, and let them come to my hall! I will give them a welcome they will not soon forget!'","The Reeve of the Norcrofts","Talk to Athelward at the Mead Hall of Cliving","'A moment, ${PLAYER}. I must apologize for my abruptness to you in Harwick. I told you of my shame, but I did not speak of my pride.\
\
'When I first came to Aldburg, I fell in love with Fleda, niece of Gártorn. We were soon married, and she bore me two daughters: Léoflad and Wynith. They have both grown into beautiful women, and they are my joy.\
\
'Though Gártorn and the warriors of Aldburg forsook me, Fleda remained faithful... she is why I remained in Éomer's service. Alas, though Fleda and Léoflad remain faithful to me, young Wynith is shamed by my dishonour... it is for her that I seek redemption.\
\
'My pardon for the interruption, but I thought it important to share this with you.'"},
[12859]={"'Well, we have come a long way, only to find the master of the house absent.'","Burnoth stands outside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.\
\
You should speak with Burnoth and discover what to do next.","'${PLAYER}! I am pleased to see you, though I will not say that I am surprised... our paths seem destined to cross at the most opportune times.\
\
'We have only just arrived ourselves. Indeed, it seems that we are both here to see the Reeve, Fastred. Would you join me?'","Talk to the doorwarden at the Mead Hall of Snowbourn","The Reeve of the Sutcrofts","'You have come too late. Reeve Fastred is abroad, hunting Orcs. If you wish to speak with him, I can show on your map where his camp lies.\
\
'Here... though I doubt you will find a warm welcome. His mood has been harsh of late, and a thirst for blood has been upon him.'","You have encountered the Riders Four once more in Snowbourn, capital of the Sutcrofts.","Talk to Burnoth outside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn","The doorwarden stands before the doors to the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.\
\
You should seek entrance to the Mead Hall of Snowbourn."},
[12860]={"'You say Aldor Harding believes he will die at the hands of the Khundolar Easterlings because of portents he claims to have seen? Then we have a difficult task ahead of us....'","Talk to Burnoth at the refugee camp outside Harwick","The Reeve of the Wold","Harding sighs.\
\
'I know what message you would deliver on behalf of Burnoth and his Riders, and it is futile.\
\
'The strength of the Khundolar is not unknown to me -- already I prepare to defend the Eastemnet from their advance, and I will die defending Rohan. In truth, I know this, for I have seen the omens.\
\
'Go now and leave me to my work.'","Aldor Harding is at the Mead Hall of Harwick.\
\
Burnoth has asked you to speak with Aldor Harding and deliver news of the Easterlings' true strength.","Burnoth and the Riders Four have been unable to secure an audience with Harding, Reeve of the Wold and Aldor of the Eastemnet.","Burnoth is at the refugee camp, outside of Harwick.\
\
You should return to Burnoth with Harding's reply.","'For a stranger to these lands, you seem to have some freedom to move about. That speaks highly of you. Perhaps you can be of assistance to me and my companions.\
\
'We have been trying to secure an audience with Aldor Harding, but he refuses to speak with us. There is no doubt that he knows already of the Easterlings upon his threshold, for his men have engaged with them, but he knows not their true strength, as we do.\
\
'Will you go to the Mead Hall and speak with the Aldor? Perhaps he will listen to the warnings of one who has been further abroad... and I hear that you have already seen him.'","Talk to Harding at the Mead Hall of Harwick"},
[12861]={"As you enter, you see an older Woman to your left, and the noises of a child upstairs","Beneath the veil of this Rohirric bassinet, you see a small boy. He coos inquisitively at your presence, but then appears to lull himself back to sleep.","'Welcome back, ${PLAYER}. I have considered the note you brought me, considered your efforts thus far, and I have decided what needs to be done.\
\
'If you would, have a drink, and we shall speak further.'","'${PLAYER}, Reeve Fastred has expressed a desire for you to meet with his family. Once you have met with them, you should return to him as soon as you are able.'","Fastred has set out a drink on the table in front of him inside of the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.\
\
Reeve Fastred bids you drink with him.","'Ah, so my son has sent you to me?\
\
'I overheard him speaking to Elflád of a mighty visitor in these lands.... You are welcome here, traveller. Fastred would not send you to us unless you earned his trust.\
\
'Sadly, my son has lost sight of my husband's ideals. He would be wise to heed Éomer's call to abandon these lands, if only to spare the defenceless. Such stubbornness is difficult to influence, though....'","Talk to Folcred","Talk to Fastred","Talk to Elflád","As you finish your drink, Fastred looks as if he has more yet to say","Share a drink with Fastred","After meeting with Fastred's family, you should now return to him in the Mead Hall","Fastred can be found inside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.\
\
Reeve Fastred desires to speak with you.","Elflád can be found on the second floor of Fastred's home in central Snowbourn.","Fastred has appreciated your labour thus far and wishes for you to meet his family before speaking further with him.","'I trust you enjoyed the drink? Aye, our mead is among the finest in Rohan, as you will come to learn. On the matter at hand, though... that note has raised my ire.\
\
'I have enough trouble dealing with the Orcs and ignoring the King's call to retreat from the Eastemnet. I will not uproot my people, under any circumstance. If the Sutcrofts are to fall, I will fall with them and not before I slay every Orc that dares stand against me.\
\
'Snowbourn must ready itself for battle; meanwhile, I will instruct my guards to attempt to expose the traitor, whomever he may be.'","Elflád's words are bold, mirroring the resolve of her husband","Talk to Théodhild","Talk to Fastred in the Mead Hall of Snowbourn","Folcred can be found on the second floor of Fastred's house near Elflád.","Fastred's home can be found slightly south and east of the Mead Hall.","Théodhild can be found inside Fastred's home in central Snowbourn.","Fastred can be found inside the Mead Hall of Snowbourn.\
\
Cynelac has informed you that Fastred wants to speak with you after you have finished meeting with his family.","The Reeve's Family","'Hello, traveller. Fastred has told me much of your journey through the Eastemnet and the aid you provided for Garsfeld.\
\
'I thank you for bringing renewed hope to the people of the Sutcrofts. While many of the soldiers stand by my husband, some of the crofters fear for their safety. Our son would perhaps be safer elsewhere, but Fastred has decreed that none shall leave. As always, I must stand with him.\
\
'You are always welcome here, ${PLAYER}. I must tend to Folcred, so you may return to Fastred when you see fit.'","Fastred's mother grows concerned by her son's leadership, but will say no more","Enter Fastred's home"},
[12863]={"You should speak with the Black Númenórean captive.","The captive flinches","'If I speak to thee, Dulgabêth shall have me killed. The Black Word is not one to be reckoned with.'\
\
'My name is Lômazar. I was once a faithful servant to Dulgabêth. I have made more than one mistake and as punishment was struck blind. To escape further torment, I severed my bonds, only to be captured again and brought here.'\
\
'Perchance, will you spare me torment inside the walls of Mordor in the exchange of knowledge?'","It seems the captive's will is starting to break","Intimidate the Black Númenórean captive","The Reluctant Captive","Talk to the captive","'I have nothing to say to the likes of you.'","'As we have fought together on the Pelennor, I well know you can protect yourself. Still, the plains of Gorgoroth are filled with fires and crevasses caused by the eruption of Mount Doom. It is a dangerous place and we must tread carefully.\
\
'Our first scouting party has just returned, and with them, they bring a captive. The man they have captured is a Black Númenórean servant. He refuses to speak to us. We must either persuade him of our cause or somehow convince him to talk. \
\
'I was hoping that you would try speaking to the man. See if you can find out what he knows and who he serves.'","Try talking to the captive again","Gondorian soldiers have intercepted a Black Númenórean fleeing from Barad-dûr.","You should intimidate the Black Númenórean captive.","You should intimidate the Black Númenórean captive again.","The captive looks worried","The captive does nothing","Talk to the Black Númenórean captive","You question the captive. The man seems to have no interest in anything you tell him or any question you ask."},
[12864]={"Dwarves of Nori's expedition might be found in Skarháld.\
\
After learning that a small company of Longbeards has remained in Skarháld, Dori has asked you to speak to them and learn if his brother has abandoned his quest.","After learning that a small company of Longbeards has made camp in Skarháld, Dori hopes to learn more of the fate of his brother's expedition.","Find the dwarves of Nori's expedition in Skarháld","Collected fallen branches from the Thornholt (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'What have you learned, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You inform Dori that only a few Longbeards remain in Skarháld and that Nori and the rest of his expedition followed the Men Angrún to Thikil-gundu. You also inform Dori that the Zhélruka made mention of Karazgar, Vethúg Wintermind, and strange dwarves wandering in the night.\
\
'Strange dwarves? The Zhélruka have called the Longbeards many things in many tongues, but I have never known them to call us strange. I wonder what the truth of that tale could be....\
\
'If Nori and his expedition have travelled to Thikil-gundu by way of the Men Angrún, he will have passed through Óinsbridge. It is there we must go!'","Dori can be found at the stables in eastern Skarháld.\
\
Troubling tales have been spreading among the Zhélruka in Skarháld. You should return to Dori and tell him what you have learned.","Collected meat from the beasts of the Ered Mithrin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Pried information out of Zhélruka at Skarháld (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","You discover the dwarf, Órug, standing among a few of his kin...","Talk to Dori at Skarháld","The Remnants of Grárik","Órug can be found in the heights of Skarháld.\
\
You have discovered the dwarf, Órug, standing with a small company of Longbeards, but you have not found Nori. You should speak to Órug.","Órug can be found in the heights of Skarháld.\
\
You have gathered a great deal of meat and firewood for the Longbeards in Skarháld. You should now deliver the supplies to Órug.","'I never thought to see Tharrazhâr with my own eyes....'\
\
Dori looks around and appears lost in thought for a moment.\
\
'Long ago, these mountains were rich and little explored, ${PLAYER}, but in his wisdom, Thorin I reshaped them into the Dwarf-kingdom of Grárik. It flourished for a time and great wealth was found beneath the peaks of the Grey Mountains, but that very wealth proved the doom of Grárik. Drawn by a powerful greed, it was the dragons of the wastes beyond that laid siege to Grárik. First fell Ablâk-khadar, the Stormwall, and its forges were extinguished. Second fell Tharrazhâr, and its keep was shattered. Third fell Aglâmbazar, the great Glimmerdeep, and it was there Smaug the Golden made his lair. Last fell Thikil-gundu, the Steel Keep and seat of Grárik, and I need not name the great cold-drake who slew King Dáin I and his son, Frór, along with countless others. The Dwarf-kingdom of Grárik was no more.\
\
'I tell you this so you understand, ${PLAYER}. Tharrazhâr... bah, Skarháld, belongs to Durin's Folk!\
\
'Are there any other Longbeards here in the remnants of Grárik? If Zádokh Flint-eye has not spoken true, gold will be the least of his troubles.'","Zhélruka can be found throughout Skarháld.\
\
Órug informed you that Nori continued the expedition to Thikil-gundu, but he knows little else. You should speak to the Zhélruka and try to pry information out of them.","Meat can be collected from any of the beasts in the Ered Mithrin, and fallen branches can be found within the Thornholt.\
\
Órug has asked for your aid in supplying his group, but he is uncertain if he can help Dori and Company.","'You have done us a great service, ${PLAYER}. I wish I could offer you more in return, but I have told you all there is to tell!\
\
'Nori and his company continued onward to Thikil-gundu without us, but not long after, the Zhélruka arrived....'\
\
Órug pauses for a moment and gazes into the fire.\
\
'I have known the Zhélruka to embellish their tales, but there are often hints of truth within them.\
\
'There are many Zhélruka in Skarháld... perhaps a few among them will have the answers you seek!'","Collect meat from the beasts of the Ered Mithrin (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collect fallen branches from the Thornholt (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Órug","'${PLAYER}....\
\
'How have you come to be in this place? Does my mind now play tricks upon me?'\
\
You inform Órug that you have come to the Grey Mountains with Dori and Company in search of Nori and his expedition.\
\
'It has been many days since last we saw Nori and the rest of his expedition. Before we came to Tharrazhâr, the expedition was beset by Orcs of Gundabad. The Orcs were slain to the last, but a few of our number sustained grave wounds in the battle. It was decided that we would remain behind in Tharrazhâr and work to rebuild it as it was in the time of Grárik. After we restored the first hall of the keep, I saw that a small company of Zhélruka had arrived. At first, I thought nothing of it, but then more arrived... and more... and more out of the East. They must number in the hundreds now! There has been little talk between our peoples, but we have at least agreed to put aside our separate tongues. It is Skarháld now... not Tharrazhâr or Brúgrad!\
\
'And so it has been! I wish there was more to be told, but I know only that Nori and his expedition continued to the south along the Men Angrún. It is the most well-travelled path to Thikil-gundu, but it was the work of Angmar... and even now, it is often travelled by the foes of the Longbeards.\
\
'I have done my best to tend the wounds of my kinsfolk, but I am no healer. All I know is that a warm meal and a hot fire would do much to aid us!'","Deliver the meat and firewood to Órug at Skarháld","Pry information out of Zhélruka at Skarháld (${CURRENT}/${MAX})"},
[12865]={"Reniaril beckons you to her.\
\
'You look like you can take care of yourself.'\
\
She studies you intently, while being aware of her surroundings.\
\
'My name is Reniaril. I'm in charge of patrols along these roads. We could use someone of your ability if you could help. Imloth Melui has got its hands full with restoration efforts, and we have supplies being carted all along these roads. Sometimes these supplies get lost. I'm concerned that Dindal's Overlook has been overrun by remnant Orcs. I used to oversee the supply routes from there but I can no longer patrol in peace.\
\
'Just follow the road east until you see a path through the forest to the north into the cliffside. Perhaps you could do us all a favour and clear the way.'","Reniaril is concerned that Dindal's Overlook has been overrun by remnant Orcs.","Talk to Reniaril","'I could hear the cries of the Orcs all the way from here.\
\
'So the deed is done then. Hopefully we won't have to deal with anymore stray Orcs in the area. With so many fleeing from the war, it can be difficult to track them all down.\
\
'Thank you for your service.'","The Remnants of Orcs","Reniaril has asked you to defeat any Orcs you find along the path to Dindal's Overlook.\
\
Dindal's Overlook can be found east of Imloth Melui.","You should inform Reniaril that Dindal's Overlook has been cleared of remnant Orcs.\
\
Reniaril can be found south of Imloth Melui and north-east of Arnach.","Has derrotado orcos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Orcs in Dindal's Overlook (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12866]={"Destroy siege engines (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Estandartes destruidos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Destroy Jangovar banners (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Jangovar encampment of Urûshoba struggles to rebuild enough to set siege to the Dale-lands once more.","Siege engines and banners can be found in the encampment of Urûshoba.\
\
You should destroy siege engines and banners.","The Remnants of Urûshoba","Completado","Destroyed siege engines (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'It would appear the Jangovar have begun to rebuild Urûshoba once again. The strategic location of their encampment has been nothing but trouble for the peoples of the North, and we cannot allow them to regain a foothold in the Dale-lands.\
\
'Travel to Urûshoba, throw down their banners, and ruin their siege equipment. Do this, and you will have my thanks.'","You have destroyed many siege engines and banners.","You have destroyed many siege engines and banners in the Jangovar encampment of Urûshoba. You have dealt a terrible blow to the Jangovar's efforts to rebuild."},
[12867]={"This is around where Oter said you should summon him to you, if you are ready to go to Cuthbald's Farm","Talk to Oter","Oter's brother must be on or around Cuthbald's Farm somewhere. With Wargs and Warg-riders around he likely didn't make it far.","Make your way to Cuthbald's Farm","Since his brother has been saved and has safely returned to Thrymm's Farm, Oter will be eager to speak with you there.","Speak with Oter","Speak with Ragnold","Ragnold will meet you back at Thrymm's Farm","'Not many of those that have been missing are found, and even fewer are found alive. I am one of the lucky ones, since you helped me find my brother! I am forever in your debt.'","'¡Ayuda!'","The Rescue in Cuthbald's Farm","Now that he is with you, speak to Oter before heading to Cuthbald's Farm.","Use the horn on the road south of Thrymm's Farm","Speak with Oter at Thrymm's Farm","'I am ready to come with you to find my brother. It isn't a good sign that he hasn't shown up yet, and that smoke rises from there. He is in trouble, so let us please hurry to Cuthbald's farm!'","Cuthbald's Farm is the closest of the outlying farms to Thrymm's Farm, where those working the farms were supposed to meet should the outlying farms be attacked. Oter made it there and is worried because his brother Ragnold has not yet arrived.","Find Cuthbald's Farm","Find and help Oter's brother","Oter's brother was trapped under debris, but appears to be all right. He looks eager to leave Cuthbald's Farm quickly, but would like to speak to you first.","Cuthbald's Farm is south-east of Thrymm's Farm.","Oter asked you to call him over to you on your way to Cuthbald's Farm. On the road south of Thrymm's Farm is likely a good spot to summon him.","'With the farms being attacked by Warg-riders, I expected my brother to be here by now. He works on Cuthbald's Farm, which is just to the south-east of here. I think I see black smoke rising in the distance from that direction!\
\
'I want to go look for him, but if Warg-riders are there I will be in as much trouble as he is. Can you help me find out what happened to him?\
\
'I need just a moment to collect myself before we go. Here, take this horn and summon me when you are ready to go, and I should be ready by then. Use the horn down the road south of here, and I will catch up with you.'","Oter's brother, Ragnold, has gone back to Thrymm's Farm. You should speak to Oter about saving his brother.","Cuthbald's Farm appears to be destroyed! Where is Oter's brother?","'I sincerely cannot thank you enough. I'm getting out of here as soon as I can, and you should do the same!'","'Any ${RACE} that would risk their life to save my brother is a friend of mine. Thank you, friend. I should probably follow him back to Thrymm's Farm, to make sure he makes it back all right.'"},
[12869]={"'Me gustaría saber más sobre lo que sucedió aquí, ${PLAYER}. ¿Por qué el puente está roto? Y... ¿no sientes un aire de inquietud en los orcos cercanos?\
\
'Si pudieras interrogar a uno de sus líderes, podrías descubrir algo sobre lo que sucedió.'","Papeles chamuscados recogidos","Se pueden encontrar orcos alrededor del Borde del Abismo en Nud-melek, cerca del puente destruido de Khazad-dûm.\
\
Debes interrogar a los orcos para descubrir qué sucedió en el puente de Khazad-dûm para causar tal inquietud.","Busca un orco en el Borde del Abismo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Svanr te ha pedido que te acerques al campamento de orcos en el Borde del Abismo para ver si hay alguna evidencia de por qué el puente de Khazad-dûm está destruido.","Svanr se encuentra en el puente destruido de Khazad-dûm, en el borde oeste del abismo en Nud-melek.\
\
Debes hablar con Svanr.","Lleva los papeles chamuscados a Svanr","'Por favor, descubre lo que puedas, ${PLAYER}. Me gustaría descansar aquí y contemplar el abismo.'","Los orcos inquietos del borde del abismo","Svanr lee los papeles chamuscados que le entregas.\
\
'Interesante... Veo la palabra \\qGhâsh\\q -- eso es fuego. Y miedo, terror, escrito en lengua común. Este grupo particular de orcos parece estar en movimiento, rápido, hacia el Valle del Arroyo Sombrío, ya que no son de aquí, ni desean quedarse aquí. Creo que buscan un breve respiro antes de continuar su camino.\
\
'Algo ciertamente los ha puesto inquietos, pero me pregunto qué podría haberlos hecho superar su miedo al fuego y al sol para seguir este camino. ¿Por qué se dirigen hacia el Valle?'"},
[12871]={"Talk to Felgúr","'Yes, I heard what the Ungoladan said. He was practically shouting! His suggestion is worth consideration. He is of little threat to us now that the enemy knows our location. He cannot skin-change and attack us himself, after all. Furthermore, several of my Rangers were injured in Rûkhor's attack and we are short-handed. Perhaps I can also pity someone who has lost everything....\
\
'Fine. You can tell Felgúr he has a deal. Just make sure you keep an eye on him. He has not earned my trust, just a jot of leniency.'","Felgúr has been taken prisoner, and is being kept in Echad Taerdim.\
\
You should talk to Felgúr.","Felgúr has asked you to propose a deal to Mablung on his behalf.\
\
You should talk to Mablung in Echad Taerdim.","Complete Instance: Ambush at Echad Taerdim","Talk to Mablung","'Good to see you came out of that attack unscathed, ${PLAYER}. I am no worse off myself, just the gnawed leg from earlier.'\
\
He chuckles and then groans, stroking his injured leg. You ask him how he came to Cirith Ungol and if he knew anything of the tower.\
\
'Ah... after you departed Lhingris, I worked up the courage to enter the tower myself. It was the site of a massacre! Dead Orcs and spiders everywhere, not much of anything alive inside. I continued on and found the gate wide open. I can tell by the look on your face that you know the gate of which I speak! Yes, I entered Torech Ungol itself! Barely made it out alive, but I slew a great many spiders while I could! I then found my way to that cursed forest, Taurlingol. Easier pickings, until that big one chanced upon me and my leg, thinking to have us both for dinner. Heh!\
\
'I will stay here for now. The Rangers are gracious enough hosts. Get out there with Legolas and slay some more spiders for me! As for the tower, hmm, I think the spiders have surely overtaken it by now. If the Orcs and their evil masters attempted to re-take it, they must have failed.'","'The Pale Herald has finally made his appearance. We must be cautious. A Gúrzyul is already a formidable opponent, but something about his Uruks unnerved me. Did you notice it as well, ${PLAYER}? They possessed the foul aura of dark sorcery. I must think on our next steps. If you would, please make sure the others were unharmed in the assault.'","Felgúr stares at the ground, grimacing. His former matriarch's words must have affected him. As you approach, he looks up and speaks, his voice almost cracking with emotion.\
\
'I must speak with you, ${CLASS}! Rûkhor will betray my people, I am sure of it! But they will never accept me as I am now.\
\
'I want to make a deal with the one in charge here! Tell that Mablung I will help him find my people and the Pale Herald if he helps me find a new life among Men. I can no longer hear the call of Mam Murgwid, but I can still sniff out my own kin.'","You have discovered much in Cirith Ungol, and the time has come to regroup with the Rangers of Ithilien.","'Come, let us return to Echad Taerdim.'","Talk to Atli","Legolas wishes to return to Echad Taerdim with an injured Atli Spider-bane.\
\
You should speak with Legolas near Taurlingol to begin the journey.","The Return to Echad Taerdim","'You have returned. Forgive me, but I overheard most everything. It is a small camp.\
\
'I am not sure I agree with Mablung's decision regarding the Ungoladan, but perhaps he can be of use to us.'\
\
He turns to Felgúr and speaks just loud enough for him to hear:\
\
'I will be watching you, Ungoladan. If you betray us, you will find an arrow between your eyes.'\
\
Felgúr looks terrified and nods enthusiastically. Legolas turns his attention back to you.\
\
'Atli's account of the tower is also troubling. It may have completely fallen to the spider-horde since we departed. The time has come for us to head towards the Winding Stair and Torech Ungol. We must race to find Rûkhor and the Ungoledain before their wicked plans reach fruition.'","Atli Spider-bane is resting at Echad Taerdim.\
\
You should see how Atli is faring after Rûkhor's assault.","Felgúr calls to you as you turn away from Legolas","'When you are ready, let us depart for Echad Taerdim. Atli needs rest, and his wounds need to be better-tended than I can manage out here. I am also curious to hear if Mablung has learned more from our Ungoladan prisoner.'","Habla con Legolas.","Legolas can be found in Echad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol.\
\
You should talk to Legolas.","Legolas has returned to Echad Taerdim, the Ranger camp in Cirith Ungol.\
\
You should talk to Legolas."},
[12872]={"Word has reached you that Faeron of the Grey Company has a plan for penetrating the defences of Seregost, and has asked for you by name. You should return to Agarnaith and see how you can help.","Faeron and Rhadrog stand before a large door","Complete: The Court of Seregost - Tier 2","Talk to Faeron","Faeron and Rhadrog are somewhere inside Seregost.\
\
You should find the Rangers.","The time to strike at the heart of Seregost has come. Meet with Faeron to discuss how you can help.","Faeron can be found at the Agarnaith Ranger camp.\
\
You should talk to Faeron.","Find the Rangers in Seregost","Complete: The Court of Seregost","Faeron is outside the Court of Seregost, in Agarnaith.\
\
You should talk to Faeron.","'I believe this is it, ${PLAYER}. Are you prepared to face the horrors within?'","Talk to Rhadrog","The Return to Seregost","Faeron is waiting for you at the Agarnaith Ranger camp.\
\
You should talk to Faeron.","Complete: The Bloody Watchers","'Ah, ${PLAYER}! Per usual, your timing is uncanny. The threat of Lhaereth's plague still exists, and the time to act is now. I hear you have discovered another way into Seregost. Is this true?'\
\
You explain that the Watching Stones in Seregost consider Lhaereth an enemy as well, and have allowed you safe passage to and from Seregost. \
\
'Watching Stones? Can we really trust such fell beings? We must take the risk.\
\
'Here is my plan. I have gathered some soldiers, and more will be coming. They will move into Kala-gijak and create a bulwark there. My hope is that this will trigger an attack from the majority of the forces left in Seregost, and distract Lhaereth from our true intentions.\
\
'That is where we come in. We cannot risk a full invasion, even if that were possible, because of the plague. Only the three of us are inoculated against it, and even then, I am unsure if we will survive direct exposure to it in a concentrated form.\
\
'We have no choice. The threat to our homelands is too great. We will form a small strike team and enter this den of evil ourselves. Gather some companions, be sure they are inoculated themselves, and meet us in Seregost. We will find a way to Lhaereth's throne room, and do what we can to end this threat. \
\
'And no, I will not allow Viznak to come this time. He is but a child, after all.'","'The day is won! You should be proud, ${PLAYER}. We would never have been successful without you. \
\
'The defeat of Dulgabêth and the departure of Lhaereth will mean another shakeup in the power structure of Mordor. This can only be good news for the Free Peoples!\
\
'I am certain this is not the last we have seen of Lhaereth the Stained. Her threat made that abundantly clear. We should celebrate while we can, but keep a wary eye out for her in our future travels in Mordor.'","Complete: The Court of Seregost.","'Here we are again, ${PLAYER}. I had hoped we wouldn't need to return to Seregost, at least not so soon! Alas, we must steel our hearts and put on our bravest faces. All the Free Peoples are counting on us now.'"},
[12873]={"Muchos años atrás, valientes aventureros se enfrentaron a Thrâng, el jefe de los Ghâshfra en esta misma arena. ¿Puedes resistir las llamas y derrotarlo?","El regreso a la Falla","¡Has salido ${PLAYERNAME:victorioso[m]|victoriosa[f]} de la Grieta de Nûrz Ghâshu, derrotando a Thrâng y sus Ghâshfra! Por tus esfuerzos, serás ${PLAYERNAME:recompensado[m]|recompensada[f]}.","Thrâng derrotado","Completado.","En lo profundo de la Grieta de Nûrz Ghâshu, Thrâng, el jefe de los Ghâshfra, está listo para enfrentarse a todos los que desafíen su poder.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando abandones la instancia.</rgb>","Completado","Te has encontrado en la arena de Thrâng.\
\
¡Debes derrotar a Thrâng!","Derrota a Thrâng"},
[12874]={"'So it is true! ${PLAYER} returns to the north.\
\
'I am sorry that the Trév Duvárdain have arrived late. I would have very much liked to speak to you at Eiricháv. An urgent matter had called me away. Soltakh has told me what you have accomplished. It seems we were right to not trust the Dourhands after all, though we should have taken the tower by your side.\
\
'I was secretly meeting with Hraubrek, the Chieftain of the Grímklettar, in the north. The Trév Duvárdain and the Grímklettar have much in common. We have a common enemy, share these lands, and have been dealt many hardships for both our kind. I thank you for your assistance on this day. The Trév Duvárdain, and all free hillmen owe you much.'","'Brathar Crack-helm, you had that coming. You have caused more than enough trouble in these mountains. No more, Dourhand.'","'I believe Brathar is lying. He wants nothing more than power. Even I believed that he was doing all this for the good of everyone under the subjugation of the Iron Crown. Now I saw the look in his eyes when we won but the Rhudaur-stone was missing. It was not the look of victory, it was the look of defeat.\
\
'Do with me what you will, but know that I will follow Brathar Crach-helm no longer.'","Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire can be found at Agal Dûn.\
\
You should talk to Domongart, Chieftain of the Trév Duvárdain, at the top of Tûr Fúar.","Talk to Mézto at the top of Tûr Fúar","'Well done everyone! This is a fine day for the Zhélruka. I knew this plan would work. That is why I came up with it after all! Ha, that will teach Durin to doubt the Zhélruka. I jest, ${PLAYER}. Durin's wisdom knows no bounds, even if he underestimates the resolve of the Zhélruka.'","'That crafty Claghórd. He must have known the Rhudaur-stone was moved! That is why he did not care if we took the Drearspire. A lingering question then remains. Where was the stone taken? Where did Claghórd retreat to?'","Talk to Domongart at the top of Tûr Fúar","'We do not need to see eye to eye, ${RACE}. In fact, I do not think we ever will.\
\
'Yes, talking to the Angmarim and accepting gifts from the Dourhands were all a ruse, for my real intentions were to form a secretive pact with the Trév Duvárdain.\
\
'While there has been many lives lost, including my own kin, I will not hold you accountable. The ends have justified the lives lost. As Gundabad is a sacred site to the dwarves, beneath this spire is the sacred city of my kind. It has been lost for so long. Now, the pilgrimage is complete for those of the Grímklettar who remain.\
\
'If you and the dwarves let us be, then we will let you live under the mountain in peace. We will keep Câr Bronach free of the Iron Crown. You have my word. Now, please leave. You are not needed here any longer.'","Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire, can be found at Agal Dûn.\
\
You should talk to Hraubrek, Chieftain of the Grímklettar, at the top of Tûr Fúar.","Reach the top of Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire","Talk to Brathar Crack-helm at the top of Tûr Fúar","Talk to Rethvárd at the top of Tûr Fúar","Talk to Prince Ingór at the top of Tûr Fúar","'I must say, my plan was mostly a success, even if Prince Ingór will certainly take most of the credit! I can not blame him though. We would not be standing where we are if not for Prince Ingór's invaluable leadership!'","Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire can be found at Agal Dûn.\
\
You should talk to Múta, Mézto, Prince Ingór, and Glóin at the top of Tûr Fúar.","The Rhudaur-stone","Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire, can be found at Agal Dûn.\
\
You should talk to Brathar Crack-helm and Rethvárd at the top of Tûr Fúar.","'The Rhudaur-stone must be sitting atop the Drearspire. We must hurry and secure the artifact!'","'Even if the Rhudaur-stone should belong to me, I had no intention of taking it! My plan was to destroy it! You do not believe me?\
\
'Bah! How was I supposed to know that the Rhudaur-stone had already been moved to parts unknown?!'\
\
Brathar clutches his chin in pain.\
\
'Was that punch really necessary, Glóin?!'","Talk to Múta at the top of Tûr Fúar","Talk to Glóin at the top of Tûr Fúar","The Rhudaur-stone is gone!","Talk to Hraubrek at the top of Tûr Fúar","Atop of the broken tower of the Drearspire sits the powerful Rhudaur-stone.","Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire, can be found at Agal Dûn.\
\
You should reach the top of Tûr Fúar."},
[12875]={"Jarl Gurthilm and his company have travelled to the stronghold of Uya Hujûm to deal their vengeance upon Zarhal Kôz and the Khundolar.","'The time has come to have our revenge on Lord Zarhal Kôz, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'By now, he must know we come for him. His scouts have been slain, his warriors cut down, and his archers split upon the roads. A coward to the last, he would sooner throw his own sons before us than face his death.\
\
'Uya Hujûm snakes upward into the Mountains of Shadow, and I would wager that he has taken refuge deep within their encampment. The Khundolar will not surrender, so we must cut a path through them. Their Master has brought shame to their order, and they will share in his fate. It is our way, and it shall be done.\
\
'This is not your battle, so do not think that you must aid us in this final task. If you do, though, you shall share in the reward!\
\
'Will you join us?'","Jarl Gurthilm can be found to the south-east of Aragorn's camp on the border of Dagorlad.\
\
You have defeated the Khundolar and their treacherous leader and should now speak to Jarl Gurthilm.","'Are you prepared, ${PLAYER}?","The Riches of Rhûn","Talk to Jarl Gurthilm in the southern reaches of Dagorlad","'We have won a great victory this day... and an even greater wealth of gold and Khundolar trinkets.\
\
'Those Khundolar dogs have paid for their treachery, and now all that remains is the journey home. With such a bounty, our travels will be slowed to a crawl, but we shall live as kings in Khand!\
\
'You have been an honourable companion, ${PLAYER}, and it is time that you received your reward.'","Jarl Gurthilm can be found across the river to the south-west of Uya Hujûm.\
\
You have rallied to Jarl Gurthilm's side and should now aid him and his company in seeking vengeance against the Khundolar.","Talk to Jarl Gurthilm"},
[12876]={"'¿Qué es esto? ¿Un juego? ¡Ja! Ya veo, ¿un acertijo de Gondor, eh? Bueno, has venido al hombre indicado, sin duda.\
\
'No, me temo que no puedo darte mi cuerno ni por un minuto —pues un cuerno es, en efecto, la respuesta— porque es mi deber y responsabilidad portarlo, Pero te daré algo que debería bastar.\
\
'Esta es la insignia de mi rango, como heredero del Senescal. Como puedes ver, muestra un cuerno sobre el Árbol Blanco de Gondor. Me atrevo a decir que ese erudito elfo quedará satisfecho con este símbolo.'","Lindir ha encontrado un nuevo acertijo para que resuelvas. Una vez más, está seguro de que la respuesta se encuentra en algún lugar de Imladris.","Lleva la insignia de Boromir a Lindir","'La respuesta a este acertijo está ciertamente aquí en Imladris, ¡pero puede que no lo esté por mucho tiempo!'","'¡Excelente! Has encontrado la respuesta. Me aseguraré de que esta insignia sea devuelta a Boromir.\
\
'Bien jugado. Confío en que el hecho de que el objeto no estuviera simplemente tirado en una estantería no fue un obstáculo.'","Lindir está con Bilbo en el Salón del Fuego en Rivendel.\
\
Bilbo te dijo que Lindir tiene un nuevo acertijo para ofrecer, uno que proviene de Gondor.","Habla con Lindir","La respuesta al acertijo de Lindir se encuentra en algún lugar de Rivendel.\
\
Lindir te ha pedido que encuentres un objeto que responda a su acertijo.\
\
\
Se necesita aliento\
Advertencia atendida\
Algunos llegarán\
Con espada y cuchillo\
Mi labor termina\
Hasta que se me necesite otra vez.","Encuentra la respuesta al acertijo de Lindir en algún lugar de Rivendel","'Mientras estabas fuera, Lindir me dijo que ha ideado algo interesante para nuestro juego. Al parecer, encontró un nuevo acertijo en el reverso de un viejo pergamino de Gondor.\
\
'Deberías hablar con él de inmediato... ¡Tengo curiosidad por conocer su acertijo!'","Lindir está con Bilbo en el Salón del Fuego de La Última Morada.\
\
Boromir te ha dado un símbolo que responde al acertijo de Lindir y te ha pedido que se lo lleves a él.","'A veces es difícil encontrar pergamino en el mundo de los Hombres, así que no me sorprende tanto encontrar un acertijo garabateado en el reverso de unas viejas crónicas de Gondor. Quizás algún joven escriba de la Torre tenía demasiado tiempo libre...\
\
'Resulta que la respuesta puede encontrarse en algún lugar de Rivendel:\
\
'Se necesita aliento\
Advertencia atendida\
Algunos llegarán\
Con espada y cuchillo\
Mi labor termina\
Hasta que se me necesite otra vez.'","El Buscador de Acertijos"},
[12877]={"Bilbo te ha pedido que lo ayudes en un juego de acertijos que está jugando con Lindir:\
\
A menudo sostengo tu mano,\
Pero no tengo manos con las que sostener.\
A menudo duermo en verano,\
Pero doy lo mejor de mí cuando hace frío.\
A menudo pierdo a mi pareja,\
Pero no siento pena, si he de ser sincero.","La respuesta al acertijo de Lindir está en algún lugar de La Última Morada en Rivendel. Lindir espera tu regreso en el Salón del Fuego.\
\
Lindir está esperando que le lleves la respuesta a su acertijo.","'¡Ja! Bien hecho. La respuesta encaja como un guante, ¿no es así?'","Habla con Lindir","'No pensé que este acertijo fuera muy difícil, pero parece que a veces los acertijos más simples son los más difíciles de resolver.'","Encuentra un objeto que resuelva el acertijo de Lindir","'Hola, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} . Me pregunto si podrías ayudar a un viejo hobbit que ya no es tan ágil como solía ser. Lindir y yo estamos jugando un amistoso juego de acertijos. Este es el último que me ha dado:\
\
'A menudo sostengo tu mano,\
Pero no tengo manos con las que sostener.\
A menudo duermo en verano,\
Pero doy lo mejor de mí cuando hace frío.\
A menudo pierdo a mi pareja,\
Pero no siento pena, si he de ser sincero.\
\
'Si he de ser sincero, ¡estoy bastante desconcertado! Habla con Lindir al respecto — podría ser que haya olvidado una línea o dos importantes.'","'Pensé que por una vez intentaría uno de esos acertijos hogareños que tanto le gustan a Bilbo, en lugar de un misterio elaborado del saber élfico. Y parece que, con su mente en las nubes de la poesía sindarin, nuestro amigo aquí no puede resolver los acertijos tradicionales del estilo hobbit.\
\
'Pero te daré la pista que le di a Bilbo: La respuesta a este acertijo se encuentra aquí, en la Última Casa Amable. Solo encuentra la respuesta y tráela aquí para resolver el acertijo.'","Encontraste un par de guantes de trabajo.","Lleva los guantes a Lindir en La Última Morada","Lindir está con Bilbo en el Salón del Fuego de La Última Morada\
\
Bilbo te ha pedido que hables con Lindir sobre el acertijo que le presentó al viejo hobbit.","Juego de Acertijos"},
[12878]={"'¿Este acertijo te ha dejado perplejo? ¡Quizás tu rápida respuesta al acertijo de Lindir fue solo una coincidencia!'","'¿Y qué podría ser más hogareño que una simple escoba de ramitas? ¡Incluso los Elfos tienen que limpiar de vez en cuando, al parecer!'","Se ha encontrado una escoba de ramitas.","Bilbo está junto a Lindir en el Salón del Fuego\
\
Lindir te dijo que era el turno de Bilbo de presentar un acertijo y que deberías hablar con él.","Lleva la escoba de ramitas a Bilbo Bolsón en el Salón del Fuego","'¡Lindir me ha engañado! Estaba hurgando entre mi pequeño acervo de saber élfico buscando algún poema o relato que encajara con su verso, pero debí haber pensado en cosas más prosaicas, después de todo. ¡Me pregunto si podrá resolver mi próximo pequeño enigma!\
\
'Me gustaría ofrecer uno de mis poemas sobre la sabiduría élfica, pero temo más la risa gentil de Lindir que la espada de un trasgo. Así que seguiré su ejemplo y haré otro acertijo hogareño, uno que estoy seguro podrás resolver encontrando otro objeto aquí en La Última Morada. Aquí va:\
\
'Larga barba tengo de cerdas duras,\
Mas ni mentón ni mejilla en que posar.\
Muchas manos me toman, sin una caricia,\
Mas siempre soy la primera en limpiar la porquería.'","Habla con Bilbo","El Hacedor de Acertijos","Encuentra un objeto que resuelva el acertijo de Bilbo","La solución al acertijo de Bilbo se encuentra en algún lugar de La Última Morada, en Rivendel. Bilbo espera tu regreso en el Salón del Fuego.\
\
Bilbo está esperando que le lleves el objeto que resuelve su acertijo.","Bilbo tiene un acertijo propio para que lo resuelvas:\
\
Larga barba tengo de cerdas duras,\
Mas ni mentón ni mejilla en que posar.\
Muchas manos me toman, sin una caricia,\
Mas siempre soy la primera en limpiar la porquería.","'¡Parece que tenemos aquí a ${PLAYERNAME:un experto[m]|una experta[f]} en acertijos!\
\
'Es el turno de Bilbo de presentar un acertijo... deberías hablar con él y descubrir qué me propondrá. Bilbo está junto a Lindir en la Sala del Fuego.'"},
[12879]={"Entrega el legado de Celebrían a Elrond","'Dije que no sé dónde se encuentra la cámara que contiene el legado de Celebrían, pero puede que pueda ayudarte a entrar cuando la encuentres.\
\
'El acertijo en sí es la llave de la cámara. Si en tus viajes cerca de Imladris encuentras una cámara sellada, esas palabras pueden ofrecerte paso al interior. Debería haber una roca frente a la entrada. Coloca tu mano sobre la roca y recita el verso.\
\
'Me sorprendería que la joya estuviera en el propio valle de Imladris, ya que estos jardines y arboledas cuidadosamente cuidados son frecuentados con demasiada frecuencia por los Elfos como para que una cámara pueda estar fácilmente oculta. No tengo dudas de que está cerca, no muy lejos de Imladris... quizás en el Páramo Alto.'","'¿Qué noticias traes de tu búsqueda?'","Glorfindel no sabe dónde se encuentra el legado de Celebrían para Arwen, pero te ha dado algunos consejos que pueden ayudarte a encontrarlo.","'¡Pensar que la cámara ha permanecido sellada tanto tiempo más allá de su momento! ¡Incluso aquellos contados entre los Sabios pueden ser imprudentes, al parecer!\
\
'Pero debo agradecerte por tu perseverancia, ${PLAYERNAME:Maestro[m]|Maestra[f]} de los Acertijos. Buscas la verdad en todas las cosas, aunque eso te lleve a la oscuridad —tu habilidad y astucia te devuelven a la luz una vez más.'","'¿Has encontrado la cámara, verdad? La joya debería estar dentro.'","'Sí, en efecto, esta es la joya misma... el legado de Celebrían. Por favor, llévala a Elrond, pues es su deber entregársela a su hija.'","Elrond está en la biblioteca de Rivendel.\
\
Glorfindel te pidió que llevaras el legado de Arwen a Elrond.","Recoge el legado de Celebrían","La cámara élfica perdida está en algún lugar del Bosque de los Trolls, en las cercanías de Rivendel, probablemente en el Páramo Alto. Glorfindel espera tu regreso fuera de la casa de Elrond, junto a la cascada.\
\
Glorfindel te dijo que buscaras la cámara en el Páramo Alto y te aconsejó colocar una mano sobre una roca junto a la entrada de la cámara élfica y recitar los versos del acertijo. El legado de Celebrían para Arwen, una joya blanca, debería estar en algún lugar dentro de la cámara.","${PLAYERNAME:El Maestro[m]|La Maestra[f]} de los Acertijos","Legado de Celebrían encontrado","Lleva el legado de Celebrían a Glorfindel"},
[12880]={"'Esas viejas palabras... ay, esperaba no tener que recordar aquellos días oscuros. Pero sé que Lindir debe tener buenas intenciones. En efecto, si hubiera algún legado de su madre que pudiera dar a Arwen, lo haría con gusto.\
\
'Pero el significado de las palabras es un misterio para mí, y aquellos que podrían haberlo sabido se han ido hace muchos años.\
\
'Me sorprende, ya que esto ha venido a mi mente después de tanto tiempo. Glorfindel estuvo presente en el momento en que estas palabras fueron escritas. Nunca pensé en hablar con él sobre este tema. Búscalo junto a las aguas que caen fuera de mi casa y pregúntale el significado de las viejas palabras.'","Habla con Glorfindel","Habla con Elrond","Glorfindel está fuera de la casa de Elrond, junto a la cascada.\
\
Elrond te ha indicado que hables con Glorfindel sobre el acertijo.\
\
La joya de la luna,\
Consagrada en el agua,\
De madre a hija\
Se otorga una bendición.\
Naves zarpan al oeste,\
Olvidando toda pena,\
Arriban al día siguiente,\
A las islas de los benditos.","Bilbo está parado junto a Lindir en el Salón del Fuego, en La Última Morada.\
\
Lindir te dijo que hablaras con Bilbo para conocer el acertijo sin resolver.","Un último acertijo que concierne a la Casa de Elrond en Rivendel aún no ha sido resuelto.","'Bueno, esto fue escrito por la esposa de Elrond, Celebrían, quien hace mucho tiempo zarpó hacia el Oeste. Justo antes de partir de la Tierra Media, inscribió estas palabras. El verso probablemente no fue pensado como un acertijo, pero su significado sigue siendo oculto, incluso para su propia familia.Espero que disculpes mi pobre traducción al oestron. El acertijo dice así:\
\
'La joya de la luna,\
Consagrada en el agua,\
De madre a hija\
Se otorga una bendición.\
Naves zarpan al oeste,\
Olvidando toda pena,\
Arriban al día siguiente,\
A las islas de los benditos.\
\
'Puede que el Maestro Elrond pueda decirte algo más sobre estas palabras. Sería espléndido que el acertijo pudiera resolverse después de todos estos años, y aún más maravilloso si algún legado perdido pudiera ser hallado y entregado a la dama Arwen.'","Elrond está en su biblioteca en La Última Morada.\
\
Bilbo cree que Elrond puede saber más sobre el acertijo.\
\
La joya de la luna,\
Consagrada en el agua,\
De madre a hija\
Se otorga una bendición.\
Naves zarpan al oeste,\
Olvidando toda pena,\
Arriban al día siguiente,\
A las islas de los benditos.","'Has demostrado ser ${PLAYERNAME:un experto[m]|una experta[f]} en resolver acertijos. Bilbo y yo hemos estado contemplando últimamente un acertijo de lo más interesante — uno cuya respuesta aún no se conoce. Este acertijo parece referirse al linaje de la Casa de Elrond y puede ser de gran importancia si se resuelve.\
\
'Por una vez, no podemos decir con certeza que la respuesta realmente se encuentre en Imladris, pero es seguro que el acertijo está relacionado con Rivendel más que con cualquier otro lugar.\
\
'Bilbo puede contarte más, pero creo que para conocer toda la historia de este acertijo tendrás que hablar también con otras personas.'","Habla con Bilbo","'¿Un acertijo? ¿Un misterio? Si Elrond me lo hubiera preguntado, podría haber desentrañado estas últimas y tristes palabras de su esposa hace mucho tiempo.\
\
'Había una espléndida gema blanca, una verdadera joya de la luna como dice el verso, que hace mucho fue escondida en una cámara secreta. Este es el legado de Celebrían que estaba destinado a Arwen. Ni siquiera yo sé dónde fue escondida esa cámara, pero estoy seguro de que no pudo haber estado lejos de Imladris.'","El Buscador de Acertijos"},
[12881]={"Derrota a Glothrok el Infame","Derrota a Forzunk","Glothrok el Infame se encuentra en la Gran Escalera, al noreste de la Guardia Orca.\
\
Thithrand parecía inquieto ante la visión de un poderoso trasgo montado sobre un huargo de aspecto aún más imponente. La pareja entró en la Gran Escalera al frente de los jinetes de huargos y no ha vuelto a ser vista desde entonces.","El jinete y su montura","'Uno a uno, los orcos avanzaban por las galerías en dirección a la entrada de la Gran Escalera. A la cabeza marchaba un trasgo portaestandarte montado sobre un huargo marcado por innumerables batallas. Oí cómo sus tropas coreaban su nombre al divisar la entrada de su nuevo hogar.\
\
'Sus tributos descansaban sobre andas arrastradas por otros jinetes de huargos. Glothrok el Infame, azote de las Montañas Nubladas y líder de los jinetes de huargos, entró al frente de ellos.\
\
'Nunca había visto a un trasgo tan confiado cabalgar una bestia tan aterradora. Deben ser destruidos y, para lograrlo, debes internarte en la Gran Escalera, al noreste de la Guardia Orca.'","Los jinetes de huargos se abren paso por los riscos de las montañas y entran y salen de las sombras de Moria con facilidad. En la Gran Escalera, un líder y su envejecida montura han acudido a doblar la rodilla ante Igash el Fanático y Mazog.","Habla con Thithrand en la Guardia Orca","Glothrok el Infame derrotado","'Entra en la Gran Escalera, al noreste de la Guardia Orca, y encuentra al jinete de huargo trasgo Glothrok el Infame. Acaba con él y con la bestia que monta antes de regresar conmigo.'","Thithrand se encuentra en la Guardia Orca, al suroeste de la Gran Escalera.\
\
Deberías regresar con Thithrand para comunicarle la noticia de tu victoria.","Forzunk derrotado","'Has hecho bien al derrotar a este enemigo. Estoy seguro de que ese trasgo era uno de los más poderosos que he visto jamás.\
\
'Pensar que todos estos enemigos se estaban preparando para asaltar Lothlórien… Creo que tus esfuerzos demostrarán ser de gran valor, ${PLAYER}.'"},
[12882]={"Speak with Bregdal at the War-stead of the King's Men","Mordor Orcs can be found throughout Taur Drúadan.\
\
You should defeat Mordor Orcs to allow Bregdal safe passage to the Rohirrim encampment.","Defeat Mordor Orcs in Taur Drúadan (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Bregdal is atop Amon Dîn.\
\
You should speak with Bregdal.","Bregdal needs your assistance in tracking down the Rohirrim that ride to aid Gondor.","'${PLAYER}, welcome!\
\
'I believe that the Rohirrim have renewed their spirits with the news I brought from Gondor. They now realize that their aid will surely change the tides of victory. There is no way I would be able to return to Gondor by myself though. Too many enemies stand between here and Pelennor. I shall ride with the Rohirrim, guiding them with what knowledge of the enemy I have.\
\
'Thank you for your assistance back at the Orc encampment. It is something I shall surely never forget!'","Bregdal is at the War-stead of the King's Men, near Eilenach.\
\
You should speak with Bregdal.","'${PLAYER}! It is difficult to point out, but I believe I saw a camp-fire flickering in the woods to the north-west.'\
\
Bregdal points in the direction, showing you the approximate location.\
\
'It will be difficult getting there with all the Orcs about though. Would you defeat some, then meet me in that section of woods I pointed out?'","Speak with Bregdal atop Amon Dîn","Hike to the top of Amon Dîn","After a hard climb, you make it atop the rocky Amon Dîn","'Before you return to the Wose village, let us climb Amon Dîn. Perhaps there we will have a better vantage point and can look for signs of the Rohirrim.'","Has derrotado orcos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Amon Dîn is located in eastern Taur Drúadan.\
\
You should climb atop Amon Dîn and meet with Bregdal.","The Rider's Errand"},
[12884]={"Shoe Brynmód","'You have my thanks, friend. \
\
'It pains me to leave behind the steeds that trod upon the road before we discovered the Enemy's traps, but with fewer mounts to carry our men through the forest ahead, our journey to Gondor grows more complicated. The wounded steeds shall heal in time, but I hope we are enough to turn the battle to our favour.\
\
'Our own steeds were fortunate enough to avoid the traps on our approach to Ost Rimmon, but they have ridden long and their shoes must be worn.\
\
'Ost Rimmon surely bears no shortage of horseshoes, even in war-time. Gather them and shoe our steeds while I ready Hutha and Ulf for our ride ahead.'","Collect sets of horseshoes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ulf is at Ost Rimmon.\
\
You have spoken to Hutha and should now speak to Ulf as well.","The Riders Three","Talk to Ulf","Shoed Brynmód","Shoe Flyting","'${PLAYER}, can it be? In such dark times, I was unsure our paths would cross again.\
\
'I am sorry for the manner of our parting - we knew not how to move forward for what seemed like days after the Battle of the Hornburg. Our warden and my dear friend, Léofdag, was slain in the fighting just before dawn.\
\
'If only he had seen what we had! The ride of the Wizard and the forest that marched forth to harry our foes - such things cannot be believed if one had not been there at the battle's ending.\
\
'Time to rest has been a rare gift as of late, but our foes have laid traps for our riders and even now, we are working to disarm them before any more of our steeds come to harm.\
\
'Out beyond the gates of Ost Rimmon, they have laid jagged caltrops along the roadway. If you aid the others in removing them, we shall be able to resume our journey unhindered.'","Once known as the Riders Four, the company of Burnoth, Hutha, and Ulf struggle to ready and ride for war while still feeling the loss of their long-time friend, Léofdag.","Shoed Gesith","Destroyed caltrops on the road outside of Ost Rimmon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The steeds of the Riders Three can be found at the stables of Ost Rimmon.\
\
You have collected enough horseshoes and should now shoe the steeds of the Riders Three.","Talk to Burnoth in Ost Rimmon","'Ah... ${PLAYER}, I was gladdened to see you among the men here in Ost Rimmon. \
\
'In truth, I have been deeply troubled since the Battle of the Hornburg. The loss of my friend tears at me, and as it does, I feel a lingering guilt for the fates of the others that fell that day. Oh, that life would allow the time for mourning, but never has that been the lot of a warrior. \
\
'I have more yet to say about Léofdag, but I shall speak not of it here. There are too many eyes upon us...'","Collected sets of horseshoes (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'It is good to see you again, ${PLAYER}. These have been difficult times for the others and me, but war halts not at the wishes of a few Men. To think it has been but eleven days since we fought before the Hornburg... much has happened in so short a time! Much both good and ill...\
\
'Alas, indeed, for poor Léofdag. His absence weighs heavily on us, but I fear Ulf has felt it most keenly of us all.\
\
'We must soon speak of the manner of our parting, but now is not the time. It is better that you speak to Ulf - to see a familiar face might ease his pain, even if only for a moment.'","Shoe Gesith","Destroy caltrops on the road outside of Ost Rimmon (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Shoed Flyting","Talk to Hutha","Hutha is at Ost Rimmon.\
\
You have shoed the steeds and should now speak to Hutha as Burnoth asked.","Sets of horseshoes can be found within Ost Rimmon in the Beacon Hills.\
\
Burnoth has asked you to aid him in shoeing the horses before he and his fellows set off.","Burnoth can be found within Ost Rimmon in the Beacon Hills.\
\
You have destroyed the caltrops and should now return to Burnoth.","Caltrops can be found on and around the road outside of Ost Rimmon.\
\
Variags have laid traps along the road to slow the forces of Rohan. You should disarm these traps before any more horses are wounded."},
[12887]={"'The more we explore Umbar-môkh, the Undercity, the more danger we uncover.\
\
'My guards have established a foothold in the southern crypts of the Umbar-môkh, My scouts have patrolled outward, mapping Umbar-môkh as best they dare. Recently, several of my patrols were attacked by the dead. Nûru, the Captain of my guard, tells me they are coming from west of Mekab-kuphâr, my guard outpost, and that their attacks have become more frequent, and violent.\
\
'Far to the west of the crypts there is an area my scouts call Sektakhâb, the Silent Sepulcher. There the Dead roam freely.\
\
'I need you to make your way there and cull these dead. The last thing Umbar needs is the Dead preying on innocent Umbari civilians, or my guards.'","Defeat crypt-sentries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja, the Hall of the Kindred.","Defeated crypt-bellowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Rising Tide of Dead","Defeated crypt-sentries (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat crypt-bellowers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I am relieved. This issue of the Dead had been weighing on me. Thanks to your brave deeds, Umbari citizens and my guards can sleep much easier tonight.'","Defeated crypt-walkers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat crypt-walkers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Khôltekh in the Hall of the Kindred","Khôltekh has asked you to venture into Sektakhâb and cull the rising population of the Dead.","Khôltekh has asked you to venture into Sektakhâb and cull the rising population of the Dead. You can find them west of Mekab-kuphâr, the Temámir guard outpost in southern Khabârkhad."},
[12888]={"'Drostan ya no existe. Es Soltakh ahora, y que encuentre la paz.'","'Te agradezco tu clemencia, ${PLAYER}.'","El rito de Clúcath","Regalo de Tasgall recogido","Osbail está junto al trono de Crannog en Aughaire, Camran está en la isla central del asentamiento, y Tasgall sigue cazando bestias de las colinas al norte de Aughaire y al sureste de Nád Nathair.\
\
Crannog te ha aconsejado hablar con el pueblo de Aughaire para aprender lo que puedas sobre el desafío que se avecina: el Clúcath con los Trév Duvárdain.","El plan de Crannog ha sido revelado: tu Fém consiste en representar a los Trév Gállorg en el Clúcath contra los Trév Duvárdain y sus amos Angmarim.","'¡Te saludo, ${PLAYER}! ¡Luchaste bien y con valentía!'","'Los del Búth Sánkhas cantarán durante mucho tiempo tus hazañas, ${PLAYER}.'","'Drostan ya no existe. Se ha convertido en Soltakh, y su vida está por delante de él.'","Crannog está en su trono en Aughaire, al oeste de la isla central del asentamiento.\
\
Has salido ${PLAYERNAME:victorioso[m]|victoriosa[f]} del Clúcath con los Trév Duvárdain y ahora deberías hablar con Crannog.","'Que Fail-á-Khro sea nuestro de nuevo es una alegría para mí.'","'Luchaste con valentía y bien, ${PLAYER}, y de tus acciones nació Soltakh.'","'El tiempo del Clúcath está casi sobre nosotros, y debes prepararte para combatir; a pesar de tus habilidades contra los guerreros de los Trév Gállorg, no será suficiente. Necesitas un aliado mayor: el conocimiento.\
\
'Muchos entre los Trév Gállorg presenciaron la ilícita ruptura de los ritos del Clúcath en la que el padre de Nekhtan fue asesinado, y puede que tengan palabras con las que evites un destino similar.\
\
'Osbail, junto a mi trono, puede decirte cómo encontró la muerte Násan y quizás darte alguna manera de evitar un destino similar. Camran, en la isla central de Aughaire, te dirá a cuál de los guerreros de los Trév Duvárdain podrías enfrentarte. Tasgall, cazador de bestias de las colinas al sureste de Nád Nathair, puede haber aprendido algo durante su estancia que te sea de ayuda. Habla con estos tres, y con cualquier otro que pueda ayudar, y regresa a verme pronto. El Clúcath no esperará para siempre.'","'¡Te saludo, ${PLAYER}! Aún no he regresado a Aughaire, pues he estado vigilando Nád Nathair para asegurarme de que las bestias de las colinas no resurjan. Rona lo entenderá.\
\
'¿Has sido ${PLAYER:elegido como guerrero[m]|elegida como guerrero[f]} para el Clúcath? ¡Me quedé helado de asombro! Creía que la muerte de Násan y la traición de los Trév Duvárdain habían puesto fin a ese rito para siempre. ¿Venciste a Nekhtan en combate singular? No puede haberse sentido satisfecho con eso; si Avair es elegida como guerrera de los Trév Duvárdain, Nekhtan lo verá como una oportunidad perdida de vengarse del asesino de su padre.\
\
'He tallado una pequeña figura con el diente de Murragrath, y me gustaría que la tuvieras. Llévala entre tus pertenencias. Quizás te traiga fortuna en las pruebas que se avecinan.'","Crannog está en su trono en Aughaire, al oeste de la isla central del asentamiento.\
\
Crannog te espera para hablar contigo y poder viajar juntos a Fail-á-Khro para el Clúcath con los Trév Duvárdain.","'Recordaremos durante mucho tiempo tus hazañas en el Clúcath, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} .'","'Habla con el pueblo de Aughaire para aprender todo lo que puedas del rito del Clúcath. Debes usar su conocimiento para prevalecer.\
\
'Nekhtan creía que sería él quien se enfrentara a los Trév Duvárdain en el Clúcath, y está enojado por haber sido privado de ello. Tiene el genio vivo. ¡Si te importa lo que piensa, habla con él! Pero como jefe, creo que debe aceptar su debilidad por sí mismo, a su debido tiempo.'","'¡Finalmente, hemos sido redimidos, , y hemos triunfado sobre los Trév Duvárdain y sus amos angmarim! Násan ha sido vengado, y Domongart ha pagado por sus traiciones.\
\
'El que se llamaba Drostan se ha unido a los Trév Gállorg, pero su nombre se ha perdido; a partir de ahora se le conocerá como Soltakh, \\qEl que ha cambiado.\\q La que se llamaba Avair no aceptó esta elección; ahora no es ni Trév Gállorg ni Trév Duvárdain. Ha hecho mucho mal y solo podía ver eso en los demás; aunque Nekhtan podría haber perdonado su pasado, siento que ella no podría. Ahora vaga por las tierras sin caminos, una mujer sin nombre ni hogar.\
\
'Tu Fém ha llegado a su fin, y te saludo no solo como jefe de los Trév Gállorg, sino también como Crannog, humilde miembro de la tribu de Aughaire. Quizás el regalo de Tasgall te haya traído buena fortuna después de todo, y quizás no. Que seas tú quien decida si crees en él o no, pero cree siempre en ti mismo, ${PLAYER:amigo[m]|amiga[f]} ${PLAYER}. Considero que tú haces tu propia fortuna.'","'¿Has adquirido la sabiduría de mi pueblo? Por tu bien y el de los Trév Gállorg, espero que sí, ${PLAYERNAME:Sureño[m]|Sureña[f]}.\
\
'El Clúcath comenzará pronto en Fail-á-Khro. Habla conmigo cuando estés preparado, e iremos juntos a encontrarnos con el destino.'","Habla con Crannog y viaja a Fail-á-Khro","'Los Trév Gállorg controlan de nuevo Fail-á-Khro, como lo hicimos antaño.'","'Tus hazañas en el Clúcath harán una digna canción, ${PLAYER}.'","'Debería haberlo sabido, cuando me ayudaste contra los huargos que vinieron a Fasach-larran, que traerías gran honor a los Trév Gállorg. Pero temo que esto pueda ser demasiado para ti, ${PLAYER}. Los Trév Duvárdain ya han roto las reglas del Clúcath una vez; ¿quién dice que no lo harán de nuevo?\
\
'Nuestro gran guerrero, Násan, se enfrentó a Avair de los Trév Duvárdain mientras el sol se levantaba sobre Fail-á-Khro. Durante un tiempo, todo parecía como debía ser: primero Avair tenía la ventaja, y luego Násan tomó la ventaja. Pero a medida que el Clúcath continuaba, el jefe de los Trév Duvárdain, Domongart, se volvió inquieto. A su lado se sentaban dos extraños, Hombres de Carn Dûm, se cree.\
\
'Domongart se levantó de repente y dio un tremendo grito: ¿una señal preestablecida? La atención de Násan se desvió, y en ese momento Avair lo derribó al suelo. El Clúcath terminó, pero Domongart no estaba satisfecho y exigió que Avair matara a su indefenso oponente. Esto hizo ella, y quedó claro que los Trév Duvárdain, nuestros antiguos parientes, estaban irremediablemente corrompidos. El hijo de Násan, Nekhtan, juró vengar a su padre, pero tú debes hacerlo en su lugar, porque lo has vencido y no es apto para representar a los Trév Gállorg en el Clúcath. Estate atento, ${PLAYER}, cuando comience el Clúcath. Debes estar preparado para cualquier cosa.'","Crannog está en su trono en Aughaire, al oeste de la isla central del asentamiento.\
\
Has hablado con algunos de los Trév Gállorg y deberías regresar a ver a Crannog como te aconsejó.","'Estoy seguro de que los Trév Duvárdain no han olvidado cómo destruiste los estandartes que ondeaban sobre Tór Gailvin, y yo tampoco. Te diré lo que sé sobre lo que podrías enfrentar en el Clúcath.\
\
'La guerrera que mató a Násan y mancilló el rito se llama Avair, y es una maestra de las artes sangrientas. Ha matado a muchos de los nuestros en los años desde el último Clúcath, y su nombre infunde miedo en los corazones de todos excepto Nekhtan, quien ha jurado acabar con ella. Domongart, líder de los Trév Duvárdain, seguramente piensa que Nekhtan será nuestro guerrero; puede presentar a Avair con la esperanza de que Nekhtan se deje cegar por la ira y sea fácilmente derrotado. Es difícil decirlo, y hay otros.\
\
'Drostan de los Trév Duvárdain es feroz, pero su batalla más reciente terminó en una retirada cobarde; luchó con Fonghala durante un día y una noche antes de escapar. Prefiere luchar a distancia, y teme los peligros de enfrentarse cara a cara con un oponente. Seguramente está deseando tener la oportunidad de redimir su honor. Quizás no te haya sido de ayuda en absoluto, ${PLAYER}. Aun así, espero que puedas aprovechar lo que te he dicho.'","Habla con Crannog","'Vamos ahora al Clúcath, ${PLAYER}. Espero que estés preparado.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>Esta es una misión en solitario y no puede completarse con una Comunidad.</rgb>"},
[12889]={"Collect Anduin moss (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Ingelfled","The River Provides","'Hello there. Have you come to help the village? I have a task for you, if you are willing.\
\
'Much of the nearby flora is valuable to us, in one way or another. I am low on two items in particular: reeds and moss from the nearby river-bank. The reeds can be dried and woven into baskets and mats. The moss can be soaked in medicine and applied to wounds. If you could gather some of both, I would be very appreciative! You can get to the river quickly by taking the path east through the hills. Perhaps the fishermen at the docks could also use your help.'","Ingelfled can be found in the village of Arhaim in Duskenvale.\
\
You should deliver the moss and reeds to Ingelfled.","Many useful plants grow along the river Anduin. Ingelfled has asked you to gather some to help the village of Arhaim.","Anduin moss and river reeds can be gathered from the river-banks of the Anduin in Duskenvale.\
\
You should collect Anduin moss and river reeds.","Collected river reeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Ingelfled carefully inspects the reeds and moss clumps you gathered.\
\
'These will do nicely, thank you ${PLAYER}. Since you did so well on this task, I have another for you! This one involves my portly friend here.'\
\
She pats the pig sitting next to her.","Collect river reeds (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Collected Anduin moss (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12890]={"The second southernmost watch-tower can be found on the edge of the Great River in the northern Wold, south-east of Langhold.\
\
You should ride to the watch-tower and ensure that all is well.","'Hail, ${CLASS}! Are you on patrol?\
\
'You may ride on, friend. There is nothing out of the ordinary here -- just the ordinary dangers of the plains.'","The southern tower reports no danger","The central tower reports no danger","'Hail, Rider! If rider you are... that is not quite a war-steed, but I suppose it will do for now.\
\
'You are on patrol, yes? I am afraid we have spotted movement on the ford -- Easterlings, most like.\
\
'You should ride to the tower on Anduin's edge and see what they have to report. We are safe... for now.'","The men of this tower have spotted Easterling movement at the ford","'I will think on the threats of the brigands, ${PLAYER}, but in the meantime, I would ask you to perform the patrol of the ford watch-towers.\
\
'We do this regularly, but I would like to keep my riders close, in case those fool brigands get it into their empty heads to attack the town. I will welcome them... with spears and arrows! Let them come.'","The highest watch-tower can be found on the tallest hill overlooking the Great River in the northern Wold, slightly north of the first tower.\
\
You should ride to the watch-tower and ensure that all is well.","'Hail, traveller. Are you on patrol this week? All is clear here; you may ride on.'","Speak to a watchman at the northern central tower","The central watch-tower can be found on the edge of the Great River in the northern Wold, slightly north of the first tower.\
\
You should ride to the watch-tower and ensure that all is well.","'Easterlings are upon us! They have gathered at the ford, and begin to swarm the river-banks on this side. Their numbers are still small -- I believe we still have a chance to fend them off.'","Utred has long kept watch against the passage of foes across the ford, and he has asked you to perform a regular patrol of the River Watch forts.","Speak to a guard at the second southernmost watch-tower","The River Watch Patrol","The watch-tower at the Great River's edge can be found north of the high tower, down the slopes towards the water.\
\
You should speak with the watchman at the river-edge tower.","Speak to a guard at the central watch-tower","Speak to the watchman guarding the northernmost tower"},
[12891]={"Defeat zizani near Charganpâta (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Kôrzan in Sen Chatâk with news of your success.","Return to Kôrzan in Sen Chatâk","Defeated zizani near Charganpâta (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The river betrays us. She has been our ready companion for years, but now she's abandoned us.\
\
'Nothing that we cannot fix, however! It is the zizani. They have gotten quite aggressive, and moved into our favourite spots along the river. They feed on the same fish that we hunt.\
\
'I am a fisher, not a warrior! And even if I was, the zizani are large and fierce. But you look like a fierce sort! Perhaps you could deal with these zizani, that we may fish again in peace? They make their camp near the foetid ponds of Charganpâta.'","The River's Sting","The fisher Kôrzan tells you that the local zizani have muscled the fishers of Sen Chatâk out of their spots along the White-wrath River. Defeat these zizani so that the fishers may return.","The fisher Kôrzan has requested you deal with the nearby zizani, who have moved into the best fishing spots along the White-wrath river. The zizani can be found clustered near the foetid ponds of Charganpâta. Charganpâta is north-east of Sen Chatâk.","'Thank you. I believe nature is once more in balance, and the river can now prosper, along with our people. And I do so love to fish upriver.'"},
[12892]={"El camino está despejado","Albin Cotonorte está en la Granja de Cotonorte.\
\
Albin Cotonorte se alegrará de saber que Nibs está listo y el camino está despejado.","'Con el lobo fuera, el camino a Dwaling ahora está despejado. Es una buena noticia porque muchos de Dwaling suelen bajar para el mercado. Traen su cristalería y la cambian por nuestros productos.\
\
'Albin Cotonorte, ahí arriba en la Granja de Cotonorte, querrá saber que por aquí estamos listos y que el camino está despejado.'","'El camino finalmente está despejado.'","'¿Está todo listo con Nibs? ¿Y dices que el camino a Cebadabilla también es seguro? ¡Has estado ocupado!'","Se ha despejado el camino y se ha derrotado al lobo.","Habla con Albin Cotonorte"},
[12893]={"El Camino es Nuestro","Los enanos del Mirador de la Gran Excavación desean marcar la Extensión Solitaria como un paso ahora propiedad de los enanos, y de ninguna otra criatura de Moria.","Planta una bandera para reclamar la Extensión Solitaria para los enanos","'¿Has visto ya la Extensión Solitaria? Es un puente que conecta la Gran Excavación con la Sala Vigesimoprimera de Zelem-melek, y es un punto de control vital para nuestra expedición.\
\
'Si es seguro, deberías plantar una bandera de los enanos allí. ¡Mientras esté en pie, sabremos que la Extensión Solitaria está en manos de los enanos de Khazad-dûm!'","Sót está en el Mirador de la Gran Excavación de Moria.\
\
Debes regresar con Sót ahora que el puente hacia la Sala Vigesimoprimera ha sido reclamado por la expedición de enanos.","Se ha plantado una bandera de enano en la Extensión Solitaria","La Extensión Solitaria se encuentra siguiendo el camino hacia el este más allá de la Cámara de Enfriamiento desde el campamento del Mirador de la Gran Excavación.\
\
Debes dirigirte a la Extensión Solitaria y plantar una bandera de los enanos allí.","'¡Bien hecho, ${PLAYER}! Mientras esa bandera esté en pie, la Extensión Solitaria estará segura para los miembros de esta expedición y todos los Pueblos Libres que deseen usar este camino una vez más. Fue una tarea pequeña, pero significativa.'","Regresa con Sót en el Mirador de la Gran Excavación"},
[12895]={"'You have done well, ${PLAYER}. While there can never be an ideal time for such a journey, I believe our best opportunity has arrived.\
\
'The journey shall be long, but I trust in your efforts in the Harrowdale, and I know my people will remain safe and sheltered from the White Hand. I can only hope my men at Dunharrow have finished readying the camp.\
\
'When you are ready, we will lead my people to safety at Dunharrow.'","Talk to Éowyn outside Meduseld","'The time has come, ${PLAYER}! Kingstead faces harsh times, and Dunharrow remains the only place to keep my people from the White Hand and their savagery.\
\
'Through our labours, the people of Kingstead stand ready to journey to Dunharrow. We shall travel south through the Harrowdale and climb the Stair of the Hold to Dunharrow. It is there we shall join my men at the camp they have prepared and wait for word from Théoden King. \
\
'You have done well to prepare my people, and I am confident the path south will be free of danger through your efforts. When I am certain that my people and I are ready, we shall begin the journey!'","The Road to Dunharrow","Éowyn can be found outside Meduseld in Edoras.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>You must complete the quests 'Edoras: In Need of Cheering-up', 'Book 12, Chapter 5: Eyes of Edoras', and 'Book 12, Chapter 6: Through the Net' before Éowyn's people can depart for Dunharrow.</rgb>","Éowyn can be found outside Meduseld in Edoras.\
\
You have finished readying Éowyn and her people. You should now speak to Éowyn.","Talk to Éowyn at Dunharrow","Prepare Éowyn and her people to journey to Dunharrow","Prepared Éowyn and her people to journey to Dunharrow","'You have aided the people of Rohan far beyond anything I could have expected, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'Your efforts in the Eastemnet, and now here in Kingstead show well your care for my people. There remains much to do in these grim days of war, but I and the others can rest more easily knowing the ally we have in you.\
\
'We shall remain here at Théoden King's order, for the people shall be safe from the Enemy. Wander not too far, ${PLAYER}, for I am sure our paths will cross again!'","Éowyn, Mágla, and Ellen Fremedon have made their preparations, and now, they stand ready to guard the people of Kingstead as they travel to Dunharrow.","'My people and I have made ready! Let us lead my people to safety at Dunharrow.'","Talk to Éowyn","DNT -- Players will not see","Éowyn can be found outside Meduseld in Edoras.\
\
You have prepared the people of Middlemead and the Harrowdale for their journey to Dunharrow. You should now speak to Éowyn.","Éowyn can be found with the people of Kingstead on the Firienfeld at Dunharrow.\
\
You have defended the people of Rohan as they made shelter. You should speak to Éowyn."},
[12896]={"Athradnir is anxious to hear what has become of the Malledhrim host who marched east to Emyn Lûm, for the closer the Elves draw to Dol Guldur, the more perilous the journey becomes.","Fuirgam should be among the Malledhrim at their stronghold in Emyn Lûm.\
\
You should seek Fuirgam and establish a line of communication between the Elves of Emyn Lûm and the Dourstocks.","Talk to Fuirgam in Emyn Lum","The Road to Emyn Lûm","'Fuirgam is a commander among the host that marched east to Emyn Lûm -- you should speak with him first.'","'We have split into many factions in order to organize our assault on Dol Guldur. While we feel that this is the best way to plan our offence, we worry very much during those periods in which we hear nothing from our kindred while they establish their footing.\
\
'It is not safe to send scouts out until we hear from the advancing party, so we wait. If you are going to Emyn Lûm, will you keep an eye out for the host that marched thence? They will welcome your presence gladly, for we are stretched in every direction.\
\
'Emyn Lûm is a dangerous wilderness to the east of here, closer to Dol Guldur. You should seek Fuirgam, for he is a commander of that faction. Be wary, ${PLAYER}; keep your wits about you! We do not know what evils lie yonder.'","'Mae govannen! How fare my kin in the Dourstocks? I am glad you have come -- I was anxious for word from Athradnir. Now that we have established a line of communication, there will be but one more small burden lifted from my shoulders.\
\
'There is much to be done between marches, as I am sure you can understand. Will you be staying with us for a while?'"},
[12897]={"Mounted uruks can be found on the Road to Thornhope.\
\
Holenmal has asked that you clear mounted uruks from the Road to Thornhope.","'The road to Thornhope is not yet cleared, and more battles are yet to be fought, but you have won some great victories today.'","Mounted uruks are marauding across the north of the Entwash Vale, closing off the road to Thornhope and threatening any effort to reclaim the town.","Talk to Holenmal at Eaworth","Holenmal is at Eaworth.\
\
Holenmal is waiting to speak with you about your victories along the road to Thornhope.","Defeat mounted uruks on the road to Thornhope (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'If we have any hope of reclaiming Thornhope for the people of Rohan, the road to the north must be kept clear and open. If we cannot travel along those paths, then there is no chance Thornhope will be ours ever again.\
\
'The road is currently being patrolled by groups of mounted uruks. Roving bands move through the hills to the east and west of the road itself. While the enemy holds this ground, Thornhope will never return to our control.\
\
'Speak with me when you are ready to ride north.'","Defeated mounted uruks on the road to Thornhope (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","<rgb=#FF0000>Completing Aiding the Eastemnet will cancel this quest</rgb>","'Let me know when you are ready to depart for the road to Thornhope.'\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>This is an instanced public questing area.</rgb>","The Road to Thornhope"},
[12898]={"Habla con Glorfindel en Rivendel","Instancia La batalla por Erebor completada","El Maestro Elrond te convoca a la Última Morada","Espera a que Elrond te convoque.","Completa la instancia La batalla por Erebor","A Gandalf el Gris le preocupan los recientes movimientos en el Este. Se pregunta qué ha sido de sus aliados y enemigos del pasado.","'Amigo mío, como sabes, hace muchos años se libró una gran batalla al pie de la Montaña Solitaria. Ahora, con los problemas que se agitan en el Este, estoy preocupado.\
\
'Deseo saber qué ha pasado con nuestros aliados y enemigos del pasado. El Maestro Elrond en Rivendel está preparando un Consejo, que incluye representantes de todos los pueblos y muchas tierras. Quizás él tenga más información sobre los problemas.\
\
'¿Estás dispuesto a viajar a Rivendel en mi nombre? He organizado el viaje más rápido posible a Imladris.'","Deberías reunir a tus aliados y emprender las misiones que te han encomendado Glorfindel, Legolas y Boromir.\
\
Glorfindel desea que rescates un huevo de águila de los gigantes de piedra de las Montañas Nubladas. Legolas te ha pedido que encuentres a los exploradores de Thranduil en las Hondonadas Enmarañadas. Boromir sugiere que invadas la Ciudad de los Trasgos y te ocupes del nuevo Gran Trasgo.","Instancia Huida a la Montaña Solitaria completada","Habla con Boromir en la casa de huéspedes de Rivendel","'${PLAYER}, Lord Glóin de la Montaña Solitaria habló de un emisario del Señor Oscuro que vino a buscar noticias de Bilbo. Lo rechazaron, pero el emisario los amenazó con la guerra.\
\
'Deberías hablar con Gimli, el hijo de Glóin, aquí en Rivendel para saber más sobre sus preocupaciones.'","Glorfindel está cerca del arroyo fuera de la Última Morada. Legolas y Boromir están en las Casas de Huéspedes en Rivendel.\
\
El Maestro Elrond te sugirió que hablaras con sus invitados Glorfindel, Legolas y Boromir sobre el paradero y los tratos de los amigos y enemigos que participaron en la gran batalla en la Montaña Solitaria.","Instancia Las Campanas de Valle completada","Completa la instancia escalada del Asiento del Gran Trasgo","Habla con el Maestro Elrond en la Última Morada en Rivendel","Habla con Elrond en La Última Morada en Rivendel","Completa la instancia Los fuegos de Smaug","'Has hecho bien por los Pueblos Libres de la Tierra Media, ${PLAYER}, y mereces una gran canción... pero me han llegado noticias nefastas, y ahora debo pensar en el curso de acción correcto.\
\
'Te convocaré de nuevo cuando haya tomado una decisión. Gracias.'","El camino a la Montaña Solitaria","Completa la instancia Huida a la Montaña Solitaria","'He visto que tu ayuda ha sido de gran beneficio para los Hombres de Valle y los Enanos de la Montaña Solitaria... sin embargo, ha habido un gran costo.\
\
'Gandalf llegó no hace mucho... dile lo que has aprendido, tanto de tus aventuras en el extranjero como de nuestras palabras juntos. Dile que la ayuda no vendrá del Norte, ni para los Pueblos Libres ni para el Señor Oscuro....'","El Maestro Elrond está en la Última Morada en Rivendel.\
\
Gandalf te ha enviado a hablar con el Maestro Elrond sobre los problemas en el Este.","Completa la instancia escalada del Pico de Iorbar","'Hola, buen ${RACE}. Mientras viajaba aquí desde Gondor en el sur, fui molestado por trasgos de las Montañas Nubladas.\
\
'Por sus palabras y por los rumores que escuché de los Hombres dispersos en el extranjero, considero que un nuevo Gran Trasgo ha surgido entre ellos. Pensé que esto podría ser motivo de preocupación para el Maestro de Rivendel, ya que Imladris se encuentra a la sombra de las montañas.\
\
'Ojalá pudiera emprender yo mismo la gloriosa aventura de derrumbar las cuevas de estos trasgos sobre sus orejas, pero mi encargo es de una importancia mucho mayor. ¿Quizás podrías emprender tú esta aventura?'","'${PLAYER}, eres un ${CLASS} de cierta importancia. Quizás puedas ser de ayuda para mi padre.\
\
'Fui enviado aquí con noticias nefastas de las que solo hablaré en el Consejo del Maestro Elrond, pero hay otro asunto de importancia que debe ser tratado. A mi padre le preocupa la creciente agitación de las Grandes Arañas. Nuestros exploradores rastrearon el origen hasta las Hondonadas Enmarañadas en el sur del Bosque Negro, pero no hemos sabido nada de ellos desde entonces.\
\
'¿Viajarás a las Hondonadas Enmarañadas con tus aliados y descubrirás qué les ha pasado? Se te proporcionará un viaje rápido.'","Habla con Legolas en la casa de huéspedes de Rivendel","Deberías reunir a tus aliados y emprender las misiones de Gimli para ayudar a Valle y la Montaña Solitaria.","'Bienvenido, ${PLAYER}, y bien hallado. Entiendo que Gandalf el Gris te ha enviado a mí. Eso está bien, porque de hecho tengo conocimiento de nuestros aliados y enemigos de antaño... o más bien, aquellos que han venido a pedir consejo.\
\
'Si yo fuera tú, hablaría con Glorfindel junto al arroyo fuera de mi casa. Tiene amigos entre las Grandes Águilas y ha recibido noticias nefastas.\
\
'Además, habla con el príncipe elfo Legolas y Boromir, Capitán General de Gondor, en las casas de huéspedes. También traen noticias del mundo exterior.'","'Ah, ${PLAYER}, ${RACE} de gran reputación. Supongo que el Maestro Elrond te ha hablado de mis problemas, o al menos de algunos de ellos.\
\
'He recibido noticias de Gwaihir, el Señor del Viento, un rey de las Grandes Águilas de las Montañas Nubladas. Los gigantes de piedra han robado un huevo de los nidos de las Grandes Águilas y se proponen comérselo.\
\
'Gwaihir está muy angustiado, pero no puede encargarse del asunto él mismo. Ha pedido ayuda, y quizás tú puedas dársela. Viaja al Pico de Iobar y rescata el huevo de las Águilas.'","Habla con Gandalf el Gris en la Última Morada en Rivendel","El Maestro Elrond está en la Última Morada en Rivendel.\
\
Deberías volver con el Maestro Elrond para recibir más instrucciones.","Gandalf el Gris está en la Última Morada en Rivendel.\
\
Elrond te dijo que le llevaras tus noticias a Gandalf el Gris.","'Ah, amigo mío, el Maestro Elrond dice la verdad. Un emisario vino y pronunció palabras aterradoras al Rey Dáin. No revelamos ninguna información que le fuera de utilidad, y nos advirtió de la guerra.\
\
'No hemos recibido noticias de enemigos que se muevan sobre nuestros reinos, pero si te encuentras viajando por el Norte, ¿podrías determinar qué amenazas, si las hay, son evidentes allí?'","Completa la instancia escalada de las Telarañas Enmarañadas","Gimli está en la Casa de Huéspedes en Rivendel.\
\
Elrond te pidió que hablaras con Gimli sobre el emisario del Señor Oscuro que vino a Erebor.","El Maestro Elrond está en la Última Morada en Rivendel.\
\
Deberías volver con el Maestro Elrond con noticias de tus éxitos.","El Maestro Elrond está en la Última Morada en Rivendel.\
\
Deberías volver con el Maestro Elrond y contarle tu historia.","'Entonces, ¿los Elfos del Bosque Negro están sitiados por arañas y los Muertos? No podemos esperar ayuda de ellos, en ese caso. Los trasgos de la Ciudad de los Trasgos están ocupados riñendo entre ellos, así que preveo que supondrán poca amenaza. Las Grandes Águilas siempre han sido mis amigas, y confío en que esa amistad no decaiga.\
\
'Lamento que la gente de Brand y de Dáin no acuda en ayuda de Gondor, pero al menos reconforta saber que los enemigos que marchen contra ellos no se volverán contra el Reino del Sur.\
\
'Gracias, ${PLAYER}, por tu ayuda.'","Espera a que el Maestro Elrond te convoque de nuevo","Completa la instancia Las campanas de Valle","Instancia Los fuegos de Smaug completada"},
[12899]={"Encuentra el cruce de caminos al oeste de Herne","Los caminos cerca de Herne","Brioc está en los confines del norte de la ciudad de Herne, esperando tu informe.","'Herne se alza sobre una meseta rocosa con vistas a Páramo Rojizo, y el camino da un amplio rodeo alrededor de la ciudad. ¿Crees que podrías ir a los cruces de caminos al oeste y al norte de Herne, y <rgb=#00FF00>buscar</rgb> cualquier señal de peligro? Un humor sombrío se ha asentado sobre la ciudad en los últimos días, y cada vez me preocupa más que algún mal haya puesto sus ojos en esta ciudad donde nací.\
\
'No recuerdo que fuera así en todos mis años, y mi hermana y yo hemos vivido aquí toda nuestra vida.'","Brioc te pidió <rgb=#00FF00>buscar</rgb> amenazas para Herne en dos cruces de caminos cerca de la ciudad: uno al oeste y otro al norte.","'¿Crees que podrías ir a los cruces de caminos al oeste y al norte de Herne, y <rgb=#00FF00>buscar</rgb> cualquier señal de peligro? Un humor sombrío se ha asentado sobre la ciudad en los últimos días, y cada vez me preocupa más que algún mal haya puesto sus ojos en esta ciudad donde nací.'","Habla con Brioc en Herne","Este es uno de los cruces de caminos que Brioc quería que explorases","'¿No viste nada preocupante ni al oeste ni al norte de Herne? Eso es un alivio. Gracias por tranquilizarme.'","Brioc quiere que explores en busca de peligros potenciales en el camino que rodea Herne.","<rgb=#00FF00>Busca</rgb> peligros para Herne en el cruce de caminos occidental","No hay amenazas evidentes en este cruce de caminos al noroeste de Herne","Encuentra el cruce de caminos al noroeste de Herne","<rgb=#00FF00>Busca</rgb> peligros para Herne en el cruce de caminos del norte","Todo está tranquilo en este cruce de caminos al oeste de Herne"},
[12902]={"Talk to Kyrstig","Kyrstig can be found near Ibdêkh-buzru, the Thing-fold.\
\
You should talk to Kyrstig.","'Did you clear out those snow-beasts? Thank you, ${PLAYER}. Snow-beast ambushes are not a pretty sight, and now our reinforcements need not fear one. They will have enough to worry about with all these hobgoblins and Angmarim around!'","The Roaring Stones","Defeated Stormbár","Defeat Stormbár","Snow-beasts have made their home in Grymmclúd, the Roaring Stones.","Defeat snow-beasts in Grymmclúd (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'I discovered a pack of vicious snow-beasts living in a craggy area near the Clovengate. I have taken to calling it Grymmclúd, or the Roaring Stones, because you can hear the echoing roars from quite far away. So? What are you waiting for?'\
\
Kyrstig looks at you expectantly.\
\
'I don't need to convince you that a pack of dwarf-eating beasts so near the road is dangerous, do I? Please clear the place out, ${PLAYER}!'","A pack of snow-beasts has been discovered in Grymmclúd, near the Clovengate.\
\
You should defeat snow-beasts and their pack-leader, Stormbár, in Grymmclúd.","Defeated snow-beasts in Grymmclúd (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12903]={"Barad Tharsír se encuentra al sureste de Tinnudir, en Barandalf, al otro lado del Brandivino.\
\
Unitaria Tilden te ha pedido que derrotes a los miembros de la banda de saqueadores que ha tomado Barad Tharsír, así como a sus miembros más infames: Anselmo Boscoso y Ogden Roblealto.","'Tenemos que hacer algo con los saqueadores de tumbas, ${PLAYER}. He hablado con los montaraces sobre este asunto, pero están sobrepasados. Deben concentrarse en las amenazas a las tumbas de sus antepasados en Men Erain y las criptas de Annúminas, aun cuando otras zonas corran peligro.\
\
'Al sureste de Tinnudir, las arenas de Barandalf y la hierba de las dunas son barridas por las brisas que provienen del Brandivino, pero ahora las suaves brisas transportan también los ásperos gritos y las órdenes de una banda de saqueadores de tumbas. Han establecido un campamento en las ruinas de Barad Tharsír, al otro lado del Brandivino, y temo que dentro de poco cruzarán el río y pasarán a las tierras pacíficas del sur.\
\
'Serás recompensado si logras derrotar a los saqueadores de tumbas en Barad Tharsír, incluidos algunos de sus miembros más infames: el arquero, Anselmo Boscoso, y el perrero, Ogden Roblealto. Quizás quieras traer a un amigo o dos, porque el lugar está plagado de esos tipejos desagradables.'","Unitaria Tilden está en el campamento de los montaraces en la isla de Tinnudir, al noroeste de Barandalf y al oeste de Parth Aduial.\
\
Unitaria está esperando a que le comuniques que has derrotado a los saqueadores en Barad Tharsír.","'Barad Tharsír está al sureste de Tinnudir, en Barandalf, al otro lado del río Brandivino. Serás recompensado si logras derrotar a los saqueadores de tumbas allí antes de que crucen el río y pasen a las pacíficas tierras del sur. Busca también a Anselmo Boscoso y a Ogden Roblealto y pon fin a sus crueles legados. No estaría de más que trajeras a un aliado o dos, pues muchos saqueadores de tumbas merodean por esa ruina.'","Derrota a Anselmo Boscoso","'La promesa de un tesoro saca a relucir lo peor de los hombres.'","'Barad Tharsír es más seguro gracias a tus esfuerzos.'","Ogden Roblealto derrotado","Anselmo Boscoso derrotado","Saqueadores de tumbas derrotados en Barad Tharsír (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Derrota a los saqueadores de tumbas en Barad Tharsír (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los saqueadores de Barad Tharsír","Unitaria Tilden teme que los saqueadores de tumbas hayan tomado el control de las ruinas de Barad Tharsír en Barandalf.","'¿Has derrotado a Anselmo y a Ogden? ¡Me alegra oírlo y saber que los saqueadores tienen menos control sobre Barad Tharsír que antes!\
\
'¡Te doy las gracias, ${PLAYER}! Por favor, acepta esta recompensa con mi gratitud.'","Derrota a Ogden Roblealto"},
[12904]={"Habla con Eliot Bencroft en Rantost","'Una vez que hayamos alterado a los saqueadores de tumbas, podremos hacer una señal a los Montaraces para que vengan con un grupo más grande.'","Eliot Bencroft está en la esquina sureste de Rantost.\
\
Eliot Bencroft querrá oír que Rantost se ha debilitado hasta el punto de quedar expuesto a un asalto mayor.","'El caos reina en el campamento. Parece que ha llegado el momento de lanzar la verdadera ofensiva.'","Ayuda a Eliot Bencroft en Rantost","Los ladrones de Rantost","La isla de Rantost es donde los saqueadores de tumbas han establecido su campamento central. Allí se guarda gran parte de la historia.","Ayuda a Wal Simpkins en Rantost","Ayuda a Leighton Kipps en Rantost","Hay varias cosas que hacer en Rantost para perturbar las operaciones de los saqueadores de tumbas.","'Los saqueadores de tumbas están mucho más organizados de lo que pensábamos, y Rantost es el núcleo de su villanía. Todo lo que saquean de las tumbas y criptas de Evendim pasa por aquí.\
\
'Llevamos un tiempo observando, y a cada uno se nos ocurre una forma de entorpecer sus esfuerzos. Si podemos reducirlos lo suficiente, podríamos darles a los Montaraces la oportunidad de atacar. Esto les permitiría acabar con los saqueadores de tumbas, recuperar sus reliquias y fortalecer la amistad restaurada entre Ost Forod y Tinnudir.\
\
'Habla con mis asociados aquí sobre lo que creemos que debe hacerse. La lista no es larga, pero debería tener un gran impacto.'"},
[12905]={"Talk to Raghda-gûn","The Roc","'Finally, a visitor who has the sense to address me with any respect. I greet you. You may call me Raghda-gûn. You come bearing a warning for me? I will hear it.'","A stranger has offered you coin for stealing a Roc's egg.","Itho has asked you to steal a roc's egg, a most heinous act.\
\
You should warn any rocs you find. Rocs may found at Aklâradum, a cliff south of Halrax.","'Hello there, stranger. Fancy making some coin? I have a job for only the most capable of adventurers, and you have just the right kind of look about you.\
\
'Have you heard of a roc? Vicious, nasty creatures they are. Massive birds with talons like daggers, beaks strong enough to pierce the hull of even the sturdiest ships.\
\
'Well, I represent a wealthy buyer who is interested in acquiring one of these beasts for himself. Fancies if he raises the thing from birth, it'll be loyal. Could you imagine? The power of a roc tamed.\
\
'So here's the job: Go to the roc's nest south of here and nab one of their eggs. Bring it back to me, and you'll have enough coin to live comfortably for the rest of your life anywhere in the world.'\
\
As you recall, Rocs are intelligent creatures, not the mere beasts that this brigand claims them to be. It may be worth warning the nearby rocs that someone has designs on their eggs."},
[12906]={"El árbol de los nidos","'¿Has encontrado ya el nido de los crebain, ${PLAYER}? Intenta buscar en el extremo norte del valle hacia el este.'","'Has reducido el número de crebain en la zona, pero desafortunadamente más volverán para reemplazar a los que has matado.\
\
'Para expulsarlos por completo, tendrás que deshacerte de su medio de descanso y refugio. Sin duda han encontrado un gran árbol en el que anidar... por mucho que me disguste la idea, tendrás que quemar ese árbol. Solo entonces los crebain se retirarán de Eregion.\
\
'Regresa al valle hacia el este y busca el árbol donde anidan. Probablemente se encuentre cerca de una gran cantidad de crebain. Cuando lo encuentres, quémalo por completo.'","Los crebain del norte de Eregion se han establecido en estas tierras, encontrando buenos lugares para anidar.","El árbol de los nidos de los crebain se encuentra en el valle al este de Gwingris.\
\
Thaliondir te ha pedido que quemes el árbol de los nidos de los crebain.","Habla con Thaliondir en Gwingris","Destruye el árbol de los nidos","'Tus esfuerzos contra los crebain nos han ayudado en nuestra lucha contra la Mano Blanca. Gracias, ${PLAYER}.'","Thaliondir está en Gwingris, al oeste del árbol de los nidos.\
\
Deberías volver a ver a Thaliondir con las noticias de tu éxito.","'Excelente trabajo, ${PLAYER}. Con su lugar de anidado destruido, lo más probable es que los crebain de esta zona regresen a las Tierras Brunas.'"},
[12907]={"'¡{Bendito[m]|Bendita[f]} seas! ¡Gracias a ti, por fin tendré la oportunidad de quitarme por fin el frío de mis viejos huesos y la mugre de la piel!\
\
'¡A la casa de baños!\
'Oh, y por favor, acepta esto como recompensa.'","Weth se encuentra en Zigilgund, al sur de las fuentes de vapor.\
\
Has derrotado a la gran sierpe Ringdagnir. A Weth le complacerá saberlo.","Ringdagnir derrotada","Ringdagnir se encuentra en la parte oeste de los manantiales termales cerca de Zigilgund.\
\
Weth te ha pedido que derrotes a la gran sierpe invernal Ringdagnir.","'Parece que nuestros esfuerzos hayan agitado a Ringdagnir, una enorme sierpe invernal. Hasta que sus ataques no sean contenidos, no tengo esperanza de poder darme un baño.\
\
'¿Podrías hacer una cosa más por mí? ¿Derrotarías a Ringdagnir para asi poner fin a la amenaza de las sierpes invernales?\
\
'Puedes encontrar a Ringdagnir en los manantiales de agua caliente cerca de Zigilgund.'","'¿Qué estás haciendo aquí? Ringdagnir no va a dejarnos en paz por sí solo, ¿sabes? ¡Ve allá donde el agua desprende vapor y ahuyéntalo!'","Vuelve a ver a Weth con las noticias de tu éxito","La raíz del problema","Derrota a Ringdagnir","La raíz del problema con las grandes sierpes invernales que han estado atacando los canales enanos parece estar en una sierpe particularmente violenta apodada Ringdagnir."},
[12908]={"Bring the Uruks' orders to Quickbeam","The tent of the Uruk-commander lies somewhere in the Vale below Quickbeam's home.\
\
You should search for orders in the tent of the Uruk-commander.","'Ta-room. Yes, well, there are rather a lot of Orcs, are there not? I suppose you cannot drive them all away.\
\
'Well then, we shall have to learn more about them and get to the root of why they are here... and what purpose Saruman has for them.\
\
'They must have a leader... if you can find his dwelling, perhaps you might learn more.'","'Hoom, does the foul leader of the burárum yet live?'","'Hoom-hom. Saruman intends to march south, and soon I think. My fellows are unlikely to decide on their purpose before then, for they are not so quick to judge as I.\
\
'That is unfortunate, I think, for so many Orcs can cause a great deal of trouble, yet at least they will be out of our forests for a time.\
\
'It also means that fewer will be here, near Isengard. Hoom, ta-rum, now that presents possibilities!'","Quickbeam is at his home upon the north-eastern slopes above Nan Curunír.\
\
You should bring the Uruks' orders to Quickbeam.","Quickbeam feels that to get at the root of the Orc-problem, he will need to learn more about the Uruks' purposes... and those of Saruman.","The Uruk-commander is at his tent.\
\
You have been discovered by the Uruk-commander.","You examined the Uruks' orders, but you hear a sound behind you...","La raíz del problema","Defeat the Uruk-commander (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Have you found the burárum's orders yet, little ${RACE}?'","Examine the Uruks' orders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","You defeated the Uruk-commander"},
[12909]={"'It seems that the Elf Erymeldir agrees...the source of the venom is likely within the nearby caves.\
\
'If we could enter ourselves, it would be a simple enough matter to clear out any vermin within...but alas, a full-grown Ent is much too large for such a place.\
\
'If you could see fit to gather your friends and take a look around inside, it might be a great relief to us. I suppose we could even consider helping the Elves with their little problem....'","You have discovered a band of Orcs in the lower stretches of the cavern.\
\
You must locate their leader and defeat him in battle in order to drive the rest from the caverns.","The Roots of Fangorn","Protect the roots of Fangorn","Thickbark believes that something may be awry within the caves that cut beneath the Limlight Falls, where the roots of Fangorn gather to drink from the pure waters of the river.","You have discovered the entrance to the roots of Fangorn","Thickbark has asked you to gather your fellowship and explore the interior of the caves that stretch beneath the Limlight Falls.\
\
These caves can be found a short way from the Limlight Glade, on the western side of the river.","Discover the roots of Fangorn"},
[12910]={"Return to Tálbiral in Laivárth","Spiders and Huorns in the area are threatening Laivárth. Tálbiral has asked you to thin their numbers and destroy any blighted spider eggs you find.","Destroy blighted spider eggs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The grove will now be safer for a time thanks to you and your efforts, ${CLASS}.\
\
'Laivárth still has much work to do, so your help here is appreciated. Thankfully it will now be easier to fight the blight with fewer of those beasts nearby.'","Blighted spiders killed (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Return to Tálbiral and inform him that you have reduced the number of spiders and Huorns threatening Laivárth.","Blighted Huorns killed (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Kill blighted spiders (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'The creatures to the north have become more daring in recent days. It has begun to make my efforts here in the grove more difficult.\
\
'I ask that you go and put a stop to the Huorns and spiders that are becoming more aggressive from their blight infections. Be sure to destroy the eggs of the spiders as well.'","Blighted spider eggs destroyed (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Rot Runs Deep","Kill blighted Huorns (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12911]={"Cánnakh se encuentra en Aughaire.\
\
Deberías hablar con Cánnakh.","Habla con Cánnakh","'Saludos, viajero. Soy Cánnakh. Si tienes un momento, debo comunicarte noticias graves.\
\
'Criaturas de la Grieta de Nûrz Ghâshu han salido de la sombra y el fuego para irrumpir en estas tierras. ¡Caminan por Angmar! Temo que busquen algo y que todas sirvan a la misma causa. He estado investigando antiguos relatos para descubrir su propósito, pero me temo que tendrán éxito antes de que yo lo logre. Apostaría a que algún poder ancestral yace enterrado en Angmar y que estas bestias tratan de desenterrarlo. ¿Me ayudarás derrotando a estas criaturas antes de que Angmar sea sumida en la oscuridad por sus planes impíos?'","Cánnakh necesita ayuda, pues Angmar vuelve a estar bajo amenaza.","Durante tu ausencia, nuevas amenazas han surgido en Angmar. Cánnakh, un erudito de Aughaire, busca la ayuda de un héroe valiente mientras trabaja para desenterrar un oscuro secreto del pasado.","Las amenazas errantes de Angmar"},
[12913]={"Brangil requires assistance as Evendim faces a renewed threat.","'Hail ${RACE}, what brings you to Evendim this day? There is danger out there my friend.\
\
'Calenglad has tasked me with scouting the lands for new threats. He has heard my latest report and now I will share what I have seen with you if you are willing to listen.\
\
'The enemy has taken a renewed interest in Annúminas. Strong enemies now roam the hills and lakeside looking for hidden artifacts and treasures. We could use your assistance in dealing with these threats.'","In your absence, new threats have come to Evendim. Brangil, a Ranger in Tinnudir, seeks the assistance of a brave hero as he works to stop the advancement of the enemy upon Annúminas.","Speak with Brangil","Brangil can be found in Tinnudir.\
\
You should speak with Brangil.","The Roving Threats of Evendim"},
[12914]={"Ostasänt requires assistance as Forochel is once again under threat.","Ostasänt can be found in Sûri-kylä.\
\
You should speak with Ostasänt.","'I am looking for a warrior. Is that you?\
\
'I have recently returned to Sûri-kylä from a hunting expedition. I saw beasts of such evil. Forochel does have its share of deadly beasts, but these were unlike anything I have seen before. I fear a darkness is coming. I can feel it in the wind. I do not know if I will be able to defend my people if the darkness spreads to my village. I hope that you are able to help me restore peace to Ice-Bay.'","In your absence, new threats have come to Forochel. Ostasänt, a warrior from Sûri-kylä, seeks assistance in defeating the threats that she has recently encountered.","The Roving Threats of Forochel","Speak with Ostasänt"},
[12916]={"Othwen can be found in Esteldín.\
\
You should speak with Othwen.","Speak with Othwen","In your absence, new threats have come to The North Downs. Othwen, a defender of Esteldín, seeks the assistance of a brave hero as she works to halt the Angmarim's efforts in the north.","Othwen requires assistance as The North Downs is once again under threat.","'The foulness of Angmar has grown stronger. It slowly pours out of the gate at Ost Crithlanc and is spreading. I've seen dead birds and angered wolves.\
\
'Recently even fouler creatures have emerged. Even the spirits resting in the barrows near Fornost have been angered by the evils of Angmar. I fear if nothing is done, Esteldín will fall.'","The Roving Threats of The North Downs"},
[12919]={"Líder de la manada del páramo derrotado","'¡Gracias! Espero que esto calme las cosas. Herne no necesita más problemas.'","La manada de lobos que vivía al norte de Herne es víctima de un frenesí mortal.","Acaba con escurridizos del páramo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Aulladores del páramo derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'¡La vida en Herne nunca ha sido fácil, pero últimamente una oscuridad asola la tierra, atrayendo a todo tipo de criatura maligna! Hay una manada de lobos al norte de Herne que no suele causar problemas en la aldea o en los caminos. Sin embargo, últimamente se han vuelto agresivos, atacando a los viajeros y asaltando la ciudad al anochecer.\
\
'Si pudieras reducir el número de la manada, sería de gran ayuda.'","Acaba con el líder de la manada del páramo","Escurridizos del páramo derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Vuelve con Maddoc","Deberías decirle a Maddoc que has acabado con muchos lobos iracundos cerca de Herne.\
\
Maddoc está dentro de la posada de Herne.","Acaba con aulladores del páramo (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL}","Maddoc te ha pedido que reduzcas el número de lobos que habitan en Dientelupino, al norte de Herne.\
\
Dientelupino está en el oeste de Cardolan.","La manada del Páramo Rojizo"},
[12923]={"'Te doy mi enhorabuena, ${PLAYERNAME:extranjero[m]|extranjera[f]}. Con tu ayuda, el Enemigo no logrará afianzarse en estas tierras. Aquí tienes lo prometido'.","En lo alto, sobre las aguas del río Mitheithel, se alzan las ruinas de Eitheldir. Lo que fue una fortaleza de los Noldor, hoy cobija entre sus cúpulas a hordas de orcos y forajidos que se disputan estas tierras. Sin embargo, los ojos de los elfos aún vigilan el lugar, y la exploradora Merileg aguarda agazapada entre las sombras, más abajo en el camino.","Derrota a los enemigos en Eitheldir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Las ruinas de Eitheldir","Merileg está en el camino a Eitheldir, en el norte del Ángulo.\
\
Deberías volver con ella.","Derrota al capitán de Eitheldir","Vuelve con Merileg","Eitheldir está en el norte del Ángulo.\
\
Deberías derrotar a los enemigos en Eitheldir.","'Esa escoria mancilla este lugar con su presencia'.","Enemigos derrotados en Eitheldir (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Te hallas ante las ruinas de Eitheldir, ${PLAYERNAME:extranjero[m]|extranjera[f]}. Lo que antaño fue una gran fortaleza de mi pueblo, hoy yace en ruinas y podredumbre. Los siervos del Enemigo se han infiltrado tras esos muros, en otro tiempo formidables, y han mancillado estas tierras. ¿Deseas ayudar a nuestra causa? Haz lo que puedas por mermar sus filas y te recompensaré con creces. No pierdas de vista a su capitán; dicen que es una bestia despiadada'."},
[12924]={"Busca botines enterrados (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Los saqueadores podrían haber escondido las reliquias perdidas por Minas Vrûn, en el oeste de Annúndir.\
\
Debes buscar en Minas Vrûn las reliquias perdidas, en caso de que los saqueadores las enterraran para recuperarlas después.","Tras examinar la estatua arnoriana en Minas Vrûn, te das cuentas de que varias pequeñas piezas han desaparecido.","Cuando miras a la antigua estatua, te das cuenta de que parecen faltar varias piezas pequeñas significativas, dejando huecos donde debería haber reliquias.\
\
La estatua parece haber sido saqueada, no hace mucho. Quizá estos tesoros perdidos pueda encontrarse cerca; los saqueadores podrían haberlas enterrado para recuperarlas después.","Busca las reliquias perdidas","Amarion está en Amon Raith.\
\
Debes llevar las reliquias que has encontrado a Amarion.","Lleva las reliquias de la estatua a Amarion","'¡Las reliquias robadas de una estatua arnoriana! Me alegra que las salvaras, ${PLAYER}. Claramente no es seguro restaurarlas... aunque quizá pueda hacerse en tiempos más pacíficos. Las pondré a salvo y serán atesoradas cuando vuelva a Esteldín, ya que pertenecen a los Hombres de Númenór.'","Las ruinas de Minas Vrûn","Has encontrado una reliquia que faltaba de la estatua arnoriana (${CURRENT}/${MAX})"},
[12925]={"Las ruinas de Pembar se han convertido en el refugio de semiorcos al servicio de Saruman el Blanco, quien ha sucumbido al mal. Lo que buscan en las antiguas ruinas élficas es todavía un misterio.","'Saludos, ${PLAYER}. Tus esfuerzos en el Norte han hecho tu nombre famoso entre los nuestros.\
\
'Tengo una tarea para ti, si quieres aceptarla. Los semiorcos al servicio de Saruman el Blanco han invadido las ruinas de Pembar, al noreste. No puedo decirte lo que buscan, pero están profanando las antiguas ruinas de mis ancestros.\
\
'Te pido que vayas hasta allí y busques entre los montones de escombros. Quizá puedas encontrar algo que explique el interés de Saruman en Pembar.'","'Ve a las ruinas de Pembar, al noreste de aquí, y busca en los montones de escombros que encuentres allí. Con suerte, averiguarás qué están buscando los semiorcos.'","Examina los escombros (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Escombros examinados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Hay muchos montones de escombros en Pembar, al noreste de Echad Eregion.\
\
nFaenhilith te ha pedido que busques entre los montones de escombros en Pembar para ver si puedes averiguar qué interés tienen los siervos de Saruman allí.","Faenhilith está en Echad Eregion, al suroeste de Pembar.\
\
Deberías volver a ver a Faenhilith y contarle lo que has encontrado en Pembar.","'Parece que todavía quedan fragmentos de muchas reliquias en Pembar. Podría haber vestigios de historia que no deberían caer en manos de Saruman...'","Las ruinas de Pembar","Habla con Faenhilith en Echad Eregion"},
[12926]={"Habla con Hulfryn en Herne","Las huellas de cascos llevan al noroeste, fuera de Herne.\
\
Deberías seguirlas","Hay leves huellas en la hierba.","Has visto unas leves huellas cerca del comedero fuera de la casa de Hulfryn.\
\
Deberías examinarlas.","Parece que una oveja ha huido de Herne.","Una oveja en pánico escapó del redil hacia el noroeste.","Un rastro de sangre continúa hacia el norte.\
\
Deberías seguirlo.","La oveja ha muerto hace poco","Examina las huellas de la oveja.","La oveja fugada","Examina la sangre","Espectro derrotado","Por desgracia has encontrado a la última oveha de Hulfryn.\
\
Deberías examinar su cadáver.","Las huellas de cascos que has estado siguiendo acaban de golpe en un charco de sangre.\
\
Deberías examinar la sangre.","Sigue el rastro de huellas","Lo último que hizo la oveja perdida antes de huir fue comer del comedero fuera de la casa de Hulfryn.\
\
Deberías examinar la zona en busca de huellas.","El rastro de sangre continúa hacia el norte","Las huellas continúan hacia el noroeste.","Sigue el rastro de sangre","Has acabado con el tumulario que mató a la oveja de Hulfryn.\
\
Deberías volver a Herne y decírselo.","El olor de carne en descomposición te invade mientras un tumulario avanza hacia ti.","'¿Qué ha pasado? ¿Has encontrado a la oveja?'\
\
 Mientras cuentas la historia, la cara de Hulfryn palidece.\
\
'Jinetes negros y muertos vivientes... Presagios de malos tiempos. Pero no tengo forma de dejar Herne e ir a algún sitio más seguro. Esta aldea es mi mundo. Solo espero que esos jinetes no vuelvan...\
\
'¿${PLAYER} era? Ten cuidado ahí fuera.'","El rastro se para de golpe en este charco de sangre","'¿Has seguido el rastro de un animal antes? He escuchado que los montaraces son buenos en ello, pero no sé cuánto. Deberías comprobar el redil. Antes de que huyese, lo último que hizo fue comer del comedero.\
\
'Ten cuidado. Hay lobos a las afueras de Herne... Y he oído que hay cosas peores acechando más allá. Solo de pensarlo se me pone la piel de gallina.'","Un rastro de sangre continúa hacia el norte","Busca huellas cerca del comedero fuera de la casa de Hulfryn","Examina a la oveja muerta"},
[12928]={"Defeated Ruthless Dead berserkers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'To test myself against such strange beings is an honour and a privilege, is it not?\
\
'Thank you for your aid. I will tend to whatever remains in due time.'","A battle-worn soldier would like your help to disperse the Ruthless Dead.","The Ruthless Dead of Ethillorn","Defeated Ruthless Dead (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat Ruthless Dead berserkers (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to the battle-worn soldier outside the Ruins of Ethillorn","A battle-worn soldier stands guard outside the Ruins of Ethillorn. Dirt marks his face. Sweat mats down his hair in clumps. There are scrapes across his armour, as if some beast tried to claw the heart from his chest.\
\
But he's beaming as you approach him.\
\
'Hail, traveller!'\
\
You feel his eyes assess your worth, and when he judges you a capable adventurer, he beams wider.\
\
'I have been tasked with dispersing the Ruthless Dead from within the walls of Ethillorn. I am in the middle of a respite, but if you would like a turn, you are more than welcome.'","A battle-worn soldier has offered you the chance to defeat the Ruthless Dead in the Ruins of Ethillorn, south of Linhir.\
\
Defeat the Ruthless Dead.","You have defeated many of the Ruthless Dead, and should report to the battle-worn soldier standing outside the Ruins of Ethilllorn south of Linhir.\
\
Talk to the soldier outside the Ruins of Ethillorn.","Defeat Ruthless Dead (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})"},
[12931]={"Rathon has been tasked with maintaining many of the cisterns in Minas Tirith by himself and has come to find cave-lizards who have infested the cisterns.","Cave-lizard nests and Old Stone-tail can be found within the cisterns.\
\
You should remove the cave-lizard infestation from the cisterns.","'Well, I cannot believe it. Old Stone-tail finally took off with her tail between her legs. I never thought I would see the day. Perhaps now we can get the cave-lizard population in the cisterns under control.'","The Scaled Problem","Rathon can be found outside the cistern entrance on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.\
\
You should speak with Rathon.","Speak with Rathon","Destroyed Cave-lizard nest (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Destroy Cave-lizard nests (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Mount Mindolluin has many high mountain caves and crevasses. Some of these caves link up to the higher cisterns. Every once in a while some of the Mindolluin cave-lizards will find their way into the cisterns. Lately however, more and more lizards keep getting into the tunnels. Is something driving them into the cisterns?\
\
'If you ask me, something must be done about these pests. You can disperse them by getting rid of their nests. Oh, and watch out for Old Stone-tail. She's been living in the cisterns since I was a child. Most cistern workers don't mess with her but you're an ample warrior. Perhaps you'll be the one to finally drive Old Stone-tail away for good?'","Defeat Old Stone-tail","Defeated Old Stone-tail"},
[12932]={"Éomer counsels you to shelter in the Hornburg","Éomer está en la Puerta de Helm.\
\
Debes hablar con Éomer.","Ask Aragorn how you can help the Westfold","Aragorn is at Helm's Gate.\
\
You should speak with Aragorn.","Take leave of King Théoden","Ask Éomer how you can help the Westfold","'So you have decided to part ways here, ${PLAYER}? I pray for your safe return, and I hope that there is still time to draw swords with you at the Hornburg.\
\
'Good luck with your search for Erkenbrand. Be careful -- the Westfold is not what it once was. The enemy has claimed this land.\
\
'The battle at the Hornburg will decide the fate of Rohan....'","The Scattered Lords of the Westfold","'It is nearly time for us to retreat within....'","'If you wish to help the Westfold and Rohan, think to helping yourself. Seek shelter in the Hornburg, and defend it with us! Help us ready for battle.\
\
'If reports hold true, it is folly to roam the plains right now. Yes, we need Erkenbrand...but can he get here in time, if he even lives?'\
\
You thank Éomer for his advice, but you wonder what Gandalf would have you do.","Théoden is at Helm's Gate.\
\
You should speak with Théoden.","Apparently much hope lies heavily on Erkenbrand and the lords of the Westfold -- Grimbold, Elfhelm, and Dúnhere. The Hornburg needs strong arms to defend it, but Gandalf may need help finding Erkenbrand.","Aragorn believes that hope lies in Gandalf, and in finding Erkenbrand","'If you wish to know about the state of things in Westfold, I am glad to tell you all that I know.\
\
'Erkenbrand, the lord of Helm's Deep, took command of the ford after Prince Théodred fell. Elfhelm was with him, and Grimbold too -- Grimbold is the Thane of Grimslade, a town to the east.\
\
'I do not know what happened at the Fords of Isen, but I do know that all of Westfold braces for war and awaits news of the scattered lords, for enemies of Isengard now roam free. They march here even now as we speak.\
\
'If Erkenbrand and the others can get here, we have a chance to survive. If they do not....' Gamling trails off.","'I cannot advise you easily, ${PLAYER}. I truly worry that those of us who ride on to the Hornburg will not live to see the morning -- but I believe that crossing the plains of the Westfold before Saruman's army will mean certain death.\
\
'Yet the hope lies in Gandalf. For myself, I will stay and defend Théoden and Rohan with my life, for Rohan has ever been an ally to my people.\
\
'I hope that Gandalf can find Erkenbrand in time.'"},
[12933]={"Examine the blank gravestone more closely this time","You have found the lost leaves from the book of records","'Have you found anything of interest yet?'","Habla con Prestadír en la Posada Embrujada","The Scattered Tales of Audaghaim","Examine the blank gravestone more closely","'Have you found anything yet? Sometimes it is best to trace our steps from the beginning.'","Prestadír is at the Haunted Inn in the Dourstocks, north of the graveyard.\
\
You should tell Prestadír of your encounter with the condemned Record-keeper who appeared when you searched his grave.","'I should have stood with the four who resisted, but I did not. I watched it all happen. Only when they had perished did I feel the effects of the true evil that was at work in Audaghaim. Too late did I record the truth.\
\
'When they found what I had written, they came after me as well. I anticipated them. Here is a copy of the truth that was destroyed. Let this be my last effort on behalf of the true heroes of Audaghaim who resisted the evil corruptions of the Necromancer. Our blindness was our undoing!\
\
'Yes -- the Necromancer came and promised much, and we saw the opportunity for progress and prosperity. The four that stood against him attacked the altar, and we cut them down in the name of Dol Guldur. They cursed us as they fell.\
\
'Ah! My oath is fulfilled, my redemption nigh....'","'Ah! You have found the lost pages! I am astounded. May I take a look?\
\
'At last, the truth -- and so it all comes together. Some of the townsmen resisted, and they were executed by their own folk. That settles the mystery. The guilty shade you spoke to before was the one who led the movement to accept the Necromancer's advances here. He was also the one who led in the murders.\
\
'Everything is documented in this account, until the Record-keeper writes of his own guilt for not standing up for his fallen townsfolk. Here he writes that he knows his enemy will destroy the truth and execute him as well. This is the last entry by his hand.'","You have found a book of records buried in the ruins of Audaghaim, but many pages are missing from the period when Sauron returned to Mirkwood.","'So, it appears that someone kept a faithful record, but this record was not to the liking of those who carried out the murders. \
\
'If you are still invested in the story of this town, you should look into finding the missing pages. Perhaps they have been destroyed, and perhaps not.\
\
'But where to start? In the case of hidden relics, sometimes it is best to start where you began. That blank gravestone was the first thing to rouse my interest in this mystery, and perhaps it can tell us more now.'","The blank gravestone is in the graveyard to the south of Audaghaim and the Haunted Inn.\
\
You should search the area of the uninformative gravestone again for anything you may have missed."},
[12934]={"Bothwar está en el puente en el centro de Gabilshathûr, al sur de Imlad Balchorth.\
\
Has devuelto a Arngrim a sus sentidos y deberías informar a Bothwar.","'¡Tú! ¡Has venido a robarlo, ¿verdad?! ¡Mi mithril! ¡Mi hermoso y precioso mithril! La voz me lo ha dicho. ¡La verdadera dulce voz del mithril! ¡No, retrocede, te digo! ¡No me hagas! ¡No me hagas!'","'Arngrim debería haber regresado para cumplir con su deber de guardia en lugar de continuar su tonta búsqueda de mithril en estas tierras. Búscalo al norte de aquí, en las crestas de las regiones más al sur de Imlad Balchorth.'","'¡Has hecho un buen trabajo, ${PLAYER}! Es bueno que Arngrim haya abandonado su loca búsqueda... al menos por ahora.\
\
'Toma esta recompensa y regocíjate por un trabajo bien hecho. ¡Te la has ganado!'","Arngrim está buscando mithril en la cima de una cresta en las regiones más al sur de Imlad Balchorth, al norte de Gabilshathûr.\
\
Bothwar está preocupado de que Arngrim, un poco despistado en el mejor de los casos, pueda haberse metido en problemas en las regiones del sur de Imlad Balchorth.","Encuentra a Arngrim","'No todos aquí hacen lo que se les dice, ${PLAYER}: Arngrim es uno de ellos. Ha estado actuando de forma extraña durante un tiempo, pero no se había negado a seguir órdenes directas hasta hace poco. Se le ordenó regresar a Gabilshathûr para montar la guardia contra los Orcos, al igual que yo... ¡pero él no lo hizo!\
\
'Durante mucho tiempo ha afirmado que hay mithril en esta tierra, aunque todo enano sabe que eso es una locura, pero su retraso en regresar solo puede explicarse por esta causa: ¡cree haber encontrado algo!\
\
'Si quieres ayudarme con esta última cosa, estaré muy contento. Arngrim puede haber perdido la cabeza, pero sigue siendo un enano y le debemos esto. Búscalo en las crestas situadas en las regiones más al sur de Imlad Balchorth, al norte de este puesto avanzado.'","El aroma del mithril","El enano Arngrim ha desaparecido después de decirle a algunos de los otros mineros que estaba seguro de conocer la ubicación de una veta de mithril en las colinas de Imlad Balchorth.","Has hecho entrar en razón a Arngrim"},
[12935]={"Talk to Felgúr","Legolas has asked you to unbind Felgúr and send him on his mission.\
\
You should talk to Felgúr in Echad Taerdim.","Find Rûkhor's second orders to Zabothak","Felgúr taps your shoulder, attempting to get your attention","'It is time for Felgúr to make himself useful. Have him track down his kin. I will be watching from nearby, but will keep to the shadows.'","Find the Ungoledain with Felgúr","Felgúr has begun tracking the other Ungoledain.\
\
You should travel with Felgúr.","'What have you learned, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You tell Legolas of the orders you found in the uruk camp.\
\
'Rûkhor is using the Ungoledain to seek Ungwetári? To what end? Does he intend to try to control her? Surely he is not so foolish. But it is true: pride seems a common flaw among the Gúrzyul.\
\
'If Rûkhor and the Ungoledain were not at this camp, they must have already left for Torech Ungol. We do not know Rûkhor's plan, but if he succeeds in rousing Ungwetári, she will be unleashed upon all of us! I cannot fathom the terrible rampage he may incite. Her ravenous hunger will never be sated!\
\
'We must hurry after them. We have no other choice.'","Zabothak, my most loyal servant.\
\
Belzagar has sent word. The tower must be reinforced at once or be lost to the spider-horde. Rally with Ugrukhôr's forces and re-take the tower, or Shelob may be set loose upon Gorgoroth or the Morgul Vale. Do not fail me.","The Schemes of the Pale Herald","You untie Felgúr and let him know it is time to begin tracking down the rest of the Ungoledain. He looks around sheepishly, still not entirely trusting of the Rangers or of Legolas. When he is at least mostly convinced he is not about to be shot full of arrows, he nods to you.\
\
'I will find them! Let us start by heading east.'","'Are you going in there? Eh, that was not part of my bargain. I do not think I can fight those big white Orcs without the power of the Spider. I do not smell my kin here. I might wait with the Elf, or continue the search. You can find me later.'","Find Rûkhor's first orders to Zabothak","Felgúr would like to speak with you.\
\
You should talk to Felgúr.","Find Rûkhor's third orders to Zabothak","Legolas has asked you to find evidence of Rûkhor's plans in Kaslokroz.\
\
You should find written orders to the Uruk lieutenants.","Felgúr sniffs the air and points south-east","Legolas has appeared near an Uruk camp in eastern Cirith Ungol.\
\
You should talk to Legolas.","Zabothak,\
\
Fear not, my servant. I lay the blame for this defeat on the traitor Ugrukhôr. If he had delivered the forces he promised me, the tower would be secure. His excuses do nothing but tire me. We owe no allegiance to the Lady of Blight. I care nothing for the false king Gothmog. I will be formulating a new plan. Stand by to receive new orders.","Zabothak,\
\
Thus far, we have been unable to locate Shelob's den in the maze of tunnels in Torech Ungol, but we may finally have a solution. The scouts have located a tribe of primitive Men recently arrived to the west. They have been seen skin-changing into spiders! I believe these may be the Ungoledain that Karazgar mentioned. And if they have come all the way here... perhaps they also hear the call of the Spider-queen. Prepare for a delegation.","'Hold, friend. It seems we are on the right track. There is no sign of the Ungoledain, but we did find Rûkhor's uruks. I propose we investigate the camp while we are here. Perhaps we can glean some clue as to Rûkhor's abilities and his motivation for seeking Ungwetári.'","Legolas is waiting near Kaslokroz.\
\
You should talk to Legolas.","Felgúr nods at you and points south","Legolas calls to you from nearby","The time has come to track the Ungoledain and Rûkhor the Pale Herald with the aid of Felgúr.","Felgúr grimaces and points north","Find Rûkhor's fourth orders to Zabothak","Habla con Legolas.","Zabothak,\
\
I have had an epiphany. Perhaps Shelob is not a problem we can solve. Perhaps she is not a problem at all.\
\
Rally the Bloodless. We will enter the Morgul Vale. We will enter Torech Ungol. We will find Her Ladyship Ungwetári and rouse her from her den."},
[12937]={"Confront Krûha","'Oh? One of the old man's lackeys finally grew a spine?'\
\
Akhâd sneers at you and slams his mug onto the table. After a tense moment, he barks at one of the tavern-workers.\
\
'Another round when this is done!'","'After you returned, I sent my guards to investigate the rumours Zemirah spoke of, but unfortunately, the situation is far worse than I expected.\
\
'From what I have learned, six of Balakhôr's captains remain in the Sail-haven: Medêshi, Grizagâr, Jakham, Krûha, Sikaru, and Akhâd. How they all managed to survive the Mutiny is a mystery to me, but the Kindred of the Coins cannot abide traitors in Umbar Baharbêl. I am told that some of them can be found on the decks of their ships at the edges of the harbour, but others may still haunt the local taverns.\
\
'Need I tell you what must be done, ${PLAYER}? Confront them, and slay them to the last!'","'YOU! I know you!'\
\
Krûha stares at you as if he has seen a ghost.\
\
'I was at Pelargir, ${CLASS}, but you don't remember me, do you? I know you serve the King of Gondor—that Elf-loving pretender! If you think the people of Umbar hate me, just wait until they learn who you really are!'","'Who are you to speak to me? Some foreign puppet of the Kindred?'\
\
Jakham smirks at you.\
\
'I should cut your tongue from your mouth!'","'What is this? You think I answer to you or that old fool, Eshmun?'\
\
Sikaru glares at you.\
\
'No, you were dead the moment you stepped onto my ship!'","Confront Sikaru","The Scourge's Captains","Medêshi, Grizagâr, Jakham, Krûha, Sikaru, and Akhâd can be found throughout the Sail-haven, either upon the decks of their ships in the harbour or lurking at one of the local taverns.\
\
Eshmun has asked you to find, confront, and defeat Balakhôr the Scourge's loyal captains in Umbar Baharbêl.","'You dare threaten me? I've killed better than you for far less, ${CLASS}.'\
\
Medêshi glares at you and gestures to the others at the tavern.\
\
'Let these fools relish their so-called victory because when the Scourge returns—Balakhôr or no—we shall have Umbar for our own!'","Confront Jakham","Confront Medêshi","Eshmun, Captain of the Haven, can be found at the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl.\
\
You have defeated all of Balakhôr the Scourge's loyal captains in the Sail-haven. You should return to Eshmun.","Confront Akhâd","Confront Grizagâr","'I've lost, have I? Balakhôr is dead? You know nothing, ${CLASS}, and I will not be moved. Not by Eshmun, and certainly not by you!'\
\
Grizagâr scowls at you, and chuckles to himself.\
\
'The Sail-haven is ours by right!'","Talk to Eshmun at the Harbour-warden's Tower","'It is done? Excellent!\
\
'It will take more than the Mutiny and time to wash away the stain of Balakhôr the Scourge, but you have done well to rid the Free City of his few remaining captains.\
\
'May their names and deeds be forgotten!'","Despite the success of the Sea-stone Mutiny, several captains still loyal to Balakhôr the Scourge have managed to entrench themselves in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl."},
[12939]={"Trasgos derrotados (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Destruye tiendas de trasgos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Elimina trasgos (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El explorador se convierte en cazador","Los trasgos representan una amenaza para la gente de las Quebradas del Norte y deben ser castigados por vagar tan lejos de sus tierras.","Tienda de trasgo destruida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","El campamento trasgo está al este de Amon Raith, en las colinas del sur de Annúndir.\
\
Deberías entrar en el campamento trasgo y derrotar allí a un buen número de ellos.","'Yo me daría la vuelta si fuera tú. Solo hay peligro más adelante.\
\
'El camino por el que viniste es seguro, ¿verdad? Pues iré por ahí, hacia ese tal Amarion. Suena mejor que intentar sobrevivir solo aquí.'","El montaraz Amarion está en Amon Raith, al oeste de Annúndir.\
\
Amarion está esperando noticias sobre tu ataque a los trasgos de Annúndir.","'Has hecho bien, ${PLAYER}, ¡y casi mejor de lo que esperaba! ¡Los trasgos seguramente han oído nuestro mensaje: no son bienvenidos aquí, ni lo serán nunca!\
\
'No tengo los medios para recompensarte tan generosamente como mereces, pero espero que este pequeño obsequio te sirva como recordatorio del bien que has hecho por Amarion y el pueblo de Annúndir.'"},
[12940]={"Los exploradores de la Mano Blanca te han visto","'El siguiente paso de mi plan es un desafío. Un explorador de la Mano Blanca tiene una ruta de patrulla que pasa por el extremo del Agujero Chirriante.... no se fían de los insectos que hay allí. Hay unas cuantas cajas cerca del lugar, y quiero que dejes las pruebas que has recuperado en una de ellas. La bolsa entera, sí... porque es más visible y no está en el suelo, ¡por eso!\
\
'¡Lo importante es que no te vean! Es vital que los orcos piensen que uno de los otros exploradores la dejó ahí, o incluso mejor, que juegue en contra de su naturaleza supersticiosa. Hay muchas cosas en las minas que ven con un miedo cercano a la adoración.\
\
'Ve hacia el sureste, al Agujero Chirriante, y encuentra la caja. Coloca la bolsa sobre ella, y recuerda... ¡no mates al explorador!'","'¡El plan progresa adecuadamente, gracias a ti!'","Coloca la bolsa con los restos en la caja","'Tendrás que colocar la bolsa a plena vista, sin que te vean y sin que los exploradores orcos de la Mano Blanca se alarmen por encontrar muertos a sus exploradores.'","La caja está cerca del Agujero Chirriante, al sureste de Guardia Orca.\
\
Ingifast quiere que coloques la bolsa que contiene los restos de la anterior expedición de la Mano Blanca en una superficie elevada, como una caja, cerca de la ruta de las patrullas de los exploradores de la Mano Blanca.","Bolsa con los restos colocada en la caja","Habla con Ingifast en Guardia Orca","No dejes que los exploradores de la Mano Blanca te vean","Ingifast está en Guardia Orca, al noroeste del Agujero Chirriante.\
\
Ingifast se alegrará de oír que las pruebas han sido colocadas en la caja para que el explorador las encuentre.","Entre los restos que has traído a Ingifast había algunos objetos útiles para el siguiente paso de su plan.","El informe del explorador"},
[12941]={"Las tribus de orcos compiten por las enormes riquezas de las Vetas del Cuerno Rojo. Es probable que cada tribu reúna información sobre la otra para ganar ventaja.","Encuentra el informe de la tribu de Moria","Entrega los informes a Ingifast cerca de la Guardia Orca","El informe de reconocimiento está escondido en el campamento de cada tribu.\
\
Cada tribu ha estado explorando las defensas de la otra, la ubicación de los puntos estratégicos y las operaciones mineras.","El informe del explorador","Encontraste un informe sobre la otra tribu de orcos. Es información fundamental, ya que se trata de un buen registro de las fortalezas y debilidades de su tribu. A los enanos de la Guardia Orca les resultará de gran utilidad.","Encuentra el informe de la tribu de la Mano Blanca","'Estos informes de reconocimiento son en su mayoría dibujos y resultan muy útiles. Sin duda, esto nos ayudará a acabar con la lucha de poder entre estos orcos.\
\
'Hay algunas palabras escritas aquí que no consigo entender. Los llevaré a la Guardia Orca o a la Sala Vigesimoprimera para que alguien que conozca la escritura orca me los traduzca.'","El campamento de Ingifast se encuentra en las escaleras de la Guardia Orca.\
\
Ingifast se alegrará de ver los informes que has reunido.","Informe de la tribu de Moria encontrado","Informe de la tribu de la Mano Blanca encontrado"},
[12942]={"'Pareces ser una persona de gran habilidad.'\
\
Ella hace una pausa un momento.\
\
'Pareces ser una persona de buena habilidad. Si estás dispuesto a deambular por la naturaleza y pelear contra cosas, podría usar tu ayuda. Como dijo Talfryn, dirijo a unos cuantos exploradores en entrenamiento. Me vendría bien alguien como tú para ayudar a instruirlos. Mis alumnos y yo establecimos un campamento al este. Encuéntranos allí. Pronto regresaré yo también; no me gusta dejarlos solos por mucho tiempo. ¿Quién sabe en qué problemas podrían meterse?'","'¡Qué bueno que por fin llegas! ¿Qué te tomó tanto tiempo?'","Habla con Eluna en Cuencasangre, hacia el este.","Eluna espera contar con tu ayuda para sus muchas tareas.","Eluna viajará a una pequeña zona al este del campamento de Huargos conocida como Cuencasangre.\
\
Reúnete con Eluna al este de Cuencasangre.","Los Reclutas Exploradores de Lhan Garan"},
[12943]={"'${PLAYER}! You must escape, quickly! He is coming. It is too late for me, but run, run!'","You have found Hashadîr, and Corsairs are everywhere...","Lothíriel has heard reports of Corsair scouts who may have infiltrated the great city of Dol Amroth.","<rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> for Abedec from the south-eastern watch-tower","You see no signs of Captain Abedec from this vantage point","'If we do not take out Abedec, he will not rest until we are both hunted down and beheaded, for that is his style. I always admired him for it, but not when it's my head on the line.\
\
'Do you wish to work together once more? I say we split up and investigate the two camps where Corsairs have made their landings south of Dol Amroth. You go to the beach to the south-west, and I will investigate the ruins to the south.\
\
'Search for Abedec, but do not engage him. We must fight him together. Let us meet on the cross-roads between the two camps when we're done.'","Jajax is nowhere to be found. Something must have gone wrong...","Jajax's meeting place is where the roads meet between the two Corsair encampments -- one leads from the south-west, from Hashadîr, and the other leads from the ruins to the south.\
\
You should meet Jajax at the cross-roads.","Search for Jajax in the ruins to the south","Good vantage points for searching for signs of Abedec can be found atop the watch-towers in Hashadîr, south-west of Dol Amroth.\
\
You should climb the watch-towers on the beach and <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> for signs of Abedec.","Jajax is likely somewhere in the ruins to the south of Dol Amroth.\
\
You should search for Jajax, for he is probably in need of rescue.","The Corsairs have landed on a beach south-west of Dol Amroth.\
\
Jajax has asked you to search for Abedec at the beach-side landing spot, while he searches some ruins to the south.","Find the beach upon which the Corsairs have landed","Este es un buen punto de vista","Meet Jajax at the cross-roads","The Search for Abedec","<rgb=#FF0000>Look</rgb> for Abedec from the north-western watch-tower"},
[12944]={"'Worry not, my injuries are minor. I have escaped worse places with more grievous wounds.\
\
'The Corsairs captured me, but could not agree on my fate. Some wanted me dead, though a few did not seem thrilled by the prospect. Even their efforts to search for me have been half-hearted -- none have ventured past the walls of their camp. I can understand their caution; the chances of them finding kindness outside those walls would be slim.\
\
'Before I report back to Gilanor, I have some ideas on how to weaken the Corsairs' hold here. I'm afraid I cannot approach the camp in my physical state, but your help would be enough.'","Find Dolvir near Abadec's Watch","The Search for Dolvir","You have found an injured Dolvir amongst the trees north of Abadec's Watch.\
\
You should make sure he's alright.","The scout Dolvir left Ost Lontir to assess the situation at Abadec's Watch, but has not been heard from since.","Talk to Dolvir","An injured Dolvir catches your attention","Gilanor has sent you to find Dolvir.\
\
Dolvir may be somewhere near Abadec's Watch, which lies south-west of Ost Lontir.","'The war may be over, but the remnants of enemy forces remain in Gondor. One of my scouts, Dolvir, noticed Corsair stragglers retreating south-west to what used to be Abadec's Watch. He went ahead to scout the camp further, but has not returned or sent any word of his discoveries there.\
\
'You have done much for Gondor, ${PLAYER} -- if anyone could find him, it would be you. May my anxieties be laid to rest.'"},
[12945]={"Tolwin can be found in the hall of Crithost.\
\
You should speak with Tolwin.","The Orcs seem to think that you just killed their captain","<rgb=#FF0000>Look around</rgb> for signs of Dúneth at the first farmhouse","Tolwin's mother Dúneth, has been missing since the attack on Cair Andros and he fears the worst, though Tolwin still has hope that you might be able to find her hiding in one of the still standing farm buildings in Talath Anor.","Find and defeat the captain at Parth Lisc","Parth Lisc is located in north-eastern Talath Anor and Parth Duin is located in eastern Talath Anor.\
\
You should travel to the Parth Lisc and Parth Duin and search for Dúneth.","<rgb=#FF0000>Look around</rgb> for signs of Dúneth at the fourth farmhouse","The Search for Dúneth","'Still no signs of my mother? This indeed looks glum. I wished very much that you would have found her at one of the farms.\
\
'What is this, both captains you encountered had just been slain? Someone seems to have the same agenda as us!'","It looks like the camp's captain was recently killed and some lowly warrior has stepped up to take his place","Find and defeat the captain at Parth Duin","<rgb=#FF0000>Look around</rgb> for signs of Dúneth at the second farmhouse","This farmhouse is a good place to <rgb=#FF0000>look around</rgb> for signs of Dúneth","'I still believe my mother is out there somewhere, hiding from the invaders. She might be held up in one of the abandoned farms near here. I do not know for sure but it is worth investigating.\
\
'Will you search for my mother while I help out around Crithost? My mother's name is Dúneth. I do hope she still lives.\
\
'Be warned though, Orcs and Easterlings have taken over the farms near here. Make the captains of these invaders pay for what they have done to Cair Andros.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Look around</rgb> for signs of Dúneth at the third farmhouse","Talk to Tolwin","No one's been here recently"},
[12946]={"<rgb=#FF0000>Look around</rgb> for signs of Dúneth at the first farmhouse","'My son! I did not know if you were alive until I saw you fighting that Orc in Parth Gladló! You are both brave.\
\
'Did Tolwin not tell you of my training in both stealth and blade? I suppose he was too young to remember my training.\
\
'No matter, we are safe to rest here for a short time... Where are my manners?! My name is Dúneth. I am sure Tolwin has been worried sick about me.'","Orcs have begun using the farm as a staging ground for building machines of war","The woods can be found in eastern Talath Anor.\
\
You should follow the mysterious figure into the woods.","<rgb=#FF0000>Look around</rgb> for signs of Dúneth at the second farmhouse","Speak with Tolwin.","Parth Gladló is located in southern Talath Anor.\
\
You should search buildings at Parth Gladló.","Tolwin is afraid that he may never find his mother","Dúneth was never in need of rescuing and instead has been secretly keeping Crithost safe","The trail of footprints leads deeper into the woods","Speak with Dúneth","You come across a small makeshift encampment and the woman standing there smiles","Tolwin has asked you to accompany him on the search to find his missing mother, Dúneth.","The trail of footsteps leads deeper into the woods.\
\
You should follow the trail to find this mysterious figure.","No one's been here recently, but you hear an Orc captain shouting orders nearby","'I had forgotten the words my father once said to me. He told me that we come from a long line of skilled warriors and everyone in this family is a warrior.\
\
'Of course he meant my mother too but it had slipped my mind. Thanks to you we are reunited and can both work together to find and oust The First Blade!'","No one has been here recently as all the buildings are boarded up","Travel to Parth Gladló","Dúneth is located at her camp.\
\
You should speak with Dúneth.","'There is a farm by the river, not too far from here. Farmers from Parth Forant safely evacuated to Crithost at the first signs of conflict at Cair Andros.\
\
Why have I not thought of this sooner! Parth Forant is abandoned and has not yet been taken over by the Enemy. I bet we will find my mother there!'","Search Parth Forant for Dúneth","'I can also see that no one has been here for a while.'\
\
Tolwin pauses with a frown upon his face and looks towards the ground for a moment.\
\
'The best place left to look for my mother is the farm of Parth Gladló in southern Talath Anor. I have seen many foes across the Forant River though. It will not be an easy task.\
\
'Still, we must try to find her. If we can not find her we should still send The First Blade a message that he is unwanted in Gondor.'","You notice a trail of footprints leading deeper into the woods","No one has been here recently","As Gúrdru falls you notice a human figure run away from Gúrdru's perch towards the woods","Gúrdru can be found in Parth Gladló.\
\
You should find and defeat Gúrdru.","Follow the trail of footprints deeper into the woods","Enter the woods in pursuit of the mysterious figure","Parth Forant is located in Talath Anor on the banks of the River Forant.\
\
Your should search Parth Forant for Dúneth.","Find and defeat Gúrdru","Parth Gladló is located in southern Talath Anor.\
\
Your best chance at finding Dúneth is searching Parth Gladló.","Speak with Tolwin","This farmhouse is a good place to <rgb=#FF0000>look around</rgb> for signs of Dúneth","The Search for Dúneth Continues"},
[12948]={"'¿Has encontrado a mi niña, Lalia? Si se fue en busca de su “Último Príncipe”, probablemente haya ido al túmulo del que habla Cebadilla en su historia. Su relato dice que el túmulo del Príncipe está cerca de una piedra erguida, entre el Túmulo del Norte y el Pináculo de los Caídos.\
\
'¡Si yo tengo miedo de este lugar —y lo tengo!— estoy seguro de que ella está aterrada.'","Has encontrado a Lalia","Según la historia de Cebadilla Mantecona, el Túmulo del Último Príncipe se encuentra entre el Túmulo del Norte y el Pináculo de los Caídos, cerca de una gran piedra erguida.\
\
Bob te ha pedido que busques en las Quebradas de los Túmulos a su hija desaparecida, que probablemente vino aquí en busca del legendario “Último Príncipe”.","Encuentra a la hija de Bob, Lalia","La hija de Bob, Lalia, ha desaparecido. Bob, temiendo que haya ido en busca del \\qÚltimo Príncipe\\q, un personaje de una de las historias que Cebadilla Mantecona cuenta a los viajeros, se unió a una expedición a las Quebradas de los Túmulos para buscar a su hija.","'Vine aquí a buscar a mi hija desaparecida, Lalia. Estoy terriblemente preocupado por ella. Verás, ha estado hablando sin parar sobre \\qEl Último Príncipe\\q, una de las historias de Cebadilla Mantecona. Es una de sus mejores, sin duda, pero diría que no es del todo cierta.\
\
'Lalia ha estado obsesionada con eso durante un buen tiempo. Me temo que vino aquí, a las Quebradas de los Túmulos, en busca de ese \\qpríncipe\\q suyo. Vine a buscar a mi hija, y ahora yo mismo estoy perdido.\
\
'En la historia, el túmulo del Último Príncipe está entre el Túmulo del Norte y el Pináculo de los Caídos, junto a una gran piedra. Si pudiera, empezaría a buscar allí.'","La Búsqueda de Lalia"},
[12949]={"'${PLAYER}, with these Orcs causing problems around Fenmarch, I fear for Meregyth's safety.\
\
'Could you go look for her? She was last seen heading south towards Beaconwatch. She has been known to go there when she feels the need to be alone.'","Free Meregyth","You find another flower along the road. Meregyth might be leaving a trail to help locate her","The trail of flowers leads to the south.\
\
It is very clear that Meregyth is leaving a trail in order to locate her. She may be in trouble after all. You should continue following the flowers in hopes of locating Meregyth.","'I was hoping that you would find my trail. If you had not given me those flowers, I do not know how I would have been found.\
\
'We need to leave here...I feel that it is not safe. Beaconwatch is closer than Fenmarch, so we should go there.'","There is a flower on the road that resembles the ones you gave to Meregyth","The trail of flowers goes off the road and runs adjacent to the stream.\
\
You should continue to follow Meregyth's trail.","The trail of flowers goes up a narrow path that leads behind the waterfall.\
\
You should follow the path that winds around the waterfall.","Meregyth has been gone far too long, and Thane Sparhafoc is concerned for his daughter's safety.","It seems clear now that the Orcs were responsible for Meregyth's disappearance","The Search for Meregyth","Meregyth was last seen heading along the road south towards Beaconwatch.\
\
Thane Sparhafoc asked you to find Meregyth and watch over her.","It is clear now that Meregyth was taken by the Orcs.\
\
You should find her and free her from the clutches of the Orcs.","This flower's placement indicates that Meregyth went up the path that leads behind the waterfall","Look for the trail of flowers Meregyth left behind","You found another flower. Meregyth must be nearby","Find Meregyth","'¡Ayúdame!'","Follow Meregyth's trail along the stream","Follow the road that leads south and look for Meregyth","Another flower from Meregyth leads you up a narrow path","Follow the narrow path that leads behind the waterfall","The trail of flowers leads to the south.\
\
It is possible that Meregyth is leaving a trail in order to locate her. She may be in trouble after all. You should continue following the flowers in hopes of locating Meregyth."},
[12950]={"Talk to Sapakár","'I would be wary in tracking Sapakár the Cleaver. The mighty Olog-hai might easily be out-smarted, though makes up for such in brute force. I know not where to find him.'","Lômazar explains of Sapakár the Cleaver, a powerful ally of Dulgabêth.","Off in the distance you spy a small group of enemies entering the ruins of Barad-dûr","The Search for Sapakár","Ingold has seen a foe matching Sapakár's description","Sapakár stands before you on the edge of the chasm of Mordath","Sapakár can be found somewhere in Barad-dûr.\
\
You should seek out Sapakár.","'Are you here to help? We must search the pit for The Black Word.'","Talk to Ingold","Enter Barad-dûr and seek out Sapakár","Sapakár can be found somewhere in Barad-dûr.\
\
You should confront Sapakár.","You should travel to the last known location of Sapakár.","You come across a large footprint belonging to Sapakár","Ingold can be found at the Ruins of Díngarth.\
\
You should speak with Ingold to learn anything you can about Sapakár.","Seek out Sapakár","You describe Sapakár as best as you can to Ingold.\
\
'Men under my command have reported a large creature similar in description to this Sapakár that you mention. The monster was last seen near Barad-dûr. I hope this assists you on your search, my friend.'","<rgb=#FF0000>Look Around</rgb> for signs of Sapakár at his last known location","Sapakár can be found deep within the bones of Barad-dûr.\
\
You should seek out Sapakár.","This is the last known location where Ingold said he saw someone matching Sapakár's description"},
[12952]={"A cluster of large, pale crystals","Tharrkirîn is in northern Gundabad.\
\
Gerja has asked you to discover Tharrkirîn.","'You found Tharrkirîn?'\
\
You tell Gerja about the empty pedestal.\
\
'I wonder what had been on display there. I fear anything of value will have been plundered long ago, alas.'","Return to Gerja","Flutes of dark grey basalt","Examined the displays (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","An ancient troll, turned to stone","Search for Tharrkirîn","Rocks on display! This must be Tharrkirîn!","High above the River Kurdushâlak an ancient collection of stone from across Gundabad waits to be discovered.","Gerja is located in Bazanmanar.\
\
You should let Gerja know what you found in Tharrkirîn.","'Welcome to Bazanmanar, friend. In ancient days, this area would have been a bustling marketplace. Tables and crates piled high, full of goods grown in the tiers below. From here, you can see much of the gap, and just north of here lies a tunnel which would allow outside visitors into the mountain to shop for wares.\
\
'The records speak of a grand, open-air museum, full of gems, precious metals, and stone gathered across Gundabad. All I could uncover is that it lies north of here, \\qabove the river, where the gems might glitter in the light of the sun's rays.\\q Well, good luck, friend!'","Examine the displays (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","This platform is empty","A glittering stalagmite from Stonejaws","The Search for Tharrkirîn","Tharrkirîn is in northern Clovengap.\
\
You have found Tharrkirîn, a plateau with stone-topped display platforms. You should explore the museum."},
[12953]={"Pick up the object that caught your eye","Thrymm was hurled north-west by Núrzum.\
\
You should <rgb=#FF0000>look</rgb> north-west of Scylfig for signs of Thrymm.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: This quest requires emotes.</rgb>","'Thrymm's horn! But no sign of Thrymm himself? Do not tell me this! My heart still thinks he is alive, but no one could have survived such a fall.\
\
'Gárwig must be told. I was hoping we could bear Thrymm's body to Forlaw to be buried there, but... we must deliver the horn instead.\
\
'I will meet you there, ${PLAYER}. I must attend to my people, and then I will leave.'","Gárwig, the Reeve of Wildermore, can be found in Forlaw.\
\
Cyneberg has asked you to deliver Thrymm's horn to Gárwig.","Cyneberg has recovered enough to ask that Thrymm's body be recovered for a proper burial.","This unlucky fellow is clearly not Thrymm. The hero of Wildermore is nowhere to be found","'I know what I need to bear this grief. I need to see Thrymm's body properly buried.\
\
'You saw yourself which way the giant threw him. Will you look for him, and bring him home to us? We should bear him to Forlaw then, for he is like a son to Reeve Gárwig.'","See if the body on the road below is Thrymm","Cyneberg is in Scylfig.\
\
You should return to Cyneberg and show her the horn.","A body lies below the horn in the north-western Writhendowns, upon the road.\
\
You should investigate the body, for it is likely Thrymm's.","You cannot see Thrymm's body, but something nearby catches your eye. Could it be Thrymm's horn?","Search for Thrymm's body north-west of Scylfig","The item that caught your eye (a horn, perhaps) is just to the west of your last vantage point.\
\
You should examine the item you spotted in the snow.","Bring Thrymm's horn to Gárwig, Reeve of Wildermore","The Search for Thrymm","Bring the horn to Cyneberg","You recognize the horn instantly as Thrymm's own -- the horn he carries with him always... and below, upon the road, you see a body!","This is a good place to look for Thrymm","'Cyneberg told us that you defended Scylfig like it was your own home. I thank you for that, ${PLAYER}.'","'I bid you welcome! Cyneberg told us of your valour at Scylfig.'","'More dead... and you witnessed it all, stranger. News of your deeds has reached me, and I honour you for fighting alongside my son Gársig.\
\
'More and more die, ever since this cold has set in. And now Gársig... Thrymm, Grimgar, Humbald... and Cynegar, a Thane!\
\
'Thrymm was like a son to me, and I will keep his horn to honour him until the end of my line. I name it Winter's Horn, until a hero of Thrymm's ilk can claim it again.'"},
[12954]={"Recolecta hierbas desconocidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","En busca de una cura","Recolecta plantas desconocidas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Por favor, apresúrate, ${PLAYER}. Alagos no esperará mucho más.'","'Existe un fenómeno que suele darse en la naturaleza, según el cual los remedios crecen junto a los venenos. A menudo, los hierbajos nocivos se encuentran entre las hojas que curan. Ahora que sabemos dónde se encuentra el origen de esta extraña enfermedad, deberíamos buscar en la zona cualquier planta que haya crecido para resistir el entorno dañino.\
\
'Si ves alguna planta que parezca destacar, ¿podrías recogerla para mí? Creo que podremos elaborar un remedio si logramos encontrar hierbas curativas de este pantano contaminado.\
\
'Vuelve a ese lugar enfermizo, ${PLAYER}, y apresúrate. Recoge tantas plantas como puedas. ¡Por favor, date prisa! Alagos se está desvaneciendo...'","'¡Ah, mellon! Me alegro de que hayas vuelto tan pronto. Son unas plantas extrañas, ¿verdad? Nunca había visto nada parecido. Machacaré sus hojas y veré si puedo preparar una infusión digna con sus esencias.\
\
'¡Muchísimas gracias, ! Sin duda, eres ${PLAYERNAME:un gran amigo[m]|una gran amiga[f]} de los Malledhrim. Entiendo por qué Galadriel y Celeborn te tienen en tan alta estima, a pesar de que seas ${PLAYERNAME:un forastero[m]|una forastera[f]}.'","Las plantas se pueden encontrar cerca del espantoso estanque del Bosque Ahogado, al sur de Estolad Mernael.\
\
Deberías darte prisa en llegar al estanque y recolectar muchas hierbas allí, ya que estas podrían tener alguna propiedad que pueda curar al caballo Alagos.","Plata de tallo rojo recogido (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Nestawen se encuentra en Estolad Mernael, cuidando de su corcel enfermo, Alagos.\
\
Deberías llevarle a Nestawen las plantas y flores que has recogido para ver si le pueden servir de algo.","Habla con Nestawen en Estolad Mernael","Hierba con flores recogida (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Los antídotos suelen crecer en el mismo suelo que los venenos. Recolecta las hierbas que crecen cerca del estanque contaminado para que los elfos puedan examinarlas y determinar sus propiedades medicinales."},
[12957]={"You ask Gifemund about Iothete, the man who no longer lived at Dunfast. The draughty home piques your interest once again.\
\
'Oh, Iothete? A senile old fool. He kept insisting that he was given a cursed relic, and then he left town when no one believed him.\
\
'He holes himself up in the northern woods, now.'","The Search for the Missing Man","'That was an interesting tale! It would seem that this missing fellow might have information for you, ${PLAYER}.\
\
'I will remain here and help these people get back on their feet. Do come back when you find that man! I must continue my search....","An inhabitant of Dunfast has left and abandoned his home, and you cannot help but hope that he may have information for you.","Cyneberg is at the refugees' hideout in the Whitshaws.\
\
You should speak with Cyneberg.","Based on the memories of the townsfolk, Iothete likely headed north into the woods from Dunfast.\
\
You should search for Iothete, the man with the empty home.","Find Iothete, the owner of the empty home","'Another stranger come to lay a curse on me? Or...do you seek refuge from the cold?\
\
'Which is it? Speak up at once!'","Talk to Cyneberg"},
[12958]={"Torwulf's father must be on or around Gárferth's Farm somewhere. With many Warg-riders roaming the area, he probably didn't make it far.","'My father is missing! I can't believe he didn't make it here by now. I do not want to leave these men behind, but I cannot live without knowing what happened to my father. I need to go look for him. \
\
'Can you please help me find him? Here take this horn and summon me when you are heading that way, and I'll catch up to you.'","'My father... he's gone? But he was just here. We saved him! I... don't know what to say.\
\
'At least we found him, and he can be given a proper burial now. It is the least I can do for him. I can only hope he didn't suffer too much before we arrived.'","Torwulf has gone back to Thrymm's Farm, and will want to have a word with you.","Now that he is with you, speak to Torwulf before heading to Gárferth's Farm.","This is around where Torwulf said you should summon him to you, if you are ready to go to Gárferth's Farm.","'Thank you for helping me find him. Let us make our way to Gárferth's Farm.'","Use the horn on the road south of Thrymm's Farm","'It was not the outcome I was hoping for, but I appreciate your help. There is some comfort in knowing his fate instead of a gnawing unknown. Thank you ${PLAYER}.'","Speak with Torwulf back at Thrymm's Farm","Make your way to Gárferth's Farm.","Torwulf asked you to call him to you on your way to Gárferth's Farm. On the road south of Thrymm's Farm is likely a good spot to summon him.","Gárferth's Farm is one of the three smaller farms, and was abandoned recently when the others were attacked by the White Hand. Torwulf managed to escape, but his father never made it to Thrymm's Farm.","Speak with Torwulf","The Search of Gárferth's Farm","Winerad was barely hanging on, but didn't make it. Torwulf is likely in shock from what has happened, but he wants to have a word with you at the location of his father's death.","Gárferth's Farm is down the road south of Thrymm's Farm.","Speak to Torwulf","You arrived at Gárferth's Farm, and it has been ransacked! Torwulf's father should be nearby...","You hear something approaching...","Find Gárferth's Farm","You hear the old farmer's last breath rattle from his lungs as you kneel down to check on him. A peaceful look creeps across his face, in that final moment. He must have been on the verge of death for some time. He may have found peace knowing he was found, or from catching a glimpse of his last living son.","Find Torwulf's father"},
[12959]={"Return to Siric at Thrymm's Farm","Manléof, who was left behind at Gársig's Farm, is in very poor condition. He isn't likely to live much longer.","Approaching Manléof, you hear pattering feet and hungry growls getting closer...","Gársig's Farm is on the far eastern side of the Fallows, near the Wold.","The Search of Gársig's Farm","Manléof has passed away from his injuries...","Gársig's Farm is in a remote location of the Fallows, and was recently abandoned. Siric made his way to Thrymm's Farm, where those escaping the outlying farms were supposed to escape to. But his friend Manléof, a fellow farmer, has not yet arrived.","'Thank you for trying, ${PLAYER}. The enemy came fast, and we had little chance to survive. I was lucky to make it. I will let Manléof's family know what has happened to him.\
\
'We are losing too many good men from Forlaw these days...'","Manléof didn't survive the encounter with Warg-riders at Gársig's Farm. You should let Siric know what has happened, and he is awaiting your return at Thrymm's Farm.","Find Manléof at Gársig's Farm","Check on Manléof's injuries and defeat any nearby foes","'I barely made it here from Gársig's Farm! Warg-riders came out of nowhere... Manléof and I split up trying to escape. He should have made it here by now. \
\
'Those Warg-riders got my leg while I was escaping, and had to limp my way here. I can't make it back there with my leg like this. I beg you, mighty ${CLASS}, please look for him?'","Manléof is severely injured, but still has a faint pulse... for now"},
[12960]={"At the urging of Captain Róglarg, you are to continue your search for the Elf-warrior at the gate to Imlad Morgul, Fennas Gost. Even if you do not intend to find the \\qElf-warrior\\q, you might still learn more of Gothmog's plans in Minas Morgul.","Fennas Gost can be found due south of Cirith Ungol in the heights of the Ephel Dúath.\
\
Captain Róglarg has asked you to patrol the gate to Imlad Morgul, Fennas Gost, in search of the Elf-warrior on the run in Lhingris. You should travel to Fennas Gost.","You have patrolled Fennas Gost.","'Next is... Fennas Gost....'\
\
Róglarg appears disgusted at having to speak Sindarin.\
\
'The gate to the Dead City has been sealed recently, but I doubt an Elf would have much trouble getting around it. Gothmog's plans in Gondor slipped, and now he's holed up in the Dead City. Some \\qDread Terror\\q he is!'\
\
'If the Elf-warrior's been to the gate, he's either in Imlad Morgul or... he's made it to Ithilien and the High Up will have our heads.\
\
'And lastly...'","Completado","The dread gate of Imlad Morgul looms before you...","The Search: Fennas Gost","Beyond this gate lies Imlad Morgul, where Gothmog now hides in fear of King Elessar.\
\
If the day comes to set siege to the Dead City of Minas Morgul, the bridge from Ithilien into the vale shall either have to be rebuilt or the gate of Fennas Gost must be thrown down.","Patrol Fennas Gost \\qin search of the Elf-warrior\\q"},
[12961]={"At the urging of Captain Róglarg, you are to continue your search for the Elf-warrior at the south-bridge, Iant Angos. Even if you do not intend to find the \\qElf-warrior\\q, you can still learn more of the evils in Lhingris and Talath Úrui.","'Right then.\
\
'The first place you're going to look for the Elf-warrior is at the Iant Angos....'\
\
Róglarg seems to wince at the name.\
\
'If the Elf-warrior's gotten that far, he's not our problem anymore. Urudanî's Ghâsh-hai will find him, and if he's lucky, he'll end up in Naerband.\
\
'Next...'","Iant Angos is a tremendously valuable and strategic holding for the Orcs of Lhingris.\
\
If it were to come to ruin, the forces of Lhingris and Talath Úrui would be separated almost entirely by the Morgai, save through the passes of Durthang and Lugvarg.","The bridge is intact and allows forces from Lhingris and Talath Úrui to swiftly unite...","The Search: Iant Angos","Iant Angos can be found to the south-east of Cirith Ungol in Lhingris.\
\
Captain Róglarg has asked you to patrol Iant Angos in search of the Elf-warrior on the run in Lhingris. You should travel to the bridge of Iant Angos.","Completado","You have patrolled Iant Angos.","Patrol Iant Angos \\qin search of the Elf-warrior\\q"},
[12962]={"You have patrolled Torech Ungol.","At the urging of Captain Róglarg, you are to continue your search for the Elf-warrior at the gate to Imlad Morgul, Fennas Gost. Even if you do not intend to find the \\qElf-warrior\\q, you might aid Legolas in learning more about the caverns where Shelob dwells.","Patrol Torech Ungol \\qin search of the Elf-warrior\\q","Amid the shadows of Torech Ungol, you see webbing coating nearly every stone around you...","The shadowed tunnels of Torech Ungol loom before you, but the largest tunnel appears to be sealed by rocks and debris.\
\
If Shelob still dwells within, it is likely that she has become trapped in the aftermath of Sauron's downfall.","Completado","The Search: Torech Ungol","Torech Ungol can be found up the pathway south-west of Cirith Ungol in the heights of the Ephel Dúath.\
\
Captain Róglarg has asked you to patrol Torech Ungol, Shelob's Lair, in search of the Elf-warrior on the run in Lhingris. You should travel to Torech Ungol, but remain on guard.","'Lastly, I want you to scout Shelob's lair. That's right, I want you to go to Torech Ungol!'\
\
Róglarg again appears disgusted at having to speak Sindarin.\
\
'If the Elf-warrior's not been to the others, maybe he's gone back to finish the job on old Shelob. He stuck a pin in Her Ladyship like none have before. Nar, but Shelob's had it easy for years. Probably just caught her off-guard....\
\
'Maybe he thinks he'll get lucky, but I don't think she'll make the same mistake twice!\
\
'When that's all done, come back to me and we'll try to figure out what you saw. Maybe I'll get you a brush and some paper or something... I'm sure we have tark's blood around here somewhere!'"},
[12963]={"La Estación de la Alegría","Saervereth se encuentra en Duillond, en la zona del festival.\
\
Saervereth estará ansiosa por ver el muérdago y reflexionar sobre el verdadero significado de Yule.","'¿Has encontrado ya algo de muérdago? Puede recolectarse al norte de aquí.'","Puedes encontrar muérdago en los jóvenes abetos a lo largo del camino del norte hacia el Refugio de caza de Thrasi.\
\
Saervereth te pidió que recolectaras algo de muérdago para que pudiera recordar el verdadero significado de Yule.","Recolecta muérdago (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'He presenciado el paso de más estaciones de Yule de las que une criatura joven como tú podría imaginar, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo[m]|amiga[f]}. Cada año celebramos su tránsito recogiendo el muérdago de los jóvenes abetos. Parte se usa en infusiones, parte como adorno, pero en su mayoría lo utilizamos para recordarnos lo fugaz del paso del tiempo.\
\
'Aún no he salido a recolectarlo este año, pues temo tener demasiado que hacer aquí. Si no llegara a ver el muérdago, sentiría una gran pena cuando debería estar celebrando. El invierno es el comienzo del ciclo del renacimiento de la primavera, no una muerte, como muchos mortales lo perciben. Yule y el muérdago existen para recordarnos esto.\
\
'Si tuvieras a bien seguir el camino hacia el norte en dirección al Refugio de caza de Thrasi, encontrarás jóvenes abetos justo antes de la curva, adornados con muérdago recién crecido. Tráeme un poco para que pueda reavivar mi esperanza en el renacer de la estación.'","Muérdago recolectado (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Lleva el muérdago a Saervereth en Duillond","'Tienes mi más profundo agradecimiento por haberme traído este muérdago, ${PLAYER}. Nunca debe olvidarse que la vida conduce a la muerte, y aun así la muerte trae nueva vida.'","Los elfos celebran el festival de Yule recolectando muérdago de los jóvenes abetos.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTA: Esta misión se eliminará de tu registro de misiones cuando finalice el festival actual.</rgb>"},
[12964]={"The Seat of Two Kings","You see the crumpled body of a Man in the distance...","Talk to Halhir","Search the Palace of Eldacar for the lost Ranger","'He should have known better than to tread so close to the Enemy's holdings, even if knowledge of their movements could be gained.\
\
'Do not think me a callous man, ${PLAYER}. It is hard to muster much feeling after seeing so many of one's friends murdered by these vile wraiths!'","Worried that his fellow has not yet returned, Halhir sends you to investigate the abandoned Palace of King Eldacar.","The Palace of Eldacar can be found due west of Halhir in western Osgiliath.\
\
You have spotted a crumpled body in the distance. You should examine it before leaving the Palace.","Examine the slain Ranger","The Palace of Eldacar can be found due west of Halhir in western Osgiliath.\
\
You have not found Halhir's ally, and should now search within the ruins of the Palace.","Halhir can be found due east of the Palace of Eldacar in western Osgiliath.\
\
You have found Halhir's slain ally, and should now return to him bearing the news of his friend's passing.","Strange wounds mark the man's lifeless body and a blunted Morgul-blade lies nearby...","'A fellow Ranger and I were to scout the square, but we became separated. His name is of no import to you, for you did not know him as I have.\
\
'I saw him scout near the old Palace of King Eldacar, but then he was lost from sight and I had to fall back. The Palace is a grim place, and I believe the Enemy seeks to use it as a stronghold for his servants - the Nazgûl. They spend much of their time up above on those vile beasts, but I have seen them pass among the forces here in Osgiliath and even the Orcs recoil at their approach.\
\
'If he has gone into the palace, he is likely dead, but I wish to know for certain. Search the palace, and return to me here when you have finished. Only then shall we speak of returning to the tunnels.'","You have not found the Ranger, but the air grows heavy and dreadful near the palace...","The Palace of Eldacar can be found due west of Halhir in western Osgiliath.\
\
Halhir has asked you to search near the Palace of Eldacar for a lost ally.","Search for the lost Ranger outside the Palace of Eldacar"},
[12966]={"'¿Quién eres tú para luchar por este clan de débiles? Bueno, no importa, ¡te aplastaremos y entonces la Corona de Hierro tomará Aughaire!'","Has salido victorioso","Acepta el desafío de Donnan","'Una vez más, es hora de luchar por el honor de mi clan. Has demostrado ser digno, sureño, pero ahora las reglas han cambiado.\
\
'Esta vez, los dos hermanos Donnan y Mungan afirman haber sido agraviados por nuestro clan. Mienten, pero el Juez ha permitido que ambos luchen contra nosotros al mismo tiempo. Ten cuidado con el hermano menor, Donnan, pues es el más feroz de los dos. Los encontrarás aquí en Aughaire, en el lado oeste del pueblo, esperando que respondas a su desafío.'","El segundo símbolo de honor, la piedra del Túmulo de Honor, fue más difícil de obtener, ya que requirió entrar en territorio hostil sin combatir.","Arzhur está en Aughaire.\
\
Debes regresar con Arzhur para informarle de tu victoria en el segundo desafío.","Donnan y su hermano están en Aughaire, en el lado oeste del pueblo de los montañeses, esperando tu respuesta a su desafío.\
\
Arzhur te ha pedido una vez más que luches contra los retadores de un clan hostil leal a Angmar.","'De nuevo has triunfado, sureño, esta vez contra todo pronóstico. Pero temo que, a pesar de tu victoria, la situación pronto se volverá más desesperada.'","El Segundo Desafío"},
[12967]={"'Según los antiguos registros, el segundo engranaje fue escondido en un cofre en unas ruinas antiguas al sur, en el Valle de Thráin. Las ruinas están en el lado oeste del valle, fuera del camino y al otro lado del Valle desde Noglond. Los registros indican que el cofre está en el lado sur de las ruinas.'","El segundo engranaje","Lleva el segundo engranaje a Bávor","Encuentra el segundo engranaje perdido","Bávor es un mecánico encargado de reparar el gran mecanismo que da acceso a la legendaria Bóveda de la Montaña.","'¡Sí! ¡Este es! Espera... ¿realmente encaja en algún lado? ¿Qué tal aquí? Ah, ya lo resolveré con tiempo. Por ahora, ¡debemos encontrar los otros engranajes!'","Segundo engranaje perdido encontrado","Bávor está en la Mansión de Thorin.\
\
Bávor estará complacido de ver que has conseguido el segundo engranaje.","'Ese primer engranaje ha visto días mejores, pero no está más allá de la reparación. Me pondré a trabajar en eso mientras tú buscas el segundo engranaje.\
\
'Según los antiguos registros, el segundo engranaje fue escondido en un cofre en unas ruinas antiguas al sur, en el Valle de Thráin. Las ruinas están en el lado oeste del valle, fuera del camino y al otro lado del Valle desde Noglond. Los registros indican que el cofre está en el lado sur de las ruinas.\
\
'Sin embargo, hay algo que deberías saber: los trasgos han invadido esas ruinas. Ten cuidado.'","El cofre que contiene el segundo engranaje puede encontrarse en el lado sur de las ruinas infestadas de trasgos en el Valle de Thráin, al sur de la Mansión de Thorin y al oeste de Noglond.\
\
Bávor descubrió la ubicación del segundo engranaje y te ha enviado a buscarlo mientras él repara el primero.","'Por favor, encuentra el segundo engranaje perdido. Está en las ruinas al oeste de Noglond, en el Valle de Thráin.'"},
[12969]={"Descubre y elimina el motivo de la preocupación de Lar","La Sala Decimosexta es una zona infestada de orcos, muchos de los cuales padecen una terrible enfermedad que provoca crecimientos similares a hongos en sus cuerpos.\
\
Mallas, un elfo aliado de los enanos, cree que hay algo oculto bajo la Sala Decimosexta y desea descubrir el verdadero propósito y el origen de la plaga.","'No hay palabras para describir un horror como ese, pero mi presentimiento ha desaparecido ahora que dices que ya no está. Puedo respirar un poco más tranquilo.\
\
'Le contaré a Mallas de tu gran hazaña, ${PLAYER}.'","Regresa con Lar en el Refugio Sombrío","La Sala Decimosexta se encuentra al noreste del Refugio Sombrío.\
\
Lar te ha pedido que te adentres en lo más profundo de la Sala Decimosexta y trates de encontrar el origen de su inquietud.","'La Sala Decimosexta es un sitio horrendo, ${CLASS}. Los orcos de allí padecen una enfermedad terrible, pero hay algo más que me preocupa.\
\
'Mi intuición es excelente, eso sí, o de lo contrario no te molestaría con mis conjeturas. He estado observando al enemigo de cerca desde mi vigilancia; basándome en su comportamiento, me atrevería a decir que algo se oculta allá en la lejanía.\
\
'¡Adéntrate tanto como te atrevas en la Sala Decimosexta y descubre su secreto! No te preocupes, no creo que sea una misión en vano. Encontrarás la sala dirigiéndote al noreste desde el Refugio Sombrío.'","El secreto de las profundidades","'Aunque te estoy enviando hacia un grave peligro, no puedo contarte mucho más sobre esta misión, pues ni yo mismo lo sé. Espero que confíes en mí: todas las señales indican que hay algo importante por descubrir en la Sala Decimosexta.'","Has matado al Descarriado","Lar se encuentra en el Refugio Sombrío, al suroeste de la Sala Decimosexta.\
\
Vuelve con Lar y dile lo que has descubierto y matado: una terrible criatura sin cabeza en las profundidades de la sala, acechando en una habitación llena de esporas y baba."},
[12970]={"An affable woman pulls you aside.\
\
'You there! Are you looking for work?'\
\
You begin to answer, but she doesn't let you finish.\
\
'Of course you are!'\
\
She pushes a cloth-lined basket into your hands.\
\
'There is an herb that grows outside the western gate of Pelargir. It has broad leaves and a distinct smell, like the rind of a sour fruit. I would go get it myself, but as you can see we have a lot of hungry customers to feed.'\
\
She leans in and whispers in a conspiratorial tone.\
\
'Onjópo is a great cook, but he doesn't do well under pressure. I need to make sure he doesn't burn anything.'\
\
She sends you off with a wink.","Collected savoury herbs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Jódha needs some help preparing for a rush of customers at her food stall.","You have found enough herbs to satisfy Jódha.\
\
Deliver the savoury herbs to Jódha.","With a sweep of her arm, Jódha gestures to the line of hungry patrons waiting in front of the grill.\
\
'We started out feeding just the shipbreakers and shipbuilders, but before we knew it half of Pelargir has come lining up for our food! We never expected to be so popular. Thank you for the herbs. They're one of the most important ingredients in our marinade.\
\
'You'll... keep that a secret, won't you?'","The Secret Ingredient","Collect savoury herbs (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Jódha","Jódha has asked you to pick some savoury herbs outside of Pelargir.\
\
Find herbs in the fields west of Pelargir."},
[12971]={"Exit into the Fourth Circle","'Ah, ${PLAYER}, I knew you would find it! While you have been searching, I have spoken with the others, and Gelwen and Glatham have asked if they can come along.\
\
'Would you lead the three of us into the cisterns? Ah, but perhaps you should speak to Gelwen first.'","The Finding Place lies near the cisterns' exit in the Fourth Circle.\
\
The children have spotted something they call the \\qFinding Place.\\q Walk over to it and see what it is. If you get separated, use Bergil's whistle to call the children to you.","'What is this?'\
\
Bergil takes the letter and examines it.\
\
'Oh, by Queen Beruthiel's cats! It's a letter Landath was meant to deliver. He must have lost it. How did it end up here? Well, that's the wonder of the Finding Place.\
\
'Never mind that. Let us go tell the others we have found a way up - and get Landath his letter. Maybe there's even still time for him to deliver it!'","Found the key","Meet Bergil back at the Old Guest-house","'We have set more than one thing right on this adventure, ${PLAYER}, and I am glad. But most of all, I am glad we can reach the Finding Place once again. We boys and girls have become used to looking in there - and the things we would find! Lost trinkets, sweets, a coin or two.\
\
'I would have felt doubly ashamed, if I had cut all them off from that!\
\
'But look at Landath over there, puzzling over the letter! I do wonder when Himnir's sweet treats will arrive. You must join us when they do.'","The Wrights' Fellow-hall lies on the far southern end of the First Circle.\
\
Bergil knows of a second, unwatched door into the Cisterns, which might grant the children passage directly to the Fourth Circle. A key to it was lost near the Wrights' Fellow-hall recently. Search for it in that area.","The door can be found near the Wrights' Fellow-hall, in the southern stretch of the First Circle.\
\
Enter the cisterns through the hidden door.","'What will we find, I wonder? Do you think a passage to the Fourth Circle truly exists?'","'Imagine, the Finding Place so near to the secret passage. We must go over to it at once.'","Talk to Bergil","'I plan to go through the secret passage as often as I can. The Fourth Circle! I do hope some of the poets or minstrels or stage players will still play, even though these are times of war.'","'The Finding Place! I wonder what we'll find in it this time.'","Bergil and his friends seek a new way to reach the city's upper circles, now that the Second Circle is barred to them.","Checked location for the key","You think you can see the spot Gelwen is pointing at, some yards off","Look for the key (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'Gelwen is just over there. You really should speak with her before we go.'","'I hope my sister is right about the Secret Walker. But if she is going in there, then I will go, too!'","'Oh... This is where all the water is!'","Reaching your hand into the crevice, you discover a letter!","'I must confess, it is stranger and more wonderful than I had even imagined.'","Gelwen stands in front of the Old Guest-house, in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates.\
\
Bergil says two other children, Gelwen and Glatham, would like to join you in searching the cisterns for the secret passage. He suggested that you speak with Gelwen herself, first.","Found the key!","Bergil, Gelwen, and Glatham arrive nearly on your heels","'Maybe Gelwen is right and the Secret Walker is just a tale. But how can we be sure?'","'See, Glatham? The Secret Walker didn't appear and the passage DID go through, and look! Do you see where we are? The Finding Place is very near. What fortune! We must go over to it at once!\
\
'Come, ${PLAYER}. You will see for yourself!'","Found the way up to the Fourth Circle","Talk to Gelwen","Bergil waits in front of the Old Guest-house, in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates.\
\
Tell Bergil you found the key to the cisterns' hidden door. With it, the children might find passage directly to the Fourth Circle.","The Old Guest-house lies in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates.\
\
Meet Bergil and the other children back at the Old Guest-house.","'This shall be a grand adventure, ${PLAYER}!'","'Can I see?'","'Oh! Now that I am here, my doubts seem larger and my certainty smaller than it did before. But I shall be brave... so long as you lead the way before us. You are the grown adventurer and we are but children, after all, ${PLAYER}!'","'Then we shall meet within the hidden entrance to the cisterns? Good.'","Search for a way up","If you get separated from the children, use Bergil's whistle to call them to you.\
\
Explore the cisterns with Bergil, Gelwen, and Glatham, and search for a passage up to the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith.","'What is it? What did you find?'","'Now that I think of it, there may be a way around the Second Circle, but... no, we must try, and with your help, ${PLAYER}, maybe, just maybe, it can be done.\
\
'You see, I have heard that within the City Cisterns, you may climb right up to the Fourth Circle - which is just where we wish to go! Only, we'd never be allowed in through the Clean-waters. Not by ourselves. Not whenever we pleased!\
\
'There is a hidden entrance, though, by the Wrights' Fellow-hall, that is seldom used. And as it should happen, one of the keys for it was lost just last week. I know because I heard Master Carethon cursing out the lad who lost it. If it could be found - if you could find it - why then, we'd be one step closer to that secret passage, wouldn't we?'","Enter the cisterns through the hidden door","The Secret Passage","Found the key.","Fourth Circle - Players' Tier","'Well, now my luck's taken a turn for the better!'","'If you could find that key to the hidden cisterns' door, then we'd be one step closer to reaching the upper tiers. It must be somewhere near the Wrights' Fellow-hall that it was lost.'","If you get separated from the children, use Bergil's whistle to call them to you.\
\
You have met Bergil, Gelwen, and Glatham in the cisterns. Gelwen has something to say.","If you get separated from the children, use Bergil's whistle to call them to you.\
\
Show Bergil the slightly crumpled letter you found in the crevice of the Finding Place.","'So you are ${PLAYER}. It is a pleasure to meet you. Bergil has told us of your adventure together and his plan.\
\
'The others all think that the Secret Walker lives in the cisterns and are afraid to set foot inside. I think they are wrong, and that the Secret Walker is nothing but a story made to scare little girls and boys.\
\
'In addition, I wish more than anything to see inside the cisterns. I imagine it must be wondrous and beautiful. Therefore, my brother and I wish to go with you. If you agree, then let us meet within the door.'","If you get separated from the children, use Bergil's whistle to call them to you.\
\
You have come out of the secret passage through the cisterns, to the Fourth Circle of the City. Gelwen again appears to have something she wishes to say.","Investigate the Finding Place"},
[12972]={"The Angmarim cultists have taken over the dwarf-fort Bagud-dum.\
\
You should complete objectives in Bagud-dum to prevent their plans from reaching fruition.","Talk to Hórin just outside the door to the keep in Bagud-dum","The ancient dwarf-fort known as Bagud-dum has been taken over by the Angmarim. There they plan to perform an ancient ritual which might reveal their true motives.","Hórin is standing by outside Bagud-dum.\
\
You should speak to Hórin and complete 'Instance: The Secret Ritual'.","'Did you find Loknashra?'\
\
You tell him that Loknashra has vanished, but you did what you could to hinder the efforts of the Angmarim.\
\
'Where could she have gone? Well, if she lives, I'm sure we'll find out soon enough. There are other matters to attend to for now. We are nearly at the very peak of the mountain, and as we have not yet run into Warlord Dushtalbúk and his host, there is only one place left he is likely to be.'","Loknashra and the staff are gone!","Talk to Hórin outside Bagud-dum","Talk to Hórin outside Bagud-dum and go with him to investigate","'We will enter Bagud-dum when you are ready.'","Complete 'Spirits and Summoners' for Hórin","Find Loknashra inside the keep of Bagud-dum","'This must be where most of the Angmarim travelled. This is a large camp! No sign of Loknashra out here, though... she must be inside. I do not know what horrors the Angmarim have waiting for us inside, but we have to find that staff before they complete whatever evil ritual they mean to do within! We must sneak inside, and quickly!'","'${PLAYER}? Can you hear me? ${PLAYER}! Oh thank the Valar, you are returning to consciousness! After that blast, I wasn't sure I would be able to drag you out in time. Fell spirits began to churn the very air inside that fort! I am not sure what happened after that... Is Loknashra still alive?'\
\
You tell Hórin you aren't sure, but you want to find out and take action against the Cult of Drugoth.\
\
'You want to go back in there? Truthfully I am not surprised! Go be a hero, then. I will wait for you here. Go find Loknashra, and bring her down if you can!'","The Secret Ritual","Hórin is waiting for you outside Bagud-dum.\
\
You should talk to Hórin.","Hórin has dragged you out of Bagud-dum.\
\
You should talk to Hórin.","Complete 'Apprentices of the Cult' for Hórin"},
[12973]={"Talk to Mithrandir in Thuringwath","'I am told that beyond this darkness lies Thuringwath, the Valley of Secret Shadow.\
\
'It is difficult to believe the Enemy could have hidden such a place so near to Minas Ithil of old, but it is that uncertainty which has led me here.\
\
'Have the Enemy's works crumbled to naught behind a veil of shadow? Or does some evil still dwell beneath the notice of Gondor?\
\
'I must know the truth of it, but I do not wish to walk alone. Will you accompany me, ${PLAYER}?'","Talk to Mithrandir","Mithrandir can be found in Falch Gurth.\
\
Mithrandir has asked you to accompany him into Thuringwath. You should talk to Mithrandir when you are prepared.","'Ven, ${PLAYER}.'","'Es peor de lo que temía, ${PLAYER}.'","Mithrandir can be found in Thuringwath.\
\
You have passed through Falch Gurth into Thuringwath with Mithrandir. You should talk to Mithrandir.","The Secret Shadow","Thuringwath, the Valley of Secret Shadow, has remained hidden among the slopes of Ephel Dúath since the Second Age of the world."},
[12974]={"Talk to King Thorin III","An old tome found in Erebor leads to the mystery of The Secret Stone. What does it mean?","'Tome? What Tome? I'm sorry, I know nothing about it. Perhaps you should ask King Thorin.'","The Secret Stone","A tome rests on this bench, left behind by someone.  It seems ancient, like it might just turn to dust if handled too roughly. Several pages have been torn out and are missing. A poem is written on the page that was left open:\
\
Beneath the Misty Mountains, deep,\
The ancient shadows hold their keep.\
Came Durin King, his crown of stars,\
To carve new halls, claim kingdom ours.\
Above the dwarf-made forges glow,\
While unknown dangers lurk below.\
\
For many thousand years it slept,\
In darkened depths, where fell-things crept.\
And then, one day, the stone was found,\
Dark as night, and perfectly round.\
Its beauty beckons but a glance,\
But ensnares the mind in a trance.\
\
Many were lost, driven insane,\
And then we unearthed Durin's Bane.\
From Moria, the Longbeards flee\
In hand, the stone-that-should-not-be.\
By King Thráin's orders, it is sealed,\
By secret door never revealed.\
\
Just the line of Durin may know,\
Of Secret Stone, born of shadow.\
Heed this warning, do not seek it,\
This fell thing you cannot outwit!\
The stone must remain locked away\
Do not seek the hidden doorway!\
\
King Thorin III is in the line of Durin. Perhaps he would be willing to share more about this Secret Stone.","You very gently pick up the tome","King Thorin III can be found at his seat in Erebor.\
\
You should bring the tome to King Thorin III.","'What have you brought me, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
He takes the tome from you and gently leafs through the pages. Realization suddenly lights his eyes.\
\
'Abnubuzûr! The Secret Stone! Where did you find this, ${PLAYER}?'\
\
You tell him you found it left on a bench here in Erebor.\
\
'I can hardly believe my eyes! Knowledge of the stone was passed down from my father, but its location has been lost. I believe my people took the Stone with them when they fled Moria, but not even I know where this secret door can be found.'","Collect the dusty tome"},
[12975]={"The Secret of Stormwall","Talk to Agátur","Beyond the corpse of a spider lies a large crack in the old dwarf crafting halls of Stormwall. Singed webbing coats the abyss. You wonder what could lie within these ancient spider tunnels. Perhaps the spider in front of you has more clues.","You should return to Agátur, back in Skarháld.","Deep within Stormwall lies a fiery secret, slumbering in the shadows.","A spider corpse can be found deep within Stormwall, high in the mountains north-east of Skarháld.\
\
You should examine the spider corpse.","Examine the spider corpse","As you look at the spider remains, you hear sounds in the tunnel. Not the sounds of spiders, but the sounds of drakes and other dragon-kind. They are drawing near. Prepare to defend yourself!","'${PLAYER}. You have returned, alive. Of that I am most glad! This dwarf you rescued, Drengur, claims that he saw not a drake or worm, but a dragon.\
\
'I will speak with Hórin. If Etterfang yet lives, she is a mortal enemy to both the Longbeards and the Zhélruka! We must act before the beast awakes!'"},
[12977]={"Puede que un Elfo esté acampado cerca de Casa del Bosque, al sur de Bolgovado.\
\
Linda Bolger quedó desconcertada por tu hallazgo de un collar donde ella había visto al gran lobo. No pudo leer las letras del collar, pero pensó que quizá el Elfo que Milo creyó ver podría descifrarlas.","'Dicen que los Elfos a veces pasan por la Comarca camino a las Torres Blancas o al Mar, o eso cuentan las viejas historias, si te interesan esas cosas.\
\
Mi esposo dice que habló con un Elfo acampado en el bosque cerca de Casa del Bosque, al suroeste. Dicen que los Elfos saben mucho sobre escrituras antiguas y esas cosas. Quizá, si Milo no estaba viendo cosas que no existen, ese Elfo podría leer las letras. Casa del Bosque está al sur de Bolgovado, y el Elfo supuestamente acampaba en la colina que domina el pueblo.\
\
Espero que pueda ayudar. No me avergüenza decir que estoy simplemente aterrada de los lobos.'","'Sí, vi a un Elfo en la colina sobre Casa del Bosque, al sur de Bolgovado. He oído que los Elfos saben todo sobre letras. Ese Elfo podría ayudar.'","El secreto del collar","Lleva el collar con runas al Elfo cerca de Casa del Bosque","'Si Milo no estaba viendo cosas que no existen, ese Elfo en Casa del Bosque podría leer las letras de este collar. ¿Por qué no vas a echar un vistazo allí?'","Has encontrado un collar inscrito con runas que no puedes leer, aparentemente enterrado por el lobo inusualmente grande que Linda Bolger vio la noche en que los lobos atravesaron Bolgovado.","'${PLAYERNAME:Bienvenido[m]|Bienvenida[f]}, , soy Orthir de Rivendel. No es común que reciba visitas en este lugar. ¿Qué es eso que quieres que examine?\
\
Son letras malignas, ${PLAYERNAME:amigo mío[m]|amiga mía[f]}, pero las leeré si eso trae entendimiento. Las runas inscritas en el collar identifican a esta criatura como un gran cacique de lobos, un huargo de Angmar llamado Laugfût.\
\
Si Laugfût se ha liberado de su collar, probablemente piense en servirse a sí mismo en vez de a sus antiguos amos. No dudo que el huargo fue enviado en alguna misión maligna, pero ahora busca causar algún mal por su propia cuenta.'"},
[12978]={"'¡Estoy impaciente por descubrir el secreto de este nuevo mapa! Parece indicar un destino situado al sureste de aquí. Si yo fuera tú, investigaría por Nud‑melek… veamos, dijiste que el camino descendía… ¿quizá la sección sur de la Sala Segunda?'","'¡Por mis robustas botas, qué historia! Pistas y mapas, sombras y enigmas y monstruos… ¡esto dará para un gran relato cuando llegue a viejo!\
\
'Así que encontraste la cámara más interior de este extraño lugar… ¿Y qué hallaste allí? ¿Un hacha? ¿Un hacha marcada como \\qMatadragones\\q? ¡Por la barba de Durin!\
\
'${PLAYER}, creo que aquí hay más de lo que parece a simple vista. No me agrada dar este consejo, pero pienso que deberías hablar con uno de los elfos aquí en Moria; Lenglammel parece la indicada, aunque tendrás que descender hasta el Refugio Sombrío para encontrarla. Cuéntale tus peripecias y lo que hallaste en tu destino, y escucha lo que tenga que decir.'","'Deberías hablar con la elfa Lenglammel en el Refugio Sombrío. Puede que sepa algo sobre lo que has encontrado.'","Geirfast se encuentra en la Sala Vigesimoprimera.\
\
Deberías regresar de inmediato con Geirfast.","Habla con Geirfast en la Sala Vigesimoprimera","Habla con Geirfast y descubre los secretos de tu misterioso destino","El secreto del Consejo","'Los relatos sobre tu redescubrimiento del hacha Matadragones han llegado hasta mí, ${PLAYER}.'","Lenglammel se encuentra acampada en el Refugio Sombrío.\
\
Geirfast te sugirió que hablaras con la elfa Lenglammel.","Geirfast se encuentra en la Sala Vigesimoprimera, al noroeste de la Sala Segunda.\
\
Deberías regresar con Geirfast para contarle dónde se halla la cámara.","'Recuperar Matadragones no es empresa menor, ${PLAYER}; deberías sentirte orgulloso.'","'¿Estás ${PLAYERNAME:preparado[m]|preparada[f]}?\
\
'Qué época tan emocionante para encontrarse en Khazad-dûm… ¡tantos misterios saliendo a la luz por primera vez en tantísimo tiempo!'","'¿Eres tú, ${RACE}, quien halló el lugar de reposo del hacha Matadragones?'","'¿Puede ser? ¿Eres tú? El hacha que describes me es conocida, pero solo por las leyendas. Se profetizó que alguien ajeno a nuestro número —el casi olvidado consejo secreto de elfos y enanos— la encontraría de nuevo, en nuestro antiguo cuartel general, en los recovecos más profundos de la mina enana.\
\
'El mapa que hallaste fue un último intento desesperado de dejar constancia, por si el escondite de Matadragones caía en el olvido; algo que entonces parecía imposible, pero no previmos el despertar del Azote de Durin, el abandono de Khazad‑dûm ni su degeneración en la temida Moria. Cuando Smaug aterrorizaba la Montaña Solitaria, algunos de los nuestros fueron enviados a buscar registros sobre el paradero de Matadragones, sin encontrar nada.\
\
'Tú, valiente ${RACE}, has descubierto un tesoro sin parangón. El señor Elrond será avisado, al igual que dama Galadriel… tu nombre será cantado por los miembros del consejo durante Eras enteras.'","Habla con Geirfast","Has descubierto la cámara secreta","La entrada se encuentra en algún lugar de Nud-melek, al sureste de la Sala Vigesimoprimera, quizá en la Sala Segunda.\
\
Geirfast te ha pedido que encuentres la entrada a la cámara secreta representada en el mapa de sombras.","'Creo que la entrada a la cámara se encuentra en algún punto de la Sala Segunda.'","Geirfast se encuentra en la Sala Vigesimoprimera.\
\
Deberías hablar con Geirfast cuando estés listo para viajar.","Habla con Lenglammel en el Refugio Sombrío","'¡Asombroso, lo has encontrado! Ahora que sabemos dónde está, regresar allí será mucho más rápido.\
\
'Quizá te convenga llevar contigo a uno o dos compañeros si vas a sondear los secretos de esta cámara. ¿Quién sabe qué peligros podrían aguardarte en su interior?\
\
'Sospecho que las extrañas adivinanzas del reverso de este mapa te ayudarán en esta última exploración. Te haré una copia fiel de ellas, para que puedas llevarla contigo a la cámara.'","'El relato de tus hazañas se adelantó a tu llegada, ${PLAYER}. Hallaste la antigua cámara de reuniones del consejo secreto… impresionante.'","Descubre la entrada a la cámara secreta","Según la descripción del mapa que la antorcha proyectó en la pared, Geirfast cree que la cámara secreta debe encontrarse en algún punto de Nud‑melek, quizá en la parte sur de la Sala Segunda."},
[12979]={"El secreto de las espadas","'¡${PLAYERNAME:Bienvenido, extraño[m]|Bienvenida, extraña[f]}! He permanecido aquí mucho tiempo, buscando desentrañar un misterio de tiempos pasados. ¿Quizás puedas ayudarme? Al menos Banfuir cree que tienes cierta habilidad, de lo contrario no te habría enviado.\
\
'Mira las siete estatuas detrás de mí; sin duda notas que a cada una le falta la espada que una vez sostuvo. Este lugar es de un mal antiguo, algo que he estudiado durante mucho tiempo, y conozco demasiado bien las cicatrices que ha dejado a su paso.\
\
'Este lugar detestable puede ser donde se forjó la perdición de los reinos del norte, pero no hablaré más de ello hasta que haya recuperado las siete espadas.'","Hay muchas viejas historias olvidadas en Angmar, pero Nethraw solo está interesado en una.","El maestro del saber Nethraw se encuentra en el Krúsle Lannan, a una considerable distancia al este de Gabilshathûr.\
\
Banfuir te sugirió que hablaras con el maestro del saber Nethraw.","'¿Conoces algo del saber de Angmar?\
\
'Bueno, no importa. Aprenderás... si Nethraw tiene algo que decir al respecto. Se encuentra en un valle solitario, el Krúsle Lannan, muy al este de aquí, meditando sobre los Siete Centinelas.\
\
'No tengo duda de que podría necesitar tu ayuda.'"},
[12980]={"The Secrets of Gloomingtarn","Hersegg rushes to your side!","Scout Lochan Dúv with Hersegg","Hersegg can be found at the entrance to Mîn Lorg within Lochan Dúv in Gloomingtarn.\
\
You have found the entrance to Mîn Lorg. You should talk to Hersegg.","'A-ha! This must be it.\
\
'Over here, ${PLAYER}.'","Lochan Dúv can be found to the west of Lugun-nâla in Gloomingtarn.\
\
Hersegg has asked you to accompany her in combatting the Iron Crown at Lochan Dúv. You should travel to Lochan Dúv with Hersegg.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you become separated from Hersegg, use the horn she gave you to summon her back to your side.</rgb>","Talk to Hersegg at Mîn Lorg","Lochan Dúv has been thrown into disarray!","The Iron Crown commander can be found at Lochan Dúv. Hersegg can be found at your side.\
\
You should defeat the Iron Crown commander at Lochan Dúv and aid Hersegg with her task.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you become separated from Hersegg, use the horn she gave you to summon her back to your side.</rgb>","'It's worse than I thought, ${PLAYER}. There must be a hundred of them all told!'\
\
Hersegg looks around Lochan Dúv, and her eyes stop when she spots a small metal cage.\
\
'Ukhrâsh?! What use could these Men possibly have for them? More importantly, someone must be leading this expedition here in Lochan Dúv—and they will know what the Iron Crown has planned for Gloomingtarn.\
\
'Hmm, I have an idea, ${PLAYER}, but it might be a bit risky!'","Within the cavern, you hear distant Angmarim voices...","Defeat the Iron Crown commander at Lochan Dúv","The entrance to Mîn Lorg can be found somewhere within Lochan Dúv in Gloomingtarn.\
\
The Iron Crown commander held orders demanding an excavation of Mîn Lorg before the arrival of his master, Allaban the Collector. You should search for the entrance to Mîn Lorg.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you become separated from Hersegg, use the horn she gave you to summon her back to your side.</rgb>","After learning that the Angmarim of the Iron Crown appear to have uncovered a secret passage known as Mîn Lorg, Hersegg resolves to stop them and discover the secrets of Gloomingtarn for the Gabil'akkâ.","Hersegg can be found at your side.\
\
You have defeated the Iron Crown commander and helped to sow discord at Lochan Dúv. You should talk to Hersegg.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you become separated from Hersegg, use the horn she gave you to summon her back to your side.</rgb>","'I can't be sure it was their doing, but it looks like the Men of the Iron Crown have used some of the old crystal-lamps to light the way deeper into the cavern. At least we won't have to fumble around in the dark!\
\
'Whatever they uncovered must be something of great power or worth, ${PLAYER}, and that worries me!'","Talk to Hersegg","Determined to discover lost artifacts, the Angmarim of the Iron Crown toil within Lochan Dúv","As the Iron Crown commander falls defeated, Hersegg swiftly collects the scroll-case he carried","Hersegg can be found at your side.\
\
You have found the entrance to Mîn Lorg. You should talk to Hersegg.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you become separated from Hersegg, use the horn she gave you to summon her back to your side.</rgb>","Aid Hersegg with 'Curious Captives'","'Honourless villains! It was the Iron Crown that stole away the Black Stone Anvil of Durin the Deathless, and they do not intend to stop there.\
\
'They now send their servants not only to Gloomingtarn, but into the Clovengap and into the heights of the Welkin-lofts. It seems they seek to lay claim to everything in Mount Gundabad, but that shall not be so! The Angmarim gather to Lochan Dúv like moths to the flame, and I fear the tide of battle may soon turn against my grandfather's expedition—and the Gabil'akkâ.\
\
'We must stop them here, ${PLAYER}, and strike at the very heart of their encampment!'","'Hah! That worked better than I'd hoped! Now then, let's have a look at this....'\
\
Hersegg produces the scroll-case she recovered from the Iron Crown commander and begins to read it. Her eyes widen, and she looks to you.\
\
'It seems these Angmarim have discovered an ancient passage here in Gloomingtarn, and if these notes are to be believed, they suspect it was an early dwelling of Durin the Deathless. The eldest house... if such a thing can truly be!\
\
'Among these writings were orders demanding that the passage—which they have named Mîn Lorg—be excavated and their findings gathered before the arrival of their master, Allaban, from Câr Bronach.\
\
'From what I can tell, Mîn Lorg must lie somewhere within Lochan Dúv. We must find it, ${PLAYER}, and prevent the Iron Crown from defiling it!'","Hersegg can be found at your side.\
\
You have entered Lochan Dúv with Hersegg. You should talk to Hersegg.\
\
<rgb=#FF0000>NOTE: If you become separated from Hersegg, use the horn she gave you to summon her back to your side.</rgb>","Find the entrance to Mîn Lorg"},
[12981]={"¡Había un collar en el esqueleto!","Rhiangar te ha pedido que estés atento a cualquier señal de que su madre pudo haber visitado Sarch Vorn.\
\
Sarch Vorn está en el norte de Cardolan.","Busca pistas","Los secretos de Sarch Vorn","Lleva el collar a Rhiangar","Hace muchos años, la madre de Rhiangar desapareció. ¿Podrían estar escondidas en Sarch Vorn pistas sobre su paradero?","'¿Qué tienes ahí? Oh... ¿dónde lo...?'\
\
Le cuentas acerca del esqueleto que encontraste cerca de Sarch Vorn.\
\
'Pero esto... este era el collar de mi madre.'\
\
Permanece en silencio durante un momento, su mano cerrándose alrededor del collar deslustrado. Luego te mira con una sonrisa triste.\
\
'Gracias. Supongo que saber lo que ocurrió significa que puedo cerrar la puerta de mi corazón que dejé abierta, esperando que algún día regresara. Sin embargo, creo que siempre supe que no lo haría.'","'No sé lo que puedas encontrar en Sarch Vorn, pero me pregunto si podría pedirte que busques cualquier pista de que mi madre pudo haber ido por allí. Sospecho que, al igual que nosotros, ella estaba siguiendo los pasos de Luilloth.\
\
'No sé lo que podrías encontrar, pero cualquier cosa me interesaría. Estoy regresando a Herne. El guiso debe necesitar que lo remuevan ya. Llevas mucha esperanza contigo, y guardaré esperanza en mi corazón de que te volveré a ver.'","Has encontrado un viejo collar en el esqueleto desgastado por el clima de una mujer. Sospechas que Rhiangar estaría interesada en este objeto.\
\
Deberías llevarle el collar a Herne."},
[12982]={"'That was the biggest troll I have ever seen! Let's get back to Viznak's hideout before it finds another way out!'","'Please tell me you're ready to get out of here!'","Derrota a las merrevail (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to the Uruk Prisoner","Rhadrog is right next to you!\
\
You should talk to Rhadrog.","You have managed to escape with Rhadrog and Viznak.\
\
You should talk to Rhadrog.","Defeat Stained merrevail (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","'No, no! Get away from me! If they see me speaking to outsiders, they will torture me more!'","Run!","Screams and moans from many different creatures echo around in the chamber before you","Find an entrance into Seregost","'These poor men... Lhaereth must be subjecting them to her plague.  If we cannot get any information out of them, we may need to extract some from these Orcs and goblins...\
\
'That Uruk over there still looks aware. We don't have anything to lose; let's try talking to him.'","Viznak is somewhere deeper in the prison.\
\
Now that you have the information you need, you should find Viznak.","Merrevail derrotadas (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeated Stained merrevail (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Viznak","'What... what is this place? Ugh, that stench! I have a feeling these cells do not all contain living beings. We need to find Viznak quickly and get out of here!\
\
'No, no, I am letting my fears win and forgetting the mission! We need to find information on the plague first, rescue Viznak second. Let's see if any of these prisoners are alive and willing to speak to us.'","You and Viznak are prepared to enter Seregost. What secrets and what dangers can be found within?","Talk to Rhadrog","'The pain! So much pain... I was always loyal to Lord Sauron. Why is this happening? Curse that wretched Lhaereth!'","Defeated the Blood-witch","Viznak can be found near Seregost.\
\
You should talk to Viznak.","Defeat the Blood-witch","Living prisoners can be found inside the prison.\
\
You should talk to these prisoners.","Find Viznak","Rhadrog is standing by inside the prison.\
\
You should talk to Rhadrog.","The merrevail have Viznak tied to an altar","'Right, here's the plan. Get in, get shinies, get out before Blight Lady gets home.\
\
'You ready? I'm ready! Let's do this!'","Talk to the Easterling prisoner","Bolvág the Cursed is chasing you!\
\
You should run!","Viznak has been ambushed by merrevail on Seregost's terrace!\
\
You should defeat the merrevail.","The Secrets of Seregost","The Blood-witch can be found in the deepest chamber of Seregost's prison.\
\
You should defeat the Blood-witch and her merrevail.","Viznak has been taken into Seregost.\
\
You should find a way inside.","'You... ${RACE}. You will be the instrument of my revenge! Come closer. I will tell you everything!'","Talk to the Nurnhoth prisoner","Bolvág the Cursed roars behind you, but you are safe for now"},
[12983]={"Rúzat, Agátur, and Náth can be found at Limlók.\
\
You should talk to the three dwarves.","'Aye, it looks like my curiosity was warranted. I am glad that we stopped those goblins from joining forces with Gundabad.'","'I overheard some goblins talking while I was in Sundergrót. At the time, I did not think much of it, but perhaps I should revisit what it was I heard.\
\
'Do you find it odd that the goblins work and camp as if they are commanded, yet there is no commander in sight? Yes, well, I heard a few goblins talking about an important meeting that is soon to happen in Sundergrót. Could this meeting be with this mysterious, absent commander? I say we find this meeting, and learn what is really going on here!'","Sundergrót can be found in the Floodfells.\
\
You should talk to Agátur outside of Sundergrót.","'Thank you for your assistance on our survey mission. I hope that you will return to Skarháld with us. Please, bring us word from Grimbeorn as soon as you hear something.'","'It is always a pleasure to receive assistance from the great ${PLAYER}. I hope our paths cross once more, my friend!'","Talk to Agátur at Limlók","Talk to Agátur outside of Sundergrót","'${PLAYER}, something bothers me about the goblins in Sundergrót. I know not what, but something is amiss! Agátur looks as if he has something to say. Spit it out, my friend!'","The Secrets of Sundergrót","Talk to Náth at Limlók","The goblins of Sundergrót have set up a secret meeting within the old dwarf ruins.","Talk to Rúzat at Limlók"},
[12984]={"This person was buried with what looks like an ornate dog collar","This person was buried with what looks like a board game, the pieces carved from stone","Andûmu has asked you to examine the grave goods buried with the people in north-eastern An Shêru to learn something of who they were and what their lives were like. You started at Naxar Dâl, north of Gadim-ûn, and next went to the Crypts of Khâb Daku, examining grave goods at each location. You should return to Andûmu in Gadim-ûn and tell him what you discovered.","Defeat wights at Naxar Dâl (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","This person was buried with a small statue that looks Gondorian in style","'Tell me, friend. What did you learn?'\
\
You tell him that many of these people appear to have been wealthy and learned, and traded with the Temámir as well as Gondor. They were not without soldiers but were probably not particularly warlike, and are likely the ancestors of the Shagâni living here today.\
\
'Do you think they lived in Zajâna of old? Much trade happens there, I believe. They say it was founded by the Kingdom of Nísaka, which fell even before my grandfather was born. The Ordâkhai destroyed Nísaka on their march northward. Zajâna is all that remains of that kingdom.\
\
'Well, Zajâna, and perhaps this boneyard! I fear these wights, as any sane man should, but it is also fascinating to me that these bodies belonged to people of a different time. It sounds like many of them had good lives.\
\
'Thank you for taking the time for this.'","This person was buried with jewellery, some of which is of Temámir-make","This person was buried with weapons similar to those used by Shagâni today","Andûmu has asked you to examine the grave goods buried with the people in north-eastern An Shêru to learn something of who they were and what their lives were like. You started at Naxar Dâl, north of Gadim-ûn, and next went to the Crypts of Khâb Daku, to the south, where you defeated some of the wights there, clearing some space for yourself.","'I cannot help but be curious about the people buried here. They are unlike any Shagâni I know. How long ago did they live? Why are there so many, and why are they in this place?\
\
'It is common in many cultures to include personal items when they lay their dead to rest. It is bad luck to disturb the dead in their graves, but these poor souls are already disturbed. If you would be willing to humour me, would you mind taking a look at some of the graves and examining their belongings? There are many graves to be found in Naxar Dâl to the north, and Khâb Daku to the south. Perhaps the items they were buried with could tell us something of their story.'","The Secrets of the Dead","This person was buried wearing clothes interwoven with gold","Examine grave goods at the Crypts of Khâb Daku (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Naxar Dâl wights defeated (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat wights at Khâb Daku (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Andûmu has asked you to examine the grave goods buried with the people in north-eastern An Shêru to learn something of who they were and what their lives were like. You should start at Naxar Dâl, north of Gadim-ûn, and defeat some wights there to clear some space for yourself.","This person was buried with wine bottles, now dusty and dry","Many wights have risen from the grave in An Shêru, but who were they?","Andûmu has asked you to examine the grave goods buried with the people in north-eastern An Shêru to learn something of who they were and what their lives were like. You started at Naxar Dâl, north of Gadim-ûn, and defeated some of the wights, clearing some space for yourself.","This person was buried with a collection of scrolls, the paper crumbling and unreadable","Examine grave goods at Naxar Dâl (${CURRENT}/${MAX})","Talk to Andûmu in Gadim-ûn","Khâb Daku wights defeated (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Andûmu has asked you to examine the grave goods buried with the people in north-eastern An Shêru to learn something of who they were and what their lives were like. You started at Naxar Dâl, north of Gadim-ûn, and should now go to the Crypts of Khâb Daku, to the south. Defeat some of the wights there to clear some space for yourself."},
[12985]={"La Semilla de la Putrefacción","'Ha pasado tiempo, ¿verdad? ¿Descubristeis qué estaba ocurriendo en el Bosque Viejo?\
\
'Relatas la historia al Alguacil, que escucha atentamente con los ojos muy abiertos.\
\
'He de decir que esto me supera. Espadas malvadas y trolls silvanos dan para una buena historia, pero me alegra saber que el bosque se está calmando. Aun así, todo estuvo peligrosamente cerca de Los Gamos. A partir de ahora estaremos más vigilantes.\
\
'Los Guardacercas están en deuda contigo… ¡y también con Marigold!'","Completa «El infortunio del sauce» en cualquier nivel de dificultad","«El infortunio del sauce» completada","Hob Guardacercas vigila el Portal del Este.\
\
Deberías contarle lo que ha sucedido desde la última vez que lo viste.","Tom te ha dicho que la espada se encuentra cerca del Viejo Hombre Sauce.\
\
Deberías colaborar con Marigold para encontrar la espada y destruirla.","Habla con Hob Guardacercas","Habla con Marigold","Completa «El infortunio del sauce» en cualquier nivel de dificultad.\
\
A partir del nivel 20, usa el Buscador de instancias para entrar en El infortunio del sauce.","Depende de ti proteger el Bosque Viejo, para que no sea invadido por trolls silvanos y espíritus malignos.","'¿Buscáis romper la espada? El viejo Tom no os lo impedirá. Pero no vayáis solos mientras ese viejo Hombre Sauce siga cantando. Su canción hoy es más oscura que antaño, peligrosa y cruel.\
\
'¡Adelante, pequeños amigos! Que nuestra hobbit muestre el camino. Evitad los peligros funestos y, si no podéis, mantened la fortaleza y la prudencia.'","'¿Trolls silvanos? Bueno, eso es nuevo para mí; ¡no muchos hobbits se han enfrentado a trolls!\
\
'Debí imaginar que a Tom no le interesaría venir con nosotros, pero no importa. Podemos encontrar al Viejo Hombre Sauce por nuestra cuenta. Si prefieres llamar a otros amigos, me quedaré aquí para cubriros las espaldas.\
\
'Cuando hayáis decidido qué hacer, nos pondremos en marcha.'"},
[12986]={"Grind up the digestive roots at the grinding stone north of Herestan","Collected digestive roots (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The Seeping Poison","The grinding stone is at the armour-making pavillion north of Herestan.\
\
You now have some digestive roots and need to grind them into powder.","'You think...you can help me? I am...so weak from...the poison....'\
\
You remember the powder Maelona made that cured Iwan of his self-inflicted poisoning and think you might be able to help Herestan. You need to find digestive roots from the base of certain trees located around the lake in Tâl Methedras.","'I do not feel well...so weak....'\
\
You think back to your time in Tûr Morva and remember Iwan of the Falcon-clan experimenting with poisons. You remember too the words of Maelona, who spoke of collecting certain roots throughout Tâl Methedras and grinding them up to form a digestive powder. The roots could be found at the base of certain trees around the lake in Tâl Methedras.\
\
You tell Herestan that you may be able to help him.","Herestan has suffered a poisoned wound from a Dunlending blade and needs your help to brew an antidote.","'¿No tienes nada para mí?'","'I am sorry that I cannot...be of more help...to you...so weak....'\
\
You remember the grinding stone at the pavillion to the north. You can use that to grind up the digestive roots.","Collect digestive roots (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Herestan is to the south of the grinding stone, by the lake's edge, where you left him.","You grind the roots into a powder","'You have...returned...my friend....'\
\
You gently give Herestan the root powder, and he swallows it with some difficulty. After a moment, he takes a deep breath and much of the colour returns to his face.\
\
'I feel much better already, my friend. Thank you for taking the time to find this antidote! But...how did you know how to make this curative? I am fortunate you did!'","Bring the digestive root-powder to Herestan","Digestive roots can be found throughout Tâl Methedras, around the shores of the lake and on the eyot in the middle of the water, at the base of trees."},
[12987]={"Defeated sekbiri (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Defeat sekbiri (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Sekbiri have attacked Zamarzîr. A local guard would like to cull down their numbers to prevent another attack from happening.","A worried guard at the gate of Halrax has asked you to cull down the sekbir population in their den on the north side of the island.\
\
Sekbiri may be found at Ghar Jâdam to the north of Zamarzîr.","'You there, with the sword. Or is that an axe? Or a big rock? I can't see very well. Anyway, you look tough.\
\
'Some of the sekbiri from up north strayed close to the gate last week. Thankfully no one got hurt. Well, except for Itho and nobody likes him anyway.\
\
'The town's promised some funds to the idiot -- I mean brave soul -- who's willing to cull down their numbers.'","The Sekbiri of Ghar Jâdam"},
[12988]={"Atli moves to a safer location to tend to his injury","Help Atli with 'Before They Become a Problem'","'I doubt there is much else to learn here, ${PLAYER}. I would like to continue on with our mission. We should next investigate the spiders to the east. The Rangers report the spiders there isolate themselves from the spiders of Torech Ungol. I suspect I may know their reasons for this, but I would like to confirm my suspicions with my own eyes before I share my thoughts.\
\
'I will bring the Ungoladan prisoner back to Echad Taerdim. Mablung may wish to question Felgúr himself. I will meet you near the spider-infested forest, Taurlingol.'","Find Taurlingol","According to the Rangers, the spider-infested forest of Taurlingol can be found in eastern Cirith Ungol.\
\
You should find Taurlingol.","Atli Spider-bane is engaged in combat with a giant spider!","You hear shouts nearby!","Legolas has asked for your assistance with tasks in Taurlingol.\
\
You should complete 'The Daughters of Iphantemel,' 'The Trees of Taurlingol,' 'Before They Become a Problem,' and 'The Only Solution.'","Atli has moved to a safe location nearby.\
\
You should find and talk to Atli Spider-bane.","Help Atli with 'The Only Solution'","Help Legolas with 'The Daughters of Iphantemel'","Find the source of the shouting","Legolas wishes to next investigate the spider-infested woods in eastern Cirith Ungol, Taurlingol.","'I apologize for not arriving sooner, ${PLAYER}. I did see the spider you fought, and my suspicions were proven correct: these are the Mirkwood spiders, Iphantamel's own brood. This forest is too small to hold all that vanished from Eryn Lasgalen, however. Perhaps some have already entered Torech Ungol. I admit I do not fully understand the quarrelling between spiders. It matters not. The old enemy of my people has been found, and we must deal out vengeance upon them.\
\
'I must tend to Atli's wounds, thus I must rely on you to venture into Taurlingol and slay my enemies for me. I know that you are capable of this task.'\
\
You ask Legolas how he and Atli are acquainted. He allows the briefest hint of a smile to cross his face.\
\
'Ah, I encountered him when we were last in Lhingris, in a very similar situation, in fact. He was engaged in combat with several very large brood-mothers, and I stepped in to assist him. I believe he was embarrassed, and accused me of \\qstealing his kill\\q.\
\
'But that is quite absurd!'","'Oof, thanks for the assistance, ${PLAYER}. And Legolas is here as well! I am happy to see some faces with fewer than eight eyes! It also helps that you're not trying to devour me. Haha! Erk....'\
\
Atli doubles over and grabs his leg. His injuries seem to be worse than he let on.\
\
'Aye, she chewed up my leg something fierce. Oh, don't worry about me, I will be fine. I just need to rest a bit....'","You have found Atli Spider-bane in combat with a giant spider of Taurlingol.\
\
You should help Atli defeat the spider!","Help Legolas with 'The Trees of Taurlingol'","'Well done, ${PLAYER}. With the death of Iphantamel's daughters, the rest of the spiders will likely disperse into Cirith Ungol. I will return to track and kill them myself, one by one. For now, we must escort Atli to Echad Taerdim. He should be able to travel on his wounded leg, but it is not safe to remain here.'","You should inform Legolas of your success defeating the Mirkwood Spiders.\
\
Legolas can be found on a hill near Taurlingol.","Talk to Atli Spider-bane","Help Atli defeat the spider","Habla con Legolas.","The Sequestered Spiders","Legolas is tending to Atli Spider-bane's injuries on an overlook near Taurlingol.\
\
You should talk to Legolas.","As you entered Taurlingol, you heard someone shouting.\
\
You should find the source of the shouting."},
[12990]={"Léothred, the Rohirric scholar, seeks to complete the journey his ancestors took north, from the Vales of Anduin through Misthallow.","Thokvist can be found in the south of Misthallow.\
\
You should travel to Thokvist.","Orcs can be found in Misthallow.\
\
You should defeat Orcs in Misthallow.","'I am sure that Skarding is pleased with our efforts. The slaying of Orcs is just as the Ai-thúda would have done when they first came here. Now, if we are to stay near Thokvist for a while longer, I have some thoughts on what to search for next!'","Defeated Orcs in Misthallow (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","Talk to Léothred at Thokvist","Defeat Orcs in Misthallow (${NUMBER}/${TOTAL})","The camp's occupants glance and nod towards you and Léothred as you enter","Léothred can be found at Thokvist.\
\
You should talk to Léothred.","'I find it curious that one would not be sure of the past of their kind. I have never had this problem and wish Léothred luck in finding the answers he seeks.'","'Hmm, if you want to dig up rocks, I will not stop you. There are more important things to do, but who am I to tell you what is more important?'","'${PLAYER}, have you ever seen a Great Eagle this close before? Such beauty! These lands are full of impressive surprises.\
\
'It is very kind of Skarding to let us stay at his encampment and continue my research in Misthallow. It would seem that our next location to visit is the old Ai-thúda ruins of Lumrog. However, Skarding has informed me that Lumrog is currently occupied by all sorts of vicious trolls. No matter, the ruins were most likely an old farmhouse and nothing more. Yes, we shall skip these ruins and continue tracing the footsteps of the Ai-thúda as they settled throughout the valley.\
\
'Perhaps we should assist our new friend here first and defeat some of the Orcs in this valley.'","'You have been an outstanding guide on this journey. I do hope that you will continue further north with me. As you can see, my people did only pass through the Floodfells. They did not settle here. The White Mare may signify that journey. It is also the journey we must take.\
\
'I mentioned to the Beornings at Limlók that I plan to travel to Misthallow. I was told of Skarding's encampment, Thokvist. Perhaps that would be a safe place to next travel? We could ask Skarding for advice on Misthallow, since he may know more of it than we.'","The Settling of Misthallow","Travel to Thokvist in Misthallow"},
[12991]={"Las estatuas de los Siete Centinelas se encuentran en el Templo de los Siete Centinelas, al este de Gabilshathûr.\
\
Las siete espadas deben ser entregadas a los Siete Centinelas en el orden correcto antes de que se abra la bóveda.","Entrega la Espada de la Vigilia a la estatua correcta","Entrega la Espada de la Masacre a la estatua correcta","Colocas la espada en la mano de la estatua","Entrega la Espada de Rhudaur a la estatua correcta","'¡Has logrado hacerlo! Este cofre contiene tesoros de épocas pasadas forjados para combatir las fuerzas de la oscuridad.\
\
'Después de todo tu esfuerzo y el peligro que has enfrentado, es justo que elijas uno de estos objetos como tu recompensa justa. El resto será enviado a mis hermanos para ser distribuido.'","'¿No has recuperado el tesoro de los Siete Centinelas?'","Has recogido el tesoro de los Siete Centinelas","Parece que esta no es la estatua correcta","Se han recuperado las siete espadas de los Siete Centinelas, y Nethraw realiza los preparativos finales para abrir la bóveda de los Siete Centinelas.","Las siete espadas","Lleva el tesoro de los Siete Centinelas de vuelta a Nethraw","'¡Por fin ha llegado el momento de abrir la antigua bóveda! Creo que cada una de estas siete estatuas debe recibir la espada correcta antes de que se pueda abrir la bóveda... pero la historia es, desafortunadamente, un poco vaga. Supongo que podríamos probar todas las combinaciones, pero eso podría llevar mucho tiempo. \
\
'He hecho una copia de los versos relevantes -- aquí, tal vez puedas descifrarlo todo.'","Entrega la Espada de Arvedui a la estatua correcta","Esto no parece ser la estatua correcta","Recoge el tesoro de los Siete Centinelas","Entrega la Espada del Dolor a la estatua correcta","Entrega la Espada del Crepúsculo a la estatua correcta","Has resuelto el enigma de los Siete Centinelas, así que ahora es el momento de entrar en la bóveda y recuperar el tesoro.","Entrega la Espada de Gondor a la estatua correcta"},
[12992]={"Protege a Nethraw","Nethraw se encuentra en Kruslë Lannan, al este de Gabilshathûr.\
\
Debes colocar las siete espadas en sus pedestales para abrir Kruslë Lannan.","Coloca las siete espadas en sus pedestales","Nethraw derrotado","Las siete espadas","Escapa de Kruslë Lannan","Has venido con Nethraw al corazón de Kruslë Lannan.","'Mi estudio está casi completo, ${PLAYER}.'","Debes escapar de Kruslë Lannan con Nethraw.","Busca Kruslë Lannan con Nethraw.","Derrotaste la sombra de Ánraig"},
[12993]={"Nethraw se encuentra en Kruslë Lannan, al este de Gabilshathûr.\
\
Nethraw te ha pedido que lo acompañes dentro del sitio.","'Devuélveme las espadas, ${PLAYER}, ¡rápido!\
\
'Me encargaré de estas espadas y encerraré a los Perjuros que quedan dentro de Kruslë Lannan para siempre.\
\
'Te agradezco tu ayuda, ${PLAYER}, tengo muchas notas que estudiar. Por favor, toma uno de los objetos que pude recuperar de Kruslë Lannan como muestra de mi gratitud.'","Acompaña a Nethraw dentro de Kruslë Lannan.","'Has encontrado las siete espadas, es un gran logro, ${PLAYER} ! Ahora podemos devolverlas a su lugar y finalmente podremos entrar en Kruslë Lannan.\
\
'Reúne algunos compañeros dignos de confianza y vuelve a verme cuando estés ${PLAYER:listo[m]|lista[f]}. No sería prudente entrar en un lugar así sin poderosos aliados para protegerme en mis estudios.'","Las siete espadas","Nethraw se encuentra en Kruslë Lannan, al este de Gabilshathûr.\
\
Nethraw te ha pedido que encuentres aliados y lo acompañes dentro del sitio.","Nethraw se encuentra en Kruslë Lannan, al este de Gabilshathûr.\
\
Deberías hablar de nuevo con Nethraw.","'Fuiste alguien valiente y simpático, ${PLAYER}. No podría pedir nada más.'","'¿Empezamos a colocar las espadas, ${PLAYER}?\
\
'Me llevará solo un momento ordenar mis notas. Prepárate, porque no sé lo que encontraremos dentro.'","'¿Has vuelto sin las siete espadas? Sin ellas, no podremos cerrar la puerta de Kruslë Lannan!'","Habla con Nethraw","'Has vuelto, ${PLAYER}, entonces creo que puedes hacer la tarea que te espera.\
\
'Vuelve a sostener las siete espadas que has encontrado. Deberías ser tú quien las coloque en su lugar y abra la puerta.'","Has encontrado las siete espadas de Kruslë Lannan."},
[12995]={"'Estas son empuñaduras antiguas y bien forjadas. Su fabricación original parece haber sido obra de un artesano de Eregion, pues llevan muchas de las marcas y el estilo de su herrería, pero esa artesanía ha sido retorcida y corrompida hasta su forma actual.\
\
'Las runas de morgul sobre las empuñaduras llevan los juramentos de sus dueños. Es un juramento oscuro que no permitiré que se pronuncie en mis salones. Debido a su forja, creo que pueden ser deshechas... llévalas a Hemeldir en las Fraguas de Rivendel.'","'¿Cómo puedo ayudarte?'","'Puedo deshacer las empuñaduras de morgul. Es extraño que su artesanía sea similar a la de los herreros élficos de antaño, aunque llevan marcas de gran dolor y malicia. Estas empuñaduras proyectan una sombra sobre mi corazón. Temo que haya un mal mayor en su creación de lo que incluso el Maestro Elrond haya supuesto.\
\
'Su destrucción debería, en efecto, romper los hechizos que las atan a este mundo.'","Elrond puede encontrarse en Rivendel, en el Bosque de los Trolls, al sureste de las Quebradas del Norte.\
\
Istuienn te dijo que lleves las empuñaduras de morgul a Elrond el Medio Elfo para que sean destruidas.","Has recuperado las cuatro empuñaduras de morgul de los espectros en las ruinas de Fornost. Istuienn te ha pedido ayuda para encontrar una forma de destruirlas.","'Lleva estas empuñaduras de inmediato al Maestro Elrond en Rivendel... él sabrá qué hacer con ellas.'","La Sombra Cae","'¿Así que dices que has derrotado a los espectros? Me temo que no fueron destruidos por completo, pues están atados a este mundo por los hechizos sobre esas empuñaduras.\
\
'La malicia de sus espíritus aún permanece, y regresarán con el tiempo. He leído todo lo que he podido en las empuñaduras de morgul. Son retorcidas y negras, pero llevan extraños símbolos para obras del Enemigo. Te pediría que lleves las empuñaduras lo más rápido posible al valle de Rivendel, a la casa de Elrond el Medio Elfo... él sabrá cómo tratarlas mejor.\
\
'Rivendel se encuentra en lo profundo del Bosque de los Trolls, muy al sur y al este. Destruir las empuñaduras debería romper el hechizo que ata sus tendones invisibles a este mundo. Te advierto nuevamente: no manipules las empuñaduras, llévalas lo más rápido que puedas a Rivendel.'","'Hemeldir, mi maestro herrero, destruirá estas cosas malignas... llévaselas de inmediato.'","Lleva las empuñaduras de morgul a Hemeldir","Hemeldir se encuentra en las Fraguas de Rivendel, fuera de los Salones de Elrond.\
\
Elrond te dijo que lleves las empuñaduras de morgul a su maestro herrero, Hemeldir."},
[12996]={"Now that you have the key, you should return to Baradal's cage and try to open it.","The lock springs open, freeing Baradal","The lock resists your attempts","The Shadow Over Shathur-munzu","Baradal has been freed from her cage.\
\
You should talk to Baradal.","Complete 'Instance: The Shadow Hunter'","Find Baradal","Baradal is barely conscious. She stirs as you approach.\
\
'${PLAYER}...? Where am I?'\
\
She is still dazed from the warg attack. You should find a way to get her out of this cage before Ránulur returns.","This key looks like it may open the lock on Baradal's cage","'This must be Shathur-munzu. We know not what lies inside, but it is my charge to clear it of anyone or anything that would bring harm to Lady Arwen. When you are ready, we will enter.'","'${PLAYER}, I think I am recovering my senses. What has happened?'","Defeat the Orc jailor","You find yourself in a den of wargs and Orc-kind. Baradal is nowhere to be seen, and it is very likely she is in grave danger.\
\
You should make your way through Shathur-munzu and find her before it is too late. Be wary; Ránulur the warg chieftain, or the 'Shadow-hunter', as he is known to the locals, may still be near.","It seems this lock is too sturdy to be opened by force. You will need to find the key. It is probably being carried by an Orc or goblin somewhere inside Shathur-munzu.","Somewhere inside Shathur-munzu, an Orc holds the key to Baradal's cage.\
\
You should find and defeat the Orc jailor.","Attempt to break the lock","Completado.","Talk to Baradal","'Wait, do you hear that?'","Baradal is somewhere inside Shathur-munzu. She may be in danger.\
\
You should find Baradal.","The time has come to enter Shathur-munzu.\
\
You should complete 'Instance: The Shadow Hunter.'","The time has come to see what lies inside Shathur-munzu. Whatever awaits, your goal is to clear it of danger for Lady Arwen's arrival.","Acquire the crude iron key","Open the strong lock","Defeated the Orc jailor","Baradal is locked inside a cage in Shathur-munzu, injured and in danger.\
\
You should attempt to break open her cage.","Completado"},
[12997]={"'Seguramente te habrán informado de la incursión. Son noticias alarmantes. Me temo que esta pequeña fuerza es solo una partida de exploración. Les seguirán muchas más, muchas más de las que podamos manejar en combate abierto.\
\
'Si queremos derrotarlos, debemos saber cuál es su objetivo. ¿A qué parte de Evendim se dirigen? ¿Por qué vienen ahora? ¿Qué está pasando para provocar esto?\
\
'Dirígete al pequeño campamento de Tham Ornen. Nuestros exploradores vieron a los angmarines pegando cosas en las paredes. Creo que son copias de planos e información descubierta. Recoge varios y tráemelos.'","La sombra se extiende","'Así que se dirigen a Annuminas y buscan algo dentro de las antiguas ruinas inundadas. Afortunadamente, parece que tenemos algo de tiempo para prepararnos antes de que llegue el grueso de las tropas.'","Nadfaron se encuentra en Tinnudir, al suroeste de Tham Ornen.\
\
Nadfaron querrá examinar las órdenes que encontraste en el campamento angmarin de Tham Ornen.","'No podemos ir a la batalla contra Angmar a ciegas. Debemos saber qué es lo que buscan.'","Tham Ornen ha sido ocupada por las fuerzas de Angmar. Se desconoce qué valor ven en las ruinas.","Tham Ornen se encuentra al noreste de Tinnudir.\
\
Nadfaron te pidió que fueras a Tham Ornen y recogieras órdenes del campamento angmarin."},
[12998]={"Habla con Lethi","'Ah, ${PLAYER}. ¡Es bueno verte en un día tan espléndido!\
\
'Nos has ayudado durante muchos meses a restaurar la Mansión de Thorin, y espero que ahora te sientas bienvenido entre nosotros. No he olvidado la forma en que nos conocimos, ni los sombríos acontecimientos que la precedieron. Hay inquietud en el aire, y temo que aún no hayamos visto lo último de Skorgrím Duramano ni de las sombras de Angmar que lo guían.\
\
'Aún queda mucho por hacer en la Mansión de Thorin, pero cuando llegue el momento, te concedo permiso para buscar tu propia aventura. El mal ya no se molesta en ocultarse, y los Pueblos Libres necesitarán ayuda... especialmente de alguien como tú, ${PLAYER}.'\
\
'Ha llegado el momento, creo, de que regreses al mundo.'","'¡Es ahora o nunca, ${PLAYER}!'","'¡Ha comenzado!'\
\
Lethi mira a su alrededor, observando los cuerpos dispersos de Orcos, Hombres y Hachetones.\
\
'Antes de que me diera cuenta de lo que estaba ocurriendo, Vaski y los demás mataron a los Hombres de la Orden y huyeron de las mazmorras. Yo no quería formar parte de esta conspiración, ¡pero será peor para nosotros si permanecemos aquí mucho más tiempo! Tal vez podamos escondernos en Udûn... ¿pero escapar de Mordor? ¡No lo creo!\
\
'No importa adónde vayamos, ¡pero tenemos que salir de aquí! Conozco el camino hacia las puertas de la Torre Oscura, pero necesitaré tu ayuda.\
\
'¿Qué decides?'","La Sombra de Mordor","Habla con Dwalin en la Mansión de Thorin","Lethi puede encontrarse en las mazmorras de Barad-dûr.\
\
Los Hachetones han comenzado a rebelarse dentro de la Torre Oscura. Deberías hablar con Lethi.","A medida que la sombra de Mordor se alarga sobre la Tierra Media, el Enemigo ordena la liberación de un prisionero misterioso, provocando intrigas y revueltas en Barad-dûr.","Dwalin puede encontrarse en la Mansión de Thorin.\
\
Has pasado muchos meses ayudando a deshacer el daño causado en la Mansión de Thorin por los Duramano. Deberías hablar con Dwalin."},
[12999]={"Examine the food scraps","Narchraw was said to be imprisoned in the jails of Barad-dûr.\
\
You should follow the trail of scratch marks.","Examined the chamber.","It looks as if the cloth has been ripped apart by large claws","While the marks show that the beast already escaped, you should continue to press ahead","The Shadow of Narchraw","It looks as if there was a violent scuffle here","The chamber is scattered with debris.\
\
You should inspect the various debris in the chamber.","Examine the tattered cloth","Lômazar tells you of the ancient beast, Narchraw, that Dulgabêth wishes to treat with.","While the food is moldy, the beast must have escaped during a feeding","Follow the trail of scratch marks","You notice large scratch marks on a nearby wall","'If you seek allies of Dulgabêth, look first to an enemy of Sauron. Many years ago, a beast by the name of Narchraw crossed Sauron. He was locked away in the dungeons of Barad-dûr for his crimes. The dungeons can still be found within the ruins of the citadel.\
\
'There are troubling rumours that Dulgabêth has spoken with Narchraw. Find the beast and kill it at once. If the tales are true, there are few as dangerous as Narchaw in the lands of Mordor.'","While you do not notice anything out of the ordinary, the beast known as Narchraw must be very powerful.\
\
You decide to think about your next course of action.","Examine the rubble","Completado","Enter Barad-dûr","Barad-dûr is located in eastern Dor Amarth.\
\
You should enter Barad-dûr.","You come across a very old chamber"},
}
